sResult.tasks:        yield task    else:      print_aurora_log(logging.ERROR          \\\"Error: could not retrieve task information for run command: %s\\\" % resp.messageDEPRECATED)      raise ValueError(\\\"Could not retrieve task information: %s\\\" % resp.messageDEPRECATED){noformat}print_aurora_log is an undefined symbol here.  there\'s a version of it defined in apache.aurora.client.cli but including it would make for a cyclic dependency between .api and .cli.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',63,'AURORA-505','15','{\"key\": \"AURORA-505\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 15, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Add a target for a standalone clientv2\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',64,'AURORA-508','15','{\"key\": \"AURORA-508\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 15, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Fix ugliness in aurora help\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"\\\"aurora help\\\" currently has some aesthetic issues:- in some places the default name for a parameter is used: \'job status [--write-json] value\'; metavars should be used to fill that in.- In usage lists (like \\\"aurora help job\\\") the long list of usage lines is difficult to follow; blank lines in between would make it clearer.- In some cases strings aren\'t getting handled properly resulting in lists of characters isntead of strings (eg \\\"aurora help job create\\\")\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',65,'AURORA-513','15','{\"key\": \"AURORA-513\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 15, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Errors during thrift RPC calls cause ugly stack dumps\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Anonymized error message below. The user did an update; during the course of the update what appears to be a transient network glitch caused a thrift socket to become None which led to an invalid attempt to dereference None which caused a stack dump. The actual error is in thrift-generated code. INFO] Examining instances: [360 361 362 363 364 365] INFO] Adding instances: [360 361 362 363 364 365] INFO] Instances added INFO] Watching instances: [360 361 362 363 364 365]Traceback (most recent call last):  File \\\"...aurora-client/twitter/common/app/application.py\\\" line 738 in _wrap_method    return_code = method()  File \\\"...aurora-client/twitter/common/app/application.py\\\" line 760 in <lambda>    main = lambda: main_method(*args **kwargs)  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/apache/aurora/client/base.py\\\" line 72 in wrapped_function    return fn(*args)  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/apache/aurora/client/commands/core.py\\\" line 614 in update    resp = api.update_job(config options.health_check_interval_seconds options.shards)  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/apache/aurora/client/hooks/hooked_api.py\\\" line 184 in update_job    config health_check_interval_seconds=health_check_interval_seconds instances=instances))  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/apache/aurora/client/hooks/hooked_api.py\\\" line 145 in _hooked_call    resp = api_call()  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/apache/aurora/client/api/__init__.py\\\" line 128 in update_job    return updater.update(instances)  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/apache/aurora/client/api/updater.py\\\" line 455 in update    if not self._update(instance_configs):  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/apache/aurora/client/api/updater.py\\\" line 143 in _update    failed_instances = self._watcher.watch(instances_to_watch) if instances_to_watch else set()  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/apache/aurora/client/api/instance_watcher.py\\\" line 95 in watch    running_tasks = self._get_tasks_by_instance_id(instance_ids)  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/apache/aurora/client/api/instance_watcher.py\\\" line 134 in _get_tasks_by_instance_id    resp = self._scheduler.getTasksStatus(query)  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/apache/aurora/client/api/scheduler_client.py\\\" line 264 in method_wrapper    return method(*(args + auth_args))  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.gen.aurora-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/gen/apache/aurora/api/ReadOnlyScheduler.py\\\" line 129 in getTasksStatus    return self.recv_getTasksStatus()  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/apache.gen.aurora-0.5.1_DEV1401741199-py2.6.egg/gen/apache/aurora/api/ReadOnlyScheduler.py\\\" line 140 in recv_getTasksStatus    (fname mtype rseqid) = self._iprot.readMessageBegin()  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/thrift-0.9.1-py2.6-macosx-10.4-x86_64.egg/thrift/protocol/TJSONProtocol.py\\\" line 317 in readMessageBegin    self.readJSONArrayStart()  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/thrift-0.9.1-py2.6-macosx-10.4-x86_64.egg/thrift/protocol/TJSONProtocol.py\\\" line 305 in readJSONArrayStart    self.readJSONSyntaxChar(LBRACKET)  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/thrift-0.9.1-py2.6-macosx-10.4-x86_64.egg/thrift/protocol/TJSONProtocol.py\\\" line 210 in readJSONSyntaxChar    current = self.reader.read()  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/thrift-0.9.1-py2.6-macosx-10.4-x86_64.egg/thrift/protocol/TJSONProtocol.py\\\" line 139 in read    self.data = self.protocol.trans.read(1)  File \\\"...aurora-client/.deps/thrift-0.9.1-py2.6-macosx-10.4-x86_64.egg/thrift/transport/THttpClient.py\\\" line 97 in read    return self.__http.file.read(sz)AttributeError: \'NoneType\' object has no attribute \'read\'\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',66,'AURORA-516','15','{\"key\": \"AURORA-516\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 15, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Increase maximum instances/job in aurora scheduler\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We\'ve got a user that needs more than 4000 instances of a job. This limit is hard-wired into the scheduler so we need to update it.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',67,'AURORA-347','15','{\"key\": \"AURORA-347\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 15, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"CLI should surface information about locks\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Client should be able to list information about locks held.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',68,'AURORA-528','15','{\"key\": \"AURORA-528\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 15, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Document available SLA metrics\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Add an .md doc describing available SLA stats and their meanings.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',69,'AURORA-537','15','{\"key\": \"AURORA-537\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 15, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"SLA safe domain host-scoped falls back to cluster-wide when no tasks returned\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"It\'s possible for the host-scoped query to not return any tasks which currently results in a follow-up no-filter full cluster pull. This is highly undesirable for perf reasons.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',70,'AURORA-539','15','{\"key\": \"AURORA-539\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 15, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Create a getTaskStatusLight RPC\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need a lightweight API to be used by UI and client in places where ExecutorConfig data is not not required. The sheer size of it slows down a large job pull to a crawl. This is especially sensible now that we switched from binary to json transport. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',71,'AURORA-542','15','{\"key\": \"AURORA-542\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 15, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"perform_maintenance_hosts should drain hosts that passed SLA check\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When using a non-default grouping with perform_maintenance_hosts the entire collection of hosts is skipped in case SLA check fails. Change it to proceed with SLA-compliant hosts instead.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',72,'AURORA-31','15','{\"key\": \"AURORA-31\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 15, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Support an authentication mechanism for client-scheduler communication\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Aurora has the plumbing for authenticated requests but no system is currently implemented.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',73,'AURORA-520','23','{\"key\": \"AURORA-520\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 23, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Update \\\"aurora job diff\\\"\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Users complain because the \\\"aurora job diff\\\" command doesn\'t work the way they\'d like it to. In its current form it\'s got two major problems.(1) It reports spurious differences between running jobs and local configurations due to automatically filled fields that shouldn\'t be part of the comparison. For example a job config specifies who created using an Identity record which has two fields: the rolename running the job and the username of the person who ran the command. For comparing live jobs against local configs that\'s irrelevant.(2) The diffs are very hard to read. Diffs are generated by downloading the running task configs for a job and writing them to the disk in json; then uploading the local config getting *it* converted to thrift and writing that to the disk in json and then running the Unix diff command on the two json files.Unix diff isn\'t the most pleasant thing to read under the best of circumstances. But making matters worse the entire json format of the files being diffed is unfamiliar to users! So they\'re looking at a hard-to-read diff syntax ranging over an unfamiliar data syntax.To fix this I\'d like to replace the use of Unix diff. The json records for the configs are semantically just trees. Writing a comparison function that compares corresponding trees is pretty easy and can generate *much* better diffs. An example of the diff to be generated by this code would be something like the following - assuming that the local config increases the number of instances from 2 to 3 and the CPU request from 2 to 4:{noformat}Local config has a different number of tasks: 3 local vs 2 runningTask diffs found in instance 1:    Field \'numCpus\' is \'4\' local but \'2\' remote2 total diff(s) found{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',74,'AURORA-571','23','{\"key\": \"AURORA-571\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 23, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Admin maintenance fails SLA check when no prod tasks on host\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Return value of _check_sla() is not initialized when no eligible tasks are found on host (e.g. non-prod/low instance count).\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',75,'AURORA-94','23','{\"key\": \"AURORA-94\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 23, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Refactor/remove SchedulerCore in favor of StateManager\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"SchedulerCore does not seem to provide much value and serves as a thin proxy primarily between SchedulerThriftInterface and StateManager.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',76,'AURORA-544','23','{\"key\": \"AURORA-544\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 23, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Add an option to allow users to specify log levels in client\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',77,'AURORA-545','23','{\"key\": \"AURORA-545\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 23, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Add a flag to allow users to prevent blocking of unknown exceptions in client\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',78,'AURORA-581','23','{\"key\": \"AURORA-581\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 23, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Add lightweight hooks for mutating clientv1 commands.\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Aurora clientv2 commands currently support very flexible hooks which get used for a variety of purposes. One of the most popular usecases is as a safety-check mechanism: hooks can add extra safety checks to commands that mutate or kill aurora jobs. Unfortunately these hooks are clientv2 only. Once we\'ve got users transitioned to clientv2 that will be fine but for now clientv1 is acting as a backdoor to allow users to bypass hooks.Cluster administrators should have the ability to prevent this by applying some kind of hooks to the aurora commands that mutate jobs. At the same time we don\'t want to provide the same level of support for hooks that we have in v2 so the v1 hooks should be simpler and lighter-weight since they\'re  just a temporary stopgap.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',79,'AURORA-350','23','{\"key\": \"AURORA-350\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 23, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Parallelize updates to speed up deploys\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The way aurora deploy works inherently contributes to depressed deploy speeds.Aurora deploy like cap/TCU uses the \\\"batch\\\" model. You have 100 things you loop in a batch of N at a time. You restart N things all at once those N things come back online all at once (cold) you wait for the all of them to become available and repeat.Disadvantages:- you can proceed no faster than the slowest guy in the batch. If one instance is \\\"stuck\\\" or slow the whole deploy slows down.- The speed at which your deploy is bounded by your success rate which is bounded by the number of instances currently online but serving below par due to warmup (because computers). The batch methodology maximizes this effect because the restarted shards tend to come back online all at the same time.Let\'s say a full cycle of shutdown reschedule restart wait-for-online-and-good takes 2 minutes but the \\\"bad time\\\" is only 15 seconds. If we do these 8 at a time we have a period where 8 boxes are bad for 15 seconds. That\'s a big success rate spike. What if we were able to 8 of these in parallel such that only one of them is bad at any given moment. It\'s the same speed (all other things being equal) but the impact is much less. We could leverage that to make the deploy go even faster.It\'s easy to see that we could speed deploys up by 2x or more by using an algorithm which minimizes the number of instances starting at any given time but still proceeds quickly in parallel.Aurora should be rewritten to use a thread-based deploy model. You have 100 things and N threads. The main thread dispatches (in a blocking fashion if no threads are ready) restart tasks to each thread in a user-set rate-limited fashion (e.g. no more than one per 15 seconds) which is defined by your per instance warmup time (the time an instance is listening/serving but slow). Each thread then restarts one instance waits it to come back healthy and reports done/failure/etc. Continue until the list is exhausted.This way you have a steady stream of single instances coming online with no clumping of restarts and if any one gets hung up or slow it doesn\'t significantly impact the speed of the deploy (you can \\\"overprovision\\\" the number of threads). You can also retain most of the current deploy semantics around failure counts retry intervals etc.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',80,'AURORA-377','23','{\"key\": \"AURORA-377\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 23, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"No Veto reason is exposed for a task stuck in PENDING due to host constraints\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Tasks stuck in PENDING state due to unsatisfied host constraint don\'t have the reason set in TaskEvent.message. This makes the troubleshooting harder as neither UI nor aurora status can give any clues:{noformat}INFO] role: mesos env: test name: monitoring shard: 147 status: PENDING on Nonecpus: 0.5 ram: 512 MB disk: 3072 MBfailure count: 0 (max 1)events: 2014-05-02 09:05:43 PENDING: Nonemetadata:package: mesos/monitoring v14{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',81,'AURORA-553','23','{\"key\": \"AURORA-553\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 23, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Switch to getTasksWithoutConfig RPC on the client where applicable\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Client commands/APIs that don\'t require TaskConfig data should be switched from getTasksConfig to getTasksWithoutConfig RPC for better perf.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',82,'AURORA-585','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-585\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bhuvaneswaran A\", \"summary\": \"aurora/thermos test failure on py26 due to pex\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Bhuvaneswaran A\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 4, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 7, \"description\": \"The target {{./pants src/test/python:all -vxs}} fail because valid pex is not built. Refer to attached log for verbose output.{code}[bhuvan@build incubator-aurora]$ ./build-support/pex.venv/bin/pexTraceback (most recent call last):  File \\\"./build-support/pex.venv/bin/pex\\\" line 5 in <module>    from pkg_resources import load_entry_point  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 2876 in <module>    working_set = WorkingSet._build_master()  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 449 in _build_master    ws.require(__requires__)  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 745 in require    needed = self.resolve(parse_requirements(requirements))  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 639 in resolve    raise DistributionNotFound(req)pkg_resources.DistributionNotFound: argparse{code}The fix is to explicitly install this library.{code}./build-support/pex.venv/bin/pip install argparse==1.2.1{code}We should fix pants to include this library as one of dependent when it build the pex of pex.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 13, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('Aurora',83,'AURORA-678','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-678\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Serve static HTTP assets out of a classpath directory\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Static asset registration with our HTTP server is somewhat complicated requiring a manual mapping to be made from the request to match and the classpath entry to serve.  Jetty has built-in support for serving static assets out of a directory on the classpath which would reduce all of our asset binding code to a few lines.  It also opens the doors to easy extension of the web interface at runtime by adding to the classpath and would also reduce iteration time when developing the web interface.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',84,'AURORA-722','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-722\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"snapshot performance issues\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"In one of our larger production clusters we\'re seeing issues with snapshot performance that cause the scheduler to failover before completing a snapshot.For background the scheduler writes a compressed (when -deflate_snapshots is enabled) binary-encoded Snapshot (from api.thrift) to the mesos replicated log every hour (or -dlog_snapshot_interval). This snapshot represents most of the scheduler\'s heap usage including the configuration for all tasks running in the cluster.Add appropriate instrumentation to the snapshot routine and patch any obvious performance bottlenecks.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',85,'AURORA-649','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-649\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Implement scheduler API methods linking updater logic and storage\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 7, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',86,'AURORA-686','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-686\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Job updates may fail due to exceeding role quota\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Current way of checking job quota during in-flight updates (i.e. within addInstance transaction) may lead to failed updates and inferior user experience. Since we are tracking quota at the role level but the update lock applied at the job level there is always a possibility to exceed the allowed quota for long running updates. This is especially a problem with the server side-driven process where a resumed update will restart in a potentially quite different quota environment (i.e. due to other jobs created while the update was paused). Possible solutions:- per job quota tracking - requires significant refactoring;- hierarchical locking (e.g. add role lock in addition to job lock) - limits update concurrency per role;- front-loaded consumption (e.g. add additional job consumption during startJobUpdate and re-evaluate on update completion/termination) - will require persisting front-loaded value within job update schema but may be the way to go given current quota implementation.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',87,'AURORA-737','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-737\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Improve clientv2 usage helplines.\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This is created in response to user complaints.The \\\"usage\\\" line in aurora clientv2 help is automatically generated from command options. When an option doesn\'t explicitly declare a string to be used as the displayname of an option the system defaults to using the type of the parameter. For some parameters this is perfectly fine. For example\\\"--watch-secs=int\\\" is clear about what it expects.In other places though it\'s very unclear. For example for creating a job the user sees:{noformat}  create [--bind=pystachio-binding] [--read-json] [--wait-until=(\'PENDING\' \'RUNNING\' \'FINISHED\')] [--open-browser] CLUSTER/ROLE/ENV/NAME str{noformat}What is the \\\"str\\\" supposed to mean? In all of  the places where the typename is displayed and its meaning is unclear the code should explicitly specify a display name/format for the parameter.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',88,'AURORA-697','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-697\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"summary\": \"GZip compression regression in scheduler\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Looks like we accidentally dropped the gzip compression filter from the thrift over HTTP servlet. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',89,'AURORA-571','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-571\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Admin maintenance fails SLA check when no prod tasks on host\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Return value of _check_sla() is not initialized when no eligible tasks are found on host (e.g. non-prod/low instance count).\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',90,'AURORA-700','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-700\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"summary\": \"Scheduler UI should use asynchronous HTTP requests\", \"assignee\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Currently the scheduler UI code was written to assume synchronous network requests - every API call blocks JS execution. This is really going to limit how many API calls we can make per controller before performance is noticeably degraded. Especially with features like the new update API and the pending reasons API call. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',91,'AURORA-608','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-608\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"GcExecutorLauncher should throttle initial activity spike\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"The current implementation of the GcExecutorLauncher randomizes the GC activity by spreading different host GC execution over the hour. It does not however protect from the startup spike of accepted GC offers before the host cache is populated. This proved to be a perf problem for Mesos master under certain conditions.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',92,'AURORA-626','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-626\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Add wait_for_batch_completion option into parallel updater\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"With the parallel updater refactoring we lost an implicit but sometimes useful feature of the sequential updater - controlled batched restart of instances of the same batch. This feature could be useful for certain services with instance topology assumptions.Add a wait_for_batch_completion option into UpdateConfig to block worker threads until the entire batch is completed.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',93,'AURORA-609','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-609\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Admin host maintenance command does not block on post drain script\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Admin needs to wait on post drain script execution to honor any additional delays introduced in the script.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',94,'AURORA-94','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-94\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Refactor/remove SchedulerCore in favor of StateManager\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"SchedulerCore does not seem to provide much value and serves as a thin proxy primarily between SchedulerThriftInterface and StateManager.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',95,'AURORA-692','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-692\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"summary\": \"aurora_admin should have a find_scheduler command\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"aurora_admin should have a find_scheduler command that prints out the host/port pair of the scheduler.  this is handy if you\'re in a bind and need to figure out which is the leading scheduler e.g. if they\'re backed by serversets.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',96,'AURORA-732','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-732\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Disable server-driven job updates by default\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The server-side job updates are functional but not fully-baked yet.  Add a command line argument to disable the startJobUpdate RPC by default.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',97,'AURORA-544','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-544\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Add an option to allow users to specify log levels in client\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',98,'AURORA-545','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-545\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Add a flag to allow users to prevent blocking of unknown exceptions in client\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',99,'AURORA-131','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-131\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Deprecate v1 client\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',100,'AURORA-642','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-642\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"aurora job inspect calls print_out() incorrectly\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',101,'AURORA-613','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-613\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Implement job update logic\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Implement logic in the scheduler to execute rolling job updates.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',102,'AURORA-614','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-614\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Include information about updates in the scheduler UI\", \"assignee\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Some initial thoughts:- replace the currently-hacked progress bar with a real progress bar indicating how far along an update is (note: job configuration discrepancies should still be displayed however)- when viewing a job show update history- create a new page that shows all in-progress updats\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',103,'AURORA-495','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-495\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Suman Karumuri\", \"summary\": \"UI should always show a pending reason\", \"assignee\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Suman Karumuri\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"The pending reason in the UI is empty which leaves the user confused. The scheduler should be updated to always show a reason for pending the task.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',104,'AURORA-615','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-615\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Update aurora client to use job update RPCs\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Delete client code that orchestrates job updates and instead use the scheduler RPCs to do the same.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',105,'AURORA-717','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-717\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Store new task configuration in JobUpdateConfiguration as InstanceTaskConfig\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Convert these fields in JobUpdateConfiguration:{noformat}  /** Desired TaskConfig when the update completes. */  2: TaskConfig newTaskConfig  /** Desired instance count when the update completes. */  3: i32 instanceCount{noformat}to:{noformat}  2: InstanceTaskConfig newTaskConfig{noformat}This allows us to use {{set<Range>}} for the new task configurations and expose only the work required for a job update.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',106,'AURORA-714','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-714\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Remove 30sec wait from host_drain command\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This has been a \\\"pseudo-SLA\\\" delay to make sure hosts are not drained too fast. Now that we have a real SLA checks in place this delay is no longer needed.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',107,'AURORA-666','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-666\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Aurora job status --write-json does not convert status values\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"When using --write-json with {{aurora job status}} the status fields are not converted to literals:{noformat}  \\\"inactive\\\": [      {        \\\"status\\\": 3        \\\"assignedTask\\\": {          \\\"task\\\": {            \\\"isService\\\": 0{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',108,'AURORA-669','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-669\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Thermos runner collect_updates() gets stuck in a while loop when timeout is 0\", \"assignee\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"The following code in runner.py:collect_update() may result in an infinite while loop when the provided timeout is passed as 0:{noformat} while True:       ...        if timeout and total_time >= timeout:          break       ...{noformat}We have observed a case when the thermos runner gets stuck in a \\\"deadlocked\\\" state not reacting to SIGTERM with the last message in __main__.log as:{noformat}D0827 15:35:26.022495 30886 runner.py:856] Run loop: Work to be done within 0.0s{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',109,'AURORA-313','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-313\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bjoern Metzdorf\", \"summary\": \"Add variable min offer jitter time window so Aurora can decline offers faster\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bjoern Metzdorf\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The jitter time defining the upper bound of a random time window that gets added to {{min_offer_hold_time}} is currently hard coded to 5 minutes.This makes Aurora sit on resource offers very long and it starves other schedulers.The jitter time should be configurable so Aurora can decline offers faster.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',110,'AURORA-369','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-369\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Create a REST-like interface to aurora\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 5, \"description\": \"For ease of scripting it would be nice if a client could interact with the scheduler over a HTTP/JSON interface (REST-like but not necessarily REST).  We technically have this now using TJSONProtocol but the format is not human-friendly since it uses field IDs rather than names.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',111,'AURORA-458','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-458\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Web interface has become slow especially the job page\", \"assignee\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 7, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The web interface is noticeably more sluggish since the revamp.  This is most noticeable for large jobs where the job page may display a blank page for several seconds before showing anything useful.  We need to adapt the API to reduce the amount of data fetched to render these pages.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 7, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',112,'AURORA-579','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-579\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Jake Farrell\", \"summary\": \"Upgrading Mesos version from 0.18.0 to 0.19.0\", \"assignee\": \"Dominic Hamon\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jake Farrell\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',113,'AURORA-658','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-658\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"alexius ludeman\", \"summary\": \"unable to run scheduler without mesos infrastructure for development\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"alexius ludeman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"now that IsolatedSchedulerModule is removed in https://reviews.apache.org/r/20648/ there is no [easy] way to run the scheduler under Intellij IDEA(or similar) without mesos infrastructure.The IsolatedSchedulerModule was a huge nicety for doing development work and simulating codes paths without the overhead of configuring/running mesos itself.There should still be an equivalent option.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',114,'AURORA-679','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-679\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade jetty\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We\'re currently using a Jetty version from the 6.x series which reached end of life in 2010 \\\\[1\\\\].  In addition to moving to a supported/stable Jetty release Jetty 7 gives us the ability to rewrite HTTP requests which will be necessary to satisfy AURORA-678 for the single page angular app.\\\\[1\\\\] http://wiki.eclipse.org/Jetty/Starting/Porting_to_Jetty_7\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',115,'AURORA-683','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-683\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"vagrant up fails due to missing box ubuntu/trusty64\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"{noformat}$ vagrant upBringing machine \'devcluster\' up with \'virtualbox\' provider...There are errors in the configuration of this machine. Please fixthe following errors and try again:vm:* The box \'ubuntu/trusty64\' could not be found.{noformat}Appears to be caused by this change:{noformat}$ git show 467bc56049cc775eaf61520a464b363d44023024 Vagrantfilecommit 467bc56049cc775eaf61520a464b363d44023024Author: Joe Smith <yasumoto7@gmail.com>Date:   Wed Sep 3 15:55:17 2014 -0700    Increment Mesos version to 0.20.0        Bugs closed: AURORA-674        Reviewed at https://reviews.apache.org/r/25208/diff --git a/Vagrantfile b/Vagrantfileindex c8cb2d4..ea0b252 100644--- a/Vagrantfile+++ b/Vagrantfile@@ -1811 +187 @@ VAGRANTFILE_API_VERSION = \\\"2\\\"  Vagrant.configure(VAGRANTFILE_API_VERSION) do |config|-  config.vm.box = \\\"precise64\\\"--  # The url from where the \'config.vm.box\' box will be fetched if it-  # doesn\'t already exist on the user\'s system.-  config.vm.box_url = \\\"http://files.vagrantup.com/precise64.box\\\"+  config.vm.box = \\\"ubuntu/trusty64\\\"    config.vm.define \\\"devcluster\\\" do |dev|     dev.vm.network :private_network ip: \\\"192.168.33.7\\\"{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',116,'AURORA-694','26','{\"key\": \"AURORA-694\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 26, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"When MemStorage is layered over DbStorage SQL is not transactioned\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Noticed this when a {{JdbcSQLException}} bubbled out of a database call in a unit test which should not happen if all calls go through the {{@Transactional}} methods in {{DbStorage}}.  Closer inspection reveals that {{MemStorage}} delegates operations to {{@Delegated}} \'table\' implementations but does not delegate in a way that database transactions are used.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',117,'AURORA-585','39','{\"key\": \"AURORA-585\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 39, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bhuvaneswaran A\", \"summary\": \"aurora/thermos test failure on py26 due to pex\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Bhuvaneswaran A\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 4, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 7, \"description\": \"The target {{./pants src/test/python:all -vxs}} fail because valid pex is not built. Refer to attached log for verbose output.{code}[bhuvan@build incubator-aurora]$ ./build-support/pex.venv/bin/pexTraceback (most recent call last):  File \\\"./build-support/pex.venv/bin/pex\\\" line 5 in <module>    from pkg_resources import load_entry_point  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 2876 in <module>    working_set = WorkingSet._build_master()  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 449 in _build_master    ws.require(__requires__)  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 745 in require    needed = self.resolve(parse_requirements(requirements))  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 639 in resolve    raise DistributionNotFound(req)pkg_resources.DistributionNotFound: argparse{code}The fix is to explicitly install this library.{code}./build-support/pex.venv/bin/pip install argparse==1.2.1{code}We should fix pants to include this library as one of dependent when it build the pex of pex.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 13, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('Aurora',118,'AURORA-175','39','{\"key\": \"AURORA-175\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 39, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"summary\": \"thermos runner should discriminate failures using exit status\", \"assignee\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We do the correct thing on the executor side when there is a configuration/interpolation problem (report FAILURE.)On the thermos_runner side we don\'t exit with a separate exit status for bad configuration nor do we even pay attention to the exit status from the thermos executor.  So when the runner exits unexpectedly that\'s always treated as a LOST.  Instead there should be a contract between the thermos_runner and thermos_executor about certain classes of failures indicated by exit statuses so that we can differentiate between legit LOST and FAILURE for example if the user no longer exists on the box.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',119,'AURORA-728','39','{\"key\": \"AURORA-728\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 39, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Stephan Erb\", \"summary\": \"Executor does not handle announcer errors properly\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Stephan Erb\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"Failures in the announcer lead to mesos and aurora running out of sync.Consider the following stacktrace:{code}Traceback (most recent call last):  File \\\"/root/.pex/install/twitter.common.exceptions-0.3.0-py2-none-any.whl.aa74e2e8535b1ea39bf9512cf70dba3e5aea7b1b/twitter.common.exceptions-0.3.0-py2-none-any.whl/twitter/common/exceptions/__init__.py\\\" line 126 in _excepting_run    self.__real_run(*args **kw)  File \\\"/root/.pex/install/twitter.common.concurrent-0.3.0-py2-none-any.whl.3c9a3bf0ac76acff13a6803a37138bc9f18e54c7/twitter.common.concurrent-0.3.0-py2-none-any.whl/twitter/common/concurrent/deferred.py\\\" line 43 in run    self._closure()  File \\\"/opt/thermos/bin/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/aurora_executor.py\\\" line 258 in <lambda>  File \\\"/opt/thermos/bin/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/aurora_executor.py\\\" line 121 in _run  File \\\"/opt/thermos/bin/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/aurora_executor.py\\\" line 161 in _start_status_manager  File \\\"/opt/thermos/bin/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/common/announcer.py\\\" line 74 in from_assigned_task  File \\\"/opt/thermos/bin/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/common/announcer.py\\\" line 100 in make_serverset  File \\\"/root/.pex/install/kazoo-1.3.1-py2-none-any.whl.261c1cd5b2337063b238f0c52eeed45a1df90891/kazoo-1.3.1-py2-none-any.whl/kazoo/client.py\\\" line 475 in start    raise self.handler.timeout_exception(\\\"Connection time-out\\\")kazoo.handlers.threading.TimeoutError: Connection time-out{code}*Current behaviour:* The executor dies. Mesos considers the task as RUNNING whereas aurora will eventually consider the task as LOST.*Expected behaviour:* The executor catches the exception and dispatches TASK_LOST or TASK_FAILED\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 6, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',120,'AURORA-678','39','{\"key\": \"AURORA-678\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 39, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Serve static HTTP assets out of a classpath directory\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Static asset registration with our HTTP server is somewhat complicated requiring a manual mapping to be made from the request to match and the classpath entry to serve.  Jetty has built-in support for serving static assets out of a directory on the classpath which would reduce all of our asset binding code to a few lines.  It also opens the doors to easy extension of the web interface at runtime by adding to the classpath and would also reduce iteration time when developing the web interface.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',121,'AURORA-722','39','{\"key\": \"AURORA-722\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 39, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"snapshot performance issues\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"In one of our larger production clusters we\'re seeing issues with snapshot performance that cause the scheduler to failover before completing a snapshot.For background the scheduler writes a compressed (when -deflate_snapshots is enabled) binary-encoded Snapshot (from api.thrift) to the mesos replicated log every hour (or -dlog_snapshot_interval). This snapshot represents most of the scheduler\'s heap usage including the configuration for all tasks running in the cluster.Add appropriate instrumentation to the snapshot routine and patch any obvious performance bottlenecks.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',122,'AURORA-742','39','{\"key\": \"AURORA-742\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 39, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Add client commands to query server-driven updates.\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',123,'AURORA-780','39','{\"key\": \"AURORA-780\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 39, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"python checkstyle looks at 3rdparty\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When attempting to commit https://reviews.apache.org/r/25835/ I was blocked by Python checkstyle as the rename of checked-in bootstrap test files (some written in python) was picked up.{noformat}T401:ERROR   3rdparty/javascript/scheduler/assets/bower_components/bootstrap/test-infra/s3_cache.py:002 From import must import names in lexical order.     |from __future__ import absolute_import unicode_literals print_function divisionT401:ERROR   3rdparty/javascript/scheduler/assets/bower_components/bootstrap/test-infra/s3_cache.py:005 From import must import names in lexical order.     |from os import environ stat remove as _delete_fileT401:ERROR   3rdparty/javascript/scheduler/assets/bower_components/bootstrap/test-infra/s3_cache.py:006 From import must import names in lexical order.     |from os.path import isfile dirname basename abspathT405:ERROR   3rdparty/javascript/scheduler/assets/bower_components/bootstrap/test-infra/s3_cache.py:004 Import block starting here contains imports from multiple module types: stdlib 3rdparty.     |from sys import argvT100:ERROR   3rdparty/javascript/scheduler/assets/bower_components/bootstrap/test-infra/s3_cache.py:018 Indentation of 4 instead of 2     |    BUCKET_NAME = environ[\'TWBS_S3_BUCKET\']T100:ERROR   3rdparty/javascript/scheduler/assets/bower_components/bootstrap/test-infra/s3_cache.py:020 Indentat