"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Extract complex gradle tasks from build.gradle\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Prime candidates:- thrift codegen task- custom jacoco output parsingContext:http://www.gradle.org/docs/current/userguide/custom_tasks.html\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',145,'AURORA-839','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-839\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Add documentation describing the scheduler\'s storage system\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"The storage system in the scheduler is the most complicated part of the system and pretty unapproachable for new developers.  Some details will help acquaint people with the different moving pieces involved.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',146,'AURORA-763','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-763\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"summary\": \"Document how to use the new asynchronous updater feature\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We should document how the new async update works. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',147,'AURORA-830','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-830\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"Make Executor Overhead Configurable\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently the overhead allocated for executors is hard coded into the {{ResourceSlot}} class. This should be changed so the overhead is taken from a command line flag. This is necessary so users can choose the impact executor overhead had on their cluster.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',148,'AURORA-585','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-585\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bhuvaneswaran A\", \"summary\": \"aurora/thermos test failure on py26 due to pex\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Bhuvaneswaran A\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 4, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 7, \"description\": \"The target {{./pants src/test/python:all -vxs}} fail because valid pex is not built. Refer to attached log for verbose output.{code}[bhuvan@build incubator-aurora]$ ./build-support/pex.venv/bin/pexTraceback (most recent call last):  File \\\"./build-support/pex.venv/bin/pex\\\" line 5 in <module>    from pkg_resources import load_entry_point  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 2876 in <module>    working_set = WorkingSet._build_master()  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 449 in _build_master    ws.require(__requires__)  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 745 in require    needed = self.resolve(parse_requirements(requirements))  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/projects/mesos/incubator-aurora/build-support/pex.venv/lib/python2.6/site-packages/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 639 in resolve    raise DistributionNotFound(req)pkg_resources.DistributionNotFound: argparse{code}The fix is to explicitly install this library.{code}./build-support/pex.venv/bin/pip install argparse==1.2.1{code}We should fix pants to include this library as one of dependent when it build the pex of pex.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 13, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('Aurora',149,'AURORA-440','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-440\", \"votes\": 2, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Document cron\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',150,'AURORA-175','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-175\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"summary\": \"thermos runner should discriminate failures using exit status\", \"assignee\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We do the correct thing on the executor side when there is a configuration/interpolation problem (report FAILURE.)On the thermos_runner side we don\'t exit with a separate exit status for bad configuration nor do we even pay attention to the exit status from the thermos executor.  So when the runner exits unexpectedly that\'s always treated as a LOST.  Instead there should be a contract between the thermos_runner and thermos_executor about certain classes of failures indicated by exit statuses so that we can differentiate between legit LOST and FAILURE for example if the user no longer exists on the box.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',151,'AURORA-728','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-728\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Stephan Erb\", \"summary\": \"Executor does not handle announcer errors properly\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Stephan Erb\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"Failures in the announcer lead to mesos and aurora running out of sync.Consider the following stacktrace:{code}Traceback (most recent call last):  File \\\"/root/.pex/install/twitter.common.exceptions-0.3.0-py2-none-any.whl.aa74e2e8535b1ea39bf9512cf70dba3e5aea7b1b/twitter.common.exceptions-0.3.0-py2-none-any.whl/twitter/common/exceptions/__init__.py\\\" line 126 in _excepting_run    self.__real_run(*args **kw)  File \\\"/root/.pex/install/twitter.common.concurrent-0.3.0-py2-none-any.whl.3c9a3bf0ac76acff13a6803a37138bc9f18e54c7/twitter.common.concurrent-0.3.0-py2-none-any.whl/twitter/common/concurrent/deferred.py\\\" line 43 in run    self._closure()  File \\\"/opt/thermos/bin/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/aurora_executor.py\\\" line 258 in <lambda>  File \\\"/opt/thermos/bin/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/aurora_executor.py\\\" line 121 in _run  File \\\"/opt/thermos/bin/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/aurora_executor.py\\\" line 161 in _start_status_manager  File \\\"/opt/thermos/bin/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/common/announcer.py\\\" line 74 in