w of https://reviews.apache.org/r/24264 as well.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',160,'AURORA-788','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-788\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"GC executor doesn\'t need to exit after period of inactivity\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The GC Executor is currently configured to exit after a hardcoded limit of activity since it processed a launchTask request. This causes needless task churn in the cluster especially given that the scheduler\'s default launch interval will cause the executor to need to be relaunched on average every 15 minutes.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',161,'AURORA-751','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-751\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Remove SANDBOX_DELETED task state\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Given the upcoming GC deprecation remove SANDBOX_DELETED state from the TaskStateMachine. It was only used to correctly drive the scheduler UI.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',162,'AURORA-786','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-786\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Client does not log Response.messageDEPRECATED errors\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The implementation of context.py:log_response() checks only the new {{details}} field but not the old {{messageDEPRECATED}} one. This leads to ignoring unhandled updater errors wrapped into a synthetic Response object:{noformat}...log(info): Cleaning upError: Update failed; see log for details.log(info): Error executing command: Update failed; see log for details.Error executing command: Update failed; see log for details.{noformat}The \\\"Update failed; see log for details.\\\" message is misleading as there will be nothing in the log in this case.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',163,'AURORA-363','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-363\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"summary\": \"the new pants selects 2.6.x by default if it\'s available\", \"assignee\": \"Joe Smith\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The new pants finds all the python interpreters on the path and selects the minimum version that is compatible with it.  Previous behavior would use sys.executable (the current interpreter) which is more desirable.  We should update pants invocations so that we select the current interpreter or at least CPython>=2.7<3\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',164,'AURORA-748','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-748\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Burg\", \"summary\": \"Help command is broken\", \"assignee\": \"Joe Smith\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Burg\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"$ aurora2.pex help update startlog(ERROR): Unknown error: sequence item 24: expected string instancemethod foundlog(ERROR): Unknown error: sequence item 24: expected string instancemethod foundThis also happens for `help update pause`.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',165,'AURORA-781','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-781\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Fix bind parameter processing in client\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"In client commands there are two problems involving pystachio bindings:(1) Binding parameters sometimes don\'t work correctly;(2) If a binding never gets resolved an error isn\'t generated.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',166,'AURORA-142','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-142\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 2, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Suman Karumuri\", \"summary\": \"Remove getVersion API from client\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Suman Karumuri\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 2, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 3, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The getVersion RPC has been deprecated in favor of the Response.serverInfo field.  Change the client to stop using getVersion.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',167,'AURORA-333','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-333\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"summary\": \"finish all deprecations in schema/base.py\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"There are currently a number of deprecations listed in src/main/python/apache/aurora/config/schema/base.pycron_policydaemonhealth_check_interval_secsand a number of other structs that should be removed:recipesPacker\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',168,'AURORA-504','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-504\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Chengwei Yang\", \"summary\": \"there should be a section to describe how to clone git repo in howtocontribute page\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Chengwei Yang\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The aurora how to contirbue guide here http://aurora.incubator.apache.org/docs/howtocontribute/says not a lot of useful information for example even not a section to describe where to find the latest code.It may confusing people who try to find latest code at this page and then follow other doc to build-deploy.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',169,'AURORA-770','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-770\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"V2 client logs HTTP connections to info\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"I see this with all v2 client commands:{noformat}log(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): 192.168.33.7log(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): 192.168.33.7{noformat}Presumably these should be debug-level log messages.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',170,'AURORA-801','42','{\"key\": \"AURORA-801\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 42, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"deadlock in scheduler startup\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The recently-added update code adds a deadlock to the scheduler whenever there are concurrent {{SchedulerActive}} and {{TasksDeleted}} events on the EventBus.Relevant bits from /threads{noformat}Name: AsyncProcessor-0State: BLOCKEDDaemon: trueID: 2461    org.apache.aurora.scheduler.updater.JobUpdateEventSubscriber.tasksDeleted(JobUpdateEventSubscriber.java:64)    sun.reflect.NativeMethodAccessorImpl.invoke0(Native Method)    sun.reflect.NativeMethodAccessorImpl.invoke(NativeMethodAccessorImpl.java:57)    sun.reflect.DelegatingMethodAccessorImpl.invoke(DelegatingMethodAccessorImpl.java:43)    java.lang.reflect.Method.invoke(Method.java:606)    com.google.common.eventbus.EventSubscriber.handleEvent(EventSubscriber.java:74)    com.google.common.eventbus.SynchronizedEventSubscriber.handleEvent(SynchronizedEventSubscriber.java:47)    com.google.common.eventbus.EventBus.dispatch(EventBus.java:322)    com.google.common.eventbus.EventBus.dispatchQueuedEvents(EventBus.java:304)    com.google.common.eventbus.EventBus.post(EventBus.java:275)    org.apache.aurora.scheduler.events.PubsubEventModule$2.post(PubsubEventModule.java:68)    org.apache.aurora.sc