est::test_update_instances_wait_for_batch_completion_filled_batch\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"See https://builds.apache.org/job/Aurora/676/console\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',187,'AURORA-248','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-248\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Use Mock with specs in client tests\", \"assignee\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"While investigating AURORA-247 figured out that none of our tests is capable of catching unknown options due to spec-less way options are mocked. Use Mock(spec=[\'option1\' \'option2\' ...]) instead of Mock() everywhere in client tests to prevent issues like AURORA-247. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',188,'AURORA-72','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-72\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Improve root README.md\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"README.md is the first thing many prospective contributors will see when viewing the source code as well as the first thing many users will automatically jump to. Update it to be more helpful possibly merge with docs/README.md\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',189,'AURORA-825','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-825\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Cron tasks don\'t check quota when launched\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"We don\'t check production quota when a cron task is launched by the CronJobManager. This leaves a potential to temporarily exceed allocated quota if prod consumption grew close to the limit _after_ a cron job was created. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 13, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',190,'AURORA-886','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-886\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"aurora job create --wait-until should exit with error code if the job being waited on fails\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"If I invoke:aurora job create --wait-until=FINISHED ...and the job being waited on fails I think the aurora command should exit with an error code or should at least have the option to print something formatted that can be parsed.I\'m not sure what the current thinking on exit codes is I would understand the argument that even if the job failed the aurora client did it\'s job without error. So I\'d be happy with any way of detecting job failure (exit code or otherwise).\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',191,'AURORA-863','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-863\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 2, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"provision-dev-cluster.sh refers to mesos egg instead of mesos.native\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 2, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"This makes the executor fail to build in the vagrant environment. We were apparently depending on the mesos.native egg on pypi which was removed in MESOS-1898\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',192,'AURORA-627','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-627\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bhuvaneswaran A\", \"summary\": \"use latest psutil library for thermos in pants\", \"assignee\": \"Joe Smith\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bhuvaneswaran A\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"Unable to execute thermos due to following error. It\'s due to this bug in {{psutil}}. [issue 442|https://code.google.com/p/psutil/issues/detail?id=442]. We were using v1.1.2. We should use v1.1.3 or newer.Facing same issue with gc_executor and thermos_runner.{code}./dist/thermos_executor.pex                                                                   [latest] 18:30:53Traceback (most recent call last):  File \\\"/Volumes/apple/quark/incubator-aurora/dist/thermos_executor.pex/.bootstrap/_twitter_common_python/pex.py\\\" line 225 in execute    self.execute_interpreter()  File \\\"/usr/lib64/python2.6/contextlib.py\\\" line 34 in __exit__    self.gen.throw(type value traceback)  File \\\"/Volumes/apple/quark/incubator-aurora/dist/thermos_executor.pex/.bootstrap/_twitter_common_python/pex.py\\\" line 175 in patch_pkg_resources    yield  File \\\"/Volumes/apple/quark/incubator-aurora/dist/thermos_executor.pex/.bootstrap/_twitter_common_python/pex.py\\\" line 223 in execute    self.execute_entry(entry_point args)  File \\\"/Volumes/apple/quark/incubator-aurora/dist/thermos_executor.pex/.bootstrap/_twitter_common_python/pex.py\\\" line 271 in execute_entry    runner(entry_point)  File \\\"/Volumes/apple/quark/incubator-aurora/dist/thermos_executor.pex/.bootstrap/_twitter_common_python/pex.py\\\" line 293 in execute_pkg_resources    runner = entry.load(require=False)  # trust that the environment is sane  File \\\"/Volumes/apple/quark/incubator-aurora/dist/thermos_executor.pex/.bootstrap/pkg_resources.py\\\" line 2048 in load    entry = __import__(self.module_name globals()globals() [\'__name__\'])  File \\\"/Volumes/apple/quark/incubator-aurora/dist/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/bin/thermos_executor_main.py\\\" line 31 in <module>  File \\\"/Volumes/apple/quark/incubator-aurora/dist/thermos_executor.pex/apache/aurora/executor/thermos_task_runner.py\\\" line 31 in <module>  File \\\"/Volumes/apple/quark/incubator-aurora/dist/thermos_executor.pex/apache/thermos/core/runner.py\\\" line 70 in <module>  File \\\"/Volumes/apple/quark/incubator-aurora/dist/thermos_executor.pex/apache/thermos/core/helper.py\\\" line 21 in <module>  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/.pex/install/psutil-1.1.2-cp26-none-linux_x86_64.whl.a1805e756711e817e309c89cedf92d2a070c3ee7/psutil-1.1.2-cp26-none-linux_x86_64.whl/psutil/__init__.py\\\" line 89 in <module>    import psutil._pslinux as _psplatform  File \\\"/home/bhuvan/.pex/install/psutil-1.1.2-cp26-none-linux_x86_64.whl.a1805e756711e817e309c89cedf92d2a070c3ee7/psutil-1.1.2-cp26-none-linux_x86_64.whl/psutil/_pslinux.py\\\" line 21 in <module>    import _psutil_linuxImportError: /home/bhuvan/.pex/install/psutil-1.1.2-cp26-none-linux_x86_64.whl.a1805e756711e817e309c89cedf92d2a070c3ee7/psutil-1.1.2-cp26-none-linux_x86_64.whl/_psutil_linux.so: undefined symbol: prlimit{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',193,'AURORA-779','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-779\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"v2 client has worse error message than v1\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Copied from a user report at Twitter:I had a typo in an aurora config where I was resolving a mustache variable outside of a string:{code}instances = {{profile.instances}}{code}where I should have been doing{code}instances = \\\"{{profile.instances}}\\\"{code}The error message on the v2 client was:{quote}Error executing command: Error loading configuration: name \'profile\' is not defined{quote}The v1 client gave me a line number:{quote}  File \\\"router.aurora\\\" line 90 in <module>    instances = {{profile.instances}}NameError: name \'profile\' is not defined{quote}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 10, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',194,'AURORA-833','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-833\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Extract complex gradle tasks from build.gradle\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Prime candidates:- thrift codegen task- custom jacoco output parsingContext:http://www.gradle.org/docs/current/userguide/custom_tasks.html\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',195,'AURORA-824','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-824\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"scheduleCronJob does not check quota or task limits\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The scheduleCronJob RPC should call validateTaskLimits() and checkQuota().\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',196,'AURORA-498','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-498\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"test_end_to_end.sh uses stale aurora client\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"While working on a parallel updater noticed that running test_end_to_end.sh does not rebuild aurora client resulting in a potentially invalid run.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',197,'AURORA-839','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-839\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Add documentation describing the scheduler\'s storage system\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"The storage system in the scheduler is the most complicated part of the system and pretty unapproachable for new developers.  Some details will help acquaint people with the different moving pieces involved.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',198,'AURORA-763','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-763\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"summary\": \"Document how to use the new asynchronous updater feature\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We should document how the new async update works. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',199,'AURORA-830','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-830\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"Make Executor Overhead Configurable\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently the overhead allocated for executors is hard coded into the {{ResourceSlot}} class. This should be changed so the overhead is taken from a command line flag. This is necessary so users can choose the impact executor overhead had on their cluster.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',200,'AURORA-888','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-888\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Update client documentation to reflect the shift to clientv2.\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',201,'AURORA-476','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-476\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Run vagrant-based tests regularly\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Our end-to-end tests offer a decent amount of integration test coverage and sometimes manage to catch issues that our unit test suites otherwise do not.  It would be awesome to run these in Jenkins perhaps on AWS.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',202,'AURORA-885','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-885\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Improve lock held message in client output\", \"assignee\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When a user tries to kill a job that\'s locked by an in-progress/failed update the error message is confusing. It should clearly state that the problem is an update lock and how to release that lock.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',203,'AURORA-874','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-874\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"Make clientv2 job status include a header line for tasks like v1.\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Clientv2 status shows information in a different form than v1 and deliberately ommitted some information. However users have complained about that information being missing and some tests were written to depend on its presence.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',204,'AURORA-875','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-875\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Update Aurora to depend on mesos 0.20.1\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',205,'AURORA-877','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-877\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Build fails if thrift cannot be downloaded\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Recently failed: https://builds.apache.org/job/Aurora/669{noformat}:bootstrapThriftgzip: stdin: not in gzip formattar: Child returned status 1tar: Error is not recoverable: exiting nowmake: *** [thrift-0.9.1/compiler/cpp/thrift] Error 2 FAILED{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('Aurora',206,'AURORA-84','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-84\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Deprecate the Identity struct\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 6, \"description\": \"The Identity field is nested in several structs and the {{role}} field it contains is ~always redundant to a field in {{JobKey}}. Consider removing Identity and using (or adding) a non-user-bearing field like JobKey.An open question is whether whether {{Identity.user}} should be retained.  Most likely yes.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 29, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',207,'AURORA-878','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-878\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"Cache Host Attributes along Offer\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"At a large production cluster [~wfarner] and I have noticed that a lot of time is spent reading from the attribute store during scheduling. This is because when scheduling tasks we need to check the attributes of the slave before accepting an offer. We do this to compute diversity constraints.We can prevent frequent reading from the attribute store in this process by caching attributes alongside the offers. That way when we get an offer from a slave we can check the diversity constraints without reading from the AttributeStore.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',208,'AURORA-880','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-880\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"Add some wiggle room when requiring min coverage be raised\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"There are apparently differences in the calculation between local and jenkins builds to reduce build flakiness we should account for this.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',209,'AURORA-887','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-887\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"\\\"aurora job create --open-browser\\\" fails with error.\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When calling \\\"aurora job create\\\" with the \\\"--open-browser\\\" flag it fails with:{noformat}Internal error executing command: \'AnnotatedAuroraConfig\' object has no attribute \'env\'{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',210,'AURORA-883','46','{\"key\": \"AURORA-883\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 46, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Create a utility that provides early CI feedback on code reviews\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We can keep our build green and make life easier for committers and reviewers alike by giving review-time feedback on unit test results.  This will make it more difficult for changes to sneak in that didn\'t run all the tests or code quality checks.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',211,'AURORA-782','46'