ary.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',215,'AURORA-914','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-914\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Instrument task scheduling pipeline\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need a better instrumentation of the task scheduling loop to helps us troubleshoot scheduling performance problems. Specifically:- Add {{@Timed}} in TaskScheduler.schedule() (inside the write lock)- Add {{@Timed}} in OfferQueue.launchFirst()- Add {{@Timed}} for every iteration of the OfferQueue.launchFirst() loop- Differentiate between \\\"static\\\" (e.g.: resource shortage) vs. \\\"dynamic\\\" (e.g.: constraint mismatch) Vetos and add a counter to track each Veto type.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',216,'AURORA-923','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-923\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"Run verb does not return an exit code.\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The run verb of the task noun does not return an exit code. This results in log messages like:{noformat}log(info): Command terminated with error code None{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',217,'AURORA-882','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-882\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"CI broken due to UpdaterTest::test_update_instances_wait_for_batch_completion_filled_batch\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"See https://builds.apache.org/job/Aurora/676/console\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',218,'AURORA-912','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-912\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Scheduler cannot read PruneJobUpdateHistory log operations\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"AURORA-743 added support for reading PruneJobUpdateHistory log operations but no support exists for reading them.  At this time the default behavior of the scheduler is to fail when encountering unknown log operation types.https://reviews.apache.org/r/27538/ was added as a short-term fix for this but it\'s apparent that job update history pruning support is incomplete without the ability to read these operations.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',219,'AURORA-889','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-889\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"aurora2 beta-update list is broken\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Subcommand always fails with:{noformat}$ aurora2 beta-update list devclusterFatal error running command; traceback can be found in /home/vagrant/.aurora/errors/aurora-1414084327.error-logvagrant@192:~$ cat /home/vagrant/.aurora/errors/aurora-1414084327.error-logERROR LOG: command arguments = [\'beta-update\' \'list\' \'devcluster\']Traceback (most recent call last):  File \\\"/usr/local/bin/aurora2/apache/aurora/client/cli/__init__.py\\\" line 406 in _execute    result = noun.execute(context)  File \\\"/usr/local/bin/aurora2/apache/aurora/client/cli/__init__.py\\\" line 515 in execute    return self.verbs[context.options.verb].execute(context)  File \\\"/usr/local/bin/aurora2/apache/aurora/client/cli/update.py\\\" line 182 in execute    update_statuses=context.options.status)TypeError: query_job_updates() got an unexpected keyword argument \'jobKey\'{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',220,'AURORA-793','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-793\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Client prints redundant messages\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 3, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The client has a tendency to print the same message multiple times:Job configuration does not exist:{noformat}$ aurora2 job create -v devcluster/www-data/devel/not_here /vagrant/hello_world.auroralog(info): Error executing command: Error loading configuration: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: \'/vagrant/hello_world.aurora\'log(info): Error executing command: Error loading configuration: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: \'/vagrant/hello_world.aurora\'Error executing command: Error loading configuration: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: \'/vagrant/hello_world.aurora\'{noformat}Job already exists:{noformat}$ aurora2 job create -v devcluster/www-data/devel/hello_world /vagrant/hello_world.auroralog(info): Creating job hello_worldlog(info): Creating job hello_worldlog(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64log(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64log(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64log(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64log(info): Message from scheduler: Job already exists: www-data/devel/hello_worldlog(info): Message from scheduler: Job already exists: www-data/devel/hello_worldjob create failed because job not foundlog(info): Error executing command: Job not foundlog(info): Error executing command: Job not foundError executing command: Job not found{noformat}Referenced job name does not exist:{noformat}$ aurora2 job create -v devcluster/www-data/devel/not_here /vagrant/hello_world.auroralog(info): Error executing command: Error loading configuration: Could not find job devcluster/www-data/devel/not_hereCandidates are:  devcluster/www-data/devel/hello_worldlog(info): Error executing command: Error loading configuration: Could not find job devcluster/www-data/devel/not_hereCandidates are:  devcluster/www-data/devel/hello_worldError executing command: Error loading configuration: Could not find job devcluster/www-data/devel/not_hereCandidates are:  devcluster/www-data/devel/hello_world{noformat}Python error in job configuration:{noformat}$ aurora2 job create -v devcluster/www-data/devel/not_here /vagrant/hello_world.auroralog(info): Error executing command: Error loading configuration: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: \'/vagrant/hello_world.py\'log(info): Error executing command: Error loading configuration: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: \'/vagrant/hello_world.py\'Error executing command: Error loading configuration: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: \'/vagrant/hello_world.py\'{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',221,'AURORA-248','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-248\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Use Mock with specs in client tests\", \"assignee\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"While investigating AURORA-247 figured out that none of our tests is capable of catching unknown options due to spec-less way options are mocked. Use Mock(spec=[\'option1\' \'option2\' ...]) instead of Mock() everywhere in client tests to prevent issues like AURORA-247. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',222,'AURORA-72','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-72\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Improve root README.md\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"README.md is the first thing many prospective contributors will see when viewing the source code as well as the first thing many users will automatically jump to. Update it to be more helpful possibly merge with docs/README.md\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',223,'AURORA-825','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-825\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Cron tasks don\'t check quota when launched\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"We don\'t check production quota when a cron task is launched by the CronJobManager. This leaves a potential to temporarily exceed allocated quota if prod consumption grew close to the limit _after_ a cron job was created. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 13, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',224,'AURORA-886','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-886\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"summary\": \"aurora job create --wait-until should exit with error code if the job being waited on fails\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mark Chu-Carroll\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"If I invoke:aurora job create --wait-until=FINISHED ...and the job being waited on fails I think the aurora command should exit with an error code or should at least have the option to print something formatted that can be parsed.I\'m not sure what the current thinking on exit codes is I would understand the argument that even if the job failed the aurora client did it\'s job without error. So I\'d be happy with any way of detecting job failure (exit code or otherwise).\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',225,'AURORA-865','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-865\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joe Smith\", \"summary\": \"IOError on aurora job status\", \"assignee\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Joe Smith\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"{noformat}[jsmith@atla-bgy-37-sr2 ~]$ cat /var/lib/jenkins/.aurora/errors/None-1413508980.error-logERROR LOG: command arguments = [\'job\' \'status\' \'atla/jenkins/test/flask_example\']Traceback (most recent call last):  File \\\"dist/aurora2.pex/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1413507664-py2.7.egg/apache/aurora/client/cli/__init__.py\\\" line 406 in _execute    result = noun.execute(context)  File \\\"dist/aurora2.pex/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1413507664-py2.7.egg/apache/aurora/client/cli/__init__.py\\\" line 515 in execute    return self.verbs[context.options.verb].execute(context)  File \\\"dist/aurora2.pex/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1413507664-py2.7.egg/apache/aurora/client/cli/jobs.py\\\" line 637 in execute    context.print_out(result)  File \\\"dist/aurora2.pex/.deps/apache.aurora.clientv2-0.5.1_DEV1413507664-py2.7.egg/apache/aurora/client/cli/__init__.py\\\" line 145 in print_out    print(\\\"%s%s\\\" % (indent_str line))IOError: [Errno 32] Broken pipe{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',226,'AURORA-859','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-859\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"\\\"No tasks to kill\\\" message is not surfaced to user in v2\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"{noformat}vagrant@vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64:~$ aurora2 job status devcluster/www-data/test/cron_hello_worldlog(info): Checking status of devcluster/www-data/test/cron_hello_worldlog(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64log(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64Active tasks (0):Inactive tasks (7):Task:  cpus: 0.1 ram: 128 MB disk: 128 MB  events:   2014-10-16 20:20:00 PENDING: None   2014-10-16 20:20:00 ASSIGNED: None   2014-10-16 2