    package_unlock    package_unset_live    package_versions    restart    role_list    run    runtask    ssh    start_cron    status    update    versionFor more help on an individual command:    aurora help <command>aurora-client: error: no such option: --logging-levelmba=science=; {noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',229,'AURORA-857','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-857\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"aurora cron schedule should ouput url\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The client should output the URL of the newly-created cron job as it did in v1\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',230,'AURORA-456','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-456\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Jay Buffington\", \"summary\": \"\\\"aurora version\\\" command raises KeyError: \'sha\'\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jay Buffington\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"{noformat}    $ ./pants src/main/python/apache/aurora/client/bin/:aurora_client    Build operating on targets: OrderedSet([PythonBinary(src/main/python/apache/aurora/client/bin/BUILD:aurora_client)])    Building PythonBinary PythonBinary(src/main/python/apache/aurora/client/bin/BUILD:aurora_client):    Wrote /home/jaybuff/incubator-aurora/dist/aurora_client.pex    $ /home/jaybuff/incubator-aurora/dist/aurora_client.pex  version    Aurora client build info:    Traceback (most recent call last):      File \\\"/home/jaybuff/.pex/install/twitter.common.app-0.3.0-py26-none-any.whl.18b046f79e32f1c14a751fbd19fe7ac97546fb80/twitter.common.app-0.3.0-py26-none-any.whl/twitter/common/app/application.py\\\" line 738 in _wrap_method        return_code = method()      File \\\"/home/jaybuff/.pex/install/twitter.common.app-0.3.0-py26-none-any.whl.18b046f79e32f1c14a751fbd19fe7ac97546fb80/twitter.common.app-0.3.0-py26-none-any.whl/twitter/common/app/application.py\\\" line 760 in <lambda>        main = lambda: main_method(*args **kwargs)      File \\\"/home/jaybuff/incubator-aurora/dist/aurora_client.pex/apache/aurora/client/commands/core.py\\\" line 117 in version        print(\\\"\\\\tsha: %s\\\" % pex_info.build_properties[\'sha\'])    KeyError: \'sha\'{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',231,'AURORA-784','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-784\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Client reports \\\"update has started\\\" for no-op update\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When initiating a scheduler-driven update that is actually a no-op the client will print {noformat}Scheduler-driven update of job devcluster/www-data/devel/hello_world has started.{noformat}In this case the scheduler is returning a message indicating the no-op:{noformat}Job is unchanged by proposed update.{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',232,'AURORA-896','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-896\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joe Smith\", \"summary\": \"Remove client stack trace redirection\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Joe Smith\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The Aurora Client currently redirects unhandled exceptions to a log file within the user\'s homedir. [Mailing List discussion|http://mail-archives.apache.org/mod_mbox/incubator-aurora-dev/201410.mbox/%3CCAFGkSCm%2B5jJZPXmEm1%3DWNz2tSh8Ld%2BEiO2KYE6Yco%3DpB_chekQ%40mail.gmail.com%3E]In practice this has led to a bit of confusion and the level of patching required to make this work seems to be rather high- yet still does not cover all the corner cases. When [attempting to test this|https://reviews.apache.org/r/26802/] I realized it\'d be best to discard that review and instead remove this feature while we reconsider the approach in a way that won\'t interfere with our testing of the client or presenting helpful information to users.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',233,'AURORA-913','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-913\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Replace MaintenanceMode field with HostAttributes in HostOffer\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Address this TODO:{noformat}  /**   * Encapsulate an offer from a host and the host\'s maintenance mode.   */  class HostOffer {    private final Offer offer;    // TODO(wfarner): Replace this with HostAttributes for more use of this caching.    private final MaintenanceMode mode;{noformat}Success here will mean avoiding O(n) (n=num offers) fetching of host attributes associated with offers when scheduling a task.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',234,'AURORA-831','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-831\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"cron deschedule help includes ambiguous options\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Highlights include: two instances of \\\"str\\\" as options random mention of aurora_cluster_config and PROXY_ADDR even though they\'re not listed anywhere in the help?{noformat}aurora help cron descheduleUsage for verb \\\"cron deschedule\\\":  deschedule [--bind=var=value] CLUSTER/ROLE/ENV/NAMEOptions:  var=value  Bind a pystachio variable name to a value. Multiple flags may be used to specify multiple values.  CLUSTER/ROLE/ENV/NAME  Fully specified job key in CLUSTER/ROLE/ENV/NAME format  aurora_cluster_config  Cluster config file  --no-no_socks_always_proxy  Always create a proxy if no proxies are supplied.  Proxies via --tunnel_host.  PROXY_ADDR  Attempt to proxy all connections through the socks proxy at PROXY_ADDR  --socks_resolve=[\'local\' \'remote\']  LOCATION to perform DNS resolution where LOCATION is one of [\'local\' \'remote\']  str  Host to tunnel commands through (default: nest1.twitter.biz)  str  The jenkins URL to fetch jenkins artifacts (default=http://jvm-ci.twitter.biz).Remove the cron schedule for a job.{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',235,'AURORA-476','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-476\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Run vagrant-based tests regularly\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Our end-to-end tests offer a decent amount of integration test coverage and sometimes manage to catch issues that our unit test suites otherwise do not.  It would be awesome to run these in Jenkins perhaps on AWS.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',236,'AURORA-794','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-794\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Client erroneously prints \\\"Job not found\\\" when job exists\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"In this case i\'m trying to create a job that already exists.  The \'message from scheduler\' lines have the correct error but the client goes on to claim \\\"Job not found\\\".  I\'m not sure if there is really a good string for the client to make up in this case as the scheduler will have the real reason the request failed.{noformat}$ aurora2 job create -v devcluster/www-data/devel/hello_world /vagrant/hello_world.auroralog(info): Creating job hello_worldlog(info): Creating job hello_worldlog(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64log(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64log(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64log(info): Starting new HTTP connection (1): vagrant-ubuntu-trusty-64log(info): Message from scheduler: Job already exists: www-data/devel/hello_worldlog(info): Message from scheduler: Job already exists: www-data/devel/hello_worldjob create failed because job not foundlog(info): Error executing command: Job not foundlog(info): Error executing command: Job not foundError executing command: Job not found{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',237,'AURORA-766','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-766\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"summary\": \"Client should show information for update details when starting an update.\", \"assignee\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When you launch a new async-update we should show:1) the URL to the scheduler UI for tracking progress of your update.2) the command you need to run to get the state from the CLI\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',238,'AURORA-917','52','{\"key\": \"AURORA-917\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 52, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"\\\"aurora job create\\\" gives misleading error when used to create a cron job\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When attempting to create a cron job via \\\"aurora job create\\\" the client errors out with a vague error code but the job is still created:{noformat}vagrant@192:~$ aurora2 job create devcluster/vagrant/test/cron_hello_world4 aurora/examples/jobs/cron_hello_world.auroralog(info): Creating job cron_hello_world4log(info): Checking status of devcluster/vagrant/test/cron_hello_world4Error occurred while creating job devcluster/vagrant/test/cron_hello_world4log(info): Command terminated with error code 4{noformat}The V2 job create syntax should fail fast when attempted with a cron job.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"a