/vagrant/aurora/dist/apache.thermos.z8KZGZ/src/apache/thermos/cli/commands/tail.py is source but does not belong to a package.                   /home/vagrant/aurora/dist/apache.thermos.z8KZGZ/src/apache/thermos/cli/bin/thermos.py is source but does not belong to a package.               FAILUREException message: Invalid target PythonLibrary(BuildFileAddress(/home/vagrant/aurora/src/main/python/apache/thermos/BUILD thermos)): Cannot add a binary to a PythonArtifact if it does not contain an entry_point.{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',377,'AURORA-1168','100','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1168\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 100, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"beta-update list should use a hierarchy for query specifications\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"{noformat}$ aurora beta-update list -husage: aurora beta-update list [-h] [--job CLUSTER/ROLE/ENV/NAME]                               [--role ROLENAME] [--user username]                               [--status {ROLLED_BACKROLL_FORWARD_PAUSEDROLL_FORWARD_AWAITING_PULSEERRORROLLING_BACKROLLING_FORWARDROLLED_FORWARDROLL_BACK_PAUSEDFAILEDABORTEDROLL_BACK_AWAITING_PULSE}]                               [--write-json] [--verbose]                               [--skip-hooks hookhook...]                               clustername{noformat}This means that to query for updates for a specific job one must use a command like this:{noformat}$ aurora beta-update list --job devcluster/vagrant/test/http_example devcluster{noformat}In addition to being redundant this is less user-friendly than the hierarchical syntax we use in other places.I suggest we change the client to drop the job and role options and instead support commands like:{noformat}aurora beta-update list clusteraurora beta-update list cluster/roleaurora beta-update list cluster/role/envaurora beta-update list cluster/role/env/job{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',378,'AURORA-1031','100','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1031\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 100, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"summary\": \"Replace libmesos w/ Pesos\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 13.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Replace the libmesos native dependency with [Pesos|https://github.com/wickman/pesos] to simplify the build and reduce memory footprint.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',379,'AURORA-1190','100','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1190\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 100, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Add a deprecation warning when the client-side updater is used\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This feature is being deprecated in 0.8.0 removed in 0.9.0\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',380,'AURORA-1206','100','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1206\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 100, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Make update status command more versatile\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The {{aurora update status}} command is rather restrictive only showing information about in-flight updates.  This command would be more useful if it could allow the same output for arbitrary updates (which can be discovered through {{aurora update list}}.To make the name match the new behavior i propose we name this command {{info}}.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',381,'AURORA-1043','105','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1043\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 105, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"/logconfig does not work when the scheduler is behind SSL\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When the /logconfig endpoint is behind SSL the JavaScript console is filled with the following errors:{noformat} Mixed Content: The page at \'https://localhost/logconfig\' was loaded over HTTPS but requested an insecure script \'http://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/1.10.1/jquery.min.js\'. This request has been blocked; the content must be served over HTTPS.logconfig:4402 Uncaught ReferenceError: $ is not defined{noformat}As a result the endpoint does not work.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',382,'AURORA-810','105','{\"key\": \"AURORA-810\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 2, \"sprint\": 105, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"summary\": \"Add an end-to-end test case for http basic auth\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 2, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"* Simple netrc-based* Including end-to-end tests\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',383,'AURORA-812','105','{\"key\": \"AURORA-812\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 105, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"summary\": \"Wire in SPNEGO HTTP module\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Wire in SPNEGO HTTP module expose as flags in ShiroAuthModule.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',384,'AURORA-813','105','{\"key\": \"AURORA-813\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 105, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"summary\": \"Add ability to configure client to use Kerberos\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Add ability to configure client to use Kerberos (depends on AURORA-812 can be developed in parallel).\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',385,'AURORA-1158','105','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1158\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 105, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Consider finding preemption slots asynchronously \", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The current Preemptor implementation performs synchronous preemption victim search. This isn\'t necessary as resource swap cannot be performed within the same scheduling loop due to victims taking time to vacate their premises (being killed). Consider asynchronous victim search/killing instead. That will move the heavy lifting out of the critical scheduling loop and remove \\\"flat\\\" preemptor perf tax applied on every failed task scheduling/assignment.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',386,'AURORA-1187','105','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1187\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 105, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Create JobKey-scoped Permissions and apply to AuroraSchedulerManager\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"https://reviews.apache.org/r/31820/ added support for coarse-grained permissions based on the thrift API method name. Support finer-grained permissions scoped down to the jobFor example calls to{code}auroraSchedulerManager.descheduleCronJob(JobKey(role=\'ksweeney\' environment=\'prod\' name=\'download_lunch_menu\') None None){code}currently check for the {{thrift.AuroraSchedulerManager:descheduleCronJob}} Permission when they should check for the {{thrift.AuroraSchedulerManager:descheduleCronJob:ksweeney:prod:download_lunch_menu}} Permission.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',387,'AURORA-1043','112','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1043\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 112, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"/logconfig does not work when the scheduler is behind SSL\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When the /logconfig endpoint is behind SSL the JavaScript console is filled with the following errors:{noformat} Mixed Content: The page at \'https://localhost/logconfig\' was loaded over HTTPS but requested an insecure script \'http://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/1.10.1/jquery.min.js\'. This request has been blocked; the content must be served over HTTPS.logconfig:4402 Uncaught ReferenceError: $ is not defined{noformat}As a result the endpoint does not work.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',388,'AURORA-1231','112','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1231\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 112, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"summary\": \"Blocked updates missing from cluster-wide in progress view\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"In the /updates endpoint updates that are in ROLL_FORWARD_AWAITING_PULSE state are not included under in progress updates. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',389,'AURORA-817','112','{\"key\": \"AURORA-817\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 2, \"sprint\": 112, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Add documentation for HTTP basic and kerberos authentication\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 2, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"Add a new markdown page linked from {{deploying-aurora-scheduler.md}} that offers instructions for using HTTP basic authentication for the web UI and API as well as an example for integrating with kerberos.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',390,'AURORA-556','112','{\"key\": \"AURORA-556\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 112, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"H2-backed implementation of TaskStore\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This tracks behavior matching but not necessarily performance.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',391,'AURORA-1214','112','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1214\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 112, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Reevaluate \\\"max_schedule_attempts_per_sec\\\" with asynchronous preemptor\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"With step 2 of AURORA-1158 completed the preemptor is removed from the critical scheduling loop making scheduling much faster (perf comparison is available here: https://reviews.apache.org/r/32225/)Reevaluate what the {{max_schedule_attempts_per_sec}} should be now. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',392,'AURORA-1219','112','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1219\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 112, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Improve preemptor efficiency\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"While AURORA-1158 makes the preemptor asynchronous and helps scheduling loop performance it loses some preemption efficiency due to adapting the original algorithm to work asynchronously:- Preemptor repeatedly searches for preemption slots with the same ClusterState increasing the probability of victim collisions. - Slave/offer/resource mappings are redundantly recomputed for every pending task slot search.- Pending tasks are repeatedly sized up against every slave (as opposed to the other way around) making internal loop optimizations more expensive (i.e. pending task count is expected to be << slave count under normal conditions).\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',393,'AURORA-1043','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1043\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"/logconfig does not work when the scheduler is behind SSL\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When the /logconfig endpoint is behind SSL the JavaScript console is filled with the following errors:{noformat} Mixed Content: The page at \'https://localhost/logconfig\' was loaded over HTTPS but requested an insecure script \'http://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/1.10.1/jquery.min.js\'. This request has been blocked; the content must be served over HTTPS.logconfig:4402 Uncaught ReferenceError: $ is not defined{noformat}As a result the endpoint does not work.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',394,'AURORA-1311','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1311\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to latest h2 version\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We have been holding back on upgrading h2 since the latest release are labeled as beta.  As it turns out the beta marker only applies to the new default MVCC storage implementation and the developers consider the builds stable when MV_STORE is disabled \\\\[1\\\\].\\\\[1\\\\] https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/h2-database/3CDRKex_EgA\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',395,'AURORA-1277','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1277\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Create a design document for Health Checks for Updates\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',396,'AURORA-1231','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1231\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"summary\": \"Blocked updates missing from cluster-wide in progress view\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"In the /updates endpoint updates that are in ROLL_FORWARD_AWAITING_PULSE state are not included under in progress updates. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',397,'AURORA-817','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-817\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 2, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Add documentation for HTTP basic and kerberos authentication\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 2, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"Add a new markdown page linked from {{deploying-aurora-scheduler.md}} that offers instructions for using HTTP basic authentication for the web UI and API as well as an example for integrating with kerberos.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',398,'AURORA-1307','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1307\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"API hooks no longer supported for certain client commands\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Certain client commands (e.g. job kill job killall update start) no longer passing aurora config to their correspondent api calls. This makes it impossible to use API level hooks. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',399,'AURORA-1291','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1291\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Replace enable_api_security arg with a value for http_authentication_mechanism\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Enabling API security involves minimally setting 2 args:{noformat}-enable_api_security=true-http_authentication_mechanism=BASIC{noformat}This could open the possibility of confusing combinations of arguments that may behave in unexpected ways or not work at all.  Remove {{enable_api_security}} in favor of {{-http_authentication_mechanism=NONE}} to be the default value.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',400,'AURORA-1290','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1290\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Allow specifying a shorthand for \\\"well-known\\\" Module FQCNs\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Right now you have to type some pretty verbose stuff to setup security.{noformat}-shiro_realm_modules=org.apache.aurora.scheduler.http.api.security.Kerberos5ShiroRealmModuleorg.apache.aurora.scheduler.http.api.security.IniShiroRealmModulecom.example.CustomRealmModule{noformat}This is ugly and not very refactor-safe. Consider adding mappings for well-known names with fallback to FQCNs.Thus the previous example could become{noformat}-shiro_realm_modules=KERBEROS5_AUTHNINI_AUTHNZcom.example.CustomRealmModule{noformat}This points out one possible weird misconfiguration:{noformat}-shiro_realm_modules=KERBEROS5_AUTHNINI_AUTHNZ-http_authentication_mechanism=BASIC{noformat}will leave the Kerberos code completely dark and pass the Basic auth credentials to IniRealm. Thus as a followup we should probably create separate INI_AUTHN and INI_AUTHZ realms that will only participate in one phase.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',401,'AURORA-1248','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1248\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Client retries 4xx errors\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Looks like the client currently retries all client errors including 4xx ones. For example using a client against a scheduler that requires Kerberos there\'s a series of lines like:{noformat} WARN] Connection error with scheduler: Unknown error talking to http://192.168.33.7:8081/api: 401 Client Error: Unauthorized reconnecting... WARN] Connection error with scheduler: Unknown error talking to http://192.168.33.7:8081/api: 401 Client Error: Unauthorized reconnecting... WARN] Connection error with scheduler: Unknown error talking to http://192.168.33.7:8081/api: 401 Client Error: Unauthorized reconnecting......{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',402,'AURORA-716','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-716\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Reconsider default for -require_slave_checkpoint\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Given that slave recovery has been stable in mesos for a very long time it\'s worth reassessing the default value of this flag [1] (or maybe removing it altogether).https://github.com/apache/incubator-aurora/blob/master/src/main/java/org/apache/aurora/scheduler/DriverFactory.java#L75-L101\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',403,'AURORA-195','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-195\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Jonathan Boulle\", \"summary\": \"remove legacy remnants of \\\"aurora\\\" executor\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Jonathan Boulle\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"e.g. in {{src/main/python/apache/aurora/client/api/command_runner.py}} - {{aurora_sandbox}} {{substitute_aurora}} etc\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',404,'AURORA-1299','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1299\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"UpdateConfigError results in stack trace\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"{noformat}$ aurora update start devcluster/vagrant/test/http_example /vagrant/src/test/sh/org/apache/aurora/e2e/http/http_example.auroraFatal error running command: Pulse interval seconds must be at least 60 seconds.Traceback (most recent call last):  File \\\"/usr/local/bin/aurora/apache/aurora/client/cli/__init__.py\\\" line 307 in _execute    result = noun.execute(context)  File \\\"/usr/local/bin/aurora/apache/aurora/client/cli/__init__.py\\\" line 383 in execute    return self.verbs[context.options.verb].execute(context)  File \\\"/usr/local/bin/aurora/apache/aurora/client/cli/update.py\\\" line 158 in execute    resp = api.start_job_update(config context.options.message instances)  File \\\"/usr/local/bin/aurora/apache/aurora/client/hooks/hooked_api.py\\\" line 190 in start_job_update    config message instances=instances))  File \\\"/usr/local/bin/aurora/apache/aurora/client/hooks/hooked_api.py\\\" line 145 in _hooked_call    resp = api_call()  File \\\"/usr/local/bin/aurora/apache/aurora/client/api/__init__.py\\\" line 165 in start_job_update    raise self.UpdateConfigError(str(e))UpdateConfigError: Pulse interval seconds must be at least 60 seconds.{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',405,'AURORA-1301','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1301\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Tests inheriting from AuroraClientCommandTest always pass\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The test case below should fail but it always passes.{noformat}$ git diffdiff --git a/src/test/python/apache/aurora/client/cli/test_supdate.py b/src/test/python/apache/aurora/client/cli/test_supdate.pyindex ccbcae6..e76681f 100644--- a/src/test/python/apache/aurora/client/cli/test_supdate.py+++ b/src/test/python/apache/aurora/client/cli/test_supdate.py@@ -1116 +1119 @@ class TestStartUpdate(AuroraClientCommandTest):     ]     self.assert_lock_message(self._fake_context) +  def test_always_passes(self):+    assert 1 == 0+   def test_update_cron_job_fails(self):     mock_config = self.create_mock_config(is_cron=True)     self._fake_context.get_job_config = Mock(return_value=mock_config){noformat}{noformat}$ ./pants test.pytest --no-fast --options=\'-v\' src/test/python/apache/aurora/client/cli:supdate | tail -n1               SUCCESS{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',406,'AURORA-1259','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1259\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"summary\": \"Add metrics for scheduler update states\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David McLaughlin\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"It would be nice to expose metrics to track the terminal states of updates. E.g. update_status_FAILED update_status_ROLLED_BACK update_status_ROLLED_FORWARD etc. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',407,'AURORA-1204','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1204\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Update upstart configurations when syncing sources\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"In the vagrant environment we perform a step where we copy the upstart configurations to /etc/init \\\\[1\\\\].  The way this is done makes it challenging to change the upstart configurations later the easiest way being to destroy and re-create the environment.  Consider updating these files that their definitions are updated by rsync along with other code.\\\\[1\\\\] https://github.com/apache/incubator-aurora/blob/ad211da2f2490722a10cce95a2bb4fb55fd1c16f/examples/vagrant/provision-dev-cluster.sh#L60-L61\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',408,'AURORA-1305','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1305\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"MemTaskStore: items are not removed from secondary index\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"An updated PMD flagged this bug (see output below).This line:{code}index.remove(key task);{code}should be:{code}index.remove(key Tasks.id(task));{code}{noformat}CodeWarningGCorg.apache.aurora.scheduler.storage.entities.IScheduledTask is incompatible with expected argument type String in org.apache.aurora.scheduler.storage.mem.MemTaskStore$SecondaryIndex.remove(IScheduledTask)Bug type GC_UNRELATED_TYPES (click for details) In class org.apache.aurora.scheduler.storage.mem.MemTaskStore$SecondaryIndexIn method org.apache.aurora.scheduler.storage.mem.MemTaskStore$SecondaryIndex.remove(IScheduledTask)Actual type org.apache.aurora.scheduler.storage.entities.IScheduledTaskExpected StringCalled method com.google.common.collect.Multimap.remove(Object Object)Invoked on org.apache.aurora.scheduler.storage.mem.MemTaskStore$SecondaryIndex.indextask passed as argumentorg.apache.aurora.scheduler.storage.entities.IScheduledTask.equals(Object) used to determine equalityAt MemTaskStore.java:[line 399]{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',409,'AURORA-1306','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1306\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to gradle 2.4\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Gradle 2.4 is out.  Among other things it claims to offer improved performance:http://gradle.org/docs/2.4/release-notes\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',410,'AURORA-1239','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1239\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"Add a way to watch a scheduler-driven update until it\'s complete\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"It would be nice for scripts that coordinate updates to have the ability to watch a scheduler-driven update until it has completed. This is currently possible by scripting the client e.g. https://github.com/apache/aurora/blob/master/src/test/sh/org/apache/aurora/e2e/test_end_to_end.sh#L149-L166 however given this is likely a common requirement we should encapsulate this functionality within the client itself.Two suggestions are adding {{aurora update watch ...}} or {{aurora update status --watch ...}}.The command should periodically poll the scheduler for the status of the update and exit 0 for successful updates and 1 for failed updates.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',411,'AURORA-1309','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1309\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Build can fail if repo directory absolute path is too long\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 5, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"See https://github.com/pypa/pip/issues/1773This manifests as pip failing:{noformat}/home/wfarner/code/aurora/apache-aurora-0.8.0-rc0-verify/apache-aurora-0.8.0-rc0/build-support/python/isort: /home/wfarner/code/aurora/apache-aurora-0.8.0-rc0-verify/apache-aurora-0.8.0-rc0/build-support/python/isort.venv/bin/pip: /home/wfarner/code/aurora/apache-aurora-0.8.0-rc0-verify/apache-aurora-0.8.0-: bad interpreter: No such file or directory{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',412,'AURORA-1310','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1310\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Remove blanket \'Error executing command: \' prefix from client output\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 5, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When `CommandError` is caught in the client it prints a generic error prefix which is not helpful.  We should strive to make our error messages contextual and stand on their own.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',413,'AURORA-1315','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1315\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"UpdateStoreBenchmarks broken\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Broken by AURORA-1305 as DbModule now requires a StatsProvider binding which UpdateStoreBenchmarks lacks.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',414,'AURORA-1298','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1298\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Make DbTaskStore suitable for use in production\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The DbTaskStore implementation has so far only targeted behavioral compliance with InMemTaskStore.  Use benchmarks to determine areas that require perf improvements and address them.  Also address relevant TODOs that should be production showstoppers.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',415,'AURORA-556','117','{\"key\": \"AURORA-556\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 117, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"H2-backed implementation of TaskStore\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This tracks behavior matching but not necessarily performance.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',416,'AURORA-1043','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1043\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"/logconfig does not work when the scheduler is behind SSL\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When the /logconfig endpoint is behind SSL the JavaScript console is filled with the following errors:{noformat} Mixed Content: The page at \'https://localhost/logconfig\' was loaded over HTTPS but requested an insecure script \'http://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/1.10.1/jquery.min.js\'. This request has been blocked; the content must be served over HTTPS.logconfig:4402 Uncaught ReferenceError: $ is not defined{noformat}As a result the endpoint does not work.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',417,'AURORA-1322','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1322\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"DB task store is enabled by default when staging a recovery\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The new DB task store implementation is turned on by default for the TemporaryStorage since it uses a unit test DB init path (1). This makes recovery from backup impossible if there is any task data triggering constraint violations during staging a recovery from backup file. (1) - https://github.com/apache/aurora/blob/65df91bfd7e3a2ada38a5fe4d620e6373d0f59bf/src/main/java/org/apache/aurora/scheduler/storage/backup/TemporaryStorage.java#L69\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',418,'AURORA-1311','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1311\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to latest h2 version\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We have been holding back on upgrading h2 since the latest release are labeled as beta.  As it turns out the beta marker only applies to the new default MVCC storage implementation and the developers consider the builds stable when MV_STORE is disabled \\\\[1\\\\].\\\\[1\\\\] https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/h2-database/3CDRKex_EgA\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',419,'AURORA-698','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-698\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"summary\": \"aurora executor _shutdown deadline calls should be daemonized\", \"assignee\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"In the aurora executor shutdown method we have deadline() calls:{noformat}  def _shutdown(self status_result):    runner_status = self._runner.status    try:      deadline(self._runner.stop timeout=self.STOP_TIMEOUT)    except Timeout:      log.error(\'Failed to stop runner within deadline.\')    try:      deadline(self._chained_checker.stop timeout=self.STOP_TIMEOUT)    except Timeout:      log.error(\'Failed to stop all checkers within deadline.\')    # If the runner was alive when _shutdown was called defer to the status_result    # otherwise the runner\'s terminal state is the preferred state.    exit_status = runner_status or status_result    self.send_update(        self._driver        self._task_id        exit_status.status        status_result.reason)    self.terminated.set()    defer(self._driver.stop delay=self.PERSISTENCE_WAIT){noformat}However if runner.stop fails with a Timeout exception the spawned AnonymousThread is not daemonized and causes the executor to fail to exit.  This means that the cgroup will not be torn down and if the runner.stop actually failed the process can stay alive even if TASK_KILLED was delivered.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',420,'AURORA-1318','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1318\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"summary\": \"Benchmark snapshot restore\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Details TBD by [~kevints]\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',421,'AURORA-1047','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1047\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 4, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"summary\": \"Implement state reconciliation within the scheduler\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 4, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 4, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 5, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 10, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',422,'AURORA-556','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-556\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"H2-backed implementation of TaskStore\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This tracks behavior matching but not necessarily performance.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',423,'AURORA-1228','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1228\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 3, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"summary\": \"Use explicit status update acknowledgements to improve driver throughput.\", \"assignee\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 3, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 3, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Mesos 0.22.0 is released and includes the ability for schedulers to perform explicit acknowledgments of status updates.This allows schedulers to process status updates asynchronously from the driver thread. Updates can then be processed in batches to reduce the per-update processing overhead. These should help provide substantial improvements to the schedulers update processing throughput.I\'ve placed this under the GC executor retirement effort per AURORA-1047.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',424,'AURORA-1321','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1321\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Create bulk version of the saveJobInstanceUpdateEvent db store method\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Perf analysis revealed unsatisfactory performance of the job update instance insertion implementation during snapshot recovery. It may take up to 5 minutes to process a total of ~100K instance events during scheduler restart. Implement and benchmark the bulk insert version of this api: https://github.com/apache/aurora/blob/b436ec52101cfd5d6f65075a5f7a857ed5a41b5f/src/main/java/org/apache/aurora/scheduler/storage/JobUpdateStore.java#L152\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',425,'AURORA-274','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-274\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Use JDK8 features in scheduler development\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',426,'AURORA-1296','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1296\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"INSTANCES_SPEC_ARGUMENT client option does not validate instance range\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"An of order instance range (e.g. \\\"/10-2\\\") results in empty list of instances. In case of a scheduler updater this leads to updating the entire job instead of specific instances.The offending line: https://github.com/apache/aurora/blob/439a168f9cdd6fe58a12009b51bedad4ac152948/src/main/python/apache/aurora/client/cli/options.py#L74\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',427,'AURORA-1267','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1267\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"Investigate upgrading pants to 0.0.32+\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"A naive upgrade to pants 0.0.32 from 0.0.28 results in the following stack trace:{noformat}Exception caught:  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/bin/pants\\\" line 9 in <module>    load_entry_point(\'pantsbuild.pants==0.0.28\' \'console_scripts\' \'pants\')()  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/bin/pants_exe.py\\\" line 66 in main    _run()  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/bin/pants_exe.py\\\" line 61 in _run    result = goal_runner.run()  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/bin/goal_runner.py\\\" line 168 in run    result = self._do_run()  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/bin/goal_runner.py\\\" line 251 in _do_run    return engine.execute(context self.goals)  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/engine/engine.py\\\" line 27 in execute    self.attempt(context goals)  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/engine/round_engine.py\\\" line 212 in attempt    goal_executor.attempt(explain)  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/engine/round_engine.py\\\" line 45 in attempt    task.execute()  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/backend/codegen/tasks/code_gen.py\\\" line 117 in execute    self.genlang(lang invalid_lang_tgts)  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/backend/codegen/tasks/apache_thrift_gen.py\\\" line 152 in genlang    gen = self.gen_python.gen  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/backend/codegen/tasks/apache_thrift_gen.py\\\" line 127 in gen_python    self._gen_python = self.create_geninfo(\'python\')  File \\\"/Users/zmanji/workspace/gh-aurora/build-support/pants.venv/lib/python2.7/site-packages/pants/backend/codegen/tasks/apache_thrift_gen.py\\\" line 101 in create_geninfo    gen = gen_info[\'gen\']Exception message: \'NoneType\' object has no attribute \'__getitem__\'{noformat}The root cause of this is pants 0.0.32 expects a differently formatted {{pants.ini}} than the one we have now. Pants 0.0.32 ships with a migration tool that informs us of changes required. With a 0.0.32 pants source we can run:{noformat} PANTS_DEV=1 ./pants run src/python/pants/option:migrate_config -- <pants.ini path>{noformat}This gives us:{noformat}Found java in section [thrift-gen]. Should be java in section [gen.thrift].Found extra_jvm_test_paths in section [ide]. Should be extra_jvm_test_paths in section [idea].  Note: extra_jvm_test_paths now must be specified separately for idea and eclipse goals.Found python_test_paths in section [ide]. Should be python_test_paths in section [idea].  Note: python_test_path now must be specified separately for idea and eclipse goals.Found python_lib_paths in section [ide]. Should be python_lib_paths in section [idea].  Note: python_lib_path now must be specified separately for idea and eclipse goals.Found python in section [thrift-gen]. Should be python in section [gen.thrift].Found strict in section [thrift-gen]. Should be strict in section [gen.thrift].Found supportdir in section [thrift-gen]. Should be supportdir in section [gen.thrift].Found python_source_paths in section [ide]. Should be python_source_paths in section [idea].Found version in section [thrift-gen]. Should be version in section [gen.thrift].Found requirements in section [python-ipython]. Should be ipython_requirements in section [repl.py].Found indices in section [python-repos]. Should be indexes in section [python-repos].Found extra_jvm_source_paths in section [ide]. Should be extra_jvm_source_paths in section [idea].  Note: extra_jvm_source_paths now must be specified separately for idea and eclipse goals.{noformat}Making the above changes to {{pants.ini}} results in some commands failing with {{Unable to detect a suitable interpreter}}. It isn\'t clear what needs to be done to fix that error. I suspect it has to do with some of the constraints in our {{pants.ini}} but I cannot determine which ones are at fault.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',428,'AURORA-1325','127','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1325\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 127, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"`src/test/python/apache/aurora/api_util.py` is not apart of any pants targets\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"There is no pants target which lists `src/test/python/apache/aurora/api_util.py` as a source file. `src/test/python/apache/aurora/BUILD` just contains:{noformat}python_test_suite(  name = \'all\'  dependencies = [    \'src/test/python/apache/aurora/admin:all\'    \'src/test/python/apache/aurora/client:all\'    \'src/test/python/apache/aurora/common:all\'    \'src/test/python/apache/aurora/config:all\'    \'src/test/python/apache/aurora/executor:all\'  ]){noformat}Improper source dependency specification can cause us some trouble if we are not careful it is probably best to move this file closer to where it is used.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',429,'AURORA-1043','131','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1043\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 131, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"/logconfig does not work when the scheduler is behind SSL\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When the /logconfig endpoint is behind SSL the JavaScript console is filled with the following errors:{noformat} Mixed Content: The page at \'https://localhost/logconfig\' was loaded over HTTPS but requested an insecure script \'http://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/1.10.1/jquery.min.js\'. This request has been blocked; the content must be served over HTTPS.logconfig:4402 Uncaught ReferenceError: $ is not defined{noformat}As a result the endpoint does not work.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',430,'AURORA-1337','131','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1337\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 131, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"summary\": \"aurora executor should write checkpoints into sandbox\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The thermos observer dual reads from /var/run/thermos and from the sandbox.  The executor should start writing checkpoints to the sandbox by default now that 0.8.0 has been released.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',431,'AURORA-1287','131','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1287\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 131, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Scheduler in-memory DB needs a direct console access\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need a direct way of getting to scheduler SQL data for troubleshooting and ad-hoc analysis purposes. Consider adding support for H2 web console: http://www.h2database.com/html/quickstart.html. The ideal solution should have a way to expose data in read-only and read-write mode depending on the connection/credential settings.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',432,'AURORA-1322','131','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1322\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 131, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"DB task store is enabled by default when staging a recovery\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The new DB task store implementation is turned on by default for the TemporaryStorage since it uses a unit test DB init path (1). This makes recovery from backup impossible if there is any task data triggering constraint violations during staging a recovery from backup file. (1) - https://github.com/apache/aurora/blob/65df91bfd7e3a2ada38a5fe4d620e6373d0f59bf/src/main/java/org/apache/aurora/scheduler/storage/backup/TemporaryStorage.java#L69\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',433,'AURORA-1341','131','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1341\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 131, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"Use TaskStatus reason field to populate the memory limit exceeded field in UserTaskLauncher\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Now that MESOS-343 is complete the reason field can be used to determine if the memory limit exceeded message should be displayed to the user.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',434,'AURORA-1352','139','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1352\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 139, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Audit log doesn\'t capture Shiro subject principal\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Scheduler RPCs that were authenticated by Shiro show UNSECURE in their audit messages.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',435,'AURORA-1139','139','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1139\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 139, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Remove backwards compatibility shims from JobUpdateKey introduction\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"AURORA-1093 introduced several shims to support data migration across the 0.8.0 barrier.  These should be removed.- Remove JobUpdateSummary.updateId and jobKey- Remove JobUpdateQuery.updateId- Remove recovery-time update id -> update key lookup in LogStorage- Remove JobUpdateStore.fetchUpdateKey- Remove JobUpdateDetailsMapper.selectUpdateKey- Remove SaveJobUpdateEvent.updateId- Change {{UNIQUE(update_id)}} constraint to {{UNIQUE(job_key_id update_id)}}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',436,'AURORA-1351','139','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1351\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 139, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Make observer POLLING_INTERVAL configurable\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Observer should have a command line option to override the default {{POLLING_INTERVAL}}: https://github.com/apache/aurora/blob/827b9abea48babe53ad5b2c521757c60f04c6dfc/src/main/python/apache/thermos/observer/task_observer.py#L55\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',437,'AURORA-1361','139','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1361\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 139, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Explicit reconciliation must use SLAVE_ASSIGNED_STATES\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"TaskReconciler is currently using ACTIVE_STATES filter when fetching tasks for explicit reconciliation. Since Mesos does not know anything about non-assigned tasks this results in log messages like this:{noformat}allowed)E0619 00:09:35.219 THREAD175 org.apache.aurora.scheduler.state.TaskStateMachine$5.execute: Illegal state transition attempted: PENDING -> LOST (not allowed)I0619 00:09:35.220 THREAD13437 org.apache.aurora.scheduler.mesos.MesosSchedulerImpl.logStatusUpdate: Received status update for task 1371518881594-mesos-pending-resources-100-77-fbbd6074-0896-495f-9a88-1d0ff48495fe in state TASK_LOST from SOURCE_MASTER with REASON_RECONCILIATION: Reconciliation: Task is unknown{noformat}While there is no harm to PENDING or THROTTLED tasks the above messages pollute logs and should be suppressed. Use SLAVE_ASSIGNED_STATES filter instead of ACTIVE_STATES.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',438,'AURORA-1344','139','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1344\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 139, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Create Aurora oversubscription design summary\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',439,'AURORA-1346','139','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1346\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 139, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade requests-kerberos to 0.7.0\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This fixes an issue where the client can infinitely recurse when it gets a 401 but does not have a Kerberos TGT in its cache.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',440,'AURORA-1353','139','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1353\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 139, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"summary\": \"MesosPathDetector double-counts checkpoint roots\", \"assignee\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Brian Wickman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"This manifests itself in the observer ballooning in resource usage.  The TaskDetector finds two copies of every task because of the \'latest\' symlink being a duplicate of the actual directory so we get race conditions in on_active/on_finished inside src/main/python/apache/thermos/observer/task_observer.py that cause it to hold onto TaskResourceMonitors which tend to be pretty expensive to run.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',441,'AURORA-1379','151','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1379\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 151, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Referential integrity violation when replaying storage\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"At startup in the Vagrant environment I observed:{noformat}E0630 20:45:54.427 THREAD1 org.apache.aurora.scheduler.SchedulerLifecycle$9.execute: Caught unchecked exception: org.apache.aurora.scheduler.storage.Storage$StorageException: ### Error updating database.  Cause: org.h2.jdbc.JdbcSQLException: Referential integrity constraint violation: \\\"CONSTRAINT_4BE: PUBLIC.TASKS FOREIGN KEY(SLAVE_ROW_ID) REFERENCES PUBLIC.HOST_ATTRIBUTES(ID) (1)\\\"; SQL statement:DELETE FROM host_attributes    WHERE host = ? [23503-187]### The error may involve defaultParameterMap### The error occurred while setting parameters### SQL: DELETE FROM host_attributes     WHERE host = ?### Cause: org.h2.jdbc.JdbcSQLException: Referential integrity constraint violation: \\\"CONSTRAINT_4BE: PUBLIC.TASKS FOREIGN KEY(SLAVE_ROW_ID) REFERENCES PUBLIC.HOST_ATTRIBUTES(ID) (1)\\\"; SQL statement:DELETE FROM host_attributes    WHERE host = ? [23503-187]org.apache.aurora.scheduler.storage.Storage$StorageException: ### Error updating database.  Cause: org.h2.jdbc.JdbcSQLException: Referential integrity constraint violation: \\\"CONSTRAINT_4BE: PUBLIC.TASKS FOREIGN KEY(SLAVE_ROW_ID) REFERENCES PUBLIC.HOST_ATTRIBUTES(ID) (1)\\\"; SQL statement:DELETE FROM host_attributes    WHERE host = ? [23503-187]### The error may involve defaultParameterMap### The error occurred while setting parameters### SQL: DELETE FROM host_attributes     WHERE host = ?### Cause: org.h2.jdbc.JdbcSQLException: Referential integrity constraint violation: \\\"CONSTRAINT_4BE: PUBLIC.TASKS FOREIGN KEY(SLAVE_ROW_ID) REFERENCES PUBLIC.HOST_ATTRIBUTES(ID) (1)\\\"; SQL statement:DELETE FROM host_attributes    WHERE host = ? [23503-187]        at org.apache.aurora.scheduler.storage.db.DbS