mary\": \"Remove duplicate thermos_observer\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Brian Brazil\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 5, \"description\": \"There are currently two thermos_observer python_binaries in the codebase one in src/main/python/apache/aurora/tools/BUILD and the other in ./src/main/python/apache/thermos/observer/bin/BUILD. This is confusing.Let\'s get rid of one of them I think the latter is the one that\'s not meant to be used.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',464,'AURORA-1402','160','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1402\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 160, \"status\": \"Accepted\", \"creator\": \"Joe Smith\", \"summary\": \"Allow overriding cluster attributes via environment variables\", \"assignee\": \"Joe Smith\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Joe Smith\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"An example usecase is giving the Aurora Client a different \'scheduler URI\' which would allow the client to bypass a downed proxy but still be able to send RPCs. Initially it seemed like this would be the only usecase but after speaking to [~wfarner] and [~kevints] a more general solution to override various parts of a cluster configuration would be useful.There is already a [mechanism to go from a cluster\'s json|https://github.com/apache/aurora/blob/master/src/main/python/apache/aurora/admin/admin.py#L494] so we should consider using the same formatting to make that read+write vs. just read.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',465,'AURORA-1395','160','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1395\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 160, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"s