160, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"End-to-end test stalls at SSH prompt\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"On {{38c2e76}} end-to-end tests stall at this prompt (not sure when specifically this was introduced):{noformat}++ aurora task run devcluster/vagrant/test/http_example lsThe authenticity of host \'192.168.33.7 (192.168.33.7)\' can\'t be established.ECDSA key fingerprint is c2:27:21:79:51:2a:cc:49:7d:f8:9b:30:94:e4:e4:ba.Are you sure you want to continue connecting (yes/no)? yes{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',469,'AURORA-1409','160','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1409\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 160, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"End-to-end tests fail with 401 unuthorized\", \"assignee\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Can be consistently reproduced on {{24088ef}}.{noformat}+ kadmin.local -q \'ktadd -keytab testdir/root.keytab root\'Authenticating as principal user/admin@KRBTEST.COM with password.Entry for principal root with kvno 2 encryption type aes256-cts-hmac-sha1-96 added to keytab WRFILE:testdir/root.keytab.Entry for principal root with kvno 2 encryption type aes128-cts-hmac-sha1-96 added to keytab WRFILE:testdir/root.keytab.Entry for principal root with kvno 2 encryption type des3-cbc-sha1 added to keytab WRFILE:testdir/root.keytab.Entry for principal root with kvno 2 encryption type arcfour-hmac added to keytab WRFILE:testdir/root.keytab.+ test_snapshot+ snapshot_as vagrant+ local principal=vagrant+ kinit -k -t testdir/vagrant.keytab vagrant++ printf snapshot-response.%s.json vagrant+ curl -u : --negotiate -w \'%{http_code}\\\\n\' -o snapshot-response.vagrant.json -s http://192.168.33.7:8081/api --data-binary \'[1\\\"snapshot\\\"10{}]\'401+ kdestroy+ cat snapshot-response.vagrant.json<html><head><meta http-equiv=\\\"Content-Type\\\" content=\\\"text/html;charset=ISO-8859-1\\\"/><title>Error 401 Unauthorized</title></head><body><h2>HTTP ERROR: 401</h2><p>Problem accessing /api. Reason:<pre>    Unauthorized</pre></p><hr /><i><small>Powered by Jetty://</small></i>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                </body></html>{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',470,'AURORA-97','160','{\"key\": \"AURORA-97\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 160, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Provide a web UI page to show history for a specific job instance\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"We currently have dashboard pages for every level of our logical system hierarchy except for \\\"instance\\\".Adding this page would be useful for sifting through completed tasks in the scope of a specific instance id.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',471,'AURORA-1410','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1410\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Publish RPM and deb for 0.9.0\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 8, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 11, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',472,'AURORA-1429','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1429\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Dan Norris\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade Mesos to 0.23\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Dan Norris\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"Mesos 0.23 was released on July 29th and contains a number of very interesting experimental features and fixes.http://mesos.apache.org/blog/mesos-0-23-0-released/\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',473,'AURORA-1381','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1381\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Brian Brazil\", \"summary\": \"Remove duplicate thermos_observer\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Brian Brazil\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 5, \"description\": \"There are currently two thermos_observer python_binaries in the codebase one in src/main/python/apache/aurora/tools/BUILD and the other in ./src/main/python/apache/thermos/observer/bin/BUILD. This is confusing.Let\'s get rid of one of them I think the latter is the one that\'s not meant to be used.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',474,'AURORA-851','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-851\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"Create nightly builds\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"It would be great if we had a Jenkins job that vetted the current state of master and published a nightly build.This would make life easier for folks deploying Aurora from master rather than the (currently anemic) released builds.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',475,'AURORA-1415','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1415\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"De-generalize resource handling in Scheduler\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"From design doc: {quote}To handle revocable resources correctly Aurora needs to de-generalize and simplify its internal resource representation. The new resource vector should be capable of aggregating resources by revocable flag. This will require refactoring existing resource handling (including  AURORA-105) which will also help to support Mesos framework role in future.{quote}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 6, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',476,'AURORA-1421','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1421\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Surface revoked task reason in the UI\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Need to investigate if fixing AURORA-1193 is still necessary to surface revoked (LOST) task status reason in the UI.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',477,'AURORA-1395','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1395\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"RescheduleCalculator precondition fails when using DbTaskStore\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 3, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When enabling the DB task store i frequently encounter this exception due to a precondition check fail in RescheduleCalculator:{noformat}E0710 22:33:48.688 THREAD138 org.apache.aurora.scheduler.events.PubsubEventModule$1.handleException: Failed to dispatch event to public void org.apache.aurora.scheduler.async.TaskThrottler.taskChangedState(org.apache.aurora.scheduler.events.PubsubEvent$TaskStateChange): java.lang.IllegalStateExceptionjava.lang.IllegalStateException        at com.google.common.base.Preconditions.checkState(Preconditions.java:161)        at org.apache.aurora.scheduler.async.RescheduleCalculator$RescheduleCalculatorImpl$1.apply(RescheduleCalculator.java:103)        at org.apache.aurora.scheduler.async.RescheduleCalculator$RescheduleCalculatorImpl$1.apply(RescheduleCalculator.java:85)        at org.apache.aurora.scheduler.async.RescheduleCalculator$RescheduleCalculatorImpl.getFlappingPenaltyMs(RescheduleCalculator.java:159)        at org.apache.aurora.scheduler.async.TaskThrottler.taskChangedState(TaskThrottler.java:72)        at sun.reflect.GeneratedMethodAccessor89.invoke(Unknown Source)        at sun.reflect.DelegatingMethodAccessorImpl.invoke(DelegatingMethodAccessorImpl.java:43)        at java.lang.reflect.Method.invoke(Method.java:497)        at com.google.common.eventbus.EventSubscriber.handleEvent(EventSubscriber.java:74)        at com.google.common.eventbus.SynchronizedEventSubscriber.handleEvent(SynchronizedEventSubscriber.java:47)        at com.google.common.eventbus.EventBus.dispatch(EventBus.java:322)        at com.google.common.eventbus.AsyncEventBus.access$001(AsyncEventBus.java:34)        at com.google.common.eventbus.AsyncEventBus$1.run(AsyncEventBus.java:117)        at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1142)        at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:617)        at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:745){noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 9, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',478,'AURORA-1431','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1431\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Slave reservation is too restrictive\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This is a regression introduced in https://reviews.apache.org/r/37001/. The updated TaskAssigner logic looks for an exclusive task->slave match any time a slave reservation is present. Any time scheduling fails and a slave reservation is created by the preemptor a task group gets effectively locked into the reserved slave. Given that reverse slave->task relationship is no longer enforced a reserved slave could be taken by some other task thus slowing down scheduling progress.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',479,'AURORA-1425','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1425\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"Speed up iteration speed when developing UI code\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Developing UI code on Aurora today is quite tedious. While assets are served from the classpath currently the only place they exist on the classpath in the vagrant image is within a jar. This means that any changes to html css or js files requires a build/restart of the scheduler. Ideally these files would be as close to hot reloadable as possible.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',480,'AURORA-1125','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1125\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"Update page UI should have some indication of ongoing activity\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Some thoughts:- The in-progress instance boxes could pulse their background color.- Add a spinner to the bottom of the instance events to indicate that we\'re continuing to monitor for new events.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',481,'AURORA-1331','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1331\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"It should be possible to link to an instance from the update page\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"E.g. if an instance ran into issues during an update it would be great to be able to link directly to it to investigate the problem (rather than having to go to the job paging and tracking it down in the list of completed tasks).\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',482,'AURORA-97','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-97\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Provide a web UI page to show history for a specific job instance\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"We currently have dashboard pages for every level of our logical system hierarchy except for \\\"instance\\\".Adding this page would be useful for sifting through completed tasks in the scope of a specific instance id.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',483,'AURORA-1427','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1427\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Move build-support/packaging to aurora-packaging repo\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"New repo: https://git-wip-us.apache.org/repos/asf/aurora-packaging.gitGoal is to pull source and history of {{build-support/packaging}} to the new repo and delete it from the source repo.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',484,'AURORA-1193','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1193\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Improve UI task status reporting experience\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Mesos may append an optional message with task status update that is currently surfacing in the UI via TaskEvent. These messages may not be user friendly and add confusion. One example is \\\"Unregistered executor\\\" issued when Mesos kills an assigned task that did not have a chance to run yet. While this message does not constitute a failure it may create an illusion of abnormal behavior in an otherwise normal operation.Consider filtering/formatting messages in the UI/scheduler to avoid adverse user experience. The ideal solution should also leverage TaskStatus.reason field to show additional status details.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',485,'AURORA-1435','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1435\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Scheduling loop terminates on the first mismatch\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This is the regression introduced in https://reviews.apache.org/r/37001/ and is happening due to scheduling loop exiting prematurely when the first mismatch is identified: https://github.com/apache/aurora/blob/cbc42c484cc599d41d5a4bd23c373a64e9b71466/src/main/java/org/apache/aurora/scheduler/state/TaskAssigner.java#L189\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',486,'AURORA-1430','163','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1430\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 163, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Set up vagrant environment for sudo-less docker commands\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Our vagrant development box has docker installed but we should take the extra steps to run docker commands without {{sudo}}.  See commands required here: http://askubuntu.com/questions/477551/how-can-i-use-docker-without-sudo/477554#477554\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',487,'AURORA-1410','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1410\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Publish RPM and deb for 0.9.0\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 8, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 11, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',488,'AURORA-1429','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1429\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Dan Norris\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade Mesos to 0.23\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Dan Norris\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"Mesos 0.23 was released on July 29th and contains a number of very interesting experimental features and fixes.http://mesos.apache.org/blog/mesos-0-23-0-released/\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',489,'AURORA-1417','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1417\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Handle revocable resources in scheduler\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"From design doc:{quote}The TaskAssigner will need to be adjusted to look only at revocable resources for best effort tasks....The OfferManager should maintain a new offer sequence sorted by the presence of revocable resources. This will be used to match best effort tasks.{quote}\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',490,'AURORA-1437','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1437\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Implement TierManager to translate tiers to task traits\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"From design doc:{quote}Scheduler will have a new TierManager module translating the task tier into the correspondent set of traits. Initial implementation will statically define test devel staging tier values as revocable. {quote}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',491,'AURORA-1418','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1418\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Ignore revocable resources in preemptor\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"From design doc:{quote}Preemptor needs to ignore best effort task resources when searching for preemption slots.{quote}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',492,'AURORA-1419','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1419\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"FrameworkInfo support for REVOCABLE_RESOURCES capability\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"From design doc:{quote}In order to start receiving revocable offers Aurora will be required to register with REVOCABLE_RESOURCES flag set as a new capability type.{quote}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',493,'AURORA-1414','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1414\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Schema changes to support revocable jobs\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',494,'AURORA-851','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-851\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"Create nightly builds\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"It would be great if we had a Jenkins job that vetted the current state of master and published a nightly build.This would make life easier for folks deploying Aurora from master rather than the (currently anemic) released builds.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',495,'AURORA-647','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-647\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Don\'t store serialized thrift objects in the database\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"To expedite AURORA-610 we accepted some technical debt by storing serialized thrift objects in the database.  Once the database is completely fronted by SQL we need to go back and manage these objects with references to other tables.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',496,'AURORA-1213','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1213\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"IP clearance and import of twitter commons java code\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 4, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"We currently have 32  dependencies on libraries from Twitter commons.  {noformat}$ grep com.twitter.common build.gradle  | wc -l      32{noformat}While these libraries have generally served us well this number of dependencies creates a transitive web that inhibits us from upgrading our direct dependencies.Consider removing these dependencies and replacing our uses of them with forks of the code in our repository.  My hunch is that we use relatively insignificant portions of them overall.  However if we end up just cloning the sources and maintaining them ourselves we should back out.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 9, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',497,'AURORA-1331','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1331\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"It should be possible to link to an instance from the update page\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"E.g. if an instance ran into issues during an update it would be great to be able to link directly to it to investigate the problem (rather than having to go to the job paging and tracking it down in the list of completed tasks).\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',498,'AURORA-97','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-97\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Provide a web UI page to show history for a specific job instance\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"We currently have dashboard pages for every level of our logical system hierarchy except for \\\"instance\\\".Adding this page would be useful for sifting through completed tasks in the scope of a specific instance id.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',499,'AURORA-1439','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1439\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Modify resource counters to support revocable slot counters\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',500,'AURORA-1442','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1442\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"Move Twitter Commons into org.apache.aurora namespace and add headers\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Once AURORA-1213 is complete the code imported from Twitter Commons needs to be moved into the org.apache.aurora namespace and the license headers need to be changed to show Apache copyright. I believe this can be done quickly with automation.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',501,'AURORA-696','174','{\"key\": \"AURORA-696\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 174, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Jay Buffington\", \"summary\": \"No way to link directly to Completed Tasks\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jay Buffington\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"I want to send someone a link directly pointing to the \\\"Completed Tasks\\\" page on http://scheduler:8081/scheduler/jaybuff/devel/hello-worldCurrently that will take them to active tasks then they have to click \\\"completed tasks\\\" \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',502,'AURORA-1441','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1441\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Document oversubscription in Aurora\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',503,'AURORA-1462','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1462\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Update quota documentation\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',504,'AURORA-1491','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1491\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Make \\\"aurora task\\\" commands support optional ssh options\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"The \\\"aurora task\\\" commands should pass \\\"-v\\\" flag down to subprocess to make sure \\\"ssh -v\\\" is invoked. Otherwise it\'s impossible to debug command failures due to misbehaving ssh.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',505,'AURORA-1459','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1459\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"DelayExecutor is flaky within scheduling loop\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"TaskGroups now uses DelayExecutor introduced to gate async operations. The problem though is that DelayExecutor queue is only flushed on DB transaction completion (1). This means no scheduling can ever proceed unless there is _some_ storage mutation activity. If/when there are no storage writes scheduling effectively halts. While it unlikely to happen in production it is consistently reproducible with e2e tests in vagrant on any subsequent run.(1) - https://github.com/apache/aurora/blob/06ddaadbcba4c66b8019815de6ca27d50a9df77d/src/main/java/org/apache/aurora/scheduler/storage/db/DbStorage.java#L175-L178\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',506,'AURORA-1345','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1345\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"Update status page for large jobs is killed by Chrome\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When I say \\\"killed by Chrome\\\" I mean if left open long enough the page turns into the Chrome \\\"Aw Snap\\\" page.This is presumably due to the continued addition of instance events to the page causing it to OOM and Chrome to kill it. One suggestion made to me by those more familiar with Angular was to add {{track by}} to the {{ng-repeat}} used to build the DOM for the instance events.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',507,'AURORA-783','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-783\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Bill Farner\", \"summary\": \"Remove redundant page header text\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Bill Farner\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"The scheduler web interface has a breadcrumb:{noformat}Home Role: www-data  Environment: devel  Job: hello_world{noformat}And a large heading:{noformat}Job hello_world in role www-data and environment devel{noformat}Consider removing the heading text as it consumes a lot of real-estate and is redundant to the breadcrumb.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',508,'AURORA-1460','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1460\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Remove quota enforcement for dedicated jobs\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',509,'AURORA-1461','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1461\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Update RPCs and client/UI to properly identify non-dedicated consumption\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',510,'AURORA-1464','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1464\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Add e2e integration tests for revocable tasks\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',511,'AURORA-1445','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1445\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"In-progress instances on Update page continue to pulse after update is aborted\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When an update is aborted any instances that were in progress still have the css class of {{instance-updating}} and as such continue to pulse.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',512,'AURORA-696','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-696\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Jay Buffington\", \"summary\": \"No way to link directly to Completed Tasks\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jay Buffington\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"I want to send someone a link directly pointing to the \\\"Completed Tasks\\\" page on http://scheduler:8081/scheduler/jaybuff/devel/hello-worldCurrently that will take them to active tasks then they have to click \\\"completed tasks\\\" \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',513,'AURORA-1474','179','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1474\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 179, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"summary\": \"Improve discoverability of dashboard link on the Job page\", \"assignee\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Joshua Cohen\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We optionally link to a job dashboard from the Job page (if {{viz_job_url_prefix}} is passed to the Scheduler on the command line). The icon for this is currently uses glyphicons halflings font stats glyph (depending on how you view it a series of 3 vertical bars or a series of hills). It\'s not at all obvious that this link takes you anywhere interesting. We should revisit the discoverability of this link.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',514,'AURORA-1441','190','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1441\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 190, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Document oversubscription in Aurora\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',515,'AURORA-1462','190','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1462\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 190, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Update quota documentation\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',516,'AURORA-1494','190','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1494\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 190, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Scheduler fails to start due to thrift/SQL schema data type mismatch\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"After https://reviews.apache.org/r/38288 we are unable to upgrade scheduler in one of our clusters due to the following failure on restart:{noformat}### Cause: org.h2.jdbc.JdbcSQLException: Numeric value out of range: \\\"3174400000031744\\\"; SQL statement:INSERT INTO task_configs (      job_key_id      creator_user      service      num_cpus      ram_mb      disk_mb      priority      max_task_failures      production      contact_email      executor_name      executor_data      tier    ) VALUES (      (        SELECT ID        FROM job_keys        WHERE role = ?          AND environment = ?          AND name = ?      )      ?      ?      ?      ?      ?      ?      ?      ?      ?{noformat}This appears due to type mismatch between TaskConfig.diskMb (i64) and task_configs.disk_mb (INT). A possible real-life scenario:- user creates a job with an oversized resource requirement and the job fails to schedule- user realizes the mistake and attempts to correct it by running {{aurora update start}}- scheduler creates an instance of the JobUpdate with the oversized TaskConfig as its initial state and persists it in the log- scheduler restarts to a new version (with the patch above) and attempts to reload job updates from the log but now instead of storing TaskConfigs as binary blobs it attempts to insert into task_configs table where resource columns have narrower type. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',517,'AURORA-1491','190','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1491\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 190, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Make \\\"aurora task\\\" commands support optional ssh options\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"The \\\"aurora task\\\" commands should pass \\\"-v\\\" flag down to subprocess to make sure \\\"ssh -v\\\" is invoked. Otherwise it\'s impossible to debug command failures due to misbehaving ssh.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',518,'AURORA-1503','191','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1503\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 191, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"Determine how best to keep up with Mesos releases\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 10, \"description\": \"Aurora 0.9.0 was released with a dependency on Mesos 0.22. The current release is Mesos 0.24. There was a change with how data was published into the Mesos ZK node in Mesos 0.23 (Protobuf to JSON) meaning that frameworks that are linked against 0.22 will get a libmesos error when using the 0.24 library.The task is to determine what is the best way forward in scenarios like this. Possible options include:* Release 0.9.x with a newer mesos dependency* Cut a new release from master that depends on 0.24Problems include backwards/forwards compatibility. For example if we release 0.9.1 with a dependency on Mesos 0.24 will Aurora still work against a Mesos Master that runs 0.22?\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 7, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',519,'AURORA-1502','191','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1502\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 191, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Create a design summary for the jobConfigDiff RPC\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',520,'AURORA-1503','197','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1503\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 197, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"Determine how best to keep up with Mesos releases\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 10, \"description\": \"Aurora 0.9.0 was released with a dependency on Mesos 0.22. The current release is Mesos 0.24. There was a change with how data was published into the Mesos ZK node in Mesos 0.23 (Protobuf to JSON) meaning that frameworks that are linked against 0.22 will get a libmesos error when using the 0.24 library.The task is to determine what is the best way forward in scenarios like this. Possible options include:* Release 0.9.x with a newer mesos dependency* Cut a new release from master that depends on 0.24Problems include backwards/forwards compatibility. For example if we release 0.9.1 with a dependency on Mesos 0.24 will Aurora still work against a Mesos Master that runs 0.22?\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 7, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',521,'AURORA-1516','197','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1516\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 197, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Add update sequence into \\\"aurora job diff\\\" command\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',522,'AURORA-1515','197','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1515\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 197, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"summary\": \"Implement getJobUpdateDiff API without TaskConfig diff support\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',523,'AURORA-814','197','{\"key\": \"AURORA-814\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 197, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"summary\": \"Migrate client off of deprecated SessionKey APIs\", \"assignee\": \"Bill Farner\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Chris Lambert\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Remove SessionKey injection from the scheduler client instead relying on transport-level authentication.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',524,'AURORA-1522','197','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1522\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 197, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"ShiroAuthorizationInterceptor doesn\'t set thriftAPIVersion\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"This is because the auth interceptor is applied first. Client users get a confusing error message about the response missing a thriftAPIVersion attribute rather than the AUTH_FAILED message as intended.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',525,'AURORA-1511','203','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1511\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 203, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"PreemptorService failure does not trigger shutdown\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"While observing AURORA-1510 in production I noticed the bug caused the {{PreemptorService}} to transition to the FAILED state. The {{/services}} endpoint had:{noformat}{name: \\\"PreemptorService\\\"state: \\\"FAILED\\\"failureCause: \\\"java.util.ConcurrentModificationException\\\"}{noformat}However the scheduler continued to run. I believe this is a bug.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',526,'AURORA-1364','203','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1364\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 203, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"summary\": \"Improve client error messages for Kerberos errors\", \"assignee\": \"Maxim Khutornenko\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Kevin Sweeney\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Currently Kerberos errors are presented as a stack trace to the user looking something like:{noformat}GSSError: ((\'Unspecified GSS failure.  Minor code may provide more information\' 851968) (\'No Kerberos credentials available\' -1765328243))401 Client Error: Authorization Required{noformat}(And similar for expired tickets). It would be helpful to catch these and display more useful information such as a suggestion to run {{kinit}}.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Aurora',527,'AURORA-1510','203','{\"key\": \"AURORA-1510\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 203, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"summary\": \"ConcurrentModificationException in PreemptorService\", \"assignee\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Zameer Manji\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 2.0,