es\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 541, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Greg Mann\", \"summary\": \"Update Docker executor to allow kill policy overrides\", \"assignee\": \"Greg Mann\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Greg Mann\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"In order for the agent to successfully override the task kill policy of Docker tasks when the agent is being drained the Docker executor must be able to receive kill policy overrides and must be updated to honor them. Since the Docker executor runs using the executor driver this is currently not possible. We could for example update the executor driver interface or move the Docker executor off of the executor driver.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',37,'MESOS-9843','542','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9843\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 542, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"summary\": \"Implement tests for the `containerizer/debug` endpoint.\", \"assignee\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Implement tests for container stuck issues and check that the agent\'s `containerizer/debug` endpoint returns a JSON object containing information about pending operations.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',38,'MESOS-9853','545','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9853\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 545, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Greg Mann\", \"summary\": \"Update Docker executor to allow kill policy overrides\", \"assignee\": \"Greg Mann\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Greg Mann\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"In order for the agent to successfully override the task kill policy of Docker tasks when the agent is being drained the Docker executor must be able to receive kill policy overrides and must be updated to honor them. Since the Docker executor runs using the executor driver this is currently not possible. We could for example update the executor driver interface or move the Docker executor off of the executor driver.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',39,'MESOS-9892','545','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9892\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 545, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Greg Mann\", \"summary\": \"Test various agent state transitions involving agent draining\", \"assignee\": \"Joseph Wu\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Greg Mann\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We should add tests which verify correct behavior in the various cases of transitions between different agent states and the DRAINING or DRAINED states.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',40,'MESOS-9893','546','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9893\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 546, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Qian Zhang\", \"summary\": \"`volume/secret` isolator should cleanup the stored secret from runtime directory when the container is destroyed\", \"assignee\": \"Qian Zhang\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Qian Zhang\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"`volume/secret` isolator writes secret into a file (its filename is a UUID) under `/run/mesos/.secret` when launching container but it does not clean up that file when the container is destroyed. Over time the `/run/mesos/.secret` directory may take up all disk space on the partition.\", \"fixVersions\": 4, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',41,'MESOS-9669','548','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9669\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 548, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"summary\": \"Deprecate v0 quota calls.\", \"assignee\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Once we introduce the new quota APIs in MESOS-8068 we should deprecate the `/quota` endpoint. We should mark this as deprecated and hide it in our documentation.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',42,'MESOS-9758','548','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9758\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 548, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"summary\": \"Take ports out of the GET_ROLES endpoints.\", \"assignee\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"It does not make sense to combine ports across agents.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',43,'MESOS-9427','548','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9427\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 548, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"summary\": \"Revisit quota documentation.\", \"assignee\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Documentation\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"At this point the quota documentation in the docs/ folder has become rather stale. It would be good to at least update any inaccuracies and ideally re-write it to better reflect the current thinking.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',44,'MESOS-9952','550','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9952\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 550, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Benjamin Bannier\", \"summary\": \"ExampleTest.DiskFullFramework is slow\", \"assignee\": \"Benjamin Bannier\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Benjamin Bannier\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Executing {{ExampleTest.DiskFullFramework}} on my setup takes almost 18s in a not optimized build. This is way too long for a default-enabled test.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',45,'MESOS-9919','553','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9919\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 553, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Greg Mann\", \"summary\": \"Health check performance decreases on large machines\", \"assignee\": \"Greg Mann\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Greg Mann\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"In recent testing it appears that the performance of Mesos command health checks decreases dramatically on nodes with large numbers of cores and lots of memory. This may be due to the changes in the cost of forking the agent process on such nodes. We need to investigate this issue to understand the root cause.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',46,'MESOS-9844','554','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9844\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 554, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"summary\": \"Update documentation describing `containerizer/debug` endpoint.\", \"assignee\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Documentation\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',47,'MESOS-9843','554','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9843\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 554, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"summary\": \"Implement tests for the `containerizer/debug` endpoint.\", \"assignee\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Implement tests for container stuck issues and check that the agent\'s `containerizer/debug` endpoint returns a JSON object containing information about pending operations.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',48,'MESOS-9908','554','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9908\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 554, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Gilbert Song\", \"summary\": \"Introduce a new agent flag and support docker volume chown to task user. \", \"assignee\": \"Gilbert Song\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Gilbert Song\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Currently docker volume is always mounted as root which is not accessible by non-root task users. users.non-root users to run as container user and docker volume needs to be supported for those non-root users. For security concerns there are use cases that operator may only allow \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',49,'MESOS-9892','555','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9892\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 555, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Greg Mann\", \"summary\": \"Test various agent state transitions involving agent draining\", \"assignee\": \"Joseph Wu\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Greg Mann\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We should add tests which verify correct behavior in the various cases of transitions between different agent states and the DRAINING or DRAINED states.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',50,'MESOS-9937','555','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9937\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 555, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"longfei\", \"summary\": \"53598228fe should be backported to 1.7.x\", \"assignee\": \"Greg Mann\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"longfei\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Commit 53598228fe on the master branch should be backported to 1.7.x. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',51,'MESOS-9942','558','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9942\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 558, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"summary\": \"Deprecate framework sorter.\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Given the flat structure of the framework there is no need to store and sort frameworks in the sorter tree structure. We should deprecate framework sorter. This would dedicate the sorter for roles opening up room for optimization and cleanup. \", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',52,'MESOS-9915','558','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9915\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 558, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"summary\": \"Store a role tree in the master.\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Currently both the master and allocator track known roles in maps (note however that the master does not currently have complete tracking of known roles). These Role It would be nice if the master (and allocator) had a complete Role tree stored and updated in an event driven manner to obtain information cheaply at any point in time. Ideally this role tree abstraction can be shared (e.g. with the allocator) which may not be trivial since the information tracked might differ.structs track some information about roles but currently do not track information hierarchically. As a result when per-role resource quantities were exposed in the API we had to add code outside of the master\'s Role struct to perform the hierarchical aggregation.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',53,'MESOS-9669','558','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9669\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 558, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"summary\": \"Deprecate v0 quota calls.\", \"assignee\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Once we introduce the new quota APIs in MESOS-8068 we should deprecate the `/quota` endpoint. We should mark this as deprecated and hide it in our documentation.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',54,'MESOS-8503','558','{\"key\": \"MESOS-8503\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 558, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Armand Grillet\", \"summary\": \"Improve UI when displaying frameworks with many roles.\", \"assignee\": \"Andrei Sekretenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Armand Grillet\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The /frameworks UI endpoint displays all the roles of each framework in a table:!Screen Shot 2018-01-29 a╠Ç 10.38.05.png! This is not readable if a framework has many roles. We thus need to provide a solution to only display a few roles per framework and show more when a user wants to see all of them.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',55,'MESOS-9758','558','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9758\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 558, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"summary\": \"Take ports out of the GET_ROLES endpoints.\", \"assignee\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"It does not make sense to combine ports across agents.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',56,'MESOS-9917','558','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9917\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 558, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"summary\": \"Store a role tree in the allocator.\", \"assignee\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently the client (role and framework) tree for the allocator is stored in the sorter abstraction. This is not ideal. The role/framework tree is generic information that is needed regardless of the sorter used. The current sorter interface and its associated states are tech debts that contribute to performance slowdown and code convolution. We should store a role/framework tree in the allocator.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',57,'MESOS-9949','558','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9949\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 558, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"summary\": \"Track allocated/offered in the allocator\'s role tree.\", \"assignee\": \"Andrei Sekretenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 4, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Currently the allocator\'s role tree only tracks the reserved resources for each role subtree. For metrics purposes it would be ideal to track offered / allocated as well. This requires augmenting the allocator\'s structs and recoverResources to hold the two categories independently and transition from offered -> allocated as applicable when recovering resources. This might require a slight change to the recoverResources interface.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',58,'MESOS-9844','559','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9844\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 559, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"summary\": \"Update documentation describing `containerizer/debug` endpoint.\", \"assignee\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Documentation\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',59,'MESOS-9843','559','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9843\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 559, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"summary\": \"Implement tests for the `containerizer/debug` endpoint.\", \"assignee\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Implement tests for container stuck issues and check that the agent\'s `containerizer/debug` endpoint returns a JSON object containing information about pending operations.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',60,'MESOS-9843','561','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9843\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 561, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"summary\": \"Implement tests for the `containerizer/debug` endpoint.\", \"assignee\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Andrei Budnik\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Implement tests for container stuck issues and check that the agent\'s `containerizer/debug` endpoint returns a JSON object containing information about pending operations.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',61,'MESOS-9942','562','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9942\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 562, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"summary\": \"Deprecate framework sorter.\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Given the flat structure of the framework there is no need to store and sort frameworks in the sorter tree structure. We should deprecate framework sorter. This would dedicate the sorter for roles opening up room for optimization and cleanup. \", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',62,'MESOS-1452','562','{\"key\": \"MESOS-1452\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 562, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"summary\": \"Improve Master::removeOffer to avoid further resource accounting bugs.\", \"assignee\": \"Andrei Sekretenko\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Benjamin Mahler\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 5, \"description\": \"Per comments on this review: https://reviews.apache.org/r/21750/We\'ve had numerous bugs around resource accounting in the master due to the trickiness of removing offers in the Master code.There are a few ways to improve this:1. Add multiple offer methods to differentiate semantics:{code}useOffer(offerId);rescindOffer(offerId);discardOffer(offerId);{code}2. Add an enum to removeOffer to differentiate removal semantics:{code}removeOffer(offerId USE);removeOffer(offerId RESCIND);removeOffer(offerId DISCARD);{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',63,'MESOS-3938','562','{\"key\": \"MESOS-3938\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 562, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Alex R\", \"summary\": \"Consider allowing setting quotas for the default \'*\' role.\", \"assignee\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Alex R\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Investigate use cases and implications of the possibility to set quota for the \'*\' role. For example having quota for \'*\' set can effectively reduce the scope of the quota capacity heuristic.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',64,'MESOS-9938','563','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9938\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 563, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Greg Mann\", \"summary\": \"Standalone container documentation\", \"assignee\": \"Joseph Wu\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Greg Mann\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Documentation\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We should add documentation for standalone containers.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',65,'MESOS-9958','563','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9958\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 563, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Benjamin Bannier\", \"summary\": \"New CLI is not included in distribution tarball\", \"assignee\": \"Benjamin Bannier\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Benjamin Bannier\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The files needed to build the new CLI are not included in distribution tarballs. This makes it impossible to build the CLI from released tarballs and users have instead build directly from the git sources.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('Meso',66,'MESOS-9942','565','{\"key\": \"MESOS-9942\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 565, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"summary\": \"Deprecate framework sorter.\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Meng Zhu\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"stor