e up this code so that it can be used inside XD.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',116,'XD-175','8','{\"key\": \"XD-175\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create and document a syslog aggregation example\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"2-3 containers (separate processes) that the stream: syslog | tcp 1 container (separate process) that aggregates the data sent from those conainers tcp | severityFilter | hdfs\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',117,'XD-169','8','{\"key\": \"XD-169\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"summary\": \"XD should run offline\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Trying to run XD offline results in an error in redis.xml because the cloudfoundry schema file is missing.  We need to add the cf-runtime jar to the classpath to resolve this.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',118,'XD-170','8','{\"key\": \"XD-170\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Home wiki page improvements\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Add more structure more easily find the reference guide.  The style that is here https://github.com/snowplow/snowplow/wikiis nice.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',119,'XD-171','8','{\"key\": \"XD-171\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create project home page for SpringXD on springsource.org/spring-xd\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"A minimal project page of a \'top level project\' page that has basic information of docs and links to the github wiki page. No need to list maven coordinates.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',120,'XD-221','8','{\"key\": \"XD-221\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Links in asciidoctor generated HTML+docbook documentation are broken\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The issue arises because the link:document[Label] asciidoc macro is meant for \\\"external documents\\\" and creates {{<ulink>}} in docbook / {{<a href=\\\"document\\\">}} in html whereas we want {{<link linkend=\\\"anchor\\\">}} / {{<a href=\\\"doc#anchor>}} resp. We also want it to continue working in github live view.I guess what could work is to have the macro (either override the link macro or create our own if github supports that) that looks like :{{link:document#anchor[Label]}}  (the #anchor works out of the box in asciidoc and should work in github) but override it for the html and docbook backends to render to the correct form.The thing is there are several ways to create/override macros (and templates they render to) some of which make sense to our setup:- having asciidoc.conf in the directory of the processed document (http://asciidoc.org/userguide.html#X27)- having docbook.conf/html.conf in the directory of the processed document (http://asciidoc.org/userguide.html#X27)- defining macros using attributes (http://asciidoc.org/userguide.html#_setting_configuration_entries)I tried all of those but to no avail. These DO WORK with plain asciidoc but not with our toolchain. Don\'t know if the problem is with asciidocTOR or with the gradle wrapper though.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',121,'XD-172','8','{\"key\": \"XD-172\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create links to SpringXD on other pages of springsource.org site\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"bottom home page - list of projectsdata/integration category landing pages - related projects.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',122,'XD-155','8','{\"key\": \"XD-155\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Add a groovy script processor module\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"A processor module that accepts either the location of a groovy script resource or an inline script (string). Also some discussion about a default classpath location for scripts. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',123,'XD-89','8','{\"key\": \"XD-89\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Documentation for gauge taps\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Put on the guide as a section in an \'input-stream\' wiki page.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',124,'XD-138','8','{\"key\": \"XD-138\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Prepare blog post for M1\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',125,'XD-137','8','{\"key\": \"XD-137\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Release Spring XD 1.0 M1\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',126,'XD-178','8','{\"key\": \"XD-178\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"DefaultContainer should have a default constructor that generates a UUID\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The current incrementAndGet approach based off redis will not easily be applicable in local model deployment\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',127,'XD-179','8','{\"key\": \"XD-179\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Have three startup scripts xd-singlenode xd-admin and xd-container\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The xd-singlenode script will launch a main application that creates both the admin node (to process http admin requests) and the container node (to execute modules for data processing) within in the same process the xd-admin script will launch a main application that creates only the admin node (remove current embeddedContainer options)the xd-container script will launch a main application that creates only the container node (as it is now)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',128,'XD-180','8','{\"key\": \"XD-180\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"The command line for xd-admin and xd-container to support an additional option pipeProtocol that is used to determine the middleware for sending admin requests and data between processing steps\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The name \'pipeProtocol\' is tentative.  1. The command line scripts for xd-admin and xd-container would support a --pipeProtocol option with the default being to use Redis.  (Otherwise use xd-singlenode).2. The xd-admin and xd-container scripts will use the value of pipeProtocol to set the java system property xd.pipeProtocol when launching the app.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',129,'XD-181','8','{\"key\": \"XD-181\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Update launcher.xml to have protocol independent beans defined and an import statement to load protocol specific defintiions from a system property defined location.\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"launcher.xml can make use of the system property xd.pipeProtocol inside an import statement.  This determines which version of the XD infrastructure to load for example what ChannelRegistry implementation Local or Redis based or specific message listener containers. File name conventions should be used so if the option passed in from the command line is --pipeProtocol localChannelthen the XML filename looked for has the \'Protocol\' suffix applied e.g. localChannelProtocol and is loaded via the classpath.Redis and Local will not be the only options other implementations will be provided in the future e.g. Rabbit and the user may be able to provide their own implementations of these infrastructure classes (an advanced task).  \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',130,'XD-182','8','{\"key\": \"XD-182\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create redisProtocol.xml that will load all the Redis specific implementations to suppor the XD container runtime and administration\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The redis specific beans that are defined in the current launcher.xml should move into this configuration file.   \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',131,'XD-183','8','{\"key\": \"XD-183\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create localChannelProtocol.xml that will load all the SI specific implementations to suppor the XD container runtime and administration\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',132,'XD-184','8','{\"key\": \"XD-184\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Add unregistration support to the channel registry\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',133,'XD-188','8','{\"key\": \"XD-188\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Add  directory to classpath in server startup scripts so groovy based processors can be easily referenced by name without a resource uri prefix\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"a stream such as time | filter --script=oddMinuteFilter.groovy | file would load the groovy script \'oddMinuteFilter.groovy\' that is located in the directory modules/processor or perhaps in modules/processor/scripts.Not sure the benefit of having a subdirectory below processor just for scripts.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',134,'XD-150','8','{\"key\": \"XD-150\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Publish Spring XD final distribution zip as part of Bamboo artifactory plugin\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently Bamboo\'s gradle artifactory plugin has the artifacts configured to projects target(build) directory \'archives\'. We need to have a way to set the final distribution archive as one of the gradle \'configurations\' in our build.gradle and refer it inside bamboo artifacts.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',135,'XD-192','8','{\"key\": \"XD-192\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Update getting started documentation to use xd-singlenode start script.\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"With the new option of starting without requiring redis the getting started documentation should reflect this easier way to start processing data.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',136,'XD-193','8','{\"key\": \"XD-193\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Need more unique resource locations for XD internal configuration\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently internal config files are in META-INF/spring with fairly generic names. To avoid potential collisions if users add their own configuration in the classpath we should have a more unique location e.g. META-INF/spring/xd\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',137,'XD-195','8','{\"key\": \"XD-195\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"The {{time}} Source Should Emit String by Default\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"When running in local mode (no Redis) {{time | tcp}} no longer works.Change the {{time}} source to emit the date as a String while allowing an option to emit a {{Date}} object.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',138,'XD-197','8','{\"key\": \"XD-197\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create a scriptProcessor module that allows the execution of a groovy (potentially jrubyjython) based SI Service Activator\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"This will enable arbitrary processing logic to be used in a processing step.See http://blog.springsource.org/2011/12/08/spring-integration-scripting-support-part-1/<int:service-activator ...>  <script:script lang=\\\"groovy\\\" location=\\\"file:scripts/groovy/myscript.groovy\\\"></int:service-activator>would be the essence of the module.  Probably \'lang\' gets detected from the file extension.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',139,'XD-199','8','{\"key\": \"XD-199\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Ensure the DELETE Operation can Delete a Tap\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"While deleting a stream doesn\'t remove any taps right now we should be able to explicitly delete a tap.Determine whether the current DELETE works and if not make it so.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',140,'XD-187','8','{\"key\": \"XD-187\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Create XD script for xd-single node\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"This script will launch XD admin along with the module container.As part of this implementation we will also remove the embedded options for XD admin & container scripts.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',141,'XD-200','8','{\"key\": \"XD-200\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Creating a tap throws an exception\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Creating a tap throws an exception. In local mode: Cannot resolve reference to bean \'redisConnectionFactory\' while setting constructor argument; nested exception is org.springframework.beans.factory.NoSuchBeanDefinitionException: No bean named \'redisConnectionFactory\' is defined  But also fails when using redis.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',142,'XD-185','8','{\"key\": 