 \"replace the hacky parser with a good one\", \"assignee\": \"Andy Clement\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Andy Clement\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Replace the existing DSL parser that uses string indexing with a more robust one based on a derivative of SpEL.  This will provide a stable base on which to quickly iterate on syntax.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',152,'XD-207','8','{\"key\": \"XD-207\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Provide configurable properties for hdfs sink.\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The config file modules/sink/hdfs.xml has a hardcoded value to locate the namenode.<hdp:configuration register-url-handler=\\\"false\\\">fs.default.name=hdfs://localhost:9000</hdp:configuration>the fs.default.name proprety should be configurable and we should also support loading an external configuration file using    <hdp:configuration properties-location=\\\"${xd.home}/config/hadoop.properties\\\">   </hdp:configuration>\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',153,'XD-141','8','{\"key\": \"XD-141\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"install-redis script should not use relative path to determine redis source dist\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently the install-redis script uses relative path to determine redis source  dist file. Since this is error prone we need to fix it.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',154,'XD-213','8','{\"key\": \"XD-213\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 8, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Temporarily add toString() Logic in Local Mode Inter-Module Comms\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',155,'XD-231','9','{\"key\": \"XD-231\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Add Twitter gardenhose source module\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"we have a prototype gardenhose adapter that was built directly upon RestTemplate (streaming on a background thread) but Spring Social Twitter has an issue on its 1.1 roadmap that is relevant:https://jira.springsource.org/browse/SOCIALTW-2\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',156,'XD-230','9','{\"key\": \"XD-230\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Add RabbitMQ source module\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"configurable parameters should include the queue-name(s) and optional binding key patternconnection info such as host and port should also be configurable but with defaults (localhost and default port) and that should likely fallback to a rabbit.properties file in the $XD_HOME/config directory\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',157,'XD-242','9','{\"key\": \"XD-242\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Add JMS source module\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',158,'XD-176','9','{\"key\": \"XD-176\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"summary\": \"Support exponential moving average in RichGauge \", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 0.0, \"description\": \"This could easily be supported in the existing gauge by adding a setAlpha method to RichGaugeService and adding the extra parameter \\\"alpha\\\" to the gauge data (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exponential_moving_average). If not set it would default to the current behaviour (simple mean) otherwise it would calculate the exponential moving average in place of the mean.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',159,'XD-144','9','{\"key\": \"XD-144\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Remove Log4j Properties/XMLs from Projects\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"If say xd-dirt is ahead of a local config on the classpath it\'s log4j.properties is found first.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',160,'XD-164','9','{\"key\": \"XD-164\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Validate processing modules declare the required channels\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Validate that modules have required channels declared according to their type.  Currently the stream deployer accepts processors with no input but the stream doesn\'t complete. We should fail earlier and more loudly.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',161,'XD-160','9','{\"key\": \"XD-160\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"summary\": \"Publish golo themed docs documentation to static.springsource.org as part of nightly build\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The wiki repo contains a script gen-docs.sh that we are planning to use to generate a pretty HTML version of the Getting Started guide. We should consider using maven (or gradle but there is currently an issue documented in build.gradle) to generate this and other reference docs and publish them automatically as part of a nightly build.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',162,'XD-226','9','{\"key\": \"XD-226\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Cleanup and Optimize gradle tasks to bundle spring-xd distribution\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"We need to cleanup some of the duplicate gradle tasks that bundle spring-xd distributions. Currently distXD does the copy of distributions from \\\"spring-xd-dirt\\\" \\\"redis\\\" and \\\"spring-xd-gemfire-server\\\" projects into \\\"$rootDir/dist/spring-xd\\\".And the task \\\"zipXD\\\" makes the zip archive.These tasks should be combined with the \\\"distZip\\\" & \\\"docZip\\\" tasks.We also need to remove the duplicate artifacts configuration from these tasks.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',163,'XD-262','9','{\"key\": \"XD-262\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Convert current REST servlet to Spring MVC\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 3.0, \"issueLinks\": 3.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 3.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',164,'XD-264','9','{\"key\": \"XD-264\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Spring MVC infrastructure tests\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',165,'XD-142','9','{\"key\": \"XD-142\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"StreamServer Context Lifecycle Issues\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The {{ModuleDeployer}} calls {{getBeansOfType}} before the context has had its {{PropertySourcesPlaceholderConfigurer}} attached. This can cause issues with {{FactoryBean}} s with placeholders in constructor args because the unresolved placeholder is used when the {{FactoryBean}} is pre-instantiated to determine the type of object it will serve up.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',166,'XD-268','9','{\"key\": \"XD-268\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Streamline command-line arg management\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Command line arguments (and especially their default values) are currently scattered around different places.The aim is to regroup those in a common place (*Options classes make sense).Also not very happy with how System properties are used as a vehicle for options.transport / options.home\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',167,'XD-294','9','{\"key\": \"XD-294\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 9, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Apply JavaDoc HotFix\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',168,'XD-260','10','{\"key\": \"XD-260\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Add command for listing streams\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',169,'XD-263','10','{\"key\": \"XD-263\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Support GET /streams\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 2.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Pagination support maybe querying by name as well\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 2.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',170,'XD-244','10','{\"key\": \"XD-244\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Michael Minella\", \"summary\": \"Create a Trigger\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Michael Minella\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 2.0, \"issueLinks\": 3.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"h2. NarrativeAs the XD system I need to be able to execute a job (or potentially a stream) based on a given condition (time data existence etc).  This story is intended is for a local trigger implementation but remote triggers will also need to exist.h2.  Acceptance Criteria# Implement the ability to register a time based trigger {{trigger <CRON_STRING>}} for example# Implement the ability to register a file existence based trigger {{trigger <PATH>}} for example# Implement the ability to execute a job via an anonymous trigger: {{job_name @ <CRON_STRING OR PATH>}}# Implement the ability to execute a job via a job via the previously registered trigger: {{job_name @ trigger_name}}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 2.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',171,'XD-317','10','{\"key\": \"XD-317\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Add Documentation Chapter on Executing Batch Jobs\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',172,'XD-315','10','{\"key\": \"XD-315\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Package Shell \\\"binary\\\" next to xd-admin and xd-container\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The shell should be an \'executable\' delivered out of the box in much the same way that xd-container and xd-admin are right now. If we follow how redis/mongo distribut the shell it sits side by side with the other binaries\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',173,'XD-339','10','{\"key\": \"XD-339\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Investigate using profiler when doing the performance testing\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Investigate how efficiently we can integrate profiler into the performance test.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',174,'XD-236','10','{\"key\": \"XD-236\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create an Aggregate Counter\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"An aggregate counter rolls up counts into discrete time buckets.  There is an existing POC implementation in Java based off the libraryhttps://github.com/thheller/timed-counter The README there has a good description of the desired feature set.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',175,'XD-334','10','{\"key\": \"XD-334\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Document the structure of the REST API\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',176,'XD-255','10','{\"key\": \"XD-255\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Set up a project for XD Shell\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Set up a basic Spring Shell project for XD Shell\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',177,'XD-256','10','{\"key\": \"XD-256\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Create a banner page for XD Shell\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.