d the use of \\\"track\\\" (https://dev.twitter.com/docs/streaming-apis/parameters#track) as well as other request parameters (delimited language etc).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',184,'XD-335','10','{\"key\": \"XD-335\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Review DSL\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 14.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"updated story points to 14 since 5 of us just participated in a 2 hour call and we still need to discuss \\\"topology\\\" support after some dev spikes later this week\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',185,'XD-336','10','{\"key\": \"XD-336\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Document Splunk source sink\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',186,'XD-301','10','{\"key\": \"XD-301\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Request to create a repo for Spring XD performance testing\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"It would be nice if we have a git repo for Spring XD performance testing.This would enable us to have a common repository (rather than inside spring-xd as a subproject) for all performance related code specific to any module message middleware etc. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',187,'XD-296','10','{\"key\": \"XD-296\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"summary\": \"Add log config file to gemfire in final distro\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The changes for XD-144 mean that log4j files are no longer in the library jars. The admin server already has a logging configuration which should be activated by the startup scripts but the separate gemfire app doesn\'t.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',188,'XD-337','10','{\"key\": \"XD-337\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Test connection pooling on Redis blocking/nonblocking operations\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',189,'XD-292','10','{\"key\": \"XD-292\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Verrol Adams\", \"summary\": \"Redis \'install-redis\' script fails on Ubuntu64\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Verrol Adams\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The installation script for redis fails on Ubuntu64 when trying to untar the redis distribution.  The script uses REDIS_ZIPNAME instead of REDIS_ZIP_PATH.  This bug will be seen on any Linux 64 bits platform and looking at the code even Linux 32 bits platform.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',190,'XD-245','10','{\"key\": \"XD-245\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Michael Minella\", \"summary\": \"Deploy Batch Jobs on XD\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Minella\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Michael Minella\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"h2. NarrativeAs a developer I need a way to deploy job configurations as well as the related custom code to XD.h2.  Acceptance Criteria# Provide the ability to register jobs that have been deployed as modules via something like {{curl -d \\\"job\\\" http://localhost:8080/streams/myJob}} where job is the name of the job definition located in /modules/job and myJob is the name of the resulting registered job# Confirm that both \\\"regular\\\" jobs and Spring Hadoop based jobs can be packaged/run.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',191,'XD-342','10','{\"key\": \"XD-342\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 10, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Fix classpath error caused by multiple conflicting servlet-api jars\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"There is some conflicting Servlet API jars on the claspath that needs cleanup. Building and running with xd-singlenode script gave this error:Jun 27 2013 3:18:16 PM org.apache.coyote.http11.AbstractHttp11Processor processSEVERE: Error processing requestjava.lang.NoSuchMethodError: javax.servlet.ServletContext.getEffectiveSessionTrackingModes()Ljava/util/Set;at org.apache.catalina.connector.CoyoteAdapter.postParseRequest(CoyoteAdapter.java:674)at org.apache.catalina.connector.CoyoteAdapter.service(CoyoteAdapter.java:402)at org.apache.coyote.http11.AbstractHttp11Processor.process(AbstractHttp11Processor.java:1004)at org.apache.coyote.AbstractProtocol$AbstractConnectionHandler.process(AbstractProtocol.java:589)at org.apache.tomcat.util.net.JIoEndpoint$SocketProcessor.run(JIoEndpoint.java:310)at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.runTask(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:895)at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:918)at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:680)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',192,'XD-355','11','{\"key\": \"XD-355\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 11, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Enable configuration of Executors in source and sink modules by default using Dispatchers in parent context\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Need to understand how individual modules may or may not share Dispatchers that are part of the parent context.  If modules have their own dispatchers those also need to be configurable.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',193,'XD-162','11','{\"key\": \"XD-162\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 11, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Create design document for implementation strategy to support message conversion in ChannelRegistry\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 7.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The conversion should be based on content-type headers similar to the way Spring\'s HttpMessageConverters work (with mime types).Also the map of available converters should be extensible while including the most common defaults (for JSON XML etc). We most likely want to add a few of our own content types also (e.g. for Tuples).Most likely this logic and the configuration methods for extending the converter map belong in AbstractChannelRegistry since it should be common across all implementations (i.e. the logic should be the same regardless of the transport used after-serialization/before-deserialization).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',194,'XD-375','11','{\"key\": \"XD-375\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 11, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Command to delete tap\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',195,'XD-371','11','{\"key\": \"XD-371\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 11, \"st