\"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Extend the DSL in the following ways:- stream naming use <name>\'=\'{code}mystream = http | file{code}- module aliasing (for later referencing) use <label>\':\'{code}mystream = http | t1: transform --expression=payload.toUpperCase() | t2: transform --expression=payload.toLowerCase(){code}- sequence of job steps with \'&\'{code}mybigjobby = step1 --option=value & step2 --option=value{code}- Channels for sources and sinks use \'>\' channels references prefixed \':\'{code}// sink channel called foohttp | transform --expression=payload.toUppercase() > :foo// source channel called foo:foo > count | file{code}- Qualify channels with a stream \':\'<stream>\'.\'<channel>{code}mystream = http | transform --expression=payload.toUppercase() > :foo:mystream.foo > count | log{code}- Reusable substreams define then reuse{code}myIntricateFlow = transform --expression=payload.toUppercase() | transform --expression=payload.toLowercase()http | myIntricateFlow | file{code}- Parameterized substreams use $XX or ${XX} to indicate parameters{code}obfuscateName = transform --expression=payload.replaceAll(\\\"${name}\\\"XXX)twitter --query=Bieber | obfuscateName --name=Justin | file{code}- Tapping (still not 100% happy about the format here){code}mystream = http | filter | t1: transform XXX | t2: transform YYY | file// These are then equivalent (tapping on a module is effectively tapping a channel hence the \'>\')tap filter > count | filetap mystream.filter > count | filemystream = http | filter > :footap :foo > count | filetap :mystream.foo > count | file{code}I\'d still like to thing about removing \'tap\' and using a symbol (perhaps \'@\' but @:mystream.foo is a little odd)still not covered topological constraints on the stream components.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',230,'XD-367','13','{\"key\": \"XD-367\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 13, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Final review of REST API structure document for streams taps and jobs\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Get closure on open discussion points for REST API wrt to streams taps and jobs.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',231,'XD-162','13','{\"key\": \"XD-162\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 13, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Create design document for implementation strategy to support message conversion in ChannelRegistry\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 7.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The conversion should be based on content-type headers similar to the way Spring\'s HttpMessageConverters work (with mime types).Also the map of available converters should be extensible while including the most common defaults (for JSON XML etc). We most likely want to add a few of our own content types also (e.g. for Tuples).Most likely this logic and the configuration methods for extending the converter map belong in AbstractChannelRegistry since it should be common across all implementations (i.e. the logic should be the same regardless of the transport used after-serialization/before-deserialization).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',232,'XD-375','13','{\"key\": \"XD-375\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 13, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Command to delete tap\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',233,'XD-371','13','{\"key\": \"XD-371\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 13, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Command for creating a job\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"optional --autostart switch to also deploy the job\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',234,'XD-372','13','{\"key\": \"XD-372\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 13, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Command to deploy a job\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Deploy an existing job. Must exist in the JobsRepository\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',235,'XD-363','13','{\"key\": \"XD-363\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 13, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Add support for creating fixed delay/ fixed rate triggers\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 