rvice layer (doesn\'t do much right now and logic would better live in the \'Handler\' IMO)4) Have REST controllers depend on XRepository in all cases\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',326,'XD-538','16','{\"key\": \"XD-538\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Develop infrastructure to enable testability of commands\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"This requires to boostrap the singlenode admin server in process submit commands to the shell programmatically and assert on the results of executing the command.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',327,'XD-539','16','{\"key\": \"XD-539\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"summary\": \"Investigate using Redis txs and pipeline for Inbound/Outbound Q Adapter perf improvements\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Investigate using transactions and pipelining to improve performance of both the inbound and outbound RedisQueue channel adapters. Involves testing against a pre-release of SDR 1.1 M2.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',328,'XD-540','16','{\"key\": \"XD-540\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Broadcast Undeploy Requests\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Use an \'undeploy\' topic to broadcast undeploy requests to all containers.Applies to Redis and Rabbit transports not local.Also rename {{ModuleDeploymentRequest}} to {{ModuleOperationRequest}} with an enum {{DEPLOY}} {{UNDEPLOY}}.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',329,'XD-542','16','{\"key\": \"XD-542\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Refactor Module to Encapsulate Group and Index\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently many methods take module group index - defining a module instance; group and index can be encapsulated in {{Module}} so one arg can be passed around.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',330,'XD-554','16','{\"key\": \"XD-554\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Separate Module Context Refresh from Context Start\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Split plugin module processing into pre and post processing where preprocessing is done before the context is refreshed and post processing is done after the refresh but before the start.In the Stream plugin wire the module into the {{ChannelRegistry}} during post processing instead of using the {{ChannelRegistrar}}.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',331,'XD-545','16','{\"key\": \"XD-545\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Display a counter\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',332,'XD-551','16','{\"key\": \"XD-551\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Add \\\"trigger list\\\" support to Spring XD Shell\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',333,'XD-430','16','{\"key\": \"XD-430\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Use a Different Default Jolokia Port for Admin Vs. Container\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Avoid the need for {{--jmxPort=xxxx}} when running both a {{Container}} and {{Admin}} on the same server\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',334,'XD-561','16','{\"key\": \"XD-561\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Failure when creating/deploying stream leaves invalid stream registry/definitions in the Repository implementations.\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"reproduce1) Create a bad stream definition name \'bad\'Try to recreate with the same name but correct stream definitions.  The system will report that the stream already exists.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',335,'XD-556','16','{\"key\": \"XD-556\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Andrew Eisenberg\", \"summary\": \"CORS support\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Andrew Eisenberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"XD instances will not accept xhr requests from browsers whose page origin does not match the XD instance.  As an example the Kodiak UI is served from a different process (and url) than the XD instance.  When users open the Kodiak UI in a browser requests from the browser to the XD instance but these requests will fail due to cross-site scripting limitations.CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) is a way to get around this.  We can configure the server to accept requests from browsers whose origins are not the XD instance.I have this working in a local branch and will submit a pull request.More information:CORS Spec: http://www.w3.org/TR/cors/SPR-9278 CORS support for SpringFramework\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',336,'XD-563','16','{\"key\": \"XD-563\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Regression test existing functionality of stream/taps based on introduction of new conversion functionality\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"make sure nothing is broken - spot check using.1) ticktock2) twitter3) gemfire\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',337,'XD-565','16','{\"key\": \"XD-565\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Documentation for using a specific Hadoop distribution\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Show how to select a specific hadoop distribution when starting embedded/standalone XDContainer.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',338,'XD-566','16','{\"key\": \"XD-566\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Document JDBC module\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affected