", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',345,'XD-503','16','{\"key\": \"XD-503\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Jobs are created even though they have an invalid definition\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Also if you deploy the Job it will fail but then you can\'t delete the job.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',346,'XD-577','16','{\"key\": \"XD-577\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"In documentation replace usage of \'raw\' hadoop command with shell \'hadoop\' commands\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',347,'XD-579','16','{\"key\": \"XD-579\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Modify startup script of xd shell to allow specifying hadoop distro to use\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',348,'XD-575','16','{\"key\": \"XD-575\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Change http command to post data by putting \'http\' as the main command option\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The current http command is of the formhttp://localhost:8080:>post httpsource --target http://localhost:9090 --data 10It isn\'t intuitive to think \'post\' rather the command can be http post --target http://localhost:9090 --data 10which will allow us to have support for other http verbs and cleanly separate the namespace from \'hadoop\' etc.The RestShell from which this came was only concerned with http actions so the leading command classification probably seemed superfluous.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',349,'XD-576','16','{\"key\": \"XD-576\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Change banner of shell to say only \'xd\'\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',350,'XD-574','16','{\"key\": \"XD-574\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Replace usage of \'raw\' curl with shell command to post http data in documentation\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"e.g. http://localhost:8080:>post httpsource --target http://localhost:9090 --data 10I believe this will also help to avoid ugly syntax to escaping quotes for json as in the gemfire example.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',351,'XD-581','16','{\"key\": \"XD-581\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 16, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"configuration conflict when using \\\"--transport\\\" \\\"local\\\" \\\"--store\\\" \\\"redis\\\" \\\"--disableJmx\\\" \\\"true\\\" \\\"--analytics\\\" \\\"redis\\\"\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"results in both in-memory and redis based definitions of RichGaugeService - can\'t satisfy autowiring because there are two candidates.Had to change --analytics=memory to get the application context to load.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',352,'XD-661','18','{\"key\": \"XD-661\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Batch Jobs: Add the ability to provide JobParameters\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',353,'XD-656','18','{\"key\": \"XD-656\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Intra-Module \\\"Pipe\\\" Naming\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Consider 2 Admins/Containers that are using discrete Redis instances but a shared Rabbit instance for the transport.If two different streams are deployed on each but with the same stream name the Rabbit queues will be common (e.g. foo.0) causing crosstalk.Stream names must be unique across all container instances sharing Rabbit infrastructure.I am not sure what the solution is; two instances of the *same* stream *do* need common queues but instances of different streams need a qualifier of some kind (container name?). I guess it\'s not *that* big of an issue because if they\'re sharing infrastructure they\'re likely to be sharing a stream repo too - in which case you\'d need unique stream names.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',354,'XD-552','18','{\"key\": \"XD-552\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Kashyap Parikh\", \"summary\": \"Add status column for \'stream list\'  shell command result\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Kashyap Parikh\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"{{stream list}} shell command should display status of the stream (deployed undeployed)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',355,'XD-645','18','{\"key\": \"XD-645\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"summary\": \"Find a way to contribute redis.properties to Rabbit Container PPC\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Need to undo the recent add of rabbit.properties to xd-common.xml. Tried to work around this by configuring rabbit-container with only the PPC it needs (pointing to only rabbit.properties) but this caused issues with redis-analytics later requiring redis.properties. Would be nice to have a way for redis-analytics to contribute redis.properties or something similar...Also strictly speaking the local admin server does not even need redis.properties let alone rabbit.properties so we should find a cleaner way to configure this.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',356,'XD-588','18','{\"key\": \"XD-588\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"RedisAggregateCounterRepository doesn\'t give proper results back\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Both Luke\'s original code and my refactored PR[1] (which uses same code snippet) seem to behave strangely.Stored values seem fine but the getCounts() method seems phony.To test:1) stream create foo --definition \\\"time|log\\\"2) tap create bar --definition \\\"tap@foo | aggregatecounter\\\"3) curl -H \\\"application/json\\\" http://localhost:8080/metrics/aggregate-counters/barthis gives default bucketing (hourly) but chances are that they are empty. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',357,'XD-597','18','{\"key\": \"XD-597\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Ad-Hoc Job needs to have option for launch and forget\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"When running an ad-hoc job without the use of a trigger (adhoc or named).  The user has to wait for job to complete before receiving a success.  We need to launch a job and get a success back to the user letting them know the job has been launched.for example --immediate\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',358,'XD-678','18','{\"key\": \"XD-678\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"change accepted-media-types to accpted-content-types\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',359,'XD-683','18','{\"key\": \"XD-683\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Change jmxDisabled option to jmxEnabled and do not enable by default\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"also the current behavior is broken; it checks if the property is set but does not actually check whether it\'s true or false\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',360,'XD-675','18','{\"key\": \"XD-675\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Cannot chain json-field-value-filter & json-field-extractor\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Because StringToJsonNodeTransformer expects a String as input one cannot chain json related processors.A simple solution would be to also accept Jackson IN and forward it directly in that case.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',361,'XD-600','18','{\"key\": \"XD-600\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Add deploy/undeploy/destroy \'all\' commands for all applicable resources (streams tap job & trigger)\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',362,'XD-690','18','{\"key\": \"XD-690\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Simplify \\\"instance\\\" deployment code \", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"AbstractDeployer has 4 subclasses 3 of which override e.g. deploy() making the boilerplate factorization ineffective.Introduce an intermediate class for those deployers that support the concept of an instance (Stream Tap Job to some extent)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',363,'XD-693','18','{\"key\": \"XD-693\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Add deploy/undeploy commands for taps\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',364,'XD-695','18','{\"key\": \"XD-695\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade SDR to get rid of temporary no-op serializer\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Spring Data Redis 1.1 M2 added the ability to use RedisTemplate with binary data. We should switch to that instead of the no-op serializer we were forced to implement previously.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',365,'XD-662','18','{\"key\": \"XD-662\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"summary\": \"No indication of failure in shell when deploying job referencing nonexistent trigger\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"I see the following output on the shell if I create a job and reference a non-existent trigger. There\'s a big stack trace in the server log but nothing on the shell side indicating failure. A subsequent \\\"jobs list\\\" also shows the job. The same thing happens if I deploy an undeployed Job after deleting its associated Trigger.$ job create --name helloWorldJob --definition \\\"myjob --trigger=nonexistenttrigger\\\"Successfully created and deployed job \'helloWorldJob\'\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',366,'XD-702','18','{\"key\": \"XD-702\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"stack overflow when trying to create a stream with the same name as a module\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"(NOTE: even if we do want to prevent the use of module names for stream names we obviously need to avoid a StackOverflowError)to reproduce:start the xd-singlenode containerstart the xd-shell and type the following:{code}xd:>stream create time --definition \\\"time | log\\\"{code}that should produce an Internal Server Error output messagecheck the xd-singlenode console and find:{code}SEVERE: Servlet.service() for servlet [xd] in context with path [] threw exception [Handler processing failed; nested exception is java.lang.StackOverflowError] with root causejava.lang.StackOverflowErrorat java.lang.StringValue.from(StringValue.java:24)at java.lang.String.<init>(String.java:178)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.Token.<init>(Token.java:46)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.Tokenizer.lexIdentifier(Tokenizer.java:195)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.Tokenizer.process(Tokenizer.java:62)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.Tokenizer.<init>(Tokenizer.java:41)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamConfigParser.parse(StreamConfigParser.java:65)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamConfigParser.parse(StreamConfigParser.java:55)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamConfigParser.lookupStream(StreamConfigParser.java:545)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamNode.resolveModuleNodes(StreamNode.java:135)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamNode.resolve(StreamNode.java:122)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamsNode.resolve(StreamsNode.java:53)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamConfigParser.parse(StreamConfigParser.java:74)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamConfigParser.parse(StreamConfigParser.java:55)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamConfigParser.lookupStream(StreamConfigParser.java:545)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamNode.resolveModuleNodes(StreamNode.java:135)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamNode.resolve(StreamNode.java:122)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamsNode.resolve(StreamsNode.java:53)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamConfigParser.parse(StreamConfigParser.java:74)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamConfigParser.parse(StreamConfigParser.java:55)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamConfigParser.lookupStream(StreamConfigParser.java:545)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamNode.resolveModuleNodes(StreamNode.java:135)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamNode.resolve(StreamNode.java:122)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.dsl.StreamsNode.resolve(StreamsNode.java:53)...ad nauseum{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',367,'XD-682','18','{\"key\": \"XD-682\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Modify file sink to avoid dot with empty suffix\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 5.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The expression currently appends \\\".\\\" + ${suffix} (where the default suffix is \'out\').If the suffix value were an empty String this would lead to the file name ending with a dot. We should update the expression so that it only appends the dot if the suffix is not empty. This might be possible with a ternary expression.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',368,'XD-692','18','{\"key\": \"XD-692\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"http source module should copy Content-Type header to SI MessageHeaders.CONTENT_TYPE\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',369,'XD-704','18','{\"key\": \"XD-704\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 18, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"summary\": \"User should be able to specify Rabbit virtual host\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Need to support Rabbit virtual host property in properties file and as args to Rabbit source and sink\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',370,'XD-703','19','{\"key\": \"XD-703\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"JobRepository should be persistent and shared across xd-admin/xd-container\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The current code is creating an in-memory job repository for each batch job that is launched.  This makes it impossible to query the tables in the job repository across the cluster.  A single job repository that is backed by a file need to be shared across all jobs that are a launched.*Implementation Suggestions** The XDAdmin server should create the job repository schema if not found in a HSQLDB database when it starts up* The bean definitions should be added to the same context that the analytics are being loaded in as it is already shared across xd-admin/xd-container.  The ΓÇÿanalyticsΓÇÖ context should be renamed to something more generic ΓÇÿshared parent contextΓÇÖ or something.* There is some clean up (removal) of the code in the current JobPlugin META-INF/spring-xd/plugins/job/common.xml wouldnΓÇÖt be needed anymore.  That might be all not sure.*How to verify it works** A JUnit test that verifies the spring batch tables were created in the job repository when xd-admin is launched.  This would require deleting the backing db file before instantiating singlenode/xd-admin/xd-container.* If you start the xd-container it should be able to find the necessary DataSource/JobRepository beans information to be able to contact the database.  We donΓÇÖt have DI style JUnit tests so this will required getting a reference to the xd-container and itΓÇÖs application context and performing ΓÇÿgetBean(JobRepository.class)ΓÇÖ\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',371,'XD-705','19','{\"key\": \"XD-705\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"A batch job can be launched by sending a message on a channel\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 16.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"*Description*  When a job is ΓÇÿcreatedΓÇÖ in SpringXD a ΓÇÿcontrol-channelΓÇÖ for that job is also created.  The listener for that channel will receive a message be able to take the ΓÇÿjobParametersΓÇÖ and other launch information from the message and be able to launch/run the job.NOTE: I can see a few other stories that should probably be made to break this up after writing it. I put estimate of 10 for now but we should break this up.  Here are some suggestions1. create ΓÇÿdata onlyΓÇÖ JobParametersBean equivalent with primitive types2. create jobLauncher source3. create jobParameterTransformer processor4. Refactoring of ChannelRegistryΓÇÖs aliasHing to use a callback strategy.*Implementation Suggestions*job create --name helloWorldJob --definition \\\"myjob --somePropertyToOverride=someValue* This would not execute the batch job immediately but instead register the job definition and deploys a ΓÇ£jobLauncherΓÇ¥ and the job definition to an XD-Container.* The XD-Container that receives the deploy request message will create a module application context will also create a channel with the Channel registry named after the job e.g. :myJob.  This should be a pub/sub channel from the point of view of the middleware.  From the point of view of the spring integration channel it should ideally be of the executor channel.  There is a limitation in the current implementation of ChannelRegistry now as ΓÇÿcreateInboundΓÇÖ only creates direct channels.  The boolean ΓÇÿaliasHintΓÇÖ should probably be extended to some type of callback that creates a channel.  The aliasHint was added to address the case of LocalChannelRegistry creating or looking up a queue backed channel or a direct channel.There will be a consumer on the SI channel in the module application context that will be responsible for getting the job launch information and launching the job.  The launching of the job may need to be explicitly done in a separate thread if direct channels are created by the ChannelRegistry.  The contents of the message should be something similar to the current ΓÇ£JobParametersBeanΓÇ¥ it needs to be easily serializable with simple types via JSON over the wire.  The current impl of ΓÇ£JobParametersBeanΓÇ¥ has ObjectMapper so that may require a bit of reworking.  The handler of the message will use the jobLauncher to launch the job using the information in the JobParametersBean.* The ΓÇÿmyjobΓÇÖ can then be launched by sending a message perhaps this is handled by having a jobLauncher sourcejobLauncher [--jobParameters <jobParameters>] [--dateFormat <dateFormat>] [--numberFormat <numberFormat>] [--makeUnique <makeUnique>]  > :myJobe.g. with no-argsjobLauncher  > :myJob*How to verify it works*With the test HelloSpringXDTasklet we should be able to create the jobjob create --name helloSpringXD --definition \\\"myjob\\\"This will not launch the job (as mentioned in the ΓÇÿimplementationΓÇÖ section.It would then be launched by jobLauncher  > :myJobwhere jobLauncher is a new source.Ideally would like to be able to test a data driven triggering.  This would require a new file source that doesnΓÇÖt use the file-to-string-transformer but lets a File object be the payload.file | jobParameterTransformer > :myJob\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',372,'XD-353','19','{\"key\": \"XD-353\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Clean up Spring Configuration\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 3.0, \"issueLinks\": 5.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"- Container context should be separate from Admin Context in local mode (consistency across transports). Provide a LocalChannelRegistry to bridge deploy and undeploy channels to the ModuleDeployer- Verify Plugins are not in common module context. They are\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 3.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',373,'XD-708','19','{\"key\": \"XD-708\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Add SingleNodeMain class \", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"SingleNodeMain(){  parent = new AC(..)   AdminMain.launch(parent);   ContainerMain.launch(parent);}This should make startup processing more consistent and symmetrical\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',374,'XD-714','19','{\"key\": \"XD-714\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Rename Plugin.postProcessSharedContext to preProcessSharedContext\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The above method is invoked before the shared context is refreshed. preProcess... is more accurate\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',375,'XD-709','19','{\"key\": \"XD-709\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Refactor TriggerPlugin \", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Remove unnecessary code that adds beans to shared context after refreshScheduler should not be in common.xml - register it in TriggerPlugin.postProcessSharedContext()\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',376,'XD-710','19','{\"key\": \"XD-710\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Update JavaDocs in Plugin interface\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Update JavaDocs in Plugin interface to clearly describe the Plugin contract i.e.  where in the lifecycle each method is invoked\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',377,'XD-711','19','{\"key\": \"XD-711\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"MBeanServer should not be declared in module common configuration\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Register in MBeanExportingPlugin.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',378,'XD-716','19','{\"key\": \"XD-716\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"summary\": \"TapCommandTests hangs when using a lazily instantiated Lettuce connection\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"A change was made in spring-data-redis to instantiate the shared Lettuce connection lazily instead of when the context is initialized. This caused TapCommandTests to hang due to a Netty worker thread trying to initialize the Lettuce connection (Lettuce uses Netty). The change was temporarily backed out of SDR but we need to consider using a NettyExecutionHandler in NettyHttpInboundChannelAdapter or making the HTTP module\'s \\\"input\\\" channel an ExecutorChannel to avoid potentially long operations like from happening in an I/O thread.Also we need to address why this failure simply hangs the shell. Shell was hung waiting on IO here:at org.springframework.http.client.SimpleClientHttpResponse.getRawStatusCode(SimpleClientHttpResponse.java:47)at org.springframework.http.client.AbstractClientHttpResponse.getStatusCode(AbstractClientHttpResponse.java:32)at org.springframework.xd.shell.command.HttpCo