Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Upgrade Lettuce to 2.3.3 and subsequently Netty to 3.6.6\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',380,'XD-722','19','{\"key\": \"XD-722\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Batch jobs send job and step events on channels \", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"This is the other side of launching a job by sending a message.  The Job plugin should add listeners at the job/step level so that the job/step context information can be sent out on a channel.:myjob.notifications is a suggested channel name that would be created automatically.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',381,'XD-717','19','{\"key\": \"XD-717\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"cat command doesn\'t work when same data is listed in file multiple times\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"$ ./xd-admin --transport redis$ ./xd-container --transport redis$ ./xd-container --transport redisxd:>stream create --name httpStream --definition \\\"http | file\\\"Created new stream \'httpStream\'xd:>tap create --name httpTap --definition \\\"tap httpStream | counter\\\"Created and deployed new tap \'httpTap\'xd:>http post --target http://localhost:9000 --data \\\"helloworld\\\"> POST (text/plain;Charset=UTF-8) http://localhost:9000 helloworld> 200 OKxd:>! cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outcommand is:cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outhelloworldxd:>http post --target http://localhost:9000 --data \\\"helloworld\\\"> POST (text/plain;Charset=UTF-8) http://localhost:9000 helloworld> 200 OKxd:>! cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outcommand is:cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outhelloworldxd:>! cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outcommand is:cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outhelloworldxd:>http post --target http://localhost:9000 --data \\\"helloworld2\\\"> POST (text/plain;Charset=UTF-8) http://localhost:9000 helloworld2> 200 OKxd:>! cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outcommand is:cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outhelloworldhelloworld2xd:>http post --target http://localhost:9000 --data \\\"helloworld3\\\"> POST (text/plain;Charset=UTF-8) http://localhost:9000 helloworld3> 200 OKxd:>! cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outcommand is:cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outhelloworldhelloworld2helloworld3xd:>http post --target http://localhost:9000 --data \\\"helloworld3\\\"> POST (text/plain;Charset=UTF-8) http://localhost:9000 helloworld3> 200 OKxd:>! cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outcommand is:cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outhelloworldhelloworld2helloworld3xd:>! cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outcommand is:cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outhelloworldhelloworld2helloworld3xd:>http post --target http://localhost:9000 --data \\\"helloworld3\\\"> POST (text/plain;Charset=UTF-8) http://localhost:9000 helloworld3> 200 OKxd:>http post --target http://localhost:9000 --data \\\"helloworld3\\\"> POST (text/plain;Charset=UTF-8) http://localhost:9000 helloworld3> 200 OKxd:>http post --target http://localhost:9000 --data \\\"helloworld3\\\"> POST (text/plain;Charset=UTF-8) http://localhost:9000 helloworld3> 200 OKxd:>! cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outcommand is:cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outhelloworldhelloworld2helloworld3xd:>http post --target http://localhost:9000 --data \\\"helloworld4\\\"> POST (text/plain;Charset=UTF-8) http://localhost:9000 helloworld4> 200 OKxd:>! cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outcommand is:cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.outhelloworldhelloworld2helloworld3helloworld4xd:>counter display --name httpTap9xd:>however in the regular shell.$ cat /tmp/xd/output/httpStream.out helloworldhelloworldhelloworld2helloworld3helloworld3helloworld3helloworld3helloworld3helloworld4\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',382,'XD-718','19','{\"key\": \"XD-718\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Use ParentLastClassLoader to create the Modules ApplicationContext.\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The ParentLastClassloader is located in the spring-hadoop project.  It will resolve classes first looking at the child context and then the parent.  This works well for XD since the we want and dependencies of the module to be considered first and if not found resolve against the parent. It would be possible to even include other versions of .jars already in the parent classloaders (e.g. Spring Integration jars) but for now we will not immediately test that case.SimpleModule needs to change to that we can pass in the classloader to use for creating the application context. The current implementation creates a GenericApplicationContext as a field initializer...that should change to be in the ctor.ModuleDeployer should implement .BeanClassLoaderAware.  The classloader passed in to the BeanClassLoaderAware callback will be used as the ΓÇÿparentΓÇÖ when creating the ParentLastClassloader.  The URL[] to pass into ParentLastClassloader should be ΓÇÿnullΓÇÖ or an empty array in this case of an older style module.  (Hopefully ParentLastClassloader  allows that type of fallback).*Implementation Suggestions:*The ModuleDeployer code is where the application context for the module is defined and instantiated.   Here is a possible impl path.1. Assuming we can always use ParentLastClassloader (even for older style modules) then the ModuleDescriptor needs to return an array of URL[] locations for the module getURL().  This is passed into the cto for SimpleModule.  The ctor then creates a new application context creates the parentclassloader sets the classloader on the application context and then proceeds as normal. 2.AbstractModuleRegistry should try and load the resource from two possible locations e.g. ./modules/source/file/config/file.xmlor./modules/source/file.xmlThe module registry needs to be a bit smarter to know ah i see a config directory let me try ./config/file.xml otherwise just ./file.xml*How to verify it works.*1. JUnit test in which one of the ModuleRegistry implementations points to a test directory that contains both old and new style modules.  FileModuleRegistry is probably a good choice here.  Need to test that the new getting for URL[] works as expected.2. Existing tests should run as they did before in particular the shell integration tests.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',383,'XD-720','19','{\"key\": \"XD-720\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Deploy a new source module *after* XD-singlenode container has started.\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"After the xd-singlenode process has started create a new module that has dependencies not already in the parent application context and then create a stream that uses the new module.*Implementation Suggestions*Develop in the test tree maybe of the xd-shell project a new module.  the lib and config should be sititng around in a directory waiting to be copied into the appropriate spot.Could try http://www.date4j.net/..The config file  would be similar to time.xml but use the date4j class.*How to verify it works*In a JUnit test case copy in a new module that has new dependencies ..copy the lib and config directories into the location where the ModuleRegisty will pick it up.Deploy a new stream date4j | file and see if there are contents in the file.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',384,'XD-727','19','{\"key\": \"XD-727\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create directory structures and move existing UI code into Spring XD repository\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Create a directory structure that best benefits UI development.  The copying of the UI files and other gradle build tasks so that the UI can be run inside the embedded servlet container of XD will be a seperate story\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',385,'XD-728','19','{\"key\": \"XD-728\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Display the UI from xd-admin container when doing development in eclipse\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The UI code will be sitting in one or more top level directories in the repositoryThis story will address the need to 1) copy over the UI code into a location so that it can be picked up by the embedded servlet container when running inside eclipse\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',386,'XD-729','19','{\"key\": \"XD-729\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Package up the UI code when building the distribution so that it can be shown by xd-admin\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The UI code will be sitting in one or more top level directories in the repositoryThis story will address the need to 1) copy over the UI code into a location so that it can be picked up by the embedded servlet container when the distribution zip is \'unzipped\'.  After running ./xd-admin or ./xd-singlenode one should be able to hit the UI at http://localhost:8999/xd(just an example)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',387,'XD-730','19','{\"key\": \"XD-730\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Add additional embedded servlet container config to load static UI resources\", \"assignee\": \"Andrew Eisenberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Configure embedded servlet container needs to know where to load the UI code.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 12.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',388,'XD-691','19','{\"key\": \"XD-691\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Change JMX option to reference \'enableJmx\' instead of \'disableJmx\'\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Make the default value of enableJmx false until we have tested/documented JMX functionality\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',389,'XD-733','19','{\"key\": \"XD-733\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Create JobLaunchRequest Transformer\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 6.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The JobLaunchRequest Transformer shall accept the following payloads:* File* JSON String* Properties* Map* TupleUse/Migrate some of the logic from *JobParametersBean* e.g. using the *DefaultJobParametersConverter*.*Special Case File*When handling a *File* add special JobParameter *absoluteFilePath* populating it with *message.getPayload().getAbsolutePath()** Add unit tests\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',390,'XD-700','19','{\"key\": \"XD-700\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Remove XD UUIDGenerator in favor of the new SI provided one\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Remove <bean id=\\\"idGenerator\\\" class=\\\"org.springframework.xd.dirt.container.UUIDGenerator\\\" />  (container.xml)Delete org.springframework.xd.dirt.container.UUIDGeneratorremove compile dependency on eaio from build.gradle\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',391,'XD-743','19','{\"key\": \"XD-743\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Ensure that when batch jobs are created they are created with the job bean definition id equal to the ΓÇÿstream nameΓÇÖ\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Unlike in spring-batch-admin in SpringXD all the jobs the /modules/jobs directory is not ΓÇÿvisibleΓÇÖ to query when the server starts.  Jobs only become visible to XDΓÇÖs ΓÇÿjobs listΓÇÖ command once they have been ΓÇÿcreatedΓÇÖ.  Creating a Job in XD is an opportunity to specify additional values to any property placeholders in the job bean definition.  This isnΓÇÖt part of spring-batch-admin.We will not worry about the creation of job definition in this story.  Assume that they have been created already and that the GET for /jobs works as it does now for Spring XD. We should however make sure that there is always a replacement of the job name in the job bean definition to match the ΓÇÿ--nameΓÇÖ specified in the command line.  That is ΓÇ£job create --name myjob --description ΓÇ£thisfunkyjobΓÇ¥will use ΓÇÿmyjob to replace <job id=\\\"${xd.stream.name}\\\" in the file thisfunkyjob.xml*Implementation Suggestions*This should hopefully just be a matter of changing job definition files to follow the naming pattern.<job id=\\\"${xd.stream.name}\\\" ΓÇª />*How to verify it works*1. Create a JUnit integration style test that has ΓÇÿjob create --name myjob --defintion ΓÇ£testJobΓÇ¥ΓÇÖ and then deploy the job.  The name ΓÇÿmyjobΓÇÖ should appear in the job execution table\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 7.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',392,'XD-739','19','{\"key\": \"XD-739\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Eliminate internal dependencies on System properties\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Remove System.setProperty() or System.getProperty() for internal xd properties. Use spring Environment abstraction instead. Also replace \\\".\\\" in property names with \'_\' (XDPropertyKeys). This is compatible with environment variable names. As a result XD should accept System properties or environment variables or command line options. Command line options should have highest precedence. Retain StandardEnvironment order wrt to System properties and environment variable. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',393,'XD-530','19','{\"key\": \"XD-530\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create XD module for syslog-tcp-reactor \", \"assignee\": \"Jon Brisbin\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Still keep existing one.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',394,'XD-754','19','{\"key\": \"XD-754\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Fix Class/Package Tangle Introduced by XD-353\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"{{container}} and {{event}}. {{XDContainer}} references and is referenced by {{ContainerStartedEvent}} (and stopped).https://sonar.springsource.org/drilldown/measures/7173?metric=package_cycles&rids%5B%5D=7717\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',395,'XD-759','19','{\"key\": \"XD-759\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"The xd-singlenode script should have execute permissions\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The xd-singlenode script currently has \'644\' permissions unlike xd-admin and xd-container (which have \'755\'): {code}-rwxr-xr-x  1 mark  staff  5899 Aug 26 16:19 xd-admin-rwxr-xr-x  1 mark  staff  5955 Aug 26 16:19 xd-container-rw-r--r--  1 mark  staff  5919 Aug 26 16:19 xd-singlenode{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',396,'XD-752','19','{\"key\": \"XD-752\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Restrict Job launcher with more than one batch job configured in job module\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently the Job launcher launches all the batch jobs configured in the job module.Please refer ModuleJobLauncher\'s executeBatchJob().This makes the JobRegistry registers with multiple batch jobs under the same Spring XD job name (group name).Also it is understood that having multiple jobs configuration under the same config xml is uncommon.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',397,'XD-676','19','{\"key\": \"XD-676\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"add PropertyAccessor for Tuple fields in SpEL\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Example using name:{code}filter --expression=\\\"payload.myfield.startsWith(\'foo\')\\\"{code}Example using index:{code}filter --expression=\\\"payload.2.startsWith(\'foo\')\\\"{code}This should support nested keys as well:{code}filter --expression=\\\"payload.myfield.subfield.startsWith(\'foo\')\\\"{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 5.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',398,'XD-671','19','{\"key\": \"XD-671\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Add support for dynamic routing\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 16.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"It should be possible to create streams like the following which rely upon named channel support and dynamic routing capabilities:{code}http | somerouter:x > xtransformer | hdfs:y > ytransformer | hdfs{code}The \'somerouter\' processor could return \\\"x\\\" or \\\"y\\\" which determines the downstream path for each message.This should be implemented in such a way that any developer adding a router module would only need to deal with existing Spring Integration semantics (in this case only considering the return of \\\"x\\\" or \\\"y\\\" - whether it be SpEL or a POJO method invocation). Perhaps in the plugin that modifies a module context we could simply add a new ChannelResolver implementation (by adding that ChannelResolver as a bean and/or a BeanPostProcessor that configures that as the resolver for any router if necessary). That ChannelResolver would have a reference to the ChannelRegistry so that the router actually sends its messages to those shared channels. The shared channels themselves would have been created as long as a valid downstream flow has been defined.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',399,'XD-779','19','{\"key\": \"XD-779\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 19, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Infinite recursion (StackOverflowError) when trying to process JobLaunchingMessageHandler\'s \\\"notifications\\\" channel output\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1