pendedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"If true(default): filter for delete messages in the twitter stream and route to a discard channel. This creates a twitter stream including only new tweets and no references to deleted ones.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',426,'XD-824','20','{\"key\": \"XD-824\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 20, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Rename ChannelRegistry\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"My current thinking is...   ChannelRegistry -> MessageBus   RabbitChannelRegistry -> RabbitMessageBus   ...Then method names change like so:   createInbound -> registerConsumer   createOutbound -> registerProducer\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',427,'XD-820','20','{\"key\": \"XD-820\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 20, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Jobs and taps should not require a leading : since they have name spaces.\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',428,'XD-827','20','{\"key\": \"XD-827\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 20, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"provide a property on twittersearch to enable the object-to-json transformer\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Twitter search source should produce JSON or Pojo. The Pojo requires a custom wrapper class that is JSON friendly (e.g. zero arg constructor). The twittersearch module should have a parameter --json true/false (default true) to control the output type.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',429,'XD-831','20','{\"key\": \"XD-831\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 20, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Update docs to cover Module config and lib directory structure\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',430,'XD-832','20','{\"key\": \"XD-832\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 20, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Update docs for new Tap syntax\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Now that taps are just channels we need to update the docs.The preceding colon is no longer needed (and will be removed altogether) so all examples should be like this:{code}tap:foo > bar{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',431,'XD-858','21','{\"key\": \"XD-858\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to Spring Data Redis 1.1.0.RELEASE\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',432,'XD-854','21','{\"key\": \"XD-854\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Update doc about modules and spring\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The doc at http://docs.spring.io/spring-xd/docs/1.0.0.M3/reference/html/#_modules_and_spring refers to an old version of the counter sink when it was still hardwired to use redis.The text next to it that explains placeholders is out of date (with respect to the redis placeholders)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',433,'XD-828','21','{\"key\": \"XD-828\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"rename Bridge to Binding and add direction\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"org.springframework.integration.x.bus.Bridge should now be called Bindingwe can also move the INBOUND/OUTBOUND direction (or possibly the CONSUMER/PRODUCER role) into this class; that should simplify its usage in conditional code within the MessageBus code and also reduce the use of \\\"in\\\" and \\\"out\\\" as Strings in that same code\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',434,'XD-859','21','{\"key\": \"XD-859\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Support for listing of modules in the REST API\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"From the CLI one should be able to get a listing of modules and be able to specifically ask for jobs sources sinks and processors.  A brief description of them would also be nice - this might come from adding some metadata into the definition.Finer grained description/implementation suggestion TBD\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',435,'XD-870','21','{\"key\": \"XD-870\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Support for listing of modules in the Shell\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Commands that pair up with the functionality described in XD-859module list  (would list all modules in a table format)module list --type=source  (would list only source modules)and so on.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',436,'XD-531','21','{\"key\": \"XD-531\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Check for high CPU usage with syslog-tcp-reactor module\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',437,'XD-868','21','{\"key\": \"XD-868\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create microbenchmark performance test of reactor syslog adapter vs standard syslog adapter\", \"assignee\": \"Jon Brisbin\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"We need to verify that we are seeing improved throughput when using the reactor based syslog adapter.  A suggestion on a basic stream to perform a microbenchmark this would be using in-memory counters singlenode with the stream definition \\\"syslog | counter\\\".Based on the results of this microbenchmark other stories may need to be created.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 8.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',438,'XD-864','21','{\"key\": \"XD-864\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Move BatchJobExecutionsByJobName to BatchJobsController from BatchJobExecutionsController\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"We need to move the BatchJobExecutionsByJobName method to BatchJobsController as that seems appropriate\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',439,'XD-689','21','{\"key\": \"XD-689\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Support serialization/deserialization of Message payloads across JVMs across all transports.\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"String -> byte[] (string.getBytes()) byte[] -> byte[] (no serialization)Pojo -> configured serialization\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',440,'XD-862','21','{\"key\": \"XD-862\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"First class JSON Path support\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 10.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Similar to xpath with XML there are now some initial support in SI that enable the use of filter/routers based on JSON Path expressions.  That support needs to be reviewed and then brought up to the level of exposure in Spring XD so that router/filter modules could use JSON Path.  json-path-filter/router are components that need to be created perhaps others.This story needs to be broken down further.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 7.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',441,'XD-811','21','{\"key\": \"XD-811\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Add REST endpoint for launching Job\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"We need a REST endpoint to launch a job.Given the constraint on JobRegistry being not persistent and not available outside the container JVM we can not use the batch job admin controller/service to launch the job.One possible way is to use the trigger source to launch the job at XD.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',442,'XD-863','21','{\"key\": \"XD-863\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Serialization of Spring Batch Context Objects\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 3.0, \"issueLinks\": 4.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Needs some investigation on how the update information from Spring Batch listeners can be sent as a message across modules in a single node configuration as well as across JVMs in a distributed node configuration.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 6.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 3.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',443,'XD-53','21','{\"key\": \"XD-53\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Design and document desired high level DSL for configuring data processing in XD\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 13.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Start to explore how the DSL can cover both advanced (non-linear) spring integration flows as well as spring batch jobs.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',444,'XD-847','21','{\"key\": \"XD-847\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Revise the available hadoopDistro options\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"We should adjust our --hadoopDistro options to the ones supported in the new spring-data-hadoop 1.0.1.RELEASE - hadoop12 (default) cdh4 hdp13 phd1 hadoop20This includes updating the wiki pages\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',445,'XD-866','21','{\"key\": \"XD-866\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Remove remaining Thread.sleeps from the job tests\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Get rid of all the thread.sleeps and code that supported them.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',446,'XD-813','21','{\"key\": \"XD-813\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Destroying XD job should remove job\'s entries at batch job repositories/batch job locator\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"When an XD job is destroyed/deleted the batch jobRepository entries for the job (associated JobInstances JobExecutions etc.) and the BatchJobLocator entries.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',447,'XD-875','21','{\"key\": \"XD-875\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Handle AdminServer shutdown cleanly\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The admin Server\'s tomcat is not shutdown properly. There is an existing method shutdownCleanly() on AdminServer but the spring-xd-shell tests hang when we use this method to shutdown the admin server. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',448,'XD-877','21','{\"key\": \"XD-877\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"summary\": \"Taps do not work when JMX is enabled\", \"assignee\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jennifer Hickey\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"When JMX is enabled the Module\'s output channel processed by StreamPlugin is a Proxy. Thus it fails the \\\"instanceof\\\" test used to apply the WireTap to the output channel. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',449,'XD-880','21','{\"key\": \"XD-880\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Update Java Version to 7\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',450,'XD-886','21','{\"key\": \"XD-886\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Fix package tangle between org.springframework.xd.dirt.plugins.job and org.springframework.xd.dirt.job\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',451,'XD-890','21','{\"key\": \"XD-890\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Run JavaScript tests (Jasmine) as part of the build process\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"We probably need to look into some options to run our JavaScript tests (Jasmine) as part of the build process - some possibilities:* Jasmine Gradle Plugin https://github.com/dzhaughnroth/jasmine-gradle-plugin* Saga - http://timurstrekalov.github.io/saga/Looks like Maven has slightly better support: http://searls.github.io/jasmine-maven-plugin/index.htmlSee also: XD-865\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',452,'XD-900','21','{\"key\": \"XD-900\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Move SpEL PropertyAccessors to Module Parent Context\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"When INT-3133 is resolved SpEL {{PropertyAccessor}} s are inherited from parent contexts.Instead of adding the {{JsonPropertyAccessor}} to each module\'s context add it to the parent instead.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',453,'XD-889','21','{\"key\": \"XD-889\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Change default admin port from 8080\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"This conflicts with and \'out of the box\' hadoop installation that uses 8080 as the \'map reduce shuffle port\'.8088 sound ok?\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',454,'XD-899','21','{\"key\": \"XD-899\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"xd-container should start even if xd-admin is not running\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"currently xd-container will not start due to a DB connection failure if the xd-admin is not already runningIn fact if someone is not using Batch jobs at all with XD they should not even need a DB connection for either xd-admin or xd-container to runso... consider using LazyConnectionDataSourceProxy so a connection failure would only occur when the DataSource is actually invoked to retrieve a connection\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',455,'XD-891','21','{\"key\": \"XD-891\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Provide a way to access currently deployed modules\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"For testing it would be useful to access the deployed Module instances to connect sources and or sinks to a module\'s input and output channels etc. This could be a simple as exposing the deployedModuleMap on ModuleDeployer or possibly something more elaborate if this level of granularity is generally useful for runtime administration.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',456,'XD-887','21','{\"key\": \"XD-887\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Package modules with their support jars\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 6.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently a lot of jars that are on the classpath of xd-dirt are there to support modules.We should move those to the lib/ construct of a module and remove them from the CP of dirt.But this should not be done by simple \\\"mv\\\" as we\'d lose version tracking and dependency management offered by gradle.Pending a \\\"dependency-aware\\\" ModuleRegistry we should be able to alter the build.gradle file so that it- knows about individual modules (maybe handles them as project)- copies its libs into the appropriate directory- does not copy dependencies that are already legitimate dependencies of xd-dirt (this can be achieved by runtime introspection of the dependeny tree of both projects)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',457,'XD-578','21','{\"key\": \"XD-578\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Can\'t access HDFS using webhdfs protocol\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"http://localhost:8080:>hadoop config fs --namenode webhdfs://localhost:50070http://localhost:8080:>hadoop fs ls /Hadoop configuration changed re-initializing shell...run HDFS shell failed. Message is: org/mortbay/util/ajax/JSONThis was on a hadoop 1.0.1 installThe hdfs http interface was available$ curl -i \\\"http://localhost:50070/webhdfs/v1/tmp?op=GETFILESTATUS\\\"HTTP/1.1 200 OKContent-Type: application/jsonTransfer-Encoding: chunkedServer: Jetty(6.1.26){\\\"FileStatus\\\":{\\\"accessTime\\\":0\\\"blockSize\\\":0\\\"group\\\":\\\"supergroup\\\"\\\"length\\\":0\\\"modificationTime\\\":1365015846724\\\"owner\\\":\\\"mpollack\\\"\\\"pathSuffix\\\":\\\"\\\"\\\"permission\\\":\\\"777\\\"\\\"replication\\\":0\\\"type\\\":\\\"DIRECTORY\\\"}}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',458,'XD-901','21','{\"key\": \"XD-901\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Wrong Jetty Util on classpath for WebHdfs\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"We currently include jetty-util-6.1.26.jar but we need to add correct jar for different distributions - PHD uses jetty-util-7.6.10.v20130312.jarNeed to check hadoop-hdfs dependencies for the distros and add jetty-util-* to the jar copy for each distro\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',459,'XD-905','21','{\"key\": \"XD-905\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Container start/stop publish events are not getting processed\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"It looks like Container\'s ContainerStartedEvent and ContainerStoppedEvent are published from ContainerLauncher\'s context whereas the ContainerEventListeners are running in XDContainer\'s context. This makes the container start/stop events not getting processed.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',460,'XD-896','21','{\"key\": \"XD-896\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Add --inputType and --outputType module parameters\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The ability to configure message conversion via parameters. Consider programatic configuration of data type channels. Values can be media type e.g. application/json or a java class name.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',461,'XD-920','21','{\"key\": \"XD-920\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"MQTT source module does not cleanly undeploy\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Was attempting to test mqtt turns out I don\'t have the proper rabbitmq thing installed. So far so good I get these kinds of exceptions:{noformat}Unable to connect to server (32103) - java.net.ConnectException: Connection refusedat org.eclipse.paho.client.mqttv3.internal.TCPNetworkModule.start(TCPNetworkModule.java:75)at org.eclipse.paho.client.mqttv3.internal.ClientComms$ConnectBG.run(ClientComms.java:521)at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:724)Caused by: java.net.ConnectException: Connection refusedat java.net.PlainSocketImpl.socketConnect(Native Method)at java.net.AbstractPlainSocketImpl.doConnect(AbstractPlainSocketImpl.java:339)at java.net.AbstractPlainSocketImpl.connectToAddress(AbstractPlainSocketImpl.java:200)at java.net.AbstractPlainSocketImpl.connect(AbstractPlainSocketImpl.java:182)at java.net.SocksSocketImpl.connect(SocksSocketImpl.java:392)at java.net.Socket.connect(Socket.java:579)at org.eclipse.paho.client.mqttv3.internal.TCPNetworkModule.start(TCPNetworkModule.java:66)... 2 more{noformat}Problem is I still get them after undeploying my \\\"mqtt | log\\\" stream\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',462,'XD-922','21','{\"key\": \"XD-922\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Handle SingleNodeServer\'s stop()  method cleanly\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"SingleNode server needs to stop cleanly with stopping both the admin server & container server. Also all the tests that require SingleNode main server needs to handle the server shutdown appropriately.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',463,'XD-915','21','{\"key\": \"XD-915\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Convert modules to be CP-aware\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Once XD-887 is merged gradually convert more modules.Recipe:1) Move the <module>.xml file to <module>/config/<module>.xml2) Declare a :module.<type>.<module> gradle project3) Move dependencies from dirt project to newly created module project4) gradle build picks it up.gradle clean build + manual testAlso have a look at gradle cleanEclipse eclipse\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',464,'XD-796','21','{\"key\": \"XD-796\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Create separate commands for \\\"--all\\\" shell commands\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Commands like \\\"stream deploy\\\" have changed over time to allow passing a \\\"--all\\\" option.So it\'s either {{stream deploy foo}} or {{stream deploy --all}}. This has a number of drawbacks given that these are the only 2 alternatives:- Implementation code is cumbersome- None of the options can be marked mandatory yet one of them is required. This has to be checked in the command code itself- TAB completion is less powerful as the shell doesn\'t know if we want the first or the second form.Consider splitting those commands into two distinct commands one as before and one literally named {{stream deploy all}}.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',465,'XD-924','21','{\"key\": \"XD-924\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Split integration.x in dedicated XD projects where appropriate\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Similar to what is done for e.g. hadoop reactor and http some of the classes in the .x package (namely gemfire splunk twitter) should go in dedicated (albeit small) projects. This would enable further modularization (see XD-915)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',466,'XD-910','21','{\"key\": \"XD-910\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Add a Processor for Restful webservices\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Offers the functionality to make http request to a web service. i.e. outbound http gateway.Example implementations:stream create --name foo --definition \\\"trigger |rest --reply-timeout=1 --url=http://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/feed/geojson/all/day|log\\\"stream create --name foos --definition \\\"trigger --payload=lat=34.0567006&lon=-84.34368810000001&site=all&smap=1&searchresult=Roswell%2C%20GA%2030076%2C%20USA#.UktzaWSG1Dd | rest --url=http://forecast.weather.gov/MapClick.php? |log\\\"\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',467,'XD-906','21','{\"key\": \"XD-906\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"summary\": \"Add aggregate counter monthly resolution query support\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',468,'XD-816','21','{\"key\": \"XD-816\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Andy Clement\", \"summary\": \"Support for composed streams\", \"assignee\": \"Andy Clement\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Andy Clement\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Some recent changes caused this to be turned off. Basically the change was to police whether a stream is well formed at create time rather than deploy time.  By deferring that check we can create composed streams that are not deployable by themselves but that are when used as building blocks in proper streams.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',469,'XD-940','21','{\"key\": \"XD-940\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Splunk Pulls in an Old SI Jar into STS\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',470,'XD-908','21','{\"key\": \"XD-908\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 21, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"summary\": \"Add aggregate counter query by number of points\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"It should be possible to supply a start or end date (or none for the present) plus a \\\"count\\\" value for the number of points required (i.e. after or prior to the given time).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',471,'XD-947','24','{\"key\": \"XD-947\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 24, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Spike for Deployment SPI\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 20.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"SPI for deployment on to YARN + Local \'dirt\' cluster.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',472,'XD-935','24','{\"key\": \"XD-935\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 24, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Implement Kryo serialization for Tuple\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently TupleCodec uses JSON for serialization/deserialization. It should use Kryo. This will require some customization and potentially changes to Tuple to address the Tuple\'s conversionService field. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',473,'XD-933','24','{\"key\": \"XD-933\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 24, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Remove work around Spring HATEOAS#89\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"See https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-hateoas/issues/89Updating HATEOAS version and removing in a lot of controllers should be possible now. See eg https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/blob/4919ea2498a13ef47aaa9437937308fb26a7a24f/spring-xd-di