Point\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Now that XD-924 is merged we can convert splunk twitter and gemfire modules to rely on the newly created projects.The hadoop module will get its own story as classpath handling is a bit more tricky for that one.From there on no new dependency should be added to DIRT for the sole purpose of a module. Rather it should directly be created as a CP-aware module and project.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',484,'XD-916','24','{\"key\": \"XD-916\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 24, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"File source should be able to produce file contents or file reference\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"File source should output either the File itself (serialized File object) or the contents as a byte[]. This option is configured by a parameter --contents=true.  The byte[] may be converted to a String using XD Message Conversion e.g. --output = text/plain;charset=UTF-8\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',485,'XD-927','24','{\"key\": \"XD-927\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 24, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"ModuleType  Refactor\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Remove ModuleType.getModuleTypeByTypeName.  All code should use the enum.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',486,'XD-957','24','{\"key\": \"XD-957\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 24, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Update SI Dependency to 4.0.0.BUILD-SNAPSHOT\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',487,'XD-961','24','{\"key\": \"XD-961\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 24, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Accessing xd-admin URLs in the browser return XML and not JSON\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Here is an example:the following request for streams:http://ec2-23-20-25-30.compute-1.amazonaws.com:9393/streamsReturns:This XML file does not appear to have any style information associated with it. The document tree is shown below.<errors xmlns:atom=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\\\"><error logref=\\\"HttpMessageNotWritableException\\\"><message>Could not marshal [PagedResource { content: [links: [<http://ec2-23-20-25-30.compute-1.amazonaws.com:9393/streams/ticktock>;rel=\\\"self\\\"]] metadata: Metadata { number: 0 total pages: 1 total elements: 1 size: 20 } links: [] }]: null; nested exception is javax.xml.bind.MarshalException - with linked exception: [com.sun.istack.SAXException2: unable to marshal type \\\"org.springframework.xd.rest.client.domain.StreamDefinitionResource\\\" as an element because it is not known to this context.]</message></error></errors>\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',488,'XD-919','24','{\"key\": \"XD-919\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 24, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Remove json parameter from twittersearch source\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"json parameter is no longer required. Use --outputType=application/json instead\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',489,'XD-962','24','{\"key\": \"XD-962\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 24, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"fix gradle clean test\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently ./gradlew clean test fails since the module dependencies are not packaged before the test task.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',490,'XD-925','24','{\"key\": \"XD-925\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 24, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Investigate Swagger to generate REST API Documents\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 7.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',491,'XD-753','25','{\"key\": \"XD-753\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"JDBC property settings need to be made externally configurable\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"We need to have a properties section (documented as well) so that users can setup their jdbc connections for the various components.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',492,'XD-937','25','{\"key\": \"XD-937\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Inject ModuleDefinitionRepository into ModulesController\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently ModulesController creates the ModuleDefinitionRepository instance with ModuleRegistry. Instead we should inject the moduleDefinitionRepository into ModulesController directly.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',493,'XD-995','25','{\"key\": \"XD-995\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Refactor tests with FileSink|FileSource to use eventually() matcher\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Some tests (esp. ModuleClasspathTests.testModuleWithClasspathAfterServerStarted) seem to fail because of a race condition.Add a Hamcrest matcher that knows how to read the content of a FileSink|Source and refactor those to read like e.g.assertThat(fileSink eventually(hasContent(\\\"foo)))\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',494,'XD-163','25','{\"key\": \"XD-163\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Enable grouping of modules for co-located deployment\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 12.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"example:{code}a | (b | c) | d{code}...where b and c modules are deployed together as a composite module.There are 2 options (maybe more) for how we could handle that. One would be defining a CompositeModule type that simply bridges the channels (b\'s output to c\'s input in this example). The second option would be to deploy those together on the same node as modules but using the LocalChannelRegistry between them.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 5.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',495,'XD-935','25','{\"key\": \"XD-935\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Implement Kryo serialization for Tuple\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently TupleCodec uses JSON for serialization/deserialization. It should use Kryo. This will require some customization and potentially changes to Tuple to address the Tuple\'s conversionService field. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',496,'XD-955','25','{\"key\": \"XD-955\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"summary\": \"Update Jobs documentation to include \\\"job launch\\\" command\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 0.0, \"description\": \"This is currently missing and probably supersedes some of the stuff that\'s in there now.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',497,'XD-966','25','{\"key\": \"XD-966\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"User requests that XD team members are issued EC2 accounts\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"* Setup groups for xd user* Setup privileges so users can only see their instances* Setup user accounts** Send created access key to users** Send username and passwords to user\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',498,'XD-976','25','{\"key\": \"XD-976\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Bootstrap Project for XD AWS Installer\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"* Create a Spring application context.  (XML or Java dealers choiceΓÇª)* Use XD eclipse code format policy* Create Source Package structure* Create Test Package Structure* Gradle build* JClouds and Spring deps\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',499,'XD-969','25','{\"key\": \"XD-969\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Add functionality to provision EC2 instance and mount EBS\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 10.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"* The Application should **  Create a Spring Application Context.**  Should take a command line parameter --config that will point to a property file with key/value pairs specified below.  By default the file xd-ec2.properties will be looked for on the classpath** Associate EBS shared volume for each machine instance* Packaging ** Use gradle application plugin to generate a ΓÇÿbinΓÇÖ directory with a script to start the application.  Seehttp://www.gradle.org/docs/current/userguide/application_plugin.html** The config file xd-ec2.properties should be in a directory (ideally a \'config\' directory parallel to \'bin\' and will be loaded by the application by default - loading via the CP is probably the easiest way.** Create a POJO to easily reference these properties vs. using a raw java Properties object.How to verify it works* Integration testing** Create JUnit based tests.  JClouds itself has extensive testing can look at those for structure.** Verify what you created has been installed.** Verify ports are openInstance Information** EBS of 50GB Base for each instance.* Report successful and failed Instances.Key-Value pairs in configuration fileproperties may include: * cluster-name= a name describing the cluster you are creating* aws-access-keys= the access key assigned to you by admin* aws-secret-key= the secret key assigned to you by admin* private-key-file= the private key file assigned to you by admin.  Used for ssh-ing into * multi-node=true/false if true then installer will run the number of nodes as enumerated in the number-nodes property value.  if false the installer will start a single node server* number-nodes=The number of nodes(containers) to deploy for this cluster.  Value is an integer > 0* machine-size=The size of machines to be assigned for admin and nodes.  small medium large* redis-port=6379* rabbit-port=5279* xd-dist-url=The url to download the XD to install.  for example: http://blahblahblah.zip* ami = The ami image to use for your cluster. for example: ami-dfadsfdadf\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',500,'XD-977','25','{\"key\": \"XD-977\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Add functionality to download XD distribution zip to each EC2 instance as specified by user \", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"* User specifies download distribution zip file from properties file.  See XD-969 for key-value pairs* Copy the distribution from the shared EBS/S3  the ebs volume assigned to the each node/admin instance  .  ** If not on shared ebs/s3 pull from http site specified by user and put on the shared EBS volume. ** Unzip the distribution from on the ebs volume for the instance to the /home/ubuntu directory** make sure privileges are set to ubuntu not root.How to verify it works* Create a JUNit style integration test that** Deletes a known .zip distribution from EBS/S3.** Invoke the application functionality (should be a 1 liner) that will start up the instance and download the .zip distribution from the URI provided in xd-ec2.properties.  Verify the file is now in EBS/S3 and also on the instance** Tear down created instance** Create new instance passing in the same URI of the .zip distribution.  Verify as before\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',501,'XD-978','25','{\"key\": \"XD-978\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Installer needs to launch a single node XD instance\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 10.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"* Create a Deployer class has methods** RunningInstance  deploySingleNode*** takes into account machine size as specified in properties file** void  destroyAllInstances()  *** or whatever JClouds returns from the destroy call** ctor gets passed in the root boostrapping credentials.* Install Script Steps** Setup XD_HOME variable** Make sure privileges are set to ubuntu not root.** start up redis and rabbit using ports as specified in xd-ec2.properties** Use port watch to make sure they started** Start singlenode after configuration.** Display hostname of singlenode server** Report successful and failed startup** Hit root of xd-admin to see if there is a response on 9393* Integration Testing** Verify that config files have been setup** Verify XD has been started** Verify XD can process a basic http post\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',502,'XD-984','25','{\"key\": \"XD-984\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create OOTB batch job for import and processing multiple files to JDBC\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 10.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Create a sample batch job for inclusion in the distribution that will perform the following tasks.ItemReader* Read a from a directory with multiple files (configurable)* Support for CSV (assume first line has header values)* Convert to tuple data structureItemProcessor* Provide groovy based no-op ItemProcessor.  (configurable)ItemWriter* Write to JDBC.** Provide ** Assume there is an DB instance running somewhere specify connection info (configurable)**The sample job should be documented**\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',503,'XD-988','25','{\"key\": \"XD-988\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create OOTB batch job for export and processing multiple files from HDFS to JDBC\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Same setup as XD-987 for ItemReader and ItemProcessor but should write to HDFS.  One can assume that the table structure has been created already external to the batch job execution.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',504,'XD-985','25','{\"key\": \"XD-985\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create OOTB \'file to HDFS\' batch import job that is launched by a stream.\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Same processing as XD-984 but the job instacne is launched via an event from the input file source.  Supporting a single file per job launch is OK.> job create blah --definition \\\"filehdfs\\\"> stream create csvStream --definition \\\"file --ref=true --dir=/Users/luke --pattern=*.csv > job:blah\\\"*the job should be documented*\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',505,'XD-987','25','{\"key\": \"XD-987\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create OOTB batch job for export and processing multiple files from HDFS to MongoDB\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The ItemReader will read multiple files from HDFS and the data will be converted to a tuple data structureThe ItemProcessor will be a no-op groovy script.The ItemWriter will write the data to a MongoDB collection** A TupleToDBObject converter will need to be developed.*the sample job should be documented*\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',506,'XD-299','25','{\"key\": \"XD-299\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Creating a tap with same name as existing streams results in infinite loop\", \"assignee\": \"Andy Clement\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"See http://stackoverflow.com/questions/17157068/counter-analytics-in-springxdThe underlying issue is stream creation with a name already taken though\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',507,'XD-998','25','{\"key\": \"XD-998\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Add documentation for gemfire cache-listener source\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Need some sample usage docs for https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/tree/master/modules/source/gemfire \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',508,'XD-282','25','{\"key\": \"XD-282\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"The HDFS Sink should support writing POJOs to HDFS using Avro Serialization\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 10.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Writing POJOs using CDK Data (Avro)We should support both partitioned and un-partitioned.  This story addresses only un-partitioned.Document limitations in terms of which Java types are supported and not supported by the Avro serialization\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',509,'XD-999','25','{\"key\": \"XD-999\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Return the step execution information in the current job execution controller\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Related to https://jira.springsource.org/browse/BATCH-2109DistributedJobService#listJobExecutionsForJob overrides SimpleJobService#listJobExecutionsForJoband does not include the *StepExecution*s. This is due to serializion issues with Jackson. In order to fix this we need to add a Jackson MixIn.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',510,'XD-1008','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1008\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Jobs list REST endpoint should include deployed/undeployed status\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently the jobs definition list REST endpoint doesn\'t include deployed/undeployed status on a given job.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',511,'XD-1000','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1000\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"User should be able to view the list of all the job definitions\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Create a tab view with tabs ΓÇ£Job DefinitionsΓÇ¥ ΓÇ£Runtime JobsΓÇ¥ (Deployed Jobs? ΓÇ£Job InstancesΓÇ¥ (Is Runtime Jobs a better name here?) and ΓÇ£Job ExecutionsΓÇ¥. On clicking ΓÇ£Job DefinitionsΓÇ¥ tab we can have a table view of job definitions. Since we bootstrap.js we can have a responsive table layout to list all the available job definitions. At the REST layer ΓÇ£/jobsΓÇ¥ provides the list of job definitions. We can expand the JobsController list()ΓÇÖs QueryOptions to add more criteria (especially to list JobDefinitionΓÇÖs status (Deployed/Undeployed).Also this is the UI implementation for the shell command ΓÇ£job listΓÇ¥\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',512,'XD-1014','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1014\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Command to show the XML of the job definition\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',513,'XD-1013','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1013\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Add additional REST endpoint that return the XML definition of a job\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',514,'XD-1015','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1015\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Create a reusable responsive UI layout to render the XD PagedResoures in tabular view\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Create a reusable responsive UI layout to render the PagedResources returned from REST endpoint. As part of this try upgrading the bootstrap to 3.0.0 and use the responsive styles offered in it.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',515,'XD-942','25','{\"key\": \"XD-942\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Change repo links in build.gradle repo.spring.io\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',516,'XD-1019','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1019\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Add Spring Retry to Rabbit Message Bus\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Log and purge bad messages\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',517,'XD-1023','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1023\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Refactor job deploy to go through XDController.deploy(name)\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Job deployment currently goes through an overloaded version of deploy() that takes 4 parameters. This prohibits job handling code from benefiting from common behavior (and eg currently breaks deployAll)Given that the 3 additional parameters are in fine handled as module parameters let\'s push them to the job definition known at creation time rather than at deployment time (as it does not really make sense to change those between deploys)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',518,'XD-1001','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1001\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"User should be able to view the list of all Deployed Jobs\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"On clicking the ΓÇ£Deployed JobsΓÇ¥ we can have a table view of all the deployed jobs.This is again a responsive table layout with all the job definitions with status ΓÇ£deployedΓÇ¥. The deployed XD job corresponds to a single batch Job Instance. This story addresses the UI layout changes to display existing JobInstance information.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',519,'XD-1003','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1003\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"UI: User should be able to launch a job from Deployed jobs page\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"From the Deployed jobs page user should be able to click on the \\\"Launch\\\" button on a specific job and specify the Job parameters as key value pairs in the text box and we will convert that into JSON string as JobParameters into JobLaunch request.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',520,'XD-1018','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1018\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"summary\": \"JobDeployer hides root exceptions on failure\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 0.0, \"description\": \"When deploying jobs the following code (line 103) hides the root cause of deployment failure:  if (exceptionClassName.equals(BEAN_CREATION_EXCEPTION) || exceptionClassName.equals(BEAN_DEFINITION_EXEPTION)) {    throw new MissingRequiredDefinitionException(definition.getName() cause.getMessage());  }For example:org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.MissingRequiredDefinitionException: Error creating bean with name \'dataSourceInitializer\' defined in file [/Users/luke/Work/spring-xd/build/dist/spring-xd/xd/modules/job/hdfsjdbc/config/hdfsjdbc.xml]: Cannot resolve reference to bean \'databasePopulator\' while setting bean property \'databasePopulator\'; nested exception is org.springframework.beans.factory.BeanCreationException: Error creating bean with name \'databasePopulator\' defined in file [/Users/luke/Work/spring-xd/build/dist/spring-xd/xd/modules/job/hdfsjdbc/config/hdfsjdbc.xml]: Initialization of bean failed; nested exception is java.lang.NullPointerExceptionat org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.JobDeployer.deploy(JobDeployer.java:103)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.JobDeployer.deploy(JobDeployer.java:67)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.rest.XDController.save(XDController.java:242)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',521,'XD-1025','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1025\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"UI: Implement Job Deploy/Undeploy from the Job Definitions page\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"From XD-1023 the job status(deployed/undeployed) is available from JobInstance Repository and a job can be deployed/undeployed correctly. Implement Job deploy/undeploy for a given job from JobDefinitions page and indicate status of the job definition (deployed/undeployed).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',522,'XD-1028','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1028\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"UI - Do not hard-code server url\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Specify the default URL as:{code}urlRoot: location.protocol+\'//\'+location.hostname+(location.port ? \':\'+location.port: \'\'){code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',523,'XD-857','25','{\"key\": \"XD-857\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Refactor FileModuleRegistry as \\\"ResourceModuleRegistry\\\"\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Apart from sanity checks there is not much that ties FileModuleRegistry to actual java.io.Files. Using the Resource abstraction would work just the same and would allow loading modules from the classpath in constrained environments or other file systems/locations. (HDFS /HTTP)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',524,'XD-1029','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1029\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Migrate to SI Redis Queue and Topic Adapters\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',525,'XD-1031','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1031\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"UI - Launch a job with parameters\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Use a modal dialog to specify runtime parameters.There should be a little text are that gives hints as to the spring batch parameter key/value conventions e.g. for type.Might be a good idea to have a checkbox that lets you select to \'auto increment\' job instance number.4 columnskey value type identifying and an \'add parameter\' button that adds a new row.This would appear as a modal dialog box polling of the state of the deployments would be suspended while the job parameter modal dialog box is shown.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',526,'XD-871','25','{\"key\": \"XD-871\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"No errors in Shell when creating stream with HTTP Source + already used port \", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"2 issues exist:1) Current this does not create an error in the shell{code}stream create --name s1 --definition \\\"http | log\\\"stream create --name s2 --definition \\\"http | log\\\"{code}On the server-side I see:{code}Caused by: java.net.BindException: Address already in useat sun.nio.ch.Net.bind0(Native Method)at sun.nio.ch.Net.bind(Net.java:344)at sun.nio.ch.Net.bind(Net.java:336)at sun.nio.ch.ServerSocketChannelImpl.bind(ServerSocketChannelImpl.java:199)at sun.nio.ch.ServerSocketAdaptor.bind(ServerSocketAdaptor.java:74)at org.jboss.netty.channel.socket.nio.NioServerBoss$RegisterTask.run(NioServerBoss.java:193)at org.jboss.netty.channel.socket.nio.AbstractNioSelector.processTaskQueue(AbstractNioSelector.java:366)at org.jboss.netty.channel.socket.nio.AbstractNioSelector.run(AbstractNioSelector.java:290)at org.jboss.netty.channel.socket.nio.NioServerBoss.run(NioServerBoss.java:42)... 3 more{code}2)The Stream should not be saved to the StreamDefinitionRepo in case of an error.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',527,'XD-1033','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1033\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Add a tcp-client source module\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Add a module that can act as a tcp *client* (as opposed to our current tcp module which acts as a server waiting for an incoming connection)Also the module should allow to send \\\"commands\\\" to the remote server. The typical minimal case for such a protocol is to send \\\"PING\\\" messages but a stateful mechanism should be put in place for more complex cases.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',528,'XD-1035','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1035\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Attempt to compose a module with same name+type as existing should fail\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As per discussion any attempt to create something that would collide with existing should fail:II) Attempt to create a composed module with same name as an already existing not composed module with same typeshould fail (EB MF)should work and shadow previous module from now onIII) Attempt to create a composed module with same name as an already existing composed module with same typeshould fail (EB MF)should work and shadow previous module from now onshould work and retroactively change definitions of streams with that module\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',529,'XD-1036','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1036\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Support composed module deletion\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 10.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Provided it is not currently used in any stream:V) Attempt to destroy a composed moduleShould not be supported at allShould not be supported if involved in at least one stream (EB? MF!)Should be supported and have no other consequences whatsoever (see IV) (EB?)Should be supported and invalidate/destroy streams involving it\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',530,'XD-1024','25','{\"key\": \"XD-1024\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 25, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Kryo Redis Serializer\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"The current (XD) uses an inadequate {{MessageRedisSerializer}} when {{extractPayload}} is false (not currently being used). When porting this to SI the serializer will be dropped.Suggest creation of Kryo serializer for Messages for when Redis source/sinks are created.\", \"fixVersions\": 