obs#pre-packaged-batch-jobs\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',622,'XD-1193','29','{\"key\": \"XD-1193\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 29, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Update to Spring Batch 2.2.4\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',623,'XD-1207','29','{\"key\": \"XD-1207\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 29, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Job Plugin - Notification Channel not correctly bound to MessageBus\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',624,'XD-1210','29','{\"key\": \"XD-1210\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 29, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Shell - \'makeUnique\' Job Parameter is true by default \", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently the shell assumes that the \'makeUnique\'job parameter is by default *false*. That is not true. As a consequence the parameter has currently no impact/does not work.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',625,'XD-1216','29','{\"key\": \"XD-1216\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 29, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Serialization of ChunkContext fails using Kryo\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',626,'XD-1222','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1222\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Duplicate MBean server definition by MBeanExportingPlugin\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The MBeanServer is referred by XD admin/launcher when JMX is enabled (by setting --jmxEnabled option) and this is defined in xd-global-beans.xml.The MBeans that are exposed by the modules also use the same MBeanServer define above and there is a duplicate MBeanServer definition (from jmx/common.xml) which the MBeanExportingPlugin adds as a component to the module which doesn\'t seem to be needed.Also currently the flag \\\"jmxEnabled\\\" is generic and used by adminserver/launcher as well as the module MBeanExportingPlugin. If we have a separate flag to enable the JMX *only* for modules then a separate definition of MBeanServer could be necessary.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',627,'XD-1223','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1223\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Unit/Integration tests need appropriate cleanup of test data during teardown\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently there are test data(e.g: stream name) not being cleaned up during teardown especially when there is a test case failure. This breaks the test suite when the same test data is used by other tests.We need to move the cleanup logic at an appropriate level so that the test data is always cleaned up irrespective of the test result.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',628,'XD-1221','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1221\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"XD modules should not have \'build\' directory upon running gradle build\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently the \'modules\' project is marked as java project to enable eclipse/idea metadata files generation. But it generates a \'build\' directory with a jar that has empty MANIFEST file.This build directory also gets copied into the bundle after \'dist\'.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',629,'XD-1214','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1214\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Make job names unique across tests that use the same JobRepository\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The job names used by the tests should be unique across the tests when use the same JobRepository.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',630,'XD-1225','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1225\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Integrate code coverage reports into the CI process\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Not sure if this is best done via Sonar our sonar build plan the nightly one or the frequent one off master...Open question is if we want to fail a build do to code coverage levels.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',631,'XD-1224','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1224\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Add code coverage to gradle build\", \"assignee\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Build should be able to generate code coverage reports.After a quick tour of the intertubes it seems that JaCoCo is a well maintained project and has first class support inside gradle.http://www.gradle.org/docs/current/userguide/jacoco_plugin.html\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',632,'XD-1226','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1226\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Review abstract base classes used in test cases to ensure proper resource cleanup.\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 6.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',633,'XD-1227','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1227\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Investigate long running tests and create refactoring issues\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 4.0, \"storyPoint\": 6.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"https://sonar.springsource.org/dashboard/index/7173?did=3Shows which of our current tests take the most time to execute.xd.dirt.stream and xd.shell.command are where the most time is spent.In xd.dirt.stream it seems likely that time can be reduced by not restarting a new single node server per test but sharing it across tests e.g. RabbitSingleNodeStreamDeploymentIntegrationTests  LocalSingleNodeStreamDeploymentIntegrationTests RedisSingleNodeStreamDeploymentIntegrationTests As a first pass the test that take longer than 15 seconds in that report should be investigated.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',634,'XD-879','31','{\"key\": \"XD-879\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Cleanup hsqldb data directory used by tests after each test completion\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently the \\\"data\\\" directory created by the HSQLDB process during the tests run is not cleaned up and may cause issues. We should delete the \\\"data\\\" directory after each test completion.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',635,'XD-1229','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1229\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create build infrastructure for Angular based UI\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 5.0, \"description\": \"Create a project that includes build and test automation for a new Angular based UI.  This work is independent of calling the UI build step from gradle.  A super minimal UI just to have some basic code is all that is required. This should use GruntJasmineKarmaBowerYUIdoc (separate story?)UI Components from backbone should be available in the base project.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',636,'XD-1230','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1230\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Integrate grunt based UI build into the XD\'s gradle build\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Blog post http://naleid.com/blog/2013/01/24/calling-gruntjs-tasks-from-gradle/  seems to be the definitive reference....\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',637,'XD-1231','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1231\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Investigate if we should use RequreJS with Angular\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 6.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 8.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',638,'XD-1194','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1194\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"CommandLine default values from container & admin options can not be overridden\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"If we have default values from Container/Admin options then they can not be overridden by the system properties or system environment. Currently the only default we have for the Container/Admin options is for \\\"jmxEnabled\\\" option and since it is a boolean it can never be overridden by sys/env property XD_JMX_ENABLED.I think we need to make sure there are no default values assigned for the non-boolean Container/Admin options and handle the boolean type option separately.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',639,'XD-1246','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1246\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"To be able to run the tests without conflicting with an existing XD admin server/launcher\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"In line with what we address at https://jira.springsource.org/browse/XD-1223 there are cases where tests fail when there is an existing instance of hsqldb running.Since hsqldb uses the same port and database it causes issues.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',640,'XD-1185','31','{\"key\": \"XD-1185\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 31, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Add redisConnectionFactory with connection pool\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"We need to add a connection pool to the Redis connection factory used for the transport otherwise we\'ll see exceptions like these:12:57:54842 ERROR inbound.tictoc.0-redis:queue-inbound-channel-adapter1 inbound.RedisQueueMessageDrivenEndpoint:183 - Failed to execute listening task. Will attempt to resubmit in 5000 milliseconds.org.springframework.data.redis.RedisSystemException: Redis exception; nested exception is com.lambdaworks.redis.RedisException: Unable to connectΓÇéΓÇéat org.springframework.data.redis.connection.lettuce.LettuceExceptionConverter.convert(LettuceExceptionConverter.java:46)ΓÇéΓÇéat