til.AbstractExpressionEvaluator.evaluateExpression(AbstractExpressionEvaluator.java:119)... 91 more\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 10.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',937,'XD-1629','47','{\"key\": \"XD-1629\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 47, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"RabbitMessageBus should prefix all created queues with a prefix in order to support HA\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"To configure Rabbit HA a naming convention should be used to identify the queue that need to be mirrored.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',938,'XD-1630','47','{\"key\": \"XD-1630\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 47, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Packaging of lib directory for shell contains many jars that are not used\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Between M5 and M6 the size of the shell/lib directory went up ~50 MB.  Investigate and remove jars from being packaged that are not used.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',939,'XD-1773','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1773\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade Curator to 2.5.0\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',940,'XD-1338','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1338\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Charlie Black\", \"summary\": \"Deployment manifest to support partitioning a stream\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Charlie Black\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 16.0, \"watchcount\": 5.0, \"description\": \"We need a methodology for providing partitioning hints.A current proposal uses message headers to provide:* partition_key ΓÇô the item to partition on* destination_region ΓÇô what to targetIn the proposal the developer used \\\"partition_key\\\" to route the stream message to the node where data was stored in process.  This was done so downstream stream operations could work on the data with out suffering any network IO.The \\\"destination_region\\\" was used to target the type of data the downstream streams were going to use in their stream processing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 7.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',941,'XD-1739','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1739\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"summary\": \"Container reconnection to ZK fails intermittently\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As reported by Matt Stine:After closing and reopening a laptop the following stack trace appears in the container log:{noformat}00:47:28226  INFO main-EventThread state.ConnectionStateManager:194 - State change: RECONNECTED00:47:28226  INFO ConnectionStateManager-0 zookeeper.ZooKeeperConnection:255 - >>> Curator connected event: RECONNECTED00:47:28322 ERROR ConnectionStateManager-0 listen.ListenerContainer:96 - Listener (org.springframework.xd.dirt.zookeeper.ZooKeeperConnection$DelegatingConnectionStateListener@6abf4158) threw an exceptionjava.lang.RuntimeException: java.lang.RuntimeException: org.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException$NodeExistsException: KeeperErrorCode = NodeExists for /xd/containers/5a8deb7b-fd93-42a7-a393-2f15023e007a        at org.springframework.xd.dirt.server.ContainerRegistrar.registerWithZooKeeper(ContainerRegistrar.java:301)        at org.springframework.xd.dirt.server.ContainerRegistrar.access$100(ContainerRegistrar.java:93)        at org.springframework.xd.dirt.server.ContainerRegistrar$ContainerAttributesRegisteringZooKeeperConnectionListener.onConnect(ContainerRegistrar.java:316)        at org.springframework.xd.dirt.zookeeper.ZooKeeperConnection$DelegatingConnectionStateListener.stateChanged(ZooKeeperConnection.java:257)        at org.apache.curator.framework.state.ConnectionStateManager$2.apply(ConnectionStateManager.java:222)        at org.apache.curator.framework.state.ConnectionStateManager$2.apply(ConnectionStateManager.java:218)        at org.apache.curator.framework.listen.ListenerContainer$1.run(ListenerContainer.java:92)        at com.google.common.util.concurrent.MoreExecutors$SameThreadExecutorService.execute(MoreExecutors.java:293)        at org.apache.curator.framework.listen.ListenerContainer.forEach(ListenerContainer.java:83)        at org.apache.curator.framework.state.ConnectionStateManager.processEvents(ConnectionStateManager.java:215)        at org.apache.curator.framework.state.ConnectionStateManager.access$000(ConnectionStateManager.java:42)        at org.apache.curator.framework.state.ConnectionStateManager$1.call(ConnectionStateManager.java:110)        at java.util.concurrent.FutureTask.run(FutureTask.java:262)        at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1145)        at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:615)        at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:744)Caused by: java.lang.RuntimeException: org.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException$NodeExistsException: KeeperErrorCode = NodeExists for /xd/containers/5a8deb7b-fd93-42a7-a393-2f15023e007a        at org.springframework.xd.dirt.container.store.ZooKeeperContainerAttributesRepository.save(ZooKeeperContainerAttributesRepository.java:75)        at org.springframework.xd.dirt.container.store.ZooKeeperContainerAttributesRepository.save(ZooKeeperContainerAttributesRepository.java:42)        at org.springframework.xd.dirt.server.ContainerRegistrar.registerWithZooKeeper(ContainerRegistrar.java:295)        ... 15 moreCaused by: org.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException$NodeExistsException: KeeperErrorCode = NodeExists for /xd/containers/5a8deb7b-fd93-42a7-a393-2f15023e007a        at org.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException.create(KeeperException.java:119)        at org.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException.create(KeeperException.java:51)        at org.apache.zookeeper.ZooKeeper.create(ZooKeeper.java:783)        at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.CreateBuilderImpl$11.call(CreateBuilderImpl.java:676)        at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.CreateBuilderImpl$11.call(CreateBuilderImpl.java:660)        at org.apache.curator.RetryLoop.callWithRetry(RetryLoop.java:107)        at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.CreateBuilderImpl.pathInForeground(CreateBuilderImpl.java:656)        at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.CreateBuilderImpl.protectedPathInForeground(CreateBuilderImpl.java:441)        at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.CreateBuilderImpl.forPath(CreateBuilderImpl.java:431)        at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.CreateBuilderImpl.forPath(CreateBuilderImpl.java:44)        at org.springframework.xd.dirt.container.store.ZooKeeperContainerAttributesRepository.save(ZooKeeperContainerAttributesRepository.java:69)        ... 17 more{noformat}This can occur if ZK does not remove the ephemeral node before the container creates a new one. This can be fixed in the following ways:* Remove the existing ephemeral node if it already exists* Register containers with a new UUID upon every new connectionFor now I\'ll implement the first solution.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',942,'XD-1742','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1742\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Remove toStringTransformer from tcp Source; Add Binary Support to the http Source\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The TCP source unconditionally converts to String. This prevents binary transfers.Remove the transformer; if the user wants a String; (s)he can use{{tcp --outputType=text/plain;charset=UTF-8}} (assuming the byte stream has valid UTF-8 encoding).Another option would be to add a {{--binary}} option but since conversion can already handle it it\'s probably better to use that.On the other hand a {{--binary}} option would enable backwards compatibility.The http source also unconditionally converts to String.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',943,'XD-1507','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1507\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Prevent submiting jobs that are not currently deployed using Admin UI\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Job modules \\\"Launch\\\" and \\\"Schedule\\\" command buttons are active even if the job module isn\'t deployed or has been destroyed.Get errors like: \\\"Yikes something bad happened while launching job myjob4\\\"\\\"The job named \'myjob4\' is not currently deployed\\\"\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',944,'XD-1650','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1650\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Update HDFS sink to accept a partition strategy\", \"assignee\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 2.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Add configuration for the partition strategy to HDFS sink to support writing files into subdirectories based on a partition key provided in the header or field in the message of the stream data.The writing using HDFS Store DataWriter should pass in the partition key value to be used for the write operation.Partition configuration could be made available to the sink using a  --format parameter:that could then be used in XML config like:{code}ΓÇéΓÇéΓÇéΓÇéΓÇéΓÇéexpression=\\\"new java.text.SimpleDateFormat(\'${format}\').format(${timestamp}){code}Similar to the time source.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 2.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',945,'XD-1416','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1416\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Charlie Black\", \"summary\": \"When there are no wiretap listeners don\'t publish messages\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Charlie Black\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 5.0, \"description\": \"Being able to listen to a stream at any point has a significant performance impact.  The reason for the impact is the message needs to be \\\"serialized + transported + deserialized\\\" to other members even if there is no one listening.  This \\\"serialized + transported + deserialized\\\" processes happens for each step in a flow - source | process | sink.Recommend creating some kind of protocol for wiretaps that allows members to know if there is someone listening in the grid so they will emit the data.  Likewise we need to deregister the listener if the wiretap is deleted.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',946,'XD-1520','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1520\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Push ${xd.stream.name} into POJO defaults\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"See XD-1283.We\'ve been waiting for 1283 to change constructs like{noformat}attr=\\\"${name:${xd.stream.name}}\\\"to just{noformat}attr=\\\"${name}\\\"{noformat}Turns out we can simply push down the ${xd.stream.name} bit in the default value (most likely initialization of a field in a POJO metadata class) and it will work just fine.We can also consider:- providing a fake value for those placeholders to use when doing \\\"module info\\\" (ie user will see  \\\"<name of the stream>\\\" instead of \\\"${xd.stream.name}\\\"\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',947,'XD-1715','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1715\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create documentation section for the shell\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Create a new section in the docs regaring shell usage in particular how to represent single and double quotes.Include some discussion of basic commands to manipulate streams jobs and list modules.  How to pass in a file that can be executed when the shell starts up.Also point to spring-shell ref docs for extensibility in terms of adding custom commands.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',948,'XD-1741','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1741\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Register StringToByteArrayMessageConverter\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The converter was not configured therefore String to byte[] for --outPutType application/octet-stream fails for a String payload.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',949,'XD-1737','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1737\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Add --verbose option to display all property values\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',950,'XD-1654','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1654\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Change twittersearch default outputType to be application/json\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 3.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"The current output type is a Java object - this raises issues wrt to consumers in other JVM that to no have the spring social tweet object in the main container classpath.  See https://jira.spring.io/browse/XD-1370Will also create another issue to update twittersearch to generate the raw twitterstream output vs. the structure of the spring social tweet object \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',951,'XD-1628','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1628\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"UI: The user can view the job properties that were specified when the job definition was created as well as job parameters when it was launched/executed\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 6.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',952,'XD-1310','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1310\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Misleading error message when trying to restart a job exec\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Disregard the missing date that is caused by another problem.Here is the setup:{noformat}xd:>job execution list  Id  Job Name  Start Time                        Step Execution Count  Status  --  --------  --------------------------------  --------------------  ---------  13  foo         Europe/Paris                    0                     STARTING  12  foo       2014-02-12 15:39:46 Europe/Paris  1                     FAILED  11  foo       2014-02-12 15:39:29 Europe/Paris  1                     COMPLETED  10  foo       2014-02-12 15:38:36 Europe/Paris  1                     COMPLETED  9   foo       2014-02-12 15:38:21 Europe/Paris  1                     COMPLETED  8   foo         Europe/Paris                    0                     STARTING  7   foo       2014-02-12 15:25:41 Europe/Paris  1                     COMPLETED  6   foo       2014-02-12 15:25:04 Europe/Paris  1                     FAILED  5   foo       2014-02-12 15:14:32 Europe/Paris  1                     FAILED  4   foo       2014-02-12 15:14:13 Europe/Paris  1                     FAILED  3   foo       2014-02-12 15:13:54 Europe/Paris  1                     FAILED  2   foo       2014-02-12 15:13:18 Europe/Paris  1                     FAILED  1   foo       2014-02-12 15:12:58 Europe/Paris  1                     FAILED  0   foo       2014-02-12 15:11:44 Europe/Paris  1                     FAILEDxd:>job execution restart --id 12Command failed org.springframework.xd.rest.client.impl.SpringXDException: Job Execution 12 is already running.{noformat}while the server exception is a bit better:{noformat}Caused by: org.springframework.batch.core.repository.JobExecutionAlreadyRunningException: A job execution for this job is already running: JobInstance: id=11 version=0 Job=[foo]at org.springframework.batch.core.repository.support.SimpleJobRepository.createJobExecution(SimpleJobRepository.java:120){noformat}I\'d argue we should not speak in terms of execution ids if possible but rather in terms of job names\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',953,'XD-1747','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1747\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Module deployment order is not guaranteed\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"We are getting test failures such ashttps://build.spring.io/browse/XD-MASTER-1381quite often in the CI environment recently.  I suspect the ordering of checks in AbstractSingleNodeStreamDeploymentIntegrationTests// Deploys in reverse orderassertModuleRequest(streamName \\\"log\\\" false);assertModuleRequest(streamName \\\"filter\\\" false);assertModuleRequest(streamName \\\"transform\\\" false);assertModuleRequest(streamName \\\"http\\\" false);// Undeploys in stream orderassertModuleRequest(streamName \\\"http\\\" true);assertModuleRequest(streamName \\\"transform\\\" true);assertModuleRequest(streamName \\\"filter\\\" true);assertModuleRequest(streamName \\\"log\\\" true);isn\'t happeningperhaps  changing nextUndeployEvent poll time from 5 seconds to higher is appropriate (no idea why CI environment seems so slow)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',954,'XD-1748','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1748\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Update to Spring Integration 4.0.1\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Add messages store optimization to the `hdfs-dataset`\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',955,'XD-1750','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1750\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Exception handling at Module info command\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"When not prefixing with appropriate module type module info command throws StringIndexOutOfBoundsException:xd:>module info filejava.lang.StringIndexOutOfBoundsException: Failed to convert \'file\' to type QualifiedModuleName for option \'name\'String index out of range: -1\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',956,'XD-1756','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1756\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Update spring-data-hadoop version to 2.0.0.RC4\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 2.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Update spring-data-hadoop version to 2.0.0.RC4 and make necessary changes to the YARN configuration.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 2.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',957,'XD-1757','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1757\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Resolve runtime module option properties using module metadata\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Since the module metadata properties are resolved at runtime (when the module gets deployed) we can resolve the module options values that are already resolved in there.For example currently the \\\"runtime modules\\\" command for \\\"log\\\" module would show this:runtime modules\\u001b[7m\\u001b[27;32m  Module            Container Id                          Options  ----------------  ------------------------------------  --------------------------------------------------------  s1.source.http-0  633f0fb1-5396-4bc0-8f1e-c9d5104e0ea7  {port=9000}  s1.sink.log-1     633f0fb1-5396-4bc0-8f1e-c9d5104e0ea7  {name=${xd.stream.name} expression=payload level=INFO}In this case we can resolve the module option \\\"name\\\" from the module metadata.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',958,'XD-1755','49','{\"key\": \"XD-1755\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 49, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"gemfire source does not offer --host nor --port options\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',959,'XD-1761','49','{\"key\": \"XD-176