ineValve.java:118)at org.apache.catalina.connector.CoyoteAdapter.service(CoyoteAdapter.java:407)at org.apache.coyote.http11.AbstractHttp11Processor.process(AbstractHttp11Processor.java:1004)at org.apache.coyote.AbstractProtocol$AbstractConnectionHandler.process(AbstractProtocol.java:589)at org.apache.tomcat.util.net.NioEndpoint$SocketProcessor.run(NioEndpoint.java:1680)at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1142)at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:617)at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:744){code}Accessing a non existing resource should probably result in a 404 status code.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',983,'XD-1787','50','{\"key\": \"XD-1787\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 50, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Detect Invalid Deployment Properties in the Bus\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Detect properties the bus doesn\'t support.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',984,'XD-1786','50','{\"key\": \"XD-1786\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 50, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Support Partitioning/Bus Properties in the RedisMessageBus\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"PR: https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/pull/926\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',985,'XD-1804','50','{\"key\": \"XD-1804\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 50, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Remove unused parser code related to \\\"substreams\\\" & co\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The XD parser had initial support for substreams which have been subsumed by composed modules.That legacy code is unused and not needed\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}');
INSERT INTO `issues_origem` VALUES ('Spring_XD',986,'XD-1807','50','{\"key\": \"XD-1807\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 50, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Paging support for ModuleMetadata/Container repositories\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Add paging support for the appropriate accessor methods in ModuleMetadata/Container repositories\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',987,'XD-1813','50','{\"key\": \"XD-1813\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 50, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to Spring Boot 1.1 SNAPSHOT\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',988,'XD-1759','50','{\"key\": \"XD-1759\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 50, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Status on Shell command prompt is inconsistent\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Deployment: xd-shell local xd-singlenode (ec2)SHA: 942c7868e3e0d0cf7730b536170438a0291f5cab[Description]<Case 1>Once successfully connected to a server if you connect to a server that is not present.  The prompt still shows XD when it should show server-unknown.  Can be reproduced consistently.Conversely:<Case 2>Attempted to connect to a xd-singlenode on ec2 using a local xd-shell.  The xd-singlenode was not running.  After bringing up the xd-singlenode I was able to connect however the status did not change from \\\"server-unknown\\\"  *This behavior can not be consistently reproduced but have seen it happen on multiple accounts.* [Steps to reproduce]<Case 1>1. Bring up shell while xd-singlenode is not running.2. Bring up xd-singlenode3. Connect to xd-singlenode* xd:>admin config server http://localhost:93934. Connect to a fake address* xd:>admin config server http://foo.bar:9393<Case 2>1.  Attempt to connect to remote server that is not available* xd:>admin config server http://ec2-54-237-186-186.compute-1.amazonaws.com:9393* Unable to contact XD Admin Server at \'http://ec2-54-237-186-186.compute-1.amazonaws.com:9393\'.2. Bring up xd-singlenode on remote* server-unknown:>admin config server http://ec2-54-237-186-186.compute-1.amazonaws.com:9393* Successfully targeted http://ec2-54-237-186-186.compute-1.amazonaws.com:93933. Still see the incorrect prompt.server-unknown:>server-unknown:>\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',989,'XD-1834','50','{\"key\": \"XD-1834\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 50, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Add single threaded executor service to DeploymentSupervisor\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"This willeliminate any race conditions between deployments and containersjoining/leaving the cluster.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',990,'XD-1772','50','{\"key\": \"XD-1772\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 50, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Do not allow a stream definition to contain ambiguous module references\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"A stream definition such as http | transform | transform | file will limit functionality such as taps since you can\'t reference which specific module to apply the tap. Should be proactive in parsing the DSL and force the use of a label to disambiguate.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',991,'XD-1585','50','{\"key\": \"XD-1585\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 50, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Tab completion does not work for stream definition following > \", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \">stream create \\\"tap:stream:foo > does not suggest modules\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',992,'XD-1777','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1777\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"summary\": \"Restore deployment properties for orphaned modules\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 20.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As part of XD-1338 we modified how module deployment works. Now module deployment requests include deployment properties as the data for the ZooKeeper node. This allows us to reuse those properties when a container exit the cluster and the module is redeployed to another container.However if there are no other containers to handle the deployment the module deployment node is erased along with the properties. This mean no module will ever handle the partition that module was responsible for.This condition needs to be handled so that partitioned streams continue to function in cases where the cluster temporarily doesn\'t have enough containers to support the stream.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',993,'XD-1794','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1794\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Module count value at module deployments path\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"In case of module count > 1 the module deployments path for each deployed module always has: {\\\"count\\\":\\\"1\\\"}For a scenario:The stream test1: \\\"http | log\\\"with the deployment manifest:module.log.count=3module.log.criteria=groups.contains(\'test\')get /xd/deployments/streams/test1ΓÇ¿module.log.count=3module.log.criteria=groups.contains(\'test\')get /xd/deployments/modules/9ecaf59a-a1f5-4ed9-984d-f5dff8cc9b57/test1.sink.log-1ΓÇ¿{\\\"count\\\":\\\"1\\\"}get /xd/deployments/modules/1bbdb2dd-97ed-48a2-a3cd-3633c3e82f52/test1.sink.log-1ΓÇ¿{\\\"count\\\":\\\"1\\\"}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 7.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',994,'XD-1745','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1745\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Girish Lingappa\", \"summary\": \"Support for hadoop name node HA configuration\", \"assignee\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Girish Lingappa\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 6.0, \"description\": \"Hadoop supports namenode HA with two name nodes running one being active and other in standby. If the active name node fails the standby name node has all the data readily available and can start serving requests. In this configuration name node url is no longer a host:port url but a logical name that translates to any active name node at runtime. This is to ensure spring xd stream can handle a name node failure for instance when writing a hdfs sink seamlessly\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 17.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',995,'XD-1901','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1901\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Job undeploy operation throws exception\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Job `undeploy` operation throws the following stacktrace:```http-nio-9393-exec-5 zookeeper.ZooKeeperJobRepository - Exception while transitioning job \'j\' state to undeployingorg.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException$NoNodeException: KeeperErrorCode = NoNode for /xd/deployments/jobs/j/statusat org.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException.create(KeeperException.java:111)at org.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException.create(KeeperException.java:51)at org.apache.zookeeper.ZooKeeper.setData(ZooKeeper.java:1266)at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.SetDataBuilderImpl$4.call(SetDataBuilderImpl.java:260)at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.SetDataBuilderImpl$4.call(SetDataBuilderImpl.java:256)at org.apache.curator.RetryLoop.callWithRetry(RetryLoop.java:107)at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.SetDataBuilderImpl.pathInForeground(SetDataBuilderImpl.java:252)at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.SetDataBuilderImpl.forPath(SetDataBuilderImpl.java:239)at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.SetDataBuilderImpl.forPath(SetDataBuilderImpl.java:39)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.zookeeper.ZooKeeperJobRepository.delete(ZooKeeperJobRepository.java:177)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.zookeeper.ZooKeeperJobRepository.delete(ZooKeeperJobRepository.java:199)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.zookeeper.ZooKeeperJobRepository.delete(ZooKeeperJobRepository.java:1)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.AbstractInstancePersistingDeployer.undeploy(AbstractInstancePersistingDeployer.java:68)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.rest.XDController.undeploy(XDController.java:125)at sun.reflect.NativeMethodAccessorImpl.invoke0(Native Method)at sun.reflect.NativeMethodAccessorImpl.invoke(NativeMethodAccessorImpl.java:57)at sun.reflect.DelegatingMethodAccessorImpl.invoke(DelegatingMethodAccessorImpl.java:43)```\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',996,'XD-1622','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1622\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Add support for typed Batch Steps\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Minella\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"This may require additional support (Jiras) for Spring Batch\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 5.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',997,'XD-1775','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1775\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"HdfsJdbc Acceptance Test\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',998,'XD-1781','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1781\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Add HdfsMongoDb Acceptance Test.\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 10.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Create Acceptance TestAdd Mongo to Ec2 Acceptance Test Environment.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',999,'XD-1814','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1814\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Acceptance Tests for Labels and taps\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1000,'XD-1767','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1767\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"JobExecution restart action should depend on job deployment status\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"At the JobExecution page if the job execution is failed and restartable then we should enable the \\\"restart\\\" action only if the job is deployed.Please see https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/pull/884 for the discussion related to this.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1001,'XD-1477','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1477\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Merge Container and ContainerMetadata as well as their \\\"repositories\\\"\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The two classes in question are:* org.springframework.xd.dirt.cluster.Container* org.springframework.xd.dirt.container.ContainerMetadataThe former is currently used by the Admin when making decisions about Module deployment. That latter was a replacement for RuntimeContainerInforEntity as we migrated the various Redis/InMemory Repositories to use the data that is now available in ZooKeeper instead.The ContainerRepository is currently used by the Admin leader and the ContainerMetadataRepository is used by the REST endpoint that supports the xd-shell\'s \'runtime containers\' command. Perhaps those can also be merged.In any case if not addressed by a larger refactoring the ContainerRepository should probably support an Iterable return rather than an Iterator. Having finders (e.g. for attribute key/values such as \\\"group\\\"==\\\"foo\\\") might be convenient for various Module deployment strategies.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1002,'XD-1360','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1360\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Karl I Lopes\", \"summary\": \"Json information returned by curl does not reflect deployed status correctly\", \"assignee\": \"Florent Biville\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Karl I Lopes\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 6.0, \"description\": \"The Json information returned by curl does not reflect deployed status correctly.To recreate:1. Start xd-singlenode2. start xd-shellIn the xd-shell    (i). stream create --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --name ticktock   (ii). stream listNote the status of the ticktock stream is deployed3. open a new command prompt & type curl http://localhost:9393/streams/ticktock4. Note the returned json stream:  {\\\"name\\\":\\\"ticktock\\\"\\\"deployed\\\":null\\\"definition\\\":\\\"time | log\\\"\\\"links\\\":[{\\\"rel\\\":\\\"self\\\"\\\"href\\\":\\\"http://localhost:9393/streams/ticktock\\\"}]}5. I would expect the json attribute \\\"deployed\\\" to be \\\"true\\\" but it is null.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 5.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1003,'XD-1591','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1591\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"summary\": \"Flatten out ephemeral nodes \", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Flatten out ephemeral nodes written by containers when deploying modules. For instance instead of {{.../streams/moduleType/moduleLabel/container}} use {{.../streams/moduleType.moduleLabel.container}}.This change allows us to derive state for a stream/job without having to traverse multiple layers of znodes. This is a big deal because:* each level of children requires a network call* Curator can only cache one level of children\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1004,'XD-1838','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1838\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"FileSourceTest needs to apply label to source and sink\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"* Currently Acceptance FileSource Acceptance Tests are failing** This is because the sink that tests the result for the file source test is a filesink.  Both use the \\\"file\\\" token.  Thus causing a failure* SimpleFileSource and SimpleFileSink needs to support a label method.* Update testFileSource to use the labels.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1005,'XD-1812','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1812\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Support Bus Producer Properties for Dynamic Producers\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Pass module properties from stream plugin to {{MessageBusAwareChannelResolver}}.Disallow partitioning properties.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1006,'XD-1840','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1840\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Document and review REST API\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 3.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"REST API needs to be finalized and documented for the GA release. The API to be reviewed by REST experts \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1007,'XD-1517','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1517\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Change request mapping for removing a stream deployment in XDController\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently _deployments - with an understore in XDController should be something else.  Need to segment up the url space better for stream/jobs to avoid a clash.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1008,'XD-1758','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1758\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"JMS Source (ActiveMQ) failing to use jmsUrl environment variable\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Deployed on: SingleNode Ec2 SingleNode MacSHA: 942c7868e3e0d0cf7730b536170438a0291f5cab[Description]JMS Source (Activemq) tried to access a broker on localhost.  The current deployment uses the following to set the JMS Broker:* export amq_url=tcp://ec2-54-221-32-82.compute-1.amazonaws.com:61616[Analysis]After reviewing the configuration of the jms-activemq-infrastructure-context.xml it was noted that the brokerUrl environment variable has been changed from amq.url to amqUrl.  While the jms-activemq.properties has not been changed (still amq.url).  After setting the following the test still failed:* export amqUrl=tcp://ec2-54-221-32-82.compute-1.amazonaws.com:61616After going into the jms-activemq-infrastructure-context.xml and replacing the amqUrl with amq.url the jms source (activemq) returned to normal operation.[Incident]Acceptance tests reported a failure on Saturday Morning\'s build that the JMS Source failed.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1009,'XD-1270','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1270\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Add states to the deployment of stream\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 2.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 3.0, \"issueLinks\": 6.0, \"storyPoint\": 20.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Improve how the state of the stream is managed.A deploy command moves the stream from the undeployed state to the deploying state. If all modules in the stream are successfully deployed the stream state is ΓÇÿdeployedΓÇÖ If one or more module deployments failed the stream state is failed.  Any modules that were successfully deployed are still running.  Sending an undeploy command will stop all modules of the stream and return the stream to the undeployed state.For the individual modules that failed we will be able to find out which ones failed.  Not yet sure if we can try to redeploy just those parts of the stream that failed.See the [design doc|https://docs.google.com/a/gopivotal.com/document/d/1kWtoH_xEF1wMklzQ8AZaiuhBZWIlpCDi8G9_hAP8Fgc/edit#heading=h.2rk74f16ow4i] for more details.Story points for this issue are the total of all the story points for the subtasks.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 3.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1010,'XD-1843','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1843\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"summary\": \"Write out initial stream deployment state\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 6.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently when a stream is deployed by {{DeploymentSupervisor}} the event thread blocks until all deployment requests have been answered or timed out. If there were any deployment errors we log a stack trace.Instead (or in addition to) we need to write out the results of the deployment request. My initial thought is that it would go under:{panel}{{/xd/deployments/streams/<name>/state}}{panel}The data for {{state}} will be a JSON map with fields {{state}} and an optional {{errorDescription}}.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1011,'XD-1844','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1844\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"summary\": \"Interface to capture required data for state calculation\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"When the state of all the individual modules for a stream are collected these states need to be examined in order to determine what the overall stream state is. These should be fed into an interface that can potentially be pluggable to handle all of the edge cases/scenarios that may arise.One possibility is:{noformat}public interface DeploymentUnitStateCalculator {DeploymentUnit.State calculate(DeploymentUnit deploymentUnitModuleDeploymentPropertiesProvider providerCollection<ModuleState> moduleStates);}{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1012,'XD-777','51','{\"key\": \"XD-777\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Add validation on tap definitions that checks for module names that are part of the stream definition\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Luke Taylor\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Try:{code}stream create --name aa --definition \\\"time | log\\\"tap create --name t1 --definition \\\"tap aa.log | log\\\"{code}Results in:{code}Command failed org.springframework.xd.rest.client.impl.SpringXDException: java.lang.NullPointerException{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 6.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1013,'XD-1810','51','{\"key\": \"XD-1810\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 51, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Assess XD Fails to connect to remote Redis Instance\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0