"Add a Kafka Source\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Geary\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"This would use the Kafka Spring Integration Extension. We have a version of this working but had to modify the adapter code as its not currently compatible with Spring Integration 4. See INTEXT-97\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 7.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1152,'XD-2092','62','{\"key\": \"XD-2092\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 62, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Enhance Container domain object\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently org.springframework.xd.dirt.cluster.Container has name and attributes (container attributes). This can be enhanced to include all the deployed modules number of deployed modules and any more useful info. and can subsequently be used to get a detailed runtime container info.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1153,'XD-2093','62','{\"key\": \"XD-2093\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 62, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"List Streams/Jobs based with deployed modules\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently there is a \\\"stream list\\\"/\\\"job list\\\" which shows the status of a given stream/job along with the DSL. and there is \\\"runtime modules\\\" which shows all the deployed modules with their container info.We need a better REST endpoint that gives all the deployed modules for a given stream/job along with the status.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1154,'XD-2094','62','{\"key\": \"XD-2094\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 62, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"UI: Cluster view of a container\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"We need a visual representation of the XD cluster with runtime container and deployed modules.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1155,'XD-2095','62','{\"key\": \"XD-2095\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 62, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"UI: Ability to deploy stream with deployment properties\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Admin UI currently allows job to be deployed with deployment properties we need similar way to deploy stream with the deployment properties (module count container matching criteria).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1156,'XD-2097','62','{\"key\": \"XD-2097\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 62, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Enable shutdown containers from admin server\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"When the container starts up it has a random http port for management configurations. If the container has management port enabled then we can store it as container attribute. If the admin can reach out to the container on that port then we can provide an option to shutdown container from the admin server.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1157,'XD-721','62','{\"key\": \"XD-721\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 62, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Deploy a new job module *after* XD-singlenode container has started.\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"After the xd-singlenode process has started create a new job that has dependencies not already in the parent application context and then create and run a new job that uses the new module.*Implementation Suggestions*Develop in the test tree we can put in the jar and config from https://github.com/SpringSource/spring-xd-samples/tree/master/batch-simple *How to verify it works.*In a JUnit test case copy in a new job that has new dependencies ..copy the lib and config directories into the location where the ModuleRegisty will pick it up.Deploy a new job and check in the job repository that the job ran and was successful.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1158,'XD-2105','62','{\"key\": \"XD-2105\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 62, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"MessageBus should see custom SpEL property accessors\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently custom SI property accessors are registered by a plugin (org.springframework.xd.dirt.plugins.SpelPropertyAccessorPlugin) and are not visible by the bus.I believe they should be.This may just be a matter of moving them around.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1159,'XD-1695','62','{\"key\": \"XD-1695\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 62, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Research how to secure Admin\'s REST endpoints\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 6.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to provide security configurations so that I can access REST endpoints in a secured manner. Ideally all the listed [REST|https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/wiki/REST-API#xd-resources] endpoints needs to be wrapped within a security layer. *Scope of this spike:** Research Spring Security and Spring Boot and the OOTB features * Design considerations and approach for XD* Developer experience** How users will be configuring security credentials?** How DSL shell will be handled?** How Admin UI will be handled?\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 5.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1160,'XD-2091','62','{\"key\": \"XD-2091\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 62, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Research approach to bootstrap custom modules\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Design Spike: Investigate various approaches to bootstrap custom modules. Can Spring Boot be leveraged? Starter POM?\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1161,'XD-2169','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2169\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Evaluate Spring Boot dependency upgrade\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to evaluate Spring Boot dependency upgrades so that I can make sure there aren\'t any side effects or impacts to existing functionalities. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1162,'XD-2146','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2146\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to spring boot 1.1.7.SNAPSHOT\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have latest Spring Boot snapshot pulled as a dependency so that I can inherit and implement the OOTB security features.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1163,'XD-2143','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2143\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add Basic Auth support\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option of _Basic Auth_ so that I\'m challenged to provide _user name_ and _password_ when making a request.Technical Implementation:This functionality is provided in Spring Boot 1.1.x it should be a matter of adding the spring boot security starter dependency to the spring-xd-dirt project.  It will be controlled using the spring boot property server.basic.enabled = true/false.  Our default in application.yml for this property should be false.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1164,'XD-2119','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2119\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Support accessing admin server endpoints over HTTPS\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to enable HTTPS so that I can access XD\'s Admin server [endpoints|https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/wiki/REST-API#xd-resources] over secured communication.Technical Implementation:This functionality is available in Spring Boot 1.2.0 M1 and has been backported into the 1.1.x branch to be released under Spring 1.1.7.  We can test against 1.1.7 SNAPSHOT.Working through the way to update the build file to pick up a new version of boot is a bit tricky :(\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1165,'XD-2145','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2145\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"XD Shell needs to be be able to authenticate using basic auth to admin server\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I want to be able to provide security credentials to the XD Shell so that I can interact with an xd admin server that is secured via basic authTechnical implementation:Add ---password and --username to the admin config command.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1166,'XD-2144','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2144\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Support Spring Boot\'s single-user security configurations\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to provide single-user security configurations so that I can override them as needed.*Reference:*[Spring Boot - Security|http://docs.spring.io/spring-boot/docs/1.1.x-SNAPSHOT/reference/html/boot-features-security.html]*Scope:*Configurations can be provided through _servers.yml_ file.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1167,'XD-1616','64','{\"key\": \"XD-1616\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"UI: The user should provide username/password to gain access to the UI\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Secure Admin UI to challenge users to enter username and password to gain access.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1168,'XD-2147','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2147\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to spring boot 1.1.7.RELEASE\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have latest Spring Boot RELEASE pulled as a dependency so that I can inherit and implement the OOTB security features.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1169,'XD-1811','64','{\"key\": \"XD-1811\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Add ResourceModuleRegistry with custom modules location\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"If someone wants to have a dedicated location (module registry) for the custom modules and can be accessed from any Spring supported resource URL location then we need to support.Currently we use Delegating ModuleRegistry which uses ResourceModuleRegistry implementations that look for location `xd.module.home` and `classpath:/modules/`. Maybe we can add an additional ResourceModuleRegistry with `xd.custom.module.home` and use it for custom modules.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1170,'XD-2170','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2170\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"summary\": \"NoNodeException for job creation\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The following exception was encountered by a few parties: for example https://gopivotal-com.socialcast.com/messages/21678398{noformat}ERROR LeaderSelector-0 leader.LeaderSelector - The leader threw an exceptionorg.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException$NoNodeException: KeeperErrorCode = NoNode for /xd/deployments/jobs/NNNN/modulesat org.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException.create(KeeperException.java:111)at org.apache.zookeeper.KeeperException.create(KeeperException.java:51)at org.apache.zookeeper.ZooKeeper.getChildren(ZooKeeper.java:1586)at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.GetChildrenBuilderImpl$3.call(GetChildrenBuilderImpl.java:214)at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.GetChildrenBuilderImpl$3.call(GetChildrenBuilderImpl.java:203)at org.apache.curator.RetryLoop.callWithRetry(RetryLoop.java:107)at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.GetChildrenBuilderImpl.pathInForeground(GetChildrenBuilderImpl.java:199)at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.GetChildrenBuilderImpl.forPath(GetChildrenBuilderImpl.java:191)at org.apache.curator.framework.imps.GetChildrenBuilderImpl.forPath(GetChildrenBuilderImpl.java:38)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.server.JobDeploymentListener.recalculateJobStates(JobDeploymentListener.java:197)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.server.DeploymentSupervisor$LeaderListener.takeLeadership(DeploymentSupervisor.java:389)at org.apache.curator.framework.recipes.leader.LeaderSelector$WrappedListener.takeLeadership(LeaderSelector.java:536)at org.apache.curator.framework.recipes.leader.LeaderSelector.doWork(LeaderSelector.java:398)at org.apache.curator.framework.recipes.leader.LeaderSelector.doWorkLoop(LeaderSelector.java:443)at org.apache.curator.framework.recipes.leader.LeaderSelector.access$100(LeaderSelector.java:63)at org.apache.curator.framework.recipes.leader.LeaderSelector$2.call(LeaderSelector.java:244)at org.apache.curator.framework.recipes.leader.LeaderSelector$2.call(LeaderSelector.java:238)at java.util.concurrent.FutureTask.run(FutureTask.java:266)at java.util.concurrent.Executors$RunnableAdapter.call(Executors.java:511)at java.util.concurrent.FutureTask.run(FutureTask.java:266)at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1142)at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:617)at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:745){noformat}No specific details on reproducing yet; although the Socialcast thread indicates:{quote}I only hit this when I have tried to deploy a job that fails deployment the first time{quote}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1171,'XD-2190','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2190\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Kashyap Parikh\", \"summary\": \"xd-shell from 1.0.1 doesn\'t work with 1.0.0 GA admin\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Kashyap Parikh\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Targeting xd-shell from 1.0.1 to 1.0.0 GA admin server failsserver-unknown:>admin config info  -------------  -------------------------------------------------------------  Result         Unable to contact XD Admin Server at \'http://localhost:9393\'.  Target         http://localhost:9393  Timezone used  Pacific Standard Time (UTC -8:00)  -------------  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------An exception ocurred during targeting:java.lang.NullPointerException    at org.springframework.xd.rest.client.impl.SpringXDTemplate.<init>(SpringXDTemplate.java:110)    at org.springframework.xd.rest.client.impl.SpringXDTemplate.<init>(SpringXDTemplate.java:137)    at org.springframework.xd.shell.command.ConfigCommands.target(ConfigCommands.java:106)    at org.springframework.xd.shell.command.ConfigCommands.afterPropertiesSet(ConfigCommands.java:191)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1172,'XD-2181','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2181\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"Document how to enable SSL and Basic authentication \", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I want to know my configuration options are for enabling SSL/HTTPS and Basic authentication for administration endpoints so that I can secure my application.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1173,'XD-2192','64','{\"key\": \"XD-2192\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 64, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Fix failing script integration test\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"See https://build.spring.io/browse/XD-SCRIPTS-723\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1174,'XD-2069','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2069\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Provide a way to debug the http source\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The http source does not provide debug logging to see information such as http headers and requests in particular if a non OK response is returned.I updated the log4j config for org.jboss.netty but it had no effect.  I suspect this is due to the need to configure the netty logging system via InternalLoggerFactory.setDefaultFactory(new Log4JLoggerFactory()).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1175,'XD-2154','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2154\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Research REST endpoint approach to push custom module\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 3.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have a REST API to point and push an archive that includes custom module definitions and configurations so that I don\'t have to manually move and set it up.*Scope of this spike:** Assess customer requirement brainstorm and document options* Socialize with the team to collect feedback* Identify phases* Create new stories\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1176,'XD-2178','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2178\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add remote partitioning on \'jdbchdfs\' job\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to supply data partitioning strategy so that I can parallelize ingest of data from RDBMS to HDFS.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1177,'XD-2180','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2180\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Expose property to change \\\"commit-interval\\\"\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to override the default \\\"commit-interval\\\" so that I can configure commit interval depending on data volume.*Note:*This would apply for all OOTB jobs that has partition support. The property could be part of _servers.yml_ file.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1178,'XD-1864','65','{\"key\": \"XD-1864\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Add paging support for UI list views\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 2.0, \"issueLinks\": 4.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have _paging_ support so that I can scroll through the list of streams jobs and containers. Currently the following error is thrown when we cross >20 rows:http://localhost:9393/jobs/definitions.jsonJSON Response:{code:xml}[{links: [ ]logref: \\\"IllegalStateException\\\"message: \\\"Not all instances were looked at\\\"}]{code}Stack trace:{code}15:51:21931 ERROR http-nio-9393-exec-9 rest.RestControllerAdvice - Caught exception while handling a requestjava.lang.IllegalStateException: Not all instances were looked atat org.springframework.util.Assert.state(Assert.java:385){code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 2.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1179,'XD-2085','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2085\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Test Recommended XD Cluster Strategy on slow/bad network\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"h1. Run Acceptance tests on the following  deployments.  h2. Slow NetworkSimulate slow network by deploying a XD cluster where the ZK Ensemble is only available via WAN.  h2. Network packet lossSimulate cases where a network packets can be lost.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1180,'XD-2061','65','{\"key\": \"XD