s\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Document Kafka source\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1187,'XD-2044','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2044\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Add SFTP source\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to use the _SFTP_ source module so that I can access transfer and mange files over any reliable data streams.*Reference:*[Spring Integration SFTP Adapter|http://docs.spring.io/spring-integration/reference/html/sftp.html]Need to consider the infrastructure for testing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1188,'XD-2060','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2060\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add JDBC source\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"As an user I\'d like to have a native _JDBC_ source module to ingest data directly from various databases. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1189,'XD-2196','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2196\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Refactor ContainerRegistrar\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Decouple from DeploymentListener. Make DL a public class to handle deployment related events.  Remove createSimpleModule() and createComposedModule() from DL.  This will be delegated to ModuleDeployer which will eventually be further refactored to use the proposed ModuleFactory.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1190,'XD-2197','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2197\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Create ModuleFactory\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"ModuleFactory is responsible for determining how the Module application context is created from available sources at the resource location exposed via the ModuleDefinition. The factory creates the application context and creates a SimpleModule or CompositeModule as appropropriate. For example if an XML file is present it is assumed to be the bean definition file used to create a CXMLAC. If no XML file is present inspect the properties file for the existence of well-known properties such as base-package-name for component scanning for an @Configuration or a module-class-name for an Annotated POJO based module (see XD-2100).  The MF is also responsible for creating composite modules.   Also includes Module refactoring add getApplicationContext() and probably setApplicationContext().  Also refactor CompositeModule code to use boot SpringApplicationBuilder  \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1191,'XD-1972','65','{\"key\": \"XD-1972\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Michael Minella\", \"summary\": \"Add ability to define nested jobs\", \"assignee\": \"liujiong\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Michael Minella\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"h3.  NarrativeAs a developer I need to be able to create a Spring XD job module that consists of a job orchestrating the execution of other Spring Batch jobs using the Spring Batch Job Step (see section 5.3.6 here: http://docs.spring.io/spring-batch/reference/html/configureStep.html) within the same module definition.h3.  Acceptance Criteria# Define the \\\"contract\\\" for a job module## Currently the contract consists of a single job definition within the assembled {{ApplicationContext}} ({{context.getBean(Job.class)}}).## The new version will need to document what job definition within the assembled {{ApplicationContext}} should be run as the entry point.  I\'m assuming it would be by id ({{context.getBean(\\\"job\\\")}} for example) of the job but am open to other options.# A custom job module that orchestrates multiple Spring Batch jobs via Job steps should be able to be deployed and executed as a single Spring XD module.## Spring XD launches the job that conforms to the previously defined \\\"contract\\\".## Spring Batch manages the execution of the child jobs.# The existing OOTB jobs should work under the new \\\"contract\\\".h3.  Assumptions# The UI should \\\"just work\\\" in that child jobs update the job repository independently so no updates should be needed for an MVP of this functionality.# *This will be a breaking change for users that have developed custom job modules.*h3.  Out of Scope# Execution of child jobs that are remote (deployed on another node / {{ApplicationContext}}).# Dynamically assembling jobs via the shell\'s DSL or the UI.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1192,'XD-1519','65','{\"key\": \"XD-1519\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Provide job repository creation schema for additonal databases\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"oracle gemfire xd (derby should be the dialect) and sybase\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1193,'XD-2231','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2231\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Document job repo schema overrides\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Minella\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the flexibility to configure DB creds so that I can use a DB of choice for batch job repository (metadata persistence). The scope of this task is to have the configuration specifics documented in the wiki.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1194,'XD-1877','65','{\"key\": \"XD-1877\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create gemfire test\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Port https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/blob/master/src/test/scripts/gemfire_stream_testsNeed to consider how to start the server maybe use the jvm fork utilities?  Look into spring-data-gemfire as well.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1195,'XD-1876','65','{\"key\": \"XD-1876\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create test that uses #jsonPath with the filter module\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The script tests does the following.{code}# Filter for good and badcreate_stream \'httpfilter\' \\\"http | good: filter --expression=#jsonPath(payload\'\\\\$.entities.hashtags[*].text\').contains(\'good\') \\\\| aftergood: filter --expression=true \\\\| bad: filter --expression=#jsonPath(payload\'\\\\$.entities.hashtags[*].text\').contains(\'bad\') \\\\| goodandbad: splitter --expression=#jsonPath(payload\'$.id\') \\\\| file --dir=$TEST_DIR\\\" \'true\'{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1196,'XD-1879','65','{\"key\": \"XD-1879\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create test with jdbc sink and initializeDb=false\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Seehttps://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/blob/master/src/test/scripts/jdbc_tests#L96andhttps://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/blob/master/src/test/scripts/jdbc_tests#L64The second assert has initializeDb=false and so there are double the number of rows running the job a second time.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1197,'XD-2215','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2215\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"summary\": \"NPE in ContainerRedeploymentTests\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Running the distributed tests ({{-Drun_distributed_tests=true}}) against d109a3a and got the following:{noformat}   java.lang.NullPointerException   at org.springframework.xd.dirt.module.store.ZooKeeperModuleMetadataRepository.updateDeploymentStatus(ZooKeeperModuleMetadataRepository.java:209)   at org.springframework.xd.dirt.module.store.ZooKeeperModuleMetadataRepository.findAllByContainerId(ZooKeeperModuleMetadataRepository.java:313)   at org.springframework.xd.dirt.container.store.ZooKeeperContainerRepository.findAllRuntimeContainers(ZooKeeperContainerRepository.java:339)   at org.springframework.xd.dirt.rest.ContainersController.list(ContainersController.java:97)   at sun.reflect.GeneratedMethodAccessor100.invoke(Unknown Source)   at sun.reflect.DelegatingMethodAccessorImpl.invoke(DelegatingMethodAccessorImpl.java:43)   at java.lang.reflect.Method.invoke(Method.java:483)   at org.springframework.web.method.support.InvocableHandlerMethod.invoke(InvocableHandlerMethod.java:215)   at org.springframework.web.method.support.InvocableHandlerMethod.invokeForRequest(InvocableHandlerMethod.java:132)   at org.springframework.web.servlet.mvc.method.annotation.ServletInvocableHandlerMethod.invokeAndHandle(ServletInvocableHandlerMethod.java:104)   at org.springframework.web.servlet.mvc.method.annotation.RequestMappingHandlerAdapter.invokeHandleMethod(RequestMappingHandlerAdapter.java:749)   at org.springframework.web.servlet.mvc.method.annotation.RequestMappingHandlerAdapter.handleInternal(RequestMappingHandlerAdapter.java:689)   at org.springframework.web.servlet.mvc.method.AbstractHandlerMethodAdapter.handle(AbstractHandlerMethodAdapter.java:83)   at org.springframework.web.servlet.DispatcherServlet.doDispatch(DispatcherServlet.java:938)   at org.springframework.web.servlet.DispatcherServlet.doService(DispatcherServlet.java:870)   at org.springframework.web.servlet.FrameworkServlet.processRequest(FrameworkServlet.java:961)   at org.springframework.web.servlet.FrameworkServlet.doGet(FrameworkServlet.java:852)   at javax.servlet.http.HttpServlet.service(HttpServlet.java:620)   at org.springframework.web.servlet.FrameworkServlet.service(FrameworkServlet.java:837)   at javax.servlet.http.HttpServlet.service(HttpServlet.java:727)   at org.apache.catalina.core.ApplicationFilterChain.internalDoFilter(ApplicationFilterChain.java:{noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1198,'XD-2235','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2235\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"Basic authentication realm is always \'null\'\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Besides the Basic authentication realm being always {{null}} {{security.basic.realm}} is always ignored.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1199,'XD-2245','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2245\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Gemfire Source throws classnotfound \", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"* Steps to reproduce.** Start admin & container.** Follow the instructions from https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/wiki/Sources#gemfire-source*** When you post the message is when the stacktrace shows up in the container.Copying the gemfire-7.0.2.jar to the lib directory will resolve the error.  The stacktrace is attached.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1200,'XD-2247','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2247\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"summary\": \"Log version number in log files\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"When answering support questions the first step is to determine what version of the software the customer is using. This question can be easily answered if we log the version as one of the fields in the log file. For example:{noformat}10:44:21212 1.0.2.BUILD-SNAPSHOT  INFO DeploymentSupervisorCacheListener-0 server.ContainerListener - Container arrived: Container{name=\'431baa56-b23b-48fc-b37d-18b52231e799\' attributes={ip=192.168.25.177 host=Patrick-Peralta-MacBook-Pro.local groups= pid=38004 id=431baa56-b23b-48fc-b37d-18b52231e799}}{noformat}This way when we receive log snippets (initial support inquires rarely include the entire log file) we can immediately determine if the issue has already been fixed in a later release.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1201,'XD-2251','65','{\"key\": \"XD-2251\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 65, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"The HTTP Source creates the ChannelPipeline inefficiently\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The ChannelPipelineFactory used by the HTTP source should cache expensive objects used by the ChannelPipeline between requests because creating them every time is inefficient (and in the case of HTTPS it can become even more expensive). \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1202,'XD-2114','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2114\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Leo Chu\", \"summary\": \"Job stuck in \\\"deploying\\\" state when no containers are available\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Leo Chu\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"A job gets stuck in \\\"deploying\\\" state when a job is deployed when there are no containers available.  When a container is started after this event the job doesn\'t automatically start because of the job is stuck in the \\\"deploying\\\" state instead of the \\\"failed\\\" state.  Refer to https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/blob/193088dc164c73e07d7b4509de22241b28bf42b3/spring-xd-dirt/src/main/java/org/springframework/xd/dirt/server/JobDeploymentListener.javaUpdate of the status in Zookeeper is inside the NoContainerException catch block.This works correctly for streams.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1203,'XD-2238','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2238\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"summary\": \"Improve module deployment distribution\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"When a container joins the XD cluster (via ZooKeeper) it triggers stream/job module deployments for modules that need to be deployed. If multiple containers are being started at around the same time this can result in the first few containers taking all of the deployments while leaving the rest without any deployments.To solve this we will introduce a \\\"quiet period\\\" where no deployments will be triggered within _n_ seconds of a container joining where _n_ will have a default value (perhaps 5 to 10 seconds). This value will be configurable.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1204,'XD-2230','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2230\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Fix the configuration problem with Filter and Transform modules\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to leverage _propertieis-location_ parameter while using *Filter* or *Transform* modules so that I can load the user-defined properties included in the external properties file. Attempting to include the _propertieis-location_ attribute errors out - refer to the attachment.It could also be beneficial to load user-defined properties through stream definition similar to deployment properties.Example:--script=myscript.groovy --variables=foo=bargoo=gaz\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1205,'XD-923','66','{\"key\": \"XD-923\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Error Channel for streams modules that fail to process a message\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to be notified when a exception is thrown in a module so that I can tap into an error channel to receive the failures for each stream/module.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1206,'XD-2300','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2300\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Document automatic declaration of DQL for each consumer queue\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The scope is to document the automatic creation and binding of DLQ for each \'pipe\' (consumer queue).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1207,'XD-2199','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2199\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Simplify ModuleRegistry\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 2.0, \"issueLinks\": 3.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"MR is responsible for looking up existing module definitions by name and type.  ModuleDefinition should contain name type and resource; where resource is a springframework.core.io.Resource containing the root path of the module definition. This could be file classpath http hdfs or something else but the contents under this path will not be inspected or processed by MR. The exception is for composite modules which should contain a list of corresponding Resources.Simplify ModuleDefinition - remove classpath. Provide support for CompositeModuleDefinition - requires a list of resources (possibly a subclass)Also retire RedisModuleRegistry\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 2.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1208,'XD-1151','66','{\"key\": \"XD-1151\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Apply Composite GoF pattern to ModuleDefinition\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1209,'XD-2268','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2268\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Create a maintenance branch\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to have a maintenance branch so that I can commit MINOR release _(ex: 1.0.2)_ code changes instead of committing to MASTER.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1210,'XD-2269','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2269\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Remove deprecated functions \", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a follow-up action from module registry refactoring we would have to clean-up deprecated functions _(ex: download of module definitions)_ within our codebase. It may also be necessary to clean-up Shell and Admin-UI modules. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1211,'XD-2078','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2078\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sina Sojoodi\", \"summary\": \"\\\"http | hdfs\\\" stream starts throwing exceptions after a few minutes \", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Sina Sojoodi\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 5.0, \"description\": \"Environment:- Hadoop Installation: PHD Service for PCF  (PHD1.1 based on Apache Hadoop 2.0.5:  2.0.5-alpha-gphd-2.1.0.0 ) running on vCHS- Spring XD running in singlenode mode (version 1.0.0.RC1) on a vCHS VMSteps to reproduce:1- Setup a stream in Spring XD shell: \\\"http --port=9000 | hdfs --rollover=10M --idleTimeout=60000\\\" --deploy2- Hit port 9000 every second with 1-10KB of JSON data3- Observe the temp file being created in HDFS under /xd/<stream name>4- Run `hadoop fs tail <file> --follow` to see that data is being written to HDFSExpected result:- HDFS sink continues to operate and eventually roll-over at 10MBActual:- After about 2 minutes of successful HDFS writes the HDFS sink crashes and starts throwing exceptions (see full log attached): \\\"\'java.io.IOException: All datanodes 192.168.109.61:50010 are bad. Aborting...\\\"- The temp file is never closed even after the stream is undeployed or destroyed.  Here are some details of our investigation that may be useful:- I start both the shell and the singlenode runner with --hadoopDistro phd1;  I also configured the hadoop fs namenode correctly in the XD shell.- \\\"http <options> | file <options>\\\" work as expected; so does \\\"http <options> | log\\\"- \\\"time | hdfs\\\" does not show the same crash problem. Up until now only the http source combined with hdfs sink presents this problem- Putting a 4-10MB file in HDFS via the `Hadoop fs put` commands in Spring XD worked fine; so it\'s not a disk limitation.- This could be related to PHD service running on vCHS since supporting this configuration is fairly new. But it\'s only reproducable (consistently) with Spring XD\'s \\\"http | hdfs\\\" stream. \", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 12.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1212,'XD-2262','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2262\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Document \'idleTimeout\' setting \", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Document --idleTimeout setting to not exceed the HDFS timeout value.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1213,'XD-2264','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2264\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Infrastructure for RabbitMQ Cluster (ECB)\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Pre-requisite for Rabbit MQ Benchmarks:* Infrastructure setup* Configuration changes* Tool-chain setup* IPerf\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1214,'XD-2265','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2265\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 66, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Vary consumers size (ECB-4)\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Using a single producer message size of 1000 bytes Pretch of 100.   Send 1M messages and increase or decrease so that a given test iteration takes about 2 minutes.Vary the number of consumers.   Measure the msg/sec rate and calculate the data transfer rate in MB/sec.*Number of consumers:** 1* 2* 4* 6* 10* 50During the measurements look at the RabbitMQ Admin UI and see if the queue is backing up.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1215,'XD-2266','66','{\"key\": \"XD-2266\", \"vo