\"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Create a 1.0.x \'Docs\' branch \", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Placeholder for Doc generation and supporting multiple doc branches.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1248,'XD-2244','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2244\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Venkatesh Sivasubramanian\", \"summary\": \"Streams sending to Job Queue issue\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Venkatesh Sivasubramanian\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Look at the below Stream definition. This gets to \\\"deployed\\\" state even without the corresponding job. And then from there the same Job or any other Job can\'t be deployed and it goes to a hung state. Here is an example of the Stream definition:stream create --name jobName --definition \\\"file --ref=true --dir=/tmp/springxdsource/dropbox --pattern=*.csv > queue:job:filetsjob-sample002\\\" --deploy\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1249,'XD-2216','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2216\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to Spring 4.1.2 SI 4.1.0 SA 1.4.0\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 3.0, \"issueLinks\": 3.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 6.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have Spring \'Core\' upgraded to 4.1.1 (_milestone_ ) so that I can benefit from performance improvements associated with \'compiled\' SpEL and other enhancements. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 7.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 3.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1250,'XD-2270','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2270\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to Spring Boot 1.2.0\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As to prepare for 1.1 release we would like to upgrade to Spring Boot 1.2.0 (RC1) (depends on Spring 4.1.2) so that we can leverage the new features enhancement and bug fixes. [Spring Boot Milestones|https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/milestones]\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1251,'XD-2271','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2271\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to Spring Integration 4.1.0\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As to prepare for 1.1 release we would like to upgrade to Spring Integration 4.1.0 (RC) so that we can leverage the new features enhancement and bug fixes. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1252,'XD-2276','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2276\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Vary message size (EC-DB-2)\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Use a single producer single consumer prefetch size = 50.  Send 1M messages and increase or decrease so that a given test iteration takes about 2 minutes.Vary the message size and measure the msg/sec rate and calculate data transfer rate in MB/sec.*Message Sizes:*100 bytes100010000100000 During the measurements look at the RabbitMQ Admin UI and see if the queue is backing up.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1253,'XD-2277','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2277\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Vary prefecth size (EC-DB-3)\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Use a single producer single consumer message size of 1000 bytes.   Send 1M messages and increase or decrease so that a given test iteration takes about 2 minutes.Vary the prefetch size.  Measure the msg/sec rate and calculate the data transfer rate in MB/sec.*Prefetch Sizes:** 1* 10* 50* 100* 10000During the measurements look at the RabbitMQ Admin UI and see if the queue is backing up.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1254,'XD-2279','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2279\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Vary consumer size (EC-DB-4)\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Using a single producer message size of 1000 bytes Pretch of 100.   Send 1M messages and increase or decrease so that a given test iteration takes about 2 minutes.Vary the number of consumers.   Measure the msg/sec rate and calculate the data transfer rate in MB/sec.*Number of consumers:** 1* 2* 4* 6* 10* 50During the measurements look at the RabbitMQ Admin UI and see if the queue is backing up.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1255,'XD-2280','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2280\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Vary producer size (EC-DB-5)\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Use the number of consumers gave a maximum throughput in the previous test (say 10 consumers) message size 100 bytes Prefetch 100.   Send 1M messagesVary the number of producers.  Measure the msg/sec rate and calculate the data transfer rate in MB/sec.*Number of producers:** 2* 4* 6* 10* 50During the measurements look at the RabbitMQ Admin UI and see if the queue is backing up.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1256,'XD-2275','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2275\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Vary Producer and Consumer in combination using 2 Queues (ECB-6)\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The results from EC2 testing show that once prefetch and message size are set varying the number of producers or consumers independently does not impact the message rate.  The in-house testing numbers need another plan to try an understand some discrepancies. Using 500 prefetch 1000 byte message size run two instances of PerfTest at the same time with each instance referencing a different queue.  Vary the number of consumer and publishers.Test 1 (one producer / one consumer):-a -u q1 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q2 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500Test 2 (one producer / two consumers):-a -u q1 -p -x 1 -y 2 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q2 -p -x 1 -y 2 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500Test 3 (two producers / one consumer):-a -u q1 -p -x 2 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 120 -q 500-a -u q2 -p -x 2 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 120 -q 500Test 4 (two producers / two consumers):-a -u q1 -p -x 2 -y 2 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q2 -p -x 2 -y 2 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1257,'XD-2278','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2278\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Vary queue number (ECB-7)\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Based on the the results from B-6 select the number of consumer/producers that give a distinct >5% increase in message rate.  Below 5% change in message rate prefer lower consumer/producer count.    Vary the number of PerfTest instances that are run simultaneously and use their own independent queue from 1 until the overall messages/sec on the broker plateaus.   Note the CPU performance using ΓÇÿtopΓÇÖ for the broker and PerfTest processes.Test 1 (2 queues)-a -u q1 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q2 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500Test 2 (3 queues)-a -u q1 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q2 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q3 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500Test 3 (4 queues)-a -u q1 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q2 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q3 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q4 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500Test 4 (5 queues)-a -u q1 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q2 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q3 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q4 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500-a -u q5 -p -x 1 -y 1 -s 1000 -z 60 -q 500etc.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1258,'XD-2283','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2283\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Vary queue number on 32 core machine (ECB-8)\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Rerun test XD-2278 on a EC2 32 core machine and see when we max out.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1259,'XD-2151','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2151\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"HDFS sink should honor --fileExtension parameter for bzip2 compressed files\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Looks like the --fileExtension isn\'t used when compressing files with bzip2 some use cases requirer bz2 instead of bzip2 as the extension. Also \'.bz2\' should be the default extension. At the same time we should change the default gzip extension to \'.gz\'.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1260,'XD-2198','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2198\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Create CompositeModuleRegistry\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently there is no ModuleRegistry contract for composite modules. The composed module definition is maintained in ZooKeeperModuleDefinitionRepository which delegates to the ModuleRegistry to define and validate component modules. The repository should be converted to a ModuleRegistry.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1261,'XD-1077','67','{\"key\": \"XD-1077\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Proof of Concept for module contributions based off Boot\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 40.0, \"watchcount\": 7.0, \"description\": \"Develop out a Proof of concept for review that allows users to easily create a new module to Spring XD. Key features to be enabled:1. Allow existing modules to be included as a classpath dependency2. Consolidate shared libraries in existing modules (e.g. a shared lib for all gemfire modules)3. User develops a module as a normal Java project4. User\'s project can then be added to a runtime container in the same way (as a dependency)Nice to have: 1. at development time container can run continuously and pick up changes from user\'s module project.2. Java config for a module.3. command line functionality to create project scaffolding.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 6.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1262,'XD-2103','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2103\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Add Kafka sink\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to write into _Kafka_ sink so that I can publish mass data into Kafka broker.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1263,'XD-2177','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2177\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Add support for Pivotal HD 2.1 (XD 1.0.2 Release)\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"*XD 1.0.2 Release + PHD 2.1 Upgrade - Action Items:** Update to SHDP 2.0.3* Add Hadoop 2.5 (hadoop25)* Change PHD 2.x from phd20 to phd21* Test PHD 2.0 with phd21 * Document that both PHD 2.1 and PHD 2.0 is supported with phd21\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1264,'XD-2307','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2307\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support for PHD 2.1 (XD 1.1 M1 Release)\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"*XD 1.1 M1 Release + PHD 2.1 Upgrade - Action Items:** Update to SHDP 2.1.M2 * Add Hadoop 2.5 (hadoop25)* Remove hadoop22* Remove PHD 1.0 (phd1) * Change PHD 2.x from phd20 to phd21* Test PHD 2.0 with phd21\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1265,'XD-2209','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2209\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add acceptance test to include Gemfire use case\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"To enrich acceptance test I\'d like to have basic coverage to evaluate Gemfire use cases. An example would be to ingest data from HTTP source and write it to Gemfire server.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1266,'XD-2213','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2213\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add stress test\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"To enrich acceptance test coverage I\'d like to have stress test scenario that includes ingesting data from _HTTP_ and then writing it to _Log_ sink.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1267,'XD-2223','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2223\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Provide proper ordering for all REST endpoints\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"With the implementation of XD-1864 we need to make sure that the (paginated) data returned from the REST endpoints has proper default ordering.Up to now we have done client-side ordering in the Admin UI but with server-side pagination the server-side should support proper pagination as well.Eventually we may even decide to provide more flexible ordering options (ASC vs DESC sort on different properties etc.) which may be a separate Jira.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1268,'XD-2296','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2296\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 67, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add config parameter to enable/disable message rates in cluster view\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have a config parameter preferably in _servers.yml_ file so that I can enable/disable message rates in the cluster view. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1269,'XD-2310','67','{\"key\": \"XD-2310\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"s