tasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"*Version:*XD: 1.1 M1*Problem:*Trying to use tcp-client source module and observing an exception while deploying the stream.*Stream Definition:*{code:xml} curl --data name=dummy-firehose --data definition=\'tcp-client --decoder=LF --port=8080 | log\' --data deploy=true http://localhost:9393/streams/definitions{\\\"name\\\":\\\"dummy-firehose\\\"\\\"status\\\":null\\\"definition\\\":\\\"tcp-client --decoder=LF --port=8080 | log\\\"\\\"_links\\\":{\\\"self\\\":{\\\"href\\\":\\\"http://localhost:9393/streams/dummy-firehose\\\"}}}{code}The same curl command works fine against XD 1.0.1 release.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1291,'XD-2306','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2306\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support to install custom module archive\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 6.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to push the custom module (built as uber-jar) via a REST API so that I can install the custom module in cluster. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 7.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1292,'XD-2383','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2383\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add a Shell command to push custom module\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have a Shell command so that I can point to the custom-built _module_ archive and push it to the runtime for immediate usage. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1293,'XD-2351','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2351\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"POM generation creates the correct dependency list\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"We are referencing Spring.IO deps when we shouldn\'t (since we moved to a different version of boot than in in the platform).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1294,'XD-2090','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2090\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Custom module packaging strategy\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 9.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have guidance to create custom modules so that I can align the development practices with recommended approach. 11/20: Update: Scope of this task is to create an example to demonstrate and document the capability.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1295,'XD-2368','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2368\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Research Spark integration options (phase #2)\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a continuation we would like to further investigate Spark develop POC and identify the best appropriate design and implementation for XD.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1296,'XD-2331','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2331\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Job deployment list returns 404 after Laptop wakes up\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"*Version:*XD 1.0.1Mac OSX 10.9.5*Problem:*- Deployed a simple batch job in \'singlenode\'- Laptop put to sleep mode- After login: notice that ZK is establishing connection - Continues to clean-up prior to redeployment but never goes through successfully- Listing job both in UI and Shell states it is \\\"undeployed\\\"*Gunnar\'s experiment:*- System is running in Single Node- Laptop goes to sleep- After waking up your laptop from sleep you cannot retrieve the list of deployed jobs anymore (in AdminUI)*Error:*Only getting back a *404* - \\\"NoSuchBatchJobException\\\" \\\"Batch Job with the name abcd doesn\'t exist\\\"\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1297,'XD-2390','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2390\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add regression test\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Verify that network interruptions will not negatively affect the XD cluster.  Verify that a container that looses connectivity will be able to rejoin the cluster cleanly.Modules will redploy when the network is back up.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1298,'XD-2124','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2124\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Research integration options for Sqoop \'tasklet\'\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the ability to mass-ingest data from various database systems so that I\'m not restricted with the current approach (_jdbchdfs_) that is dependent on JDBC drivers. *Spike Scope:** Identify integration options* Collaborate to determine the design* Document outcome (design specs)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 8.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1299,'XD-2334','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2334\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Create base perf test criteria\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Since Kafka and Rabbit have different strategies on how a message system is implemented we will need to update the tests used on rabbit to work with Kafka.  While they will not be exactly the same as before they should exercise the same principles.This story covers: * Create the consumer and producer execution configurations forkafka-producer-perf-test.sh and kafka-consumer-perf-test.sh. * Record the tests a spreadsheet much like the Rabbit Base test spreadsheet\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1300,'XD-1878','68','{\"key\": \"XD-1878\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create low volume http stress test\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"The testhttps://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/blob/master/src/test/scripts/httpbashis very simple it doesn\'t even check the results.  A small change tohttps://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/blob/master/spring-xd-test-fixtures/src/main/java/org/springframework/xd/test/generator/SimpleHttpGenerator.javaso that number of messages to post is specified would be part of this work.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1301,'XD-2120','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2120\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Provide file based storage for users groups (and roles)\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to provide file based security configurations so that I can access the endpoints in a secured manner.Ideally all the listed *endpoints* (http://localhost:9393/) needs to be encapsulated within file based security layer.Reference:[Securing Web App|https://spring.io/guides/gs/securing-web/]\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1302,'XD-2375','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2375\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Research reactor-stream integration options\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have a _reactor-stream_ processor module so that I can ingest data using XD source modules and process them as time-window operations. *Example 1:*http | reactor-stream --timeWindow=10s --field=payload.sensorData --expressions=minavgThis would give you 10 second time window of the min and avg values.*Example 2:*Reactor as a module*Example 3:*Integration with Spark streaming and reactor\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1303,'XD-2321','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2321\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"UI: Create a dedicated scheduling page for Jobs\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 4.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Create a dedicated Scheduling Page for Jobs. Currently we create a form underneath the deployments table. That is a bit unwieldy when many deployed jobs are shown in the table.Similar to XD-2320\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1304,'XD-2352','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2352\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Property replacement does not happen in XML class attribute\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"After updating to Boot 1.2 RC1 the following replacement doesn\'t work.  {code:xml}<bean id=\\\"messageConverter\\\" class=\\\"${converterClass}\\\" />{code}which appears in the rabbit source and sink.  Feels like a core spring thing but that was updated earlier.Current workaround that was commited already so the build can pass is{code:xml}<bean id=\\\"clazz\\\" class=\\\"java.lang.Class\\\" factory-method=\\\"forName\\\">  <constructor-arg value=\\\"${converterClass}\\\"/></bean><bean id=\\\"messageConverter\\\" factory-bean=\\\"clazz\\\" factory-method=\\\"newInstance\\\"/>{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 6.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1305,'XD-2367','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2367\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Investigate TypeConvertingStreamTests.testBasicTypeConversionWithTap test failure in CI builds\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"TypeConvertingStreamTests.testBasicTypeConversionWithTap() is failing intermittently. Why?\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1306,'XD-2377','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2377\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Update \\\"About\\\" section in UI with relevant release links\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have API and Documentation links in the [\\\"About\\\"|https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/blob/master/spring-xd-ui/app/scripts/shared/views/about.html] section within _admin-ui_. It would be ideal to have the version # dynamically replaced for every release.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1307,'XD-2234','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2234\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Peter Bulman\", \"summary\": \"Incorrect port in resource manager address overwrite\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 1.0, \"reporter\": \"Peter Bulman\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"the resource manager address overwrite is setting the port to 8032; the value cannot be set in servers.yml.  this occurs when pushing the config to hdfs and also when attempting to start the admin server on yarn. [ConfigurationFactoryBean] - Overwriting rmAddress=[0.0.0.0:8032] with rmAddress=[host:8032][root spring-xd-1.0.1.RELEASE-yarn]# ./bin/xd-yarn start admin  .   ____          _            __ _ _ /\\\\\\\\ / ___\'_ __ _ _(_)_ __  __ _ \\\\ \\\\ \\\\ \\\\( ( )\\\\___ | \'_ | \'_| | \'_ \\\\/ _` | \\\\ \\\\ \\\\ \\\\ \\\\\\\\/  ___)| |_)| | | | | || (_| |  ) ) ) )  \'  |____| .__|_| |_|_| |_\\\\__ | / / / / =========|_|==============|___/=/_/_/_/ :: Spring Boot ::        (v1.1.7.RELEASE)2014-10-13 16:50:28710 INFO [ConfiguringBeanFactoryPostProcessor] - No bean named \'taskScheduler\' has been explicitly defined. Therefore a default ThreadPoolTaskScheduler will be created.2014-10-13 16:50:28724 INFO [ConfiguringBeanFactoryPostProcessor] - No bean named \'taskExecutor\' has been explicitly defined. Therefore a default SyncTaskExecutor will be created.2014-10-13 16:50:30311 INFO [SpringYarnConfiguration] - Enabling CLIENT for Yarn2014-10-13 16:50:30335 INFO [SpringYarnConfiguration] - We couldn\'t figure out if we could use existing configuration2014-10-13 16:50:30335 INFO [SpringYarnConfiguration] - Building configuration for bean \'yarnConfiguration\'2014-10-13 16:50:30383 INFO [SpringYarnConfigBuilder] - Existing yarnConfiguration: null2014-10-13 16:50:30658 INFO [ConfigurationFactoryBean] - Overwriting fsUri=[hdfs://host:8020] with fsUri=[hdfs://host:8020]2014-10-13 16:50:30659 INFO [ConfigurationFactoryBean] - Overwriting rmAddress=[0.0.0.0:8032] with rmAddress=[host:8032]\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1308,'XD-2366','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2366\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Doc generation accesses http://docbook.sourceforge.net\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"When generating docs the build tries to accesshttp://docbook.sourceforge.net/release/images/draft.pngYou will observe output like:{code}Error with opening URL \'http://docbook.sourceforge.net/release/images/draft.png\': docbook.sourceforge.netBackground image not available: http://docbook.sourceforge.net/release/images/draft.pngBackground image not available: http://docbook.sourceforge.net/release/images/draft.pngBackground image not available: http://docbook.sourceforge.net/release/images/draft.pngBackground image not available: http://docbook.sourceforge.net/release/images/draft.pngBackground image not available: http://docbook.sourceforge.net/release/images/draft.pngBackground image not available: http://docbook.sourceforge.net/release/images/draft.png{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1309,'XD-2107','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2107\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Allow aggregate-counter to increment by some value of the message\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently the aggregate counter only adds +1 to the individual values even though support is there to add any increment.This ticket is about surfacing a SpEL expression on the message to choose the increment\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1310,'XD-2408','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2408\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"When a tap is re-deployed after undeploy it doesn\'t work\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"When a tap on a stream is undeployed and re-deployed it stops working.To make it work the main stream associated with the tap needs to be undeployed and re-deployed.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1311,'XD-2332','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2332\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"AdminUI - Provide Server-Side Cron Expression Validation\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"It is easy to get a cron expression wrong. Provide validation of the cron expression on the Schedule Job page using async validation. * Submit the cron expression to the server-side - and validate that the expression is valid.* Send a success message back (we may even send back some meta data ΓÇª e.g. when is the next execution going to take place)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1312,'XD-2418','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2418\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Kafka Sink: Support async Producer\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The kafka sink supports properties for an async producer (e.g. {{queue.buffering.max.ms}} ) but you cannot enable such a producer (only {{sync}} ). Async producers batch messages (at the risk of message loss).Add a new property {{async}} default {{false}} and add the corresponding attribute to the {{<int-kafka:producer-configuration/>}} element{{async=\\\"$\\\\{async\\\\}\\\"}}\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1313,'XD-2423','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2423\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"WireTap is Applied to OutputChannel Before the Tap Channel has been Bound To The Bus\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"When establishing the tap we create the tap channel and add the WireTap before the tap channel has been bound to the bus.{quote}17:00:23918 ERROR task-scheduler-8 handler.LoggingHandler - org.springframework.messaging.MessageDeliveryException: Dispatcher has no subscribers for channel \'tap:stream:foo.time.0.tap.bridge\'.; nested exception is org.springframework.integration.MessageDispatchingException: Dispatcher has no subscribersat org.springframework.integration.channel.AbstractSubscribableChannel.doSend(AbstractSubscribableChannel.java:81)at org.springframework.integration.channel.AbstractMessageChannel.send(AbstractMessageChannel.java:277)at org.springframework.integration.channel.interceptor.WireTap.preSend(WireTap.java:129){quote}\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1314,'XD-2422','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2422\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"UI Provide fixed version numbers for NPM and Bower dependencies\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1315,'XD-2429','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2429\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Bind Producer Before Consumer\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"{quote}Here is the full exception:org.springframework.messaging.MessageDeliveryException: Dispatcher has no subscribers for channel \'ResourceConfiguredModule [name=filter type=processor group=request-rate index=0 @58b0f318]:use-expressiondefaultadminsinglenodehsqldbServer:9393.output\'.; nested exception is org.springframework.integration.MessageDispatchingException: Dispatcher has no subscribersand here is that stream:topic:httpstartstop > filter --expression=payload.getHttpStartStop().getPeerType().name().equals(\'Client\') | requestRateAggregator | appMetricsSplitter | router --expression=\'topic:app-request-rate-\'+#jsonPath(payload\'$.appId\')[2:59 PM] Gary Russell: @MarkFisher  @IlayaperumalGopinathan @PatrickPeralta  This looks like another (not fixed by the previous fix) timing problem with taps when using singlenode. The tap is started before the tap stream is deployed. But it\'s not clear to me how the filter module could be deployed/bound as a consumer before the requestRateAggregator[3:08 PM] Gary Russell: I see the problem: AbstractMessageBusBinderPlugin.bindConsumerAndProducers() binds the consumer before the producer - this is the wrong order for a passive component such as the filter. /cc @DavidTuranski{quote}\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1316,'XD-2431','68','{\"key\": \"XD-2431\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 68, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Workaround latest boot snapshot issue\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"* The workaround explicitly updates spring-core (latest boot needs it)* merges all application.yml documents that are not profile-specific under on spring: key (the latest boot requires it at least for now. Boot may go back see spring-projects/spring-boot#2022\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1317,'XD-2501','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2501\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to Boot 1.2.0 RELEASE and the dependencies\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a XD Admin I\'d like to upgrade to Spring Boot 1.2.0 RELEASE and the associated dependencies so that we can catch up with the latest features bug-fixes and enhancements. *Following XD dependencies needs upgraded to sync-up with Boot 1.2.0 RELEASE:*<activemq.version>5.10.0</activemq.version><aspectj.version>1.8.4</aspectj.version><commons-dbcp2.version>2.0.1</commons-dbcp2.version><h2.version>1.4.182</h2.version><hibernate.version>dd4.3.7.Final</hibernate.version><hibernate-validator.version>5.1.3.Final</hibernate-validator.version><hikaricp.version>2.2.5</hikaricp.version><hornetq.version>2.4.5.Final</hornetq.version><httpasyncclient.version>4.0.2</httpasyncclient.version><httpclient.version>4.3.6</httpclient.version><jackson.version>2.4.4</jackson.version><janino.version>2.6.1</janino.version><jetty.version>9.2.4.v20141103</jetty.version><jetty-jsp.version>2.2.0.v201112011158</jetty-jsp.version><joda-time.version>2.5</joda-time.version><jolokia.version>1.2.3</jolokia.version><junit.version>4.12</junit.version><liquibase.version>3.3.0</liquibase.version><log4j.version>1.2.17</log4j.version><log4j2.version>2.1</log4j2.version><mockito.version>1.10.8</mockito.version><mongodb.version>2.12.4</mongodb.version><mysql.version>5.1.34</mysql.version><reactor.version>1.1.5.RELEASE</reactor.version><reactor-spring.version>1.1.3.RELEASE</reactor-spring.version><servlet-api.version>3.1.0</servlet-api.version><spring.version>4.1.3.RELEASE</spring.version><spring-batch.version>3.0.2.RELEASE</spring-batch.version><spring-data-releasetrain.version>Evans-SR1</spring-data-releasetrain.version><spring-hateoas.version>0.16.0.RELEASE</spring-hateoas.version><spring-mobile.version>1.1.3.RELEASE</spring-mobile.version><spring-security.version>3.2.5.RELEASE</spring-security.version><tomcat.version>8.0.15</tomcat.version><undertow.version>1.1.1.Final</undertow.version>\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1318,'XD-2404','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2404\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Provide an XD Starter POM for module projects\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Provide A maven pom to support module projects that will declare the Spring XD dependencies as provided configure the boot plugin for \'MODULE\' layout and other boilerplate build configuration. This should include a similar feature for gradle.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1319,'XD-2471','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2471\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Kafka Bus: Concurrency and compression support\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have concurrency and compression support for Kafka so that I can increase performance throughput and/or increase responsiveness*Things to consider:** make global configuration options be \\\"defaults\\\" and allow per-deployment overrides* add options for ** concurrency** compression support\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1320,'XD-2473','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2473\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Kafka Bus: Add support for ACK mode\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to _ACK_ messages so that I can guarantee that the message/request sent is successful. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1321,'XD-2122','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2122\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Secure endpoints using either ROLE_VIEWER and ROLE_ADMIN\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 2.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to configure default access control for endpoints so that I can grant access by _Admin_ or _Viewer_ roles.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1322,'XD-2261','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2261\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Document user-defined permission to role mapping\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to configure permissions so that I\'ll have the flexibility to bind permissions (REST endpoint) to a specific role. Default Roles:* Admin (CRUD)* Viewer (R)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1323,'XD-2260','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2260\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Document Admin and Viewer roles\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to configure _Admin_ and _Viewer_ roles so that I\'ll have the flexibility to decide role configurations.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1324,'XD-2430','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2430\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Create a Sqoop job and required batch tasklet integration code\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Based on the POC from XD-2124 we should create the actual implementation.Things to consider to store in step context:- capture Log output/MapReduce job counters- capture last-value from incremental imports\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1325,'XD-2531','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2531\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Document Sqoop job\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to refer to the documentation so that I can connect to Sqoop as recommended and create job definition based on the exposed _metadata_ options. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1326,'XD-2425','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2425\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Derek OKeeffe\", \"summary\": \"SpringXD\'s syslog source does not fully support syslog RFC5424\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Derek OKeeffe\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"SpringXD\'s syslog source cannot parse rfc5424 messages into a Map.For the messages we get in RFC 3164 springXD converts these to a Map.Since the rfc5424 data cannot be interpreted then the map contains just one key called \'UNDECODED\'.The result of this is that we get a string that looks like this (when we convert the message to a String){code} {UNDECODED=<182>Dec 02 2014 07:56:35: %ASA-6-113008: AAA transaction status ACCEPT : user = jbloggs}{code}Should be something like this (note the values below are for illustrative purposes only and should not be used as test data){code} {FACILITY=22 SEVERITY=6 TIMESTAMP=Tue Dec 02 07:56:35 HOST=the-hostname-that-sent-the-data TAG=%ASA-6-113008 MESSAGE=........}{code}h3. Root CauseSpring integration does not parse these messages. There is a JIRA for SI here:https://jira.spring.io/browse/INT-3450\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1327,'XD-2342','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2342\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Buelent Zeyben\", \"summary\": \"JDBCHDFS Job Password issue\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Buelent Zeyben\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Password for \'jdbchdfs\' job definition is only hashing the initial portion of the password not the entire password (See attached image).The password has an \'_\' char but it shouldn\'t matter. The entire password should be masked with \'*\' instead.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1328,'XD-2421','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2421\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"UI: List of Streams causes \\\"undefined is not an option\\\"\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"See Screenshot.The error is caused when loading all stream definitions in method *loadStreamDefinitions*. Only 1 or two streams exist in the system. \", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1329,'XD-2316','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2316\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"REST: \\\"jobs/configurations\\\" returns 404 if one job has error\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"There is a bug in the deployments rest end-point. *How to reproduce:* * Deploy a Batch job (success) that for example does not all necessary libraries in the class-patch and thus causes a ΓÇ£java.lang.ClassNotFoundExceptionΓÇ¥*Result:*You cannot retrieve the list of deployments list anymore using:* http://localhost:9393/jobs/configurationsThe rest endpoint will now report:[{\\\"links\\\":[]\\\"logref\\\":\\\"NoSuchBatchJobException\\\"\\\"message\\\":\\\"Batch Job with the name myJob doesn\'t exist\\\"}]This message is not entirely wrongΓÇªbut extremely misleading. I think we should still return the entire list and rather mark the job as having an error.Also returning an ΓÇ£404 Not FoundΓÇ¥ is misleading as well.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1330,'XD-2462','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2462\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Acceptance test for Kafka as a message bus\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a QA I\'d like to include acceptance test coverage for _Kafka_ as a message bus so that I can validate the functionality as part of every CI build.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1331,'XD-2426','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2426\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Travis CI improvements\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Travis CI recently introduced docker based builds.This prevents root access (which we don\'t need) but allows caching (which we could not use before) and seems to come with beefier machine specs\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1332,'XD-2475','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2475\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add batching support to Spring AMQP/Rabbit\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to setup _batching_ so that I can ingest data in batches as opposed to payload-at-a-time.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1333,'XD-2400','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2400\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Research options to improve CI reliability\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a build master I\'d like to research CI options so that I can improve CI build stability and reliability.*Potential Option:*[npm-cache|https://github.com/swarajban/npm-cache]Caching previously installed dependencies _npm-cache_ doesn\'t require downloading the internet each time we build.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1334,'XD-1461','70','{\"key\": \"XD-1461\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Use Hadoop mini-cluster test support in XD tests\", \"assignee\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"The tests that use HDFS currently require an external Hadoop installation and is hard to set up/update version in all the environments where we want to run tests e.g. bamboo travis.See if the mini-cluster described in http://docs.spring.io/spring-hadoop/docs/2.0.0.RC1/reference/html/testing.html#testing:yarn:miniclustercan be used in the test cases instead.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1335,'XD-2414','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2414\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"summary\": \"Incorrect \\\"directory\\\" option described in hdfs-dataset docs\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Please see [hdfs-dataset 1.0.2.RELEASE docs|http://docs.spring.io/autorepo/docs/spring-xd/1.0.2.RELEASE/reference/html/#hdfs-dataset-avroparquet].According to docs there should be \\\"directory\\\" option in this sink but in code \\\"basePath\\\" is used.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1336,'XD-2341','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2341\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Allan Baril\", \"summary\": \"Deleting a job and then re-adding a new definition with the same name fails\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Allan Baril\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Using single-node deployment of Spring XD 1.0 GA we needed to redefine several batch jobs. We deleted the jobs (\\\"job destroy all\\\"). When attempting to re-add we received an error that a job with the name already exists. Performing \\\"job list\\\" confirms the jobs were gone.To workaround I needed to terminate the instance (server) of Spring XD and restart it. Since this was the single-node deployment without a live stream of data coming in this was okay but would have been a major problem if bouncing the Spring XD server was not acceptable (i.e. live data being actively received).\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1337,'XD-2409','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2409\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"summary\": \"hdfs-dataset sink with getName() method in Pojo\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Having a pojo:{code}public class User{private String name;public String getName() {return user;}public void setName(String name) {this.name = name;}}{code}with:{code}hdfs-dataset --inputType=\'application/x-java-object;type=test.User\'{code}throws exception:{code}12:43:27698 1.1.0.SNAP ERROR task-scheduler-1 handler.LoggingHandler - org.springframework.messaging.MessageHandlingException: Expression evaluation failed: payload.getClass().getName(); nested exception is org.springframework.expression.AccessException: Problem invoking method: public java.lang.String test.User.getName(){code}Which I believe is caused by `correlation-strategy-expression` spel in aggregator:{code}<int:aggregatorinput-channel=\\\"input\\\"correlation-strategy-expression=\\\"payload.getClass().getName()\\\"release-strategy-expression=\\\"size() == ${batchSize}\\\"expire-groups-upon-completion=\\\"true\\\"send-partial-result-on-expiry=\\\"true\\\"message-store=\\\"messageStore\\\"output-channel=\\\"objects\\\"/>{code}Changing `getName()` method in pojo to something else works.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1338,'XD-2427','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2427\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Use repo.spring.io as NPM repository\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"In order to improve the build reliability we should be using the NPM repo provided by *repo.spring.io* See *spring-xd-ui/README.md* for further details.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1339,'XD-2378','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2378\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Add ability to logout using the Admin UI\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"While there is a server endpoint to logout we don\'t have that ability yet from the UI. As indicated by XD-2122 we will also need a meta-data REST endpoint  so we can interrogate whether security is enabled whether the user is logged etc. So we can fulfill the requirements: * Show a logout button only if a) security is enabled and b) user is logged in* Show the username and/or full name of the user being logged in \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1340,'XD-2333','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2333\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Add test coverage for Kafka source and sink modules\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a PM I\'d like to have test coverage for both Kafka source and sink modules so that we can assert its functionality as part of the CI builds. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1341,'XD-2392','70','{\"key\": \"XD-2392\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add integration tests\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\