edOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1367,'XD-2466','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2466\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Implement a dirt plugin for Spark Streaming support\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1368,'XD-2467','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2467\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Implement a Spark Streaming Driver application that can be controlled as an XD module instance\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"This should include lifecycle management so that when the module\'s stream is undeployed the Spark Streaming application should be stopped etc.Deploying a number of module instances should result in multiple receiver tasks and those should bind to the bus using the consumer side partitioning metadata.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1369,'XD-2358','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2358\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add starting offset support for Kafka source\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 3.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 2.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I want to be able to control the starting offset of the Kafka source when a stream is deployed so that I can replay a topic if necessary.Note:- starting offset is only considered when the stream is deployed- progress made by modules must survive their crash for a running stream- undeploying and redeploying a stream with a specific start offset will cause the stream to read again from the start TBD: what happens when streams are undeployed/redeployed - where do they resume from?\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 2.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1370,'XD-2347','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2347\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Document Kafka message bus\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to refer to documentation in wiki so that I can setup and configure Kafka as a message bus as recommended. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1371,'XD-2359','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2359\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add partition allocation support for Kafka source\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I want to be able to control the partition allocation for the Kafka source modules when a stream is deployed so that I can colocate with other data sources.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1372,'XD-2549','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2549\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to SI-Kafka Extension release\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"We would want to upgrade SI Kafka extension dependency to inherit the refactoring work with Kafka simple consumer API.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1373,'XD-2360','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2360\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Pre-allocate partitions for Kafka source\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I want Spring XD to pre-allocate a set of partitions between the Kafka source modules when a stream is deployed so that deployment is simpler and rebalancing doesnΓÇÖt take place. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1374,'XD-2609','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2609\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Error when listing Streams in admin-ui\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'m trying to list streams (>20) in admin-ui to use the pagination; however I ended up with blank page and the server-side errored with _java.lang.IllegalStateException_.Version: 1.1.0 SNAPSHOT (master build)Distributed: 1 admin and 2 containers*Steps to reproduce:*1) Deploy the following streams.stream create foo1 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo2 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo3 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo4 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo5 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo6 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo7 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo8 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo9 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo10 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo11 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo12 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo13 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo14 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo15 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo16 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo17 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo18 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo19 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo20 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo21 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploystream create foo22 --definition \\\"time | log\\\" --deploy2) Go to Streams tab in admin-ui to get a blank page and the following exception in admin logs.*Error:*16:55:19107 1.1.0.SNAP ERROR http-nio-9393-exec-2 rest.RestControllerAdvice - Caught exception while handling a requestjava.lang.IllegalStateException: Not all instances were looked atat org.springframework.util.Assert.state(Assert.java:385)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.rest.XDController.enhanceWithDeployments(XDController.java:207)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.rest.XDController.listValues(XDController.java:178)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.rest.StreamsController.list(StreamsController.java:63)\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1375,'XD-2541','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2541\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Define developer facing interfaces for RxJava processors\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to implement the core interface contract so that I can create a processor module that uses RxJava API.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1376,'XD-2542','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2542\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Create MessageHandler for RxJava based processor modules\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have a flexible RxJava module so that it can as a processor. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1377,'XD-2556','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2556\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Reference documentation on RxJava Stream processor\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1378,'XD-2477','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2477\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support to stop existing Sqoop jobs\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to _stop_ an existing Sqoop job so that I can clean-up resources at the time of completion.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1379,'XD-2361','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2361\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Pre-allocate partitions for Kafka message bus\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I want Spring XDΓÇÖs message bus to be able to pre-allocate partitions between nodes when a stream is deployed so that rebalancing doesnΓÇÖt happen when a container crashes and/or itΓÇÖs redeployed.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1380,'XD-2492','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2492\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Buelent Zeyben\", \"summary\": \"Increase Exit Description Text field on Job Execution Process step page\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Buelent Zeyben\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The Step Execution Process (http://localhost:9393/admin-ui/#/jobs/executions/38/52) page should list more lines of text for \'Exit Description\' field to make sense of error messages.*Scope:*Investigate how much information can be collected directly from the ExecutionContext. It may be dependent on the error types. Let\'s have the observation documented to decide next steps. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1381,'XD-2482','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2482\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Enrique Medina\", \"summary\": \"Add \\\"initialDelay\\\" to \\\"source:trigger\\\"\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Enrique Medina\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Currently the {{source:trigger}} module is based on 3 profiles: {{date}} {{cron}} or {{fixedDelay}} where the latter has precedence over the former in {{TriggerSourceOptionsMetadata}}:{code:java}@Overridepublic String[] profilesToActivate() {    if (cron != null) {        return new String[] { \\\"use-cron\\\" };    }    else if (fixedDelay != null) {        return new String[] { \\\"use-delay\\\" };    }    else {        return new String[] { \\\"use-date\\\" };    }}{code}Therefore it is not possible to combine {{date}} and {{fixedDelay}} to start off at a specific point in time and then repeat every X seconds.This is a request to provide another parameter to {{source:trigger}} such as *{{initialDelay}}* to be able to achieve the desired behaviour.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1382,'XD-2563','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2563\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"summary\": \"XD on YARN broken due to missing messagebus libs\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Admin on YARN simply fails because messagebus libs are not copied in place during a build.Already tried and simple fix is for gradle/build-dist.gradle:{code}task copyYarnMessageBusLibs(type: Copy) {  from \\\"$rootDir/lib/messagebus\\\"  into \\\"$buildDir/dist/spring-xd-yarn/xd-yarn/lib/messagebus\\\"}{code}and execute it together with copyMessageBusLibs task.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1383,'XD-2546','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2546\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Create AMI for Spark Server installed\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1384,'XD-2532','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2532\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Spark Application Job fails when using remote Spark Master\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"When executing a Spark Application Job on XD against a remote Spark Master we receive a CNF exception for FSDataInputStream.  Running against a local[1] Spark Master works normally.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 5.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1385,'XD-2416','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2416\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Dennis Hunziker\", \"summary\": \"SpelParseException is thrown when using empty string (\\\"\\\") inside of an expression\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Dennis Hunziker\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"I can only reproduce this when using single quotes around the expression:{code}stream create test --definition \\\"http | transform --expression=\'payload.replace(\\\\\\\"abc\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")\' | log\\\" --deploy true{code}The following two alternatives work fine though:{code}# Using trim on a single spacestream create test --definition \\\"http | transform --expression=\'payload.replace(\\\\\\\"abc\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\" \\\\\\\".trim())\' | log\\\" --deploy true# Not using single quotes or spaces in the expressionstream create test --definition \\\"http | transform --expression=payload.replace(\\\\\\\"abc\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\") | log\\\" --deploy true{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1386,'XD-2562','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2562\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Move the Hadoop test dependencies to a different project\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to isolate the Hadoop tests in a different project so that the DIRT project doesn\'t have to depend upon thus eliminating the incorrect CP file generation in eclipse. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1387,'XD-2075','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2075\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Add --binary Option to MQTT Source\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"See http://stackoverflow.com/questions/25226527/mqtt-source-spring-xd/25227531#25227531\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1388,'XD-2508','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2508\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"MQTT: Support the New Spring Integration 4.1 Features\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"HA Configuration async sends.http://docs.spring.io/spring-integration/reference/html/whats-new.html#4.1-mqtt\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1389,'XD-2411','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2411\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Make Redis RichGauge repository \\\"cluster safe\\\"\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The current implementation makes individual reads from redis and then writes back the average so in a cluster environment the reads and writes are not serialized client reads and writes for specific keys can interfere with each other.  Investigate options such as use of redis transactions or use of lua scripting to solve this problem.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1390,'XD-2412','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2412\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Fix Redis FieldValueCounter repo save() method\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"That method is actually currently never called but :- The case where a mapping already exists is not covered (outstanding TODO comment)- the semantics of the method should just be to \\\"save and override\\\"\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1391,'XD-2410','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2410\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Rename metrics repositories setValue(x y z) to something less \\\"javabean\\\"\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1392,'XD-2406','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2406\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Create Sample Module projects\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 2.0, \"issueLinks\": 4.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Create one or more Sample module projects in the Spring XD Examples repo to serve as templates for Spring XD module projects. Similar to https://github.com/dturanski/siDslModule these should include unit and single node integration tests and demonstrate the use of Spring XD build and packaging tools and other module development support. This may be split out into separate tasks but should include a sample for source processor sink and job using @Configuration or XML configuration (either as separate samples or using build profiles). \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 2.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1393,'XD-2384','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2384\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Document custom module install procedures\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to refer to documentation so that I can build the custom module based on recommended standards and patterns.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1394,'XD-2547','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2547\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Accept any file name for top level module resources\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Expecting <module-name> in module configuration is brittle especially in conjunction with module upload command which permits the module to be registered under a different name.  The convention should be dropped in favor of any file name. This requires at most one foo.xml foo.groovy and/or foo.properties in the top level config folder. It is an exception if multiples are found. Accepting any file name provides the most flexibility without sacrificing backward compatibility (except in rare cases in which a module developer may have violated the multiple xml or properties files condition). An alternate approach requiring a well known file name such as \'spring-module\' were rejected over concerns that it would break any existing custom module implementations.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1395,'XD-2567','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2567\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Strip MessageBus DeliveryMode Header\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Since the messagebus refactoring we now see {noformat}15:43:06379 1.1.0.M2  WARN xdbus.foo.0-1 support.DefaultAmqpHeaderMapper - skipping header \'amqp_deliveryMode\' since it is not of expected type [class org.springframework.amqp.core.MessageDeliveryMode] it is [class org.springframework.amqp.core.MessageDeliveryMode]{noformat}When using a rabbit transport and a rabbit sink (the sink Spring AMQP is in its own classloader).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1396,'XD-2570','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2570\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create a new Broadcast stream per thread\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The data that is entering a broadcast stream can only occur from one thread at a time to prevent race conditions inside the stream implementation.  The current handler shares a single broadcast stream.  Change to create a new one per thread usage.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1397,'XD-2569','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2569\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Update to Spring Boot 1.2.1.RELEASE\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1398,'XD-2566','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2566\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support to test XD on YARN in EC2\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to have acceptance test coverage for XD + YARN on EC2 so that I can verify simple XD features running on YARN on every build cycle.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1399,'XD-2572','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2572\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Set fixed NPM version for Grunt Gradle Plugin\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Ensure build works in Windows environments\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1400,'XD-2574','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2574\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Lukasz Nowanski\", \"summary\": \"Gemfire sink SpringXD module does not support multiple locators\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Lukasz Nowanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Gemfire sink module accepts useLocator host and port properties but this only allows to use one locator at a time.We have a need to use the Gemfire sink SpringXD Module in our Seamless access project that we want to go live in Q1.The Version of SpringXD we planned on using is 1.1However we need HA and we need to connect to a cluster with multiple locators. Problem is this isnΓÇÖt supported yet in SpringXD.We have used multiple locators in many projects in EMC and we donΓÇÖt want to revert back to a situation where we have to put virtual IPs in front of locators just for SpringXD.Ref to the SpringXD docs found in 1.0.3 and 1.1.0GA versions:ΓÇ£The locator option is mostly intended for integration with an existing GemFire installation in which the cache servers are configured to use locators in accordance with best practice. While GemFire supports configuration of multiple locators for failover this is currently not supported in XD. However using a single virtual IP backed by hardware routers for failover has proven to be an effective and simpler alternative.ΓÇ¥\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1401,'XD-2589','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2589\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Create sample application for RxJava\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Create port of https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd-samples/tree/master/reactor-moving-average based on RxJava\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1402,'XD-2590','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2590\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Create MessageConverter interface to allow user extensions\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the option to extend the default message handling behavior for HTTP source-module so that I can override the settings via _servers.yml_ to control the default message size.*Notes:*The adapter currently has that hard-coded (1MB limit) in the HttpChunkAggregator. We will have to expose this property for overrides. [Related PR|https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/pull/1367].\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1403,'XD-2591','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2591\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Bump Spring Integration to 4.1.2; Spring AMQP to 1.4.2\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1404,'XD-2594','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2594\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Update spring-data-hadoop version to 2.1.0.RC1\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Update spring-data-hadoop version to 2.1.0.RC1. This also includes updating the following:- adding hadoop26 (Apache Hadoop 2.6.0) as distro- adding hdp22 (Hortonworks HDP 2.2) as distro- set default distro to hadoop26- update cdh5 to version 5.3.0- remove older distros - hadoop24 hdp21\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1405,'XD-2564','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2564\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"summary\": \"Enhance XD on YARN to use SHDP container clustering\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently yarn runtime needs two yarn appmaster instances(one for admins one for containers). SHDP\'s container grouping added functionality to run different type of containers within a same appmaster.Beyond this container grouping will also give more functionality like ramping containers up/down on-demand creating groups with different settings dynamically and restarting failed containers.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1406,'XD-2606','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2606\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support to \'track history\' in message headers\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have an option to track history so that I get the visibility of stream name module name etc. added as part of the message header.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1407,'XD-2611','72','{\"key\": \"XD-2611\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 72, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Missing Log Configuration for throughput-sampler\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1