put(StringJsonNode) in ObjectNode has been deprecatedroot.put(name root.pojoNode(value));\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1436,'XD-2670','73','{\"key\": \"XD-2670\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 73, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Bump Spring AMQP to 1.4.3\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"When available\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1437,'XD-2672','73','{\"key\": \"XD-2672\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 73, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Add scala support for spark streaming module\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a scala developer someone could easily deploy the spark streaming module developed using scala.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1438,'XD-2674','73','{\"key\": \"XD-2674\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 73, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Artem Bilan\", \"summary\": \"Provide more options for the MongoDB Sink\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Artem Bilan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"See the SO question on the matter: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/28280206/how-can-i-use-authentication-in-mongo-sink\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1439,'XD-2675','73','{\"key\": \"XD-2675\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 73, \"status\": \"In Progress\", \"creator\": \"nebhale\", \"summary\": \"Add support for Sentinel in Redis Sink\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"nebhale\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Currently the Redis sink appears to be unable to write to a Redis instance if it is connected via Sentinel.  Given the following XD Container {{servers.yml}} configuration:{noformat}# Redis propertiesspring:  redis:#   port: 6379#   host: localhost    sentinel:      master: spring-xd      nodes: 10.85.30.133:2637910.85.30.134:2637910.85.30.135:26379{noformat}a stream of {{time | redis --key=ticktock}} results in the following:{noformat}Created JedisPool to master at 10.85.30.130:6379Caused by: org.springframework.messaging.MessageHandlingException: error occurred in message handler [org.springframework.integration.redis.outbound.RedisStoreWritingMessageHandler#0]; nested exception is org.springframework.data.redis.RedisConnectionFailureException: Cannot get Jedis connection; nested exception is redis.clients.jedis.exceptions.JedisConnectionException: Could not get a resource from the poolCaused by: org.springframework.data.redis.RedisConnectionFailureException: Cannot get Jedis connection; nested exception is redis.clients.jedis.exceptions.JedisConnectionException: Could not get a resource from the pool    at org.springframework.data.redis.connection.jedis.JedisConnectionFactory.fetchJedisConnector(JedisConnectionFactory.java:140)    at org.springframework.data.redis.connection.jedis.JedisConnectionFactory.getConnection(JedisConnectionFactory.java:229)    at org.springframework.data.redis.connection.jedis.JedisConnectionFactory.getConnection(JedisConnectionFactory.java:57)Caused by: redis.clients.jedis.exceptions.JedisConnectionException: Could not get a resource from the pool    at redis.clients.jedis.JedisPool.getResource(JedisPool.java:84)    at redis.clients.jedis.JedisPool.getResource(JedisPool.java:10)    at org.springframework.data.redis.connection.jedis.JedisConnectionFactory.fetchJedisConnector(JedisConnectionFactory.java:133)Caused by: redis.clients.jedis.exceptions.JedisConnectionException: java.net.ConnectException: Connection refused    at redis.clients.jedis.Connection.connect(Connection.java:150)    at redis.clients.jedis.BinaryClient.connect(BinaryClient.java:71)    at redis.clients.jedis.BinaryJedis.connect(BinaryJedis.java:1783)    at redis.clients.jedis.JedisFactory.makeObject(JedisFactory.java:65)    at redis.clients.jedis.Connection.connect(Connection.java:144){noformat}The parts that sticks out to me is the linebq. {{Created JedisPool to master at 10.85.30.130:6379}}The Sentinels aren\'t at {{.130}} that\'s a Redis and the only way that the {{JedisPool}} could know about that host is to have connected to a Sentinel instance and requested the listing of Redis nodes managed by the Sentinel.  Notably the Redis instance that the JedisPool connects to is actually responsive.{noformat}$: redis-cli -h 10.85.30.130 -p 637910.85.30.130:6379> pingPONG10.85.30.130:6379> {noformat}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1440,'XD-2676','73','{\"key\": \"XD-2676\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 73, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Resolve classloading issues for custom Hadoop based batch jobs\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 3.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"There are several issues making it hard to impossible to create batch jobs that use Pig Hive HBase or other technologies supported by Spring for Apache Hadoop project. We need to make the corresponding dependencies available on the Hadoop classpath.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1441,'XD-2677','73','{\"key\": \"XD-2677\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 73, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Remove jline from xd-dirt classpath\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently jline 2.11 gets added via zookeeper dependency we need to remove this so we can have jline 1.0 fir Pig jobs in the hadoop depndenciesThis jline version should remain for xd-shell classpath though\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1442,'XD-2678','73','{\"key\": \"XD-2678\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 73, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Add dependencies needed for running a Pig job\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1443,'XD-2679','73','{\"key\": \"XD-2679\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 73, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Add dependencies needed for running