 \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1458,'XD-2480','74','{\"key\": \"XD-2480\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 74, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Benchmark: Sqoop vs. jdbchdfs\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a QA I\'d like to benchmark _Sqoop_ vs. _jdbchdfs_ batch job so that I can compare and contrast performance stats. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1459,'XD-2749','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2749\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Placeholder for Lattice/Diego POC #1\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1460,'XD-2750','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2750\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Placeholder for Lattice/Diego POC #2\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1461,'XD-2731','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2731\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Paul Harris\", \"summary\": \"Temp files for stream create not being cleaned\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 1.0, \"reporter\": \"Paul Harris\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"During testing for Spring XD for PivotalCF we create deploy use undeploy and destroy many streams. Each stream generates {{tmp}} directories (I think 2 one for source one for sink) in the xd-admin VM\'s {{/tmp}} directory e.g.{noformat}dummy-module4635787551932601017sinkredisdummy-module252960009195893204sourcehttp{noformat}These {{tmp}} directories are not being cleared up so our system has hit the inode limit of 32768 files for a volume:{noformat}Filesystem     Inodes IUsed  IFree IUse% Mounted on/dev/loop0      32768 32768      0  100% /tmp{noformat}This causes a Java {{IOException}} the immediately relevant part of which appears to be:{noformat}[Caught] exception while handling a requestFeb 18 09:06:06 10.85.30.142-2 xd-admin-partition-default_az_guid-0:  [java.lang.RuntimeException] java.io.IOException: No space left on deviceFeb 18 09:06:06 10.85.30.142-2 xd-admin-partition-default_az_guid-0:  []    at org.springframework.xd.module.ModuleDefinitions.dummy(ModuleDefinitions.java:81){noformat}This causes the test system to fail entirely.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1462,'XD-2741','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2741\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"summary\": \"Redis sink should default to using spring.redis configuration in servers.yml\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The configuration for the redis sink must be provided for explicitly instead of falling back to values defined in servers.yml.  The default behavior configuration should be address in a manner consistent with the default behavior of module config for rabbit source/sink jdbc sink....\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1463,'XD-2719','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2719\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Invoke Rabbit REST-API to clean-up resources\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 4.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to clean-up stale queues/topics associated with the stream so when the stream gets destroyed I can clean-up resources. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1464,'XD-2730','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2730\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support to include deployment manifest from file\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to include the deployment manifest from the file so that I don\'t have spend time typing as \\\"inline properties\\\".\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1465,'XD-2557','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2557\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", 