aptured as first step.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1484,'XD-2739','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2739\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Add a Sqoop example\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1485,'XD-2755','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2755\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"Scala processor module executor trims messages\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"How to reproduce:1. Run xd-singlenode (for which setting the Spark master URL to \'local\' is a requirement). Use more than 1 worker thread. e.g. {{local[4]}}2. Deploy the word-count example3. Create a stream{{stream create spark-streaming-word-count --definition \\\"http | word-count | log\\\" --deploy}}4. Send data{{xd:>http post --data \\\"a b c d e f g\\\"}}{{xd:>http post --data \\\"a b c\\\"}}5.Observe the result2015-02-24 15:12:46018 1.2.0.SNAP  INFO Executor task launch worker-3 sink.spark-streaming-word-count - (e1)2015-02-24 15:12:46018 1.2.0.SNAP  INFO Executor task launch worker-1 sink.spark-streaming-word-count - (d1)2015-02-24 15:12:46019 1.2.0.SNAP  INFO Executor task launch worker-2 sink.spark-streaming-word-count - (b1)2015-02-24 15:12:46020 1.2.0.SNAP  INFO Executor task launch worker-1 sink.spark-streaming-word-count - (g1)2015-02-24 15:13:40020 1.2.0.SNAP  INFO Executor task launch worker-1 sink.spark-streaming-word-count - (a1)2015-02-24 15:13:40020 1.2.0.SNAP  INFO Executor task launch worker-2 sink.spark-streaming-word-count - (b1)2015-02-24 15:13:40021 1.2.0.SNAP  INFO Executor task launch worker-3 sink.spark-streaming-word-count - (c1)(the last three results are coming from the second invocation))Note: there seems to be a correlation between the number of values emitted and the number of workers as in all the attempts there aren\'t more values emitted than the number of workers.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1486,'XD-2712','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2712\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Embed local message bus in DIRT as default for singlenode\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently all message bus implementations are removed from the runtime classpath and loaded on demand from the file system according to the transport setting. Custom module projects that include in container testing must install messagebus-local on the local file system. This is currently configured as a task for module build scripts. This is also a dependency for testing in the IDE and developers need to execute the build task or configure the messagebus manually. Embedding the local MB for the singlenode application (local is not a valid transport for distributed) eliminates this step.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1487,'XD-2759','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2759\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"LocalMessageBus PubSub Needs a Bounded Task Exectutor\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Since 1.1 {{PubSub}} channels in the {{LocalMessageBus}} run on a {{CachedThreadPoolExecutor}}.For high volume environments where back-pressure might occur on a {{topic:}} thread we could overwhelm the system with threads.Add a local bus configuration to limit the thread pool used for PubSubs and queue tasks where there are no threads available.It would be a bus-wide setting.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1488,'XD-2762','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2762\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Update RHEL/CentOS yum/rpm installation instructions\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a build manager I\'d like to have Spring XD RPMs published in spring.io repository so that users can directly download the bits without having to go through appsuite repo or the EULA. *Location for 1.1.0 RELEASE:*http://repo.spring.io/libs-release-local/org/springframework/xd/spring-xd/1.1.0.RELEASE/\", \"fixVersions\": 3.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1489,'XD-2784','77','{\"key\": \"XD-2784\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 77, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Research EC2 infrastructure required for Kafka performance tests\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn 