ectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1497,'XD-2704','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2704\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Move documentation from wiki to main repo\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 2.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 2.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a consequence * change gradle script regarding generation of documentation* remove pushGeneratedDocs task etc* remove link rewriting that is no longer needed \", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 2.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1498,'XD-2070','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2070\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Get rid of custom asciidoctor link: transformations\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Remove {noformat}filter { line ->// TODO: refine regex to only match local documentsdef match = (line =~ /link:(.*?)#(.*?)\\\\[(.*?)\\\\]/)if (match) match.replaceAll(\'xref:$2[$3]\') else line}{noformat}and replace link:Foo#bar by xref:Foo#bar\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1499,'XD-2819','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2819\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"summary\": \"Broken \\\"Deployment\\\" link in docs\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Please see \\\"Deployment\\\" link on http://docs.spring.io/autorepo/docs/spring-xd/1.1.0.RELEASE/reference/html/#_module_deployment page. !broken-link-deployment.png!The link is broken and redirects to http://docs.spring.io/autorepo/docs/spring-xd/1.1.0.RELEASE/reference/html/Deployment which is a 404.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1500,'XD-2767','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2767\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"JMS Source Does Not Expose `acknowledge`\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Since the message-driven adapter uses a {{DMLC}} the default behavior is to lose messages on exceptions (with the DMLC the message is ack\'d before the listener is invoked).In order to provide recovery of such situations the source needs to expose {{acknowledge}} so it can be set to {{transacted}}.Or perhaps given that we don\'t expose complex configuration the source should use a {{SimpleMessageListenerContainer}} instead (where the ack is sent after the listener is successfully invoked).\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 2.0}'),('Spring_XD',1501,'XD-2766','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2766\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Add metadata for description of a module (itself)\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the description for each of the modules so that I can use it to understand the module purpose and it\'s capabilities (presumably what is captured in javadoc for the module definition).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1502,'XD-2758','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2758\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add module description to the JSON response\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"As  a user I\'d like to have the description for each of the modules so that I can use it to understand the module purpose and it\'s capabilities (presumably what is captured in javadoc for the module definition). \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1503,'XD-2832','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2832\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support to create custom jobs using Java Config\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to create a custom job module using Java Config so that I don\'t have to deal with XML configurations. While deploying/launching the following job I get the error attached below.{code:xml}job create --name CDK_Global --definition \\\"customBatchJob\\\" --deploymodule upload --type job --name customBatchJob --file /Users/mminella/Documents/IntelliJWorkspace/CustomBatchModule/build/libs/CustomBatchModule-1.1.0.RELEASE.jarjob launch --name CDK_Global{code}*Error:*I\'m getting an exception that the job doesn\'t exist asking if it\'s deployed\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1504,'XD-2298','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2298\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Review POC and identify scope for gpload as OOTB Batch Job\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to mass ingest data from databases (and others) into HDFS/HAWQ/GPDB so that I don\'t have to write custom code and as well as be able to ingest in an efficient way.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1505,'XD-2140','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2140\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Deployment properties should use label instead of name\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"stream create foo --definition \\\"label: bar | xxxx\\\"stream deploy foo --properties \\\"module.label.yyy=zzz\\\" seems to work but it does not. The pre-validation is correct but downstream deployment logic still looks for module.bar (instead of module.label)\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1506,'XD-2486','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2486\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jason Hubbard\", \"summary\": \"Context Deserialize Doesn\'t Use Parent First Classloader\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Minella\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Jason Hubbard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"If a class is added to a batch execution context that is located in an isolated context an exception will be thrown when that object is deserialized.  It appears the serialize doesn\'t use the ParentFirstClassloader during deserialization.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1507,'XD-2774','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2774\", \"votes\": 1.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Update to SHDP 2.1.1 for fixing hdfs store writer to recover after error writing to hdfs\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The hdfs sink doesn\'t recover after error writing to hdfs.Steps to reproduce -create a stream using hdfs sink with a small rollover:{code}xd:>stream create --name errtest --definition \\\"time | hdfs --rollover=50\\\" --deploy {code}stop the datanode(s) and wait for an exception like:{code}2015-03-03 10:41:57832 1.1.0.RELEASE ERROR task-scheduler-3 handler.LoggingHandler - org.springframework.messaging.MessageHandlingException: failed to write Message payload to HDFS; nested exception is org.apache.hadoop.ipc.RemoteException(java.io.IOException): File /xd/errtest/errtest-7.txt.tmp could only be replicated to 0 nodes instead of minReplication (=1).  There are 1 datanode(s) running and 1 node(s) are excluded in this operation.at org.apache.ha