ailed instead of complete when an exception is thrown in the writer.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1509,'XD-2388','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2388\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support to host custom module in HDFS\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the custom module (built as uber-jar) hosted in HDFS so that I can deploy the module to newly arriving containers. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1510,'XD-2287','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2287\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Have ResourceModuleRegistry transparently proxy a remote root thru filesystem\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"ArchiveModuleRegistry and the use of Boot Archives inherently relies on java.io.FileHave ResourceModuleRegistry extend/compose ArchiveMR to transparently download and cache (remote) jars that may be located in a (non-file:) location.The staging area should be customizable but some subdir of java.io.tmpdir sounds like a sensible default\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1511,'XD-2761','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2761\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Register only known classes with Kryo in PojoCodec\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently PojoCodec calls kryo.register(Class<?> type) on every ser/deser invocation. This fails with 1.1 because instances are pooled and a different instance may be used to serialize and deserialize.  See https://github.com/EsotericSoftware/kryo#registration.  The fix is to not register classes on the fly. Classes serialized by PojoCodec will not be registered by default. This will work but is less efficient. XD should provide an easy way to register types known to be serialized on the MessageBus (passed between modules)\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1512,'XD-2788','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2788\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add throughput receiving sink\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to add load receiving _sink_ module so that I can measure received throughput\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1513,'XD-2807','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2807\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Fix gradle build inconsistencies and leftovers\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"The build has some inconsistencies that should be taken care of.Amongst the one I know:* The UI project is always getting cleaned for no apparent reason (there might have been one before) thus triggering a rebuild of everything downstream most notably DIRT* The ΓÇ£exec\\\" task is not used anymore* Lots of projects are getting the boot plugin applied to them. I\'m not sure 100% what that plugin does but we don\'t need the repackage bit for example.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1514,'XD-2823','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2823\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Composite Modules should inherit \\\"xd.*\\\" properties\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently when modules are composed to a single application context properties are not inherited.https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/wiki/Modules#placeholders-available-to-all-modules\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1515,'XD-2820','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2820\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"summary\": \"Composing transformer and gemfire-json-server leads to FileNotFoundException during deployment\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Composing \\\"transform\\\" and \\\"gemfire-json-server\\\" modules leads to FileNotFoundException during stream deployment when:- xd-admin and xd-container are started as system services (after installing from RPM). - xd-singelonde is started outside of $XD_HOME/bin directory e.g. {code}$ cd \\\"$XD_HOME\\\"$ bin/xd-singelonde{code}but it\'s fully working and exception is *not* thrown when:- xd-singlenode script is started from within \\\"$XD_HOME/bin directory {code}$ cd \\\"$XD_HOME/bin\\\"$ ./xd-singelonde{code}Then using the XD Shell:{code}$ xd-shell> module compose --name \\\"cm-gem-sink\\\" --definition \\\"transform --outputType=\'application/json\' | gemfire-json-server --regionName=timeRegion --keyExpression=payload.getField(\'location\')\\\"> stream create --name \\\"cm-test-gem\\\" --definition \\\"tail --name=\'/tmp/time.json\' | cm-gem-sink\\\" > stream deploy --name \\\"cm-test-gem\\\"{code}Stream deployment will result in following exception{code}[2015-03-11 16:38:10.918] boot - 17402  INFO [DeploymentsPathChildrenCache-0] --- DeploymentListener: Deploying module [ModuleDescriptor@2095e9f9 moduleName = \'tail\' moduleLabel = \'tail\' group = \'cm-test-gem\' sourceChannelName = [null] sinkChannelName = [null] index = 0 type = source parameters = map[\'name\' -> \'/tmp/time.json\'] children = list[[empty]]]2015-03-11 16:38:11263 1.1.0.RELEASE  INFO DeploymentSupervisor-0 server.StreamDeploymentListener - Deployment status for stream \'cm-test-gem\': DeploymentStatus{state=failederror(s)=org.springframework.beans.factory.parsing.BeanDefinitionParsingException: Configuration problem: Error evaluating Groovy script: Configuration problem: Error evaluating Groovy script: ../modules/common/gemfire-sink.groovy (No such file or directory)Offending resource: URL [file:../modules/common/gemfire-sink.groovy]; nested exception is java.io.FileNotFoundException: ../modules/common/gemfire-sink.groovy (No such file or directory)Offending resource: file [/opt/spring-xd/spring-xd-1.1.0.RELEASE/xd/module