k.xd.dirt.stream.XDStreamParser.parse(XDStreamParser.java:174)at org.springframework.xd.dirt.stream.AbstractDeployer.save(AbstractDeployer.java:96)...{code}when module properties have a trailing whitespace character in type property (in example below there is a trailing space in options.myField.type value):{code}options.myField.description = this is my fieldoptions.myField.type = String {code}Can the property values be trimmed before comparing to DefaultModuleOptionsMetadataResolver#SHORT_CLASSNAMES map  to avoid this problem?\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1517,'XD-2794','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2794\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Abhinav\", \"summary\": \"Add a MongoDB source\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Abhinav\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to add a mongodb source using an xml and a property file supporting mixing in of parameters so that I can use this module to ingest data from Mongo.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 8.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1518,'XD-2828','78','{\"key\": \"XD-2828\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 78, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"XD distributed tests are broken\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"There are test failures running XD distributed tests. It looks like all the test failures are related to NPE on DeploymentProperties format:java.lang.NullPointerExceptionat org.springframework.xd.rest.domain.support.DeploymentPropertiesFormat.formatDeploymentProperties(DeploymentPropertiesFormat.java:72)at org.springframework.xd.rest.client.impl.JobTemplate.deploy(JobTemplate.java:71)at org.springframework.xd.distributed.test.JobStateTests.testJobStateTransition(JobStateTests.java:83)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1519,'XD-2382','79','{\"key\": \"XD-2382\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 79, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Re-run Kafka baseline tests in new infrastructure\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to setup a performance testing infrastructure (rackspace) so I can start benching Kafka baselines and continue with XD use-cases.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1520,'XD-2848','79','{\"key\": \"XD-2848\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 79, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Design and budget Perf Env for XD on RackSpace\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Provide design for how we are going to run XD and Kafka on Rackspace.  This includes the base design for the Kafka Perf tests environment.This will be used to provide a budget for the cloud resources  for the performance environment.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1521,'XD-2771','79','{\"key\": \"XD-2771\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 79, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"summary\": \"spring-xd-dirt is not providing all $XD_HOME/lib libraries\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"Spring XD is packaging a spring-xd-dirt dependency which aims to provide runtime libraries.spring-xd-drit-1.1.0.RELEASE is not providing all libraries from $XD_HOME/lib. See spring-xd-dirt-vs-lib.xlsx attachment generated with \\\"ls  $XD_HOME/lib\\\" and \\\"mvn dependency:list\\\" on a module with spring-xd-module-parent parent:- 100+ JARs are not provided- some are provided in different versions- some are provided but not available in $XD_HOME/libThis forces us to add and maintain missing dependencies in our own module parent e.g. to use commons-lang3 in our code which is present in $XD_HOME/lib but is not provided by spring-xd-dirt.Why there are so many differences between $XD_HOME/lib and spring-xd-dirt?\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1522,'XD-2829','79','{\"key\": \"XD-2829\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 79, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Stephane Gamard\", \"summary\": \"Add the Dependencies Required to Use #xpath in Streams\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Stephane Gamard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Thanks to Gary I found this little gem of documentation to be able to use xpath expression in XD. Only hiccup is that I had to also add the spring-xml.jar to the classpath (otherwise it is missing XPathException class). http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29110757/spring-xd-work-with-xml-payload\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1523,'XD-2844','79','{\"key\": \"XD-2844\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 79, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Create a POC for gpfdist sink\", \"assignee\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like to have the OOTB _gpfdist_ sink module so I can use this module to do ultra fast data movement from various sources into GPDB/HAWQ.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1524,'XD-2389','79','{\"key\": \"XD-2389\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 79, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"summary\": \"Streams section of doc should explicitly mention that labels are required for ambiguous modules\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently I believe we only mention labels in this section of the doc:https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/wiki/DSL-Reference#labelsAnd it is not even clear there that they are *required* when 2 or more module names would otherwise be ambiguous. It was probably written before we made that a mandatory part of the definition.We should mention this somewhere in the \'streams\' section of the manual. Even if none of the examples there currently have more than one occurrence of the same module we should add one to illustrate this point.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1525,'XD-2777','79','{\"key\": \"XD-2777\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 79, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Document trigger source\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1526,'XD-2742','79','{\"key\": \"XD-2742\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 79, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Prep for DEBS Challenge\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to study the taxi trips based on a stream of trip reports from New York City so that I can evaluate event-based systems in the context of real-time analytics using Spring XD.[Challenge Details|http://www.debs2015.org/call-grand-challenge.html]\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1527,'XD-2793','79','{\"key\": \"XD-2793\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 79, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Fix offset management for Kafka source\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 3.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to fix the offset management with Kafka _sour