$AppClassLoader.loadClass(Launcher.java:308)at java.lang.ClassLoader.loadClass(ClassLoader.java:357)at org.springframework.util.ClassUtils.forName(ClassUtils.java:249)at org.springframework.beans.factory.support.AbstractBeanDefinition.resolveBeanClass(AbstractBeanDefinition.java:395)at org.springframework.beans.factory.support.AbstractBeanFactory.doResolveBeanClass(AbstractBeanFactory.java:1349)at org.springframework.beans.factory.support.AbstractBeanFactory.resolveBeanClass(AbstractBeanFactory.java:1320)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1651,'XD-2920','83','{\"key\": \"XD-2920\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"summary\": \"Dynamic router should allow to discard messages\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently dynamic router sink has to return a valid queue name. This is problematic when the message should be discarded as part of the routing process. In this case one have to define a stream with {{filter | router}} steps where part of the SpEL is duplicated between {{filter}} and {{router}} modules.Instead the dynamic router should allow to return null to discard the message and stop further processing. Spring Integration is already providing {{resolution-required}} attribute on {{<router/>}}. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1652,'XD-3063','83','{\"key\": \"XD-3063\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Add Property maxMessagesPerPoll to All Polled Sources\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Polled message sources return only one message per poll by default.When polling say a file directory with many files files will be emitted once per {{fixedDelay}}.As a user I need to configure a limit for the number of messages that will be emitted per poll.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1653,'XD-3071','83','{\"key\": \"XD-3071\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Spike: Produce Rabbit baseline on rackspace infrastructure\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to bench Rabbit on rackspace infrastructure so I can have a sense on how it scales as we add more _xd-container_ nodes.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1654,'XD-3074','83','{\"key\": \"XD-3074\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"Backport metadata retrieval stability improvements\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Backport stability improvements added as part of XD-2958 to the 1.1.x branch.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1655,'XD-3075','83','{\"key\": \"XD-3075\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"Backport Kafka Sink input fix\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As part of XD-2958 we\'ve changed the input type of the Kafka sink from String to byte[]. The main reason for the change was that it required an arbitrary and often unneeded (but expensive) conversion to String for the bus payloads. Apply the same change to 1.1 branch.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1656,'XD-3086','83','{\"key\": \"XD-3086\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Fix random Spark streaming test failures\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The {{testTapSparkProcessor}} has the test that checks the contents at the output of spark streaming word count processor. It turns out that the order in which these messages are processed are not always in order.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1657,'XD-3081','83','{\"key\": \"XD-3081\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"When using file as a source and sink user can not use file sink --mode\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.