andan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a Spring XD user I\'d like to use Diego based Receptor implementation of XD Admin SPI (based on ModuleLauncher) so I can run data pipeline use-cases running on CF Lattice/Diego. \", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1750,'XD-3229','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3229\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Spike: XD Admin SPI to discover s-c-s modules\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-s user I\'d like to investigate the possibility of s-c-s modules self-registering themselves to service discovery so I could use Spring XD runtime (running on CF) to discover and orchestrate such modules through streams.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1751,'XD-3198','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3198\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Spike: Investigate the use of config server for spring-cloud-stream modules \", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to use spring-cloud-config server for spring-bus modules so I can centrally manage external properties.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1752,'XD-3238','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3238\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Complete remaining Kryo optimization changes\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to complete the remaining Kryo optimization changes so I can polish and get the guidelines documented appropriately. \", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1753,'XD-631','88','{\"key\": \"XD-631\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Pluralize test classes in package org.springframework.xd.shell.command\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The classes under test are pluralized. Therefore the test classes themselves should reflect that. E.g. rename *JobCommandTests* to *JobCommandsTests* as it tests class *JobCommands*. Please check all tests in that package for correct naming.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1754,'XD-2957','88','{\"key\": \"XD-2957\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Create samples and document Kryo optimization guidelines\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to document the Kryo optimization guidelines so the end-users can refer to it while tuning to improve performance.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1755,'XD-3183','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3183\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Paul Harris\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to Spring Boot 1.2.5\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Paul Harris\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Spring Boot 1.2.4 (and earlier) does not allow for the retrieval of boolean values from the vcap environment. This means that when XD Admin tries to retrieve the value of (for example) {{vcap.services.rabbitmq.credentials.protocols.amqp.ssl}} it will fail as that value returns a boolean.Spring Boot 1.2.5 (as yet unreleased) contains a fix for this issue (https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/pull/3237)\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1756,'XD-3230','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3230\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Update to Reactor 2.0.4\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to upgrade to Reactor 2.0.4 release so I could leverage the latest improvements and bug-fixes.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1757,'XD-3222','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3222\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Find a way to connect Sqoop job to Teradata\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I would like to connect the Sqoop batch job to Teradata for import jobs. I have tried the Teradata JDBC driver directly using:{code}job create tdTest --definition \\\"sqoop --command=import --args=\'--table Frequent_Flyers --connect jdbc:teradata://tdexpress/DATABASE=transportation --driver com.teradata.jdbc.TeraDriver --username dbc --password dbc --target-dir=/xd/teradata --num-mappers 1\'\\\"{code}but that results in an NPE.The only way so far is to use the Hortonworks Connector for Teradata - http://public-repo-1.hortonworks.com/HDP/tools/2.2.4.2/hdp-connector-for-teradata-1.3.4.2.2.4.2-2-distro.tar.gzThat one allows me to use the following:{code}job create tdTest --definition \\\"sqoop --command=import --args=\'--table Frequent_Flyers --connect jdbc:teradata://tdexpress/DATABASE=transportation --connection-manager org.apache.sqoop.teradata.TeradataConnManager --username dbc --password dbc --target-dir=/xd/teradata --num-mappers 1\'\\\"{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1758,'XD-3231','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3231\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support to Ambari install multiple XD Admin\'s \", \"assignee\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to update Ambari installed Spring XD cluster to spin-up multiple instances of XD-Admin servers so it is setup for HA. \", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1759,'XD-2825','88','{\"key\": \"XD-2825\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"SCS - Verify/Fix AbstractKryoMultitypeCodec implementation\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"This apparently is not tested or used internally but I expect it to fail having tried a similar approach to derive the class of a generic type in a different situation. This method does not always work due to type erasure http://stackoverflow.com/questions/3403909/get-generic-type-of-class-at-runtime.  We need to verify if this is working if not fix it. The API may require it so possibly UnsupportedOperationException... {code}/**   * Infers the type from this class\'s generic type argument   * @param kryo   * @param input   * @return */protected T doDeserialize(Kryo kryo Input input) {Class<T> type = (Class<T>) ((ParameterizedType) this.getClass().getGenericSuperclass()).getActualTypeArguments()[0];return doDeserialize(kryo input type);}{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1760,'XD-3218','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3218\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"[Backport] Handle stream/job deployment status recalculation failures\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The admin leader election fails when the stream/job module definitions doesn\'t exist in `module-registry` but still some of the references still exist in ZK (via some of the previous deployments that had this module in module registry). Though this is expected this behavior will make *all* the subsequent deployments in *deploying* state because the admin leader isn\'t elected.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1761,'XD-3194','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3194\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Spike: Investigate spring-cloud-config and the XD fit\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to have a central place to manage external properties for applications across all the environments so I can provide server and client-side support for externalized configuration for XD-Admin and XD-Container servers. \", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1762,'XD-3232','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3232\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Update Spring Integration to 4.2.0.M2 (4.1.6 on 1.2.x)\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Also Spring Framework 4.2.0.RC2 Spring AMQP 1.5.0.M1Also Batch 3.0.4\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1763,'XD-2401','88','{\"key\": \"XD-2401\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"EC2 CI build improvements\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to include the following improvements as part of the EC2 CI infrastructure so that we can reliably run the CI builds and also assert over feature functionalities.*Scope:** Enable \'distributed jvm test\'* Change from using artifactory gradle task to a command task (that calls ./gradlew)* Test w/ embedded hadoop off* Turn on maxParallelForks\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1764,'XD-3249','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3249\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Change module option type from Class to String\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"This better aligns with boot. Moreover using Class was a bad design choice (one can always get a Class from a String [modulo knowing which CL to use] while to converse is not always easy [CL not being available])\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1765,'XD-3240','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3240\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"summary\": \"Add better support for using control file with gpfdist\", \"assignee\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently only database connection info can be read from a control file yml format. Should add rest of the missing options to align how native format works.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1766,'XD-3241','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3241\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"summary\": \"Add support for update in gpfdist sink\", \"assignee\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently we can only do plain inserts should follow same logic from native gpfdist sink and add upserts.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1767,'XD-3227','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3227\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Spike: Kickoff singlenode implementation of Admin SPI\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to develop a ΓÇ£singlenodeΓÇ¥ (in a single JVM) implementation of XD Admin SPI (based on Module Launcher) so I can run data pipeline use-cases locally.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1768,'XD-3258','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3258\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Add jars for Avro and Snappy compression to Sqoop job submission\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"We need to have some jars as part of the Sqoop job submission to YARN:for Avro we need:  avro-1.7.6.jar  avro-mapred-1.7.6.jarfor Snappy we need:  snappy-java-1.0.5.jar (note: the 1.1.0.1 version from xd/lib doesn\'t work)  commons-compress-1.4.1.jarWe can either have these included using the --libjars option or automatically include them.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1769,'XD-3235','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3235\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"FileJdbc Job throws exception during Acceptance Tests \", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Currently the testFileJdbcJobMultipleInvocations fails on line 156 stating data is different in table that what is expected.  Currently this is failing on the single admin/container deployment using redis as a transport.  Also seeing the following exception in the attached log:{noformat}2.0.0.SNAP ERROR xdbus.job:ec2Job3.0.requests-1 step.AbstractStep - Encountered an error executing step step1 in job ec2Job3org.springframework.batch.item.ItemStreamException: Failed to initialize the reader...Caused by: java.lang.IllegalStateException: Input resource must exist (reader is in \'strict\' mode): URL [file:/tmp/xd/output/filejdbctest/filejdbctest1.out]{noformat}The file is should be present and data present for the test.  At least according to the checker on EC2 and local deployments.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1770,'XD-3261','88','{\"key\": \"XD-3261\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 88, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Update Groovy to 2.4.4\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"There is a vulnerability in Groovy that is fixed in 2.4.4:CVE-2015-3253: Remote execution of untrusted codeSee:http://groovy-lang.org/security.htmlhttp://mail-archives.apache.org/mod_mbox/incubator-groovy-users/201507.mbox/%3CCADQzvmmYC7RbZnsQ8O63XN4HCMYh9RGRdMiuWupVt=u=pjH8+g@mail.gmail.com%3E\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1771,'XD-3263','90','{\"key\": \"XD-3263\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 90, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"sridhar\", \"summary\": \"Pagination for containers it is limited to only 20\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"sridhar\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Hi Customer has 48 containers but it only shows 20 containers. We need pagination to browse all containers.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1772,'XD-2834','90','{\"key\": \"XD-2834\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 90, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Make doc generation part of the standard build\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Following the recent move of the doco to the main repo it makes sense to have the doc generation be part of the \\\"main\\\" build at an early stage as an incentive for developers to push doc changes as soon as they change the code.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1773,'XD-3266','90','{\"key\": \"XD-3266\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 90, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"summary\": \"No pagination for Jobs / Deployments page in Admin UI\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Karol Dowbecki\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"After successfully deploying 12 jobs the Jobs / Deployments page still shows only 10 results.It looks like {{http://localhost:9393/jobs/configurations.json?page=0&size=10}} always returns {{content.page.totalPages}} of 1 regardless of the {{size}} parameter.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1774,'XD-3270','90','{\"key\": \"XD-3270\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 90, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Create module registry abstraction\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a Spring XD developer I\'d like to create 