re for [s-c-d repo|https://github.com/spring-cloud/spring-cloud-data] so I can build the project continuously on every commits. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1785,'XD-3318','90','{\"key\": \"XD-3318\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 90, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Bootify ModuleLauncher\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-s developer I\'d like to _bootify_ {{ModuleLauncher}} so I can use Spring Boot\'s support for property setting as well as adding options and new functionality in the future such as CP augmentation.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1786,'XD-3322','90','{\"key\": \"XD-3322\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 90, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Create CI infrastructure for s-c-s-m repo\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-s developer I\'d like to setup CI infrastructure for {{spring-cloud-stream-modules}} (s-c-s-m) repo so I can build the project continuously on every commits.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1787,'XD-3313','90','{\"key\": \"XD-3313\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 90, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add in-memory stream definition repository\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a spring-cloud-data developer I\'d like to use an in-memory stream definition repository so I don\'t have to spin up a store; obviously this will not persist between application executions but it will be useful for a simplified development experience.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1788,'XD-3314','90','{\"key\": \"XD-3314\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 90, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Validate stream commands from shell\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to invoke REST APIs via shell so I can validate {{StreamController}} operations.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1789,'XD-3335','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3335\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"Kafka Source must set autoStartup=false on KafkaMessageDrivenChannelAdapter\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"If the value is not set the source may start before being bound to the bus throwing a \\\"Dispatcher has no subscribers\\\" error\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1790,'XD-3320','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3320\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Migrate StreamController from XD 1.0\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d user I\'d like to add REST support for stream commands so I can maneuver streaming pipeline backed by StreamController.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1791,'XD-3300','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3300\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Michael Minella\", \"summary\": \"Spike: Determine best way to centrally configure the job repository for batch jobs.\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Michael Minella\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"h2. NarrativeAs a developer I need to be able to run batch jobs that use the centrally configured job repository to store job state.h2. Back storyThe XD containers each used a {{BatchConfigurer}} implementation ({{RuntimeBatchConfigurer}}) to add a consistent configuration for the job repository.  This functionality needs to be replicated in some way in just a regular Spring Boot application.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1792,'XD-3267','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3267\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support for Receptor SPI to query module status\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a Spring XD on CF user I\'d like to use Receptor implementation of Admin SPI every time I deploy Spring XD modules so I can leverage the SPI to query for module status and health metrics.*Possible APIs:*{code}ModuleStatus getStatus(ModuleDescriptor descriptor);Collection<ModuleDescriptor> listModules();Map<ModuleDescriptor.Key ModuleStatus>{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1793,'XD-3344','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3344\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Implement undeploy operation for singlenode SPI \", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to implement _undeploy_ operation for {{singlenode}} (single JVM) so I can use this target to undeploy a running stream. More details in [this PR|https://github.com/spring-cloud/spring-cloud-data/pull/19].*Note:* Its a prerequisite to determine consistent _undeploy_ strategy for both {{jobs}} and {{streams}}. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1794,'XD-3271','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3271\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add automatic wiring of profile-driven SPI implementations\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a Spring XD user I\'d like to make SPI implementation profile aware so I can run {{java -jar admin}} or {{cf push}} admin or {{ltc create admin}} and the corresponding implementation gets wired-in automatically.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1795,'XD-3315','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3315\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Port Redis counter as s-c-s sink\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-s developer I\'d like to adapt redis {{counter}} from XD to s-c-s so I can build streaming pipes using s-c-s modules with simple counters to feed dashboards. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1796,'XD-3384','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3384\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Spike: Investigate distributed deployment of s-c-s modules via YARN SPI\", \"assignee\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As an s-c-d developer I\'d like to investigate the distributed deployment of s-c-s modules on YARN so I can experiment the implementation of YARN SPI and derive the strategy for {{YARNModuleDeployer}}.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1797,'XD-3350','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3350\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support to expose counter metrics for dashboarding\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to add support to expose counter (metrics) endpoints so I can consume to feed the dashboards to demonstrate {{firehose | counter}} pipe.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1798,'XD-3259','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3259\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"[SCS] Rename xd.messagebus binder properties \", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 1.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"replace with xd.messagebus prefix with spring.cloud.stream.binder\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1799,'XD-3245','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3245\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"Replace spring-xd-messagebus-* dependencies with SCS\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"XD 2.0 will not have direct dependency on the s-c-s Binder (as MB has been renamed).  The message bus code is obsolete/orphaned in XD 2.0 but some is required to support current integration tests. We can look at pruning it some more but complete removal likely depends on integrating the s-c-s enabled Admin SPI.  MB will remain in XD 1.x.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1800,'XD-3341','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3341\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Publish s-c-d image to DockerHub\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to publish the s-c-d image to DockerHub so I can incrementally push the latest commits to the remote location.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1801,'XD-3218','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3218\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"[Backport] Handle stream/job deployment status recalculation failures\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The admin leader election fails when the stream/job module definitions doesn\'t exist in `module-registry` but still some of the references still exist in ZK (via some of the previous deployments that had this module in module registry). Though this is expected this behavior will make *all* the subsequent deployments in *deploying* state because the admin leader isn\'t elected.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1802,'XD-3078','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3078\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Lukasz Nowanski\", \"summary\": \"Spring XD admin fails to redeploy modules after Spring XD container successfully reconnectes to Zookeeper\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 2.0, \"reporter\": \"Lukasz Nowanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 7.0, \"description\": \"We are running Spring XD 1.1.1 in our production environment and Zookeeper 3.4.5.  Zookeeper is running in failover mode and consists of three independent nodes set up on three separate VMs. From time to time we get \\\"Connection to Zookeeper Suspended\\\" event which causes one of the containers in the cluster to be removed from the SpringXD cluster. Modules being deployed on this removed node fail to be re-deployed to other containers in the cluster.Affected versions:- SpringXD 1.1.1- Zookeeper 3.4.5 and 3.4.6Cluster set up in PROD environment where error occurs:- 4 Spring-XD dedicated servers- 4 spring-xd containers (each running on designated server )- 2 spring-xd admins ( each running alongside one spring-xd container)- 3 Zookeeper nodes ( 3 designated servers on PAITO environment )Cluster set up in TEST environment where error also occurred:- 2 Spring-XD dedicated servers running one spring-xd container and one spring-xd admin each- 3 Zookeeper nodes running on 3 dedicated servers (PAITO Test environment)Cluster set up to reproduce error found in PROD environment:- 1 spring-xd admin- 3 spring xd-containers (each running on a designated VM )- 3 zookeeper servers running on one VMSteps to reproduce:1)Set up three node Zookeeper cluster. Attached is example zoo.cfg we are using default configuration values. In this particular test case we run all Zookeeper nodes on a single VM as we were not testing network layer interruptions.2)Set up one Spring XD admin node. Please note that we have also observed this on two node Spring XD admin cluster. 3)Set up three Spring XD container nodes. All of them belong to one group (SA) and two of them also belong to second group (HA1). This is configured in $XD_HOME/config/servers.yml however so far group configuration never influenced test outcome.4)Create and deploy a test stream using following XD Shell commands:stream create --name test-zookeeper-failover --definition \\\"syslog-udp --port=5140 | transform | file --dir=\'/opt/pivotal/spring-xd/xd/output\'\\\"stream deploy --name test-zookeeper-failover --properties \\\"module.syslog-udp.criteria=groups.contains(\'HA1\')module.syslog-udp.count=2module.file.criteria=groups.contains(\'SA\')module.file.count=3module.transform.criteria=groups.contains(\'SA\')\\\"5)Ensure that test stream works and handles traffic on UDP port 51406)Shutdown one of the Zookeeper nodes by issuing a stop command.7)Two Spring XD containers were not affected and remained in Spring XD cluster.8)One Spring XD container was kicked out of Spring XD cluster and was no longer visible on Spring XD admin Web UI. Modules previously deployed to this container were not redeployed to other cluster members.9)On the failed Spring XD container we have observed CONNECTION_SUSPEND CONNECTION_RECONECTED and CHILD_REMOVE Zookeeper events (attached is container-log.txt). Please note that Java process is still running and we see ΓÇ£ConnectionStateManager-0 server.ContainerRegistrar - Waiting for supervisor to clean up prior deploymentsΓÇ¥ messages.10)Spring XD admin failed with exception in DepartingContainerModuleRedeployer (attached is admin-log.txt). 11)We have observed that departing container node in Zookeeper (/sa/deployments/modules/allocated/1d3fd4cc-5a70-47ed-b4f3-22deef1f4d4f/) had no children. We did this after few minutes so we are not sure at which point it was cleared. 12)Restarting failed Spring XD container fixed the problem modules were correctly redeployed.Exception from point 10 is very similar to XD-1983 and this code was rewritten in XD-2004.\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 14.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1803,'XD-3306','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3306\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Jos├⌐ Carlos Valero S├ínchez\", \"summary\": \"[Flo] Some streams can\'t be created using FLO\", \"assignee\": \"Andy Clement\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Jos├⌐ Carlos Valero S├ínchez\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Trying to create streams from the flo UI may end up in weird exceptions whereas doing the same thing (copying/pasting the stream) directly from XD shell works smoothly.This simple stream is an example but this situation happens in multiple scenarios (for example using the same module several times with labels).{code:java}trigger --cron=\'0 05 14 ? * MON-FRI\' | mail --from=\'\'\'xd@mycompany.com\'\'\' --to=\'\'\'a-wise-guy@mycompany.com\'\'\' --bcc=\'\'\'me@mycompany.com\'\'\'{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 3.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}');
INSERT INTO `issues_origem` VALUES ('Spring_XD',1804,'XD-3321','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3321\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Make requirement for MD5 hash files configurable for the custom module registry \", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"Post 1.2 upgrade the custom modules no longer show up by just copying the jars to the {{xd.customModule.home}} directory. Instead I have to use the \'module upload\' command to install the modules. This is because an MD5 file is required. More details in [SO thread|http://stackoverflow.com/questions/31792220/spring-xd-1-2-0-custom-module-deployment]. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1805,'XD-3346','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3346\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Accessing step progress via REST fails with 403\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 4.0, \"description\": \"As a XD user I\'m trying to access URI (- GET /jobs/executions//steps//progress => hasRole(\'ROLE_VIEW\')) but it fails with 403 forbidden error for the role with view access. More details [here|https://issuetracker.springsource.com/browse/VESC-475].Another URL with the same error: http://<HOST>:9393/streams/definitions.json?page=0&size=10\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 8.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1806,'XD-3347','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3347\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"summary\": \"Run all shell integration tests also with enabled security\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Apply the same strategy for the Module Command Tests also to all other Shell integration tests.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1807,'XD-3353','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3353\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Add shell as a rest client to the spring-cloud-data REST API\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I would like to have shell interface to the spring-cloud-data rest API. The scope for this JIRA could be limited to stream commands.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1808,'XD-3354','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3354\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Move shell integration tests to spring-cloud-data shell \", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"This could focus only on the subset (Stream operations)\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1809,'XD-3351','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3351\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"[SCS]- Replace codec impl in spring-cloud-stream-codec with SI-Codec\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1810,'XD-3352','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3352\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"David Turanski\", \"summary\": \"[SCS] - Replace Binder XML config with @Configuration\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"David Turanski\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Create Confguration and ConfigurationProperties. Configuration must support replacing the default Kryo Codec implementation with something else.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1811,'XD-3377','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3377\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Michael Minella\", \"summary\": \"Refactor Task parsing \", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Michael Minella\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently the DSL parsing for tasks is a copy and paste of what it is for streams (minus the ability to parse multiple modules).  This results in a lot of duplication.  This should be refactored to remove duplication and remove explicit references to either streams or tasks in common code.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1812,'XD-3380','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3380\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Refactor Binder @Configuration to use AutoConfiguration\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Currently @EnableModule hardcodes references to both the redis and rabbit configuration classes which trigger or don\'t trigger based on the presence of another jar (which itself has the meat of the configuration).This is typically what boot AutoConfiguration is for.Moreover adding a new binding (eg Kafka or a stub for module testing) would require to crack open @EnableModule\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1813,'XD-3381','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3381\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"summary\": \"Provide test infrastructure for module authors\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a module author I want to be able to test my code in \\\"next to real world\\\" conditions (ie Integration Testing but not really):- I want all my module wiring to be testable- I want all my module configuration (@ConfigurationProperties) to be in effect and I want to be able to test various combination of props- I want to be able to send data to my module and assert what is coming at the other end- I want an idiomatic way of asserting the above (eg integration with Hamcrest etc)- I DONT want to have to send data to an actual bus (redis rabbit etc)\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1814,'XD-3393','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3393\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade receptor-client to comply with latest Receptor APIs\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to upgrade {{receptor-client}} to comply with latest {{Receptor}} API changes so I can sync-up and take advantage of the recent improvements. \", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1815,'XD-3396','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3396\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Add cloud connector dependencies for spring-cloud-data admin\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Spring-cloud-data admin requires lattice connector and `spring-cloud-spring-service-connector` dependencies so that the admin controllers get access to any services while running on lattice.One example is CounterContoller using `redis` service for MetricRepository.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1816,'XD-3397','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3397\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Port admin web UI to Spring Cloud Data admin\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I should be able to use the existing admin UI client for spring-cloud-data admin with the appropriate server configurations.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1817,'XD-3399','92','{\"key\": \"XD-3399\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 92, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Create CI Builds for SCD and Receptor Client\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Build SCS and SCD projects upon change in github repo.Push docker image for SCD-Admin to docker hub\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1818,'XD-3349','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3349\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Design the foundation to port XD modules to s-c-s\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Pollack\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 2.0, \"issueLinks\": 2.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As an s-c-s developer I\'d like to brainstorm and design the foundation to port XD modules as s-c-s modules so I can use it