scription\": \"As a Spring XD developer I\'d like to port {{filter}} module from XD to s-c-s repo so I can use it as {{processor}} module to build streaming pipeline.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1822,'XD-3367','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3367\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Port Transform as s-c-s module\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a Spring XD developer I\'d like to port {{transform}} module from XD to s-c-s repo so I can use it as {{processor}} module to build streaming pipeline.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1823,'XD-3395','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3395\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Module Launcher properties improvments\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Improve Spring Cloud Stream module launcher/resolver properties:1) Support comma separated remoteRepositories2) Classify/group the properties\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1824,'XD-3398','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3398\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Create auto configuration/properties for Local Binder\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-s developer I\'d like to create auto configuration for {{singlenode}} binder configuration/properties so I can automatically configure the Spring application based on the dependencies.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1825,'XD-3298','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3298\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Michael Minella\", \"summary\": \"Create basic TaskLauncher\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Minella\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Michael Minella\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"h2. NarrativeAs Spring XD I will be able to launch Spring Boot jar files as Diego Tasks.h2. Back storyThe {{TaskLauncher}} will be responsible for listening for launch requests looking up the definition in the {{TaskDescriptorRepository}} and launching it.  The first implementation of this would be a Receptor based implementation. The scope here is to produce a _basic_ version of {{TaskLauncher}} and incrementally evolve into comprehensive launch capabilities.*See:* https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q964adRCA-kJke_i0GBToJHLXJJTV_7TaTpQT0ymsbc/edit\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1826,'XD-2919','94','{\"key\": \"XD-2919\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Create persistent stream repository\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to create persistent repository for streams so I could leverage the persisted metadata and reestablish the streaming pipe under failure conditions.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1827,'XD-3430','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3430\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add support for \\\"deployment properties\\\"\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to provide optional key-value pairs as deployment properties so I could leverage them at the runtime to instruct how the modules will be deployed. _The scope of this story is to specifically support {{count}} to represent {{N}} instances of modules that share the same environment variables._\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1828,'XD-3407','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3407\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"To Do\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Document the process of resolving and adding JARs to Boot loader\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 1.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to complete documentation and test-cases on resolving and adding JAR\'s to Boot loader so we could use this as a reference while porting modules with external dependencies. \", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 1.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1829,'XD-3296','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3296\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Michael Minella\", \"summary\": \"Spike: Design a tasks repository\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Michael Minella\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"h2. NarrativeAs a developer I\'d like to be able to run a boot jar as a task on CF and obtain the result reliably.h2. Back storyCurrently Lattice/Diego\'s tasks implementation provides the ability to run things as short lived tasks.  However obtaining the result of said task can be an issue.  There are two ways to do so:# Poll for the result.# Register a callback URL to be called once the task completes.Since a task is only available for a short time after its completion before it is deleted polling can run the risk of missing the result completely.  When you consider the fact that the provided GUIDs that identify tasks can be re-used polling becomes a precarious option.Registering a callback URL would be a better option however there are no good guarantees that the message will be delivered.  The service will try to execute the callback until it\'s successful or the task is cleaned up.  \\\"Successful\\\" is defined in this case as anything other than a 502 or a 503 return code.In order for Spring XD to be able to support Diego tasks a more durable option for maintaining the result of tasks will need to be developed.*Note:* The outcome of this spike may be feature requests for the CF/Diego team.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1830,'XD-3373','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3373\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"First deploy/launch of Pig job that includes yarn-site.xml file fails\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Deploying and launching a Pig job that contains a yarn-site.xml config file fails on the first deploy after XD starts up. This happens consistently.The error is:   Error: Could not find or load main class org.apache.hadoop.mapreduce.v2.app.MRAppMasterwhich indicates that the yarn-site.xml file never made it to the classpath.Un-deploying and re-deploying the job seems to fix the problem.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1831,'XD-3416','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3416\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Create foundation to support s-c-s \'processor\' modules\", \"assignee\": \"Mark Fisher\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to create foundation to support _processor_ as OOTB modules so I can use the processor modules from {{s-c-s-m}} repo to build streaming pipeline.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1832,'XD-3417','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3417\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Add SmartLifecycle to ChannelBindingAdapter\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Make ChannelBindingAdapter implement SmartLifecycle so that it gets started with the highest precedence and before any other message producing bean.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1833,'XD-3418','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3418\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Enable \\\"offline\\\" mode for AetherModuleResolver\", \"assignee\": \"David Turanski\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-s developer I\'d like to enable {{offline}} mode for {{AetherModuleResolver}} so I can pull the module artifacts from local instead of remote maven repo.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1834,'XD-3419','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3419\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add registry to lookup module coordinates by name\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to create {{ModuleRegistry}} implementation so I can use this infrastructure to lookup module coordinates by name.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1835,'XD-3423','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3423\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Michael Minella\", \"summary\": \"Update Shell to support tasks\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Michael Minella\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"h2. NarrativeAs a user I need to be able to deploy a task (boot jar) via the CLI.h2.  Back storySince the concept of jobs as an explicit primitive within Spring XD is going away in spring-cloud-data the shell needs to be updated to reflect that.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1836,'XD-3424','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3424\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"summary\": \"Fix Cloud connector dependencies and service resolution\", \"assignee\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Ilayaperumal Gopinathan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"This JIRA addresses couple of issues:1) When the modules are deployed into cloud environment there is an issue where local configuration beans collide with cloud service beans. We witnessed an issue where there are two `RedisConnectionFactory` beans registered in the same application context.We need to have a control the way in which the auto configuration gets invoked and service beans are created.2) We need to align the cloud connector dependencies into a common place so that we don\'t have to specify them at various places like (SCS SCS-Binder SCS-modules) etc.It is a good idea to have these dependencies specified in SCS-modules so that it get used subsequently by SCS when the module is assembled at runtime.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1837,'XD-3425','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3425\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Support shell commands to interact with module registry\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 4.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to have {{module info}} {{module list}} {{module register}} and {{module unregister}} commands so I can interact with {{ModuleRegistry}}.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1838,'XD-3426','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3426\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add \\\"module info\\\" command\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to have {{module info}} shell command so I can query each of the module specifics such as description and support options. \", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1839,'XD-3427','94','{\"key\": \"XD-3427\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 94, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add \\\"module list\\\" command\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a s-c-d developer I\'d like to have {{mod