uses the composed job as if it is a normal job including seeing only the DSL.  In the background the JobFactory will deploy the composed job module.  * When the user destroys the job the module will be deleted from the file module repository.* When the user creates the job a module will be created in the file Module repository.h2. Back storyFor the composed job story we need to create a \\\"real\\\" job module to be expressed in XML so that we can take advantage of the job execution tasklet in XD-3556 so that each job can be executed as a step in the composed job.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1916,'XD-3570','99','{\"key\": \"XD-3570\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 99, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Paul Harris\", \"summary\": \"Readme has conflicting CF information\", \"assignee\": \"Paul Harris\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Paul Harris\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"In https://github.com/spring-cloud/spring-cloud-dataflow/blob/master/README.md#running-on-cloud-foundry the section starting \'Now we can configure the app\' needs to be revised - the information is both out of date and even if up-to-date misleading (it includes some values as if they are universal when they are really just examples).\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1917,'XD-3370','99','{\"key\": \"XD-3370\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 99, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Port FTP as s-c-s sink module\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchco