lationLevel: ISOLATION_SERIALIZATION```to```spring:  batch:# Configure other Spring Batch repository values.  Most are typically not needed    isolationLevel: ISOLATION_READ_COMMITTED```  And update the hsqldb datasource to:spring:  datasource:    url: jdbc:hsqldb:hsql://${hsql.server.host:localhost}:${hsql.server.port:9101}/${hsql.server.dbname:xdjob};sql.enforce_strict_size=true;hsqldb.tx=mvcc\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1952,'XD-3689','101','{\"key\": \"XD-3689\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 101, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Update default configs to support Composed Jobs\", \"assignee\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Users want the ability to use Composed Jobs (specifically parallel Jobs) without having to update the configurations for the hsqldb and the Isolation Level for spring batch.  These should be set by default.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1953,'XD-3693','101','{\"key\": \"XD-3693\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 101, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Add Timestamp to XD Message History\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"I don\'t recall why [this commit | https://github.com/garyrussell/spring-xd/commit/ba15a1390f7e448dbc723ee76a45c2e239e0994e] was not applied to master but having the timestamp for each step in the history will be useful.See [this github issue | https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd-modules/issues/24#issuecomment-154436643].\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1954,'XD-3695','101','{\"key\": \"XD-3695\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 101, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to SHDP 2.2.1.GA\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to upgrade to 2.2.1 GA release so I can leverage the latest improvements without breaking backwards compatibility. SHDP 2.3.0 uses Boot 1.3 and HDP and CDH versions that drop older Hive support. To avoid breaking changes we should instead use SHDP 2.2.1 that has backported any improvements that we need as well as move Spring and Hadoop versions to more recent ones.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1955,'XD-3698','101','{\"key\": \"XD-3698\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 101, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Execution list page includes child jobs in pagination scope\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I created a composed job with over 10 child jobs in the workflow; I expected to see \'a\' job in the execution list page without any pagination but instead I noticed empty pagination to skip to next page.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1956,'XD-3699','101','{\"key\": \"XD-3699\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 101, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Remove hardcoded buildpack commit reference\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to remove the hardcoded buildpack reference since the latest 1.6.2 ER release includes all the features required by Data Flow. \", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1957,'XD-3701','101','{\"key\": \"XD-3701\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 101, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Improve Shell Connection Diagnostics\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"When a problem occurs connecting to admin we just get {{Unable to contact Data Flow Admin}} even if the connection is successful and some problem occurs when interpreting the result.The exception is eaten.Log an error including the exception.Currently investigating an NPE in DataFlowTemplate @ line 77.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1958,'XD-3610','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3610\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"Kafka source and sink headers shouldn\'t interfere with bus functionality\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"The Kafka sink should not make use of the message headers sent by the Kafka receivers in the Kafka bus. Similarly the headers received from the Kafka source should not be propagated when sending to the Kakfa bus. https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/issues/1804\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1959,'XD-3696','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3696\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to SI 4.2.2.GA\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to upgrade to SI 4.2.2.GA release so I can leverage the latest improvements.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1960,'XD-3216','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3216\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"On specific shutdown scenarios the stream resumes from the start of the bus topic\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/issues/1727\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1961,'XD-3697','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3697\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Daniel Garcia Perez\", \"summary\": \"Output modules cannot use minPartitionCount when sending to named channels\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Daniel Garcia Perez\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"If the output module is connected to a named channel cannot be set up the property minPartitionCount it is giving an exception.Streams:stream create f --definition \\\"queue:foo > transform --expression=payload+\'-foo\' | log\\\" stream create b --definition \\\"queue:bar > transform --expression=payload+\'-bar\' | log\\\"stream deploy --name f --properties \\\"module.transform.count=2\\\"stream deploy --name b --properties \\\"module.transform.count=2\\\"stream create r --definition \\\"time | router --expression=payload.contains(\'10\')?\'queue:foo\':\'queue:bar\'\\\"stream deploy --name r --properties \\\"module.router.producer.minPartitionCount=20\\\"The error is:Caused by: java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: KafkaMessageBus does not support producer property: minPartitionCount for queue:bar.at org.springframework.xd.dirt.integration.bus.MessageBusSupport.validateProperties(MessageBusSupport.java:781) ~[spring-xd-messagebus-spi-1.2.1.RELEASE.jar:1.2.1.RELEASE]\", \"fixVersions\": 2.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1962,'XD-3652','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3652\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"The shell processor module cannot be stopped while blocked in receive()\", \"assignee\": \"Patrick Peralta\", \"priority\": 3.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Both lifecycle and send/receive methods are synchronized so if the shell command processor is blocked reading from the script\'s input - e.g. when no proper terminator is sent by the script the stop() method can\'t acquire the object lock and proceed stopping the instance and therefore the module. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1963,'XD-3673','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3673\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Multiple module instances produces duplicate messages \", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a follow-up from [XD-3613|https://jira.spring.io/browse/XD-3629] we would want to fix this experience for Kafka message bus.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1964,'XD-3690','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3690\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"summary\": \"Improve \\\"Server Configuration - Database Configuration\\\" section\", \"assignee\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Thomas Risberg\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"Make it more clear what drivers need to be copied where. See - https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-xd/issues/1653\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1965,'XD-3691','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3691\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"summary\": \"Ensure Job definitions are escaped in UI\", \"assignee\": \"Gunnar Hillert\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Glenn Renfro\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"If using the definition <aaa || bbb> where the definition starts with a \\\"<\\\" and ends with a \\\">\\\" the definition for the composed job does not appear on the definition page.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1966,'XD-3669','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3669\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Add Flo screenshots to Batch DSL section\", \"assignee\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a user I\'d like Flo Graphs as screenshots while referring to the batch DSL so it will be easy for me to relate to concepts. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1967,'XD-3692','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3692\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Optimize YARN deployer\", \"assignee\": \"Janne Valkealahti\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to optimize YARN deployer so I can deploy stream and the modules part of the definition rapidly.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1968,'XD-3702','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3702\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"summary\": \"Support partitioning for Kafka even if count == 1\", \"assignee\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Marius Bogoevici\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I want to be able to set a partitioning key for the Kafka bus even when there is a single downstream module so that I can take advantage of the native Kafka partitioning and message ordering support.\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1969,'XD-3708','102','{\"key\": \"XD-3708\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 102, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Document limitations with HSQL when using composed jobs\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Minella\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d want to document the limitations of HSQL DB when using composed jobs. \", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 0.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1970,'XD-3709','103','{\"key\": \"XD-3709\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 103, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Gary Russell\", \"summary\": \"Duplicate MBean Names With router Sink\", \"assignee\": \"Gary Russell\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Gary Russell\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 1.0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3.0, \"description\": \"For some reason the Integration {{MBeanExporterHelper}} is not preventing the standard context {{MBeanExporter}} from exporting the {{AbstractMessageRouter}}. This should be suppressed (when an IMBE is present) because it\'s annotated {{@IntegrationManagedResource}}.Causes {{InstanceAlreadyExistsException}}.Workaround in the stack overflow answer.http://stackoverflow.com/questions/33838502/error-deploying-more-than-one-stream-with-a-router-1-3-0Could be an SI issue but investigation needed. However we should probably include the stream/job name in all MBeans for the stream (as is done for the integration exporter).\", \"fixVersions\": 1.0, \"commentCount\": 4.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 1.0}'),('Spring_XD',1971,'XD-3672','103','{\"key\": \"XD-3672\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 103, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Move Mesos SPI to a separate repo\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to submit a PR for existing work on Mesos SPI. \", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 2.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1972,'XD-3715','103','{\"key\": \"XD-3715\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 103, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Move k8s SPI to a separate repo\", \"assignee\": \"Eric Bottard\", \"priority\": 4.0, \"reporter\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"subtasks\": 0.0, \"blockedBy\": 0.0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0.0, \"issueLinks\": 0.0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2.0, \"description\": \"As a developer I\'d like to move k8s SPI to it\'s own repo.\", \"fixVersions\": 0.0, \"commentCount\": 1.0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0.0, \"affectedVersions\": 0.0}'),('Spring_XD',1973,'XD-3714','103','{\"key\": \"XD-3714\", \"votes\": 0.0, \"blocks\": 0.0, \"sprint\": 103, \"status\": \"Done\", \"creator\": \"Sabby Anandan\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade XD Ambari relea