sueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',66,'USERGRID-367','70','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-367\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Refactor entity writes to run concurrently\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need to implement our operations concurrently to increase our throughput.  We need to execute the following operations in parallel.Entity WriteGraph Edge WriteEntity Indexing (still async)We have lazy repair on all reads if the system were to get out of sync.  Since we do not have a transactional store we can utilize this read repair to increase write throughput.  In the event a transaction fails we attempt to roll back. If the roll back fails it will be repaired the next time a stale entry is read.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',67,'USERGRID-193','70','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-193\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Pooja Jain\", \"summary\": \"SaveCollectionMembers in Export does not correctly export all entity data\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Pooja Jain\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"The saveConnections() and saveDictionaries() methods are called at the end of SaveCollectionMembers() in file ExportServiceImpl.java  but if collection for an entity was null then it would just return and not export the connections and dictionaries for that particular entity thus calling these functions in the start of the method ensures that all connections and dictionaries are always exported.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',68,'USERGRID-335','70','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-335\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Test Not Passing: CollectionsResourceIT\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',69,'USERGRID-371','70','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-371\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Ensure that all services that use amazon keys are using the same identifier for those amazon keys.\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently the way notifications looks for access and secret keys is different from the way that export and import services look for keys. This needs to be changed so that we all look for the same name of the keys.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',70,'USERGRID-323','70','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-323\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 70, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"summary\": \"Implement Windows phone push notifications\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"depende