-11\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 71, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"summary\": \"Limit the size of entities posted to Usergrid\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Currently you can post items of almost any size to UG. We should determine the maximum size that is still optimum (15-16MB?) and enforce this.[~zznate] do you have a recommendation?\", \"fixVersions\": 2, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',112,'USERGRID-364','71','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-364\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 71, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Get Import Service working with old queue system in 2.0\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Get all existing Import Service tests working in the two-dot-o branch with the existing Scheduler & Queue system.\", \"fixVersions\": 2, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',113,'USERGRID-313','71','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-313\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 71, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Convert ConnectionResourceTest/OwnershipResourceIT/Permissions to new Rest Framework\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',114,'USERGRID-256','71','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-256\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 71, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Use ApiResponse to parse out JsonNode responses\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 2, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently in the rest tier tests we are forced to parse the JsonNode response to see what has been returned. Instead what we want to do is use our ApiResponse and use the methods in there to retrieve and check the responses. This will make the tests easier to understand. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',115,'USERGRID-259','71','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-259\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 71, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Generify the ApiResponse so we can return any type of class\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The ApiResponse should be converted to be a generic class so that we can type case it into the specific type we need. For example : the ApiResponse can return a User type if we have ApiResponse<T> we should be able to get back a ApiResponse<User>.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',116,'USERGRID-260','71','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-260\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 71, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"composition vs inheritance for the apiresponse json node deserialization\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\"