ssignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',194,'USERGRID-273','82','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-273\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 4, \"sprint\": 82, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"5 Cleanup test harness and create a more declarative test framework\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 4, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 5, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Currently our test harnesses are a mess of spaghetti.  We need to decouple this mess and allow us to cleanly define the rules and requirements of our system.  I think we need to break it down into the following behaviors.h1. Test Execution Environmentsh2. Parallel ExecutionThis should be the default behavior.  All tests are assumed to be parallelh2. Serial ExecutionThis should be the exception and only used when parallel execution cannot be accomplished.  Tests in this classification should run in a method at a time with no concurrencyh1. External resourcesh2. Cassandra# Configure the runtime# Pre invocation hook## Create default implementation of truncating column families.  This should be manually added and not execute by default.# Post invocation hookh2. ElasticSearch # Configure the runtime# Pre invocation hook## Create default implementation of truncating column families.  This should be manually added and not execute by default.# Post invocation hookh1. LifecycleA test itself can have numerous lifecycle operations.  These should be set up as rules both class and instance and should NOT be done via inheritance of abstract tests.  This is the old Junit3 way of operating and needs removed.\", \"fixVersions\": 2, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',195,'USERGRID-366','82','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-366\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 82, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Eliminate 2 network calls for non optimistic transaction writes\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently when a write occurs that is either a new entity or a non optimistic transaction (I.E no version included in the payload) we\'re performing 2 writes in the collection module.  Instead we should perform a single write to both the transaction log and entity storage to reduce our network I/O.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',196,'USERGRID-333','82','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-333\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 82, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Fix ApplicationResourceIT\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',197,'USERGRID-409','82','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-409\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 82, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Enable system properties for customizable keyspaces\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Keyspaces should be customizable for the usergrid system.  We need to implement the ability to set the keyspace based on system properties as well as the current defaults.  We should implement this in the following way.# Add these properties to the Cassandra Fig (or create a new fig configuration)# Add the fig to the injector# Reference the injector and the fig in the current EntityManager and CassandraService setup classes\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',198,'USERGRID-418','82','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-418\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 82, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Fix system/database/setup to swallow \\\"test-app\\\" already exists error.\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 1, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Fix the endpoint to return ok even if the test-app already exists. This isn\'t really an error and should be swallowed so we don\'t confuse users. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',199,'USERGRID-422','82','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-422\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 82, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Create test that proves the issue before making any rest tier changes\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Make a rest test that shows when calling system/database/setup twice returns an exception.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',200,'USERGRID-280','82','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-280\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 82, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Implement Admin User methods in Management Class for REST tests\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Implement Admin User methods in Management Class for REST tests. Ensure that AdminUsersIT test works.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',201,'USERGRID-448','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-448\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Remove redundant appinfos collections in ManagementServiceImpl\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"There is a flaw in the two-dot-o CpEntityManagerFactory.The factory stores a collection of \\\"appinfo\\\" type entities but the ManagementServiceImpl stores a redundant collection of \\\"application_info\\\" entities. The problem becomes evident when you try to delete an application. The application will only be deleted from the \\\"appinfos\\\" collection. When you call the management org/apps end-point you will still see the application because the end-point uses the \\\"application_infos\\\". To fix this:- Ensure that only one collection is stored- Add code to migrate the existing app information collections\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',202,'USERGRID-348','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-348\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Update ExportResourceIT to new REST test framework\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',203,'USERGRID-335','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-335\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Test Not Passing: CollectionsResourceIT\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',204,'USERGRID-371','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-371\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Ensure that all services that use amazon keys are using the same identifier for those amazon keys.\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently the way notifications looks for access and secret keys is different from the way that export and import services look for keys. This needs to be changed so that we all look for the same name of the keys.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',205,'USERGRID-466','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-466\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Rejected ES Index jobs are dropped.  \", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When the index queue is full and ES rejects index requests Usergrid drops them.  The result could be that entities cannot be returned.We should handle this soon.  At a minimum we should put them in an SQS queue or something similar for future handling.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',206,'USERGRID-396','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-396\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Create UniqueIndexCleanup tool that works with 2.0\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Current instance of tools don\'t work correctly with 2.0. This should have a RESTful endpoint that is trigged with a PUT.  We should have something like this endpoint.Check all unique values across the entire system => PUT /system/database/unqiuecheckCheck all unique values across a single applications => PUT /system/database/uniquecheck/[appid]Check all unique values in a single collection => PUT /system/database/uniquecheck/[appid]/[collectionname]Check a specific unique value for a collection.PUT=> system/database/uniquecheck/[appid]/[collectionname]/[unique value]The unique check will need to audit the unique index and ensure that the unique value exists for the entity specified. If the entity does not exist they should be removed.I think we should implement specific property cleanup first then implement the other operations as an input of Observables\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',207,'USERGRID-472','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-472\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"fix array type index issue when types alternate\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',208,'USERGRID-405','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-405\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Fix hotspot from continuous writes of entities (Shawn)\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 4, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Currently performing a continuous PUT in 2.0 under heavy load causes a hotspot in our cassandra data.  Cause:# Under load entities can be PUT continuously# Asynchronous cleanups run and delete previous versions# These versions are retained in cassandra for long periods of time.  This causes severe row bloating before compaction occurs.Solution:For entity data we only care about the current max version.  We should change this column family to store only the maximum data format.  We will need to keep the log of previous versions so that we can bring ES into a consistent state\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',209,'USERGRID-456','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-456\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Change ElasticSearch mapping behavior to be per index\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently it is not possible to share multiple usergrid instances on the same cluster.  This is due to our default mapping usage in elasticsearch.  We need to change the following.# Stop putting default wildcard mappings based on the index prefix while this should work it appears it is not# Change our settings so that when an index is created the default mapping is applied per-indexAlso during an index rebuild if the write_alias exists we will also want to explicitly update the mapping during this process.   This will allow us to do an online rebuild without having to allocate a new write index and then merge.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',210,'USERGRID-416','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-416\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"SPIKE: Profile Usergrid Search\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',211,'USERGRID-443','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-443\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Implement Windows Raw Push Notifications for 1.0\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Support for Raw Push Notifications for Windows platform needs to be added to the 1.0 code base.  A separate task can be created/assigned for 2.0.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',212,'USERGRID-361','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-361\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"summary\": \"Create REST test for app delete\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',213,'USERGRID-432','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-432\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Remove redundant createIndex calls\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',214,'USERGRID-454','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-454\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Add metrics to cassandra and ES calls\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We want to add a way for UG to get metrics about calls being made to Cassandra and ES so we can measure where we have performance bottlenecks.In order to accomplish this we need to wrap our Cassandra execution calls with graphite timers. We could also set timers to check when Cassandra calls are being started or loaded up.For ES we already have timers around index updates and index deletes. We just want to check the other ES calls ( index creations delete by queries and the rest )\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',215,'USERGRID-465','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-465\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Fix remaining graphite timers in CpEntityManager\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Refactor of UG-454 where we move the timers into the constructor instead of being initialized in methods. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',216,'USERGRID-415','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-415\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Consider Not Logging this Exception\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"This exception probably shouldn\'t be logged at ERROR.  Please consider logging it at DEBUG or not at all.2015-02-25 02:35:55795 [http-bio-8080-exec-2] ERROR org.apache.usergrid.services.AbstractCollectionService- Entity 7 unable to be created in collection saparticlesorg.apache.usergrid.persistence.exceptions.DuplicateUniquePropertyExistsException: Entity saparticle requires that property named name be unique value of 000000000000226126-2538 existsat org.apache.usergrid.corepersistence.CpEntityManager.handleWriteUniqueVerifyException(CpEntityManager.java:2556)at org.apache.usergri