ation time using the new timeUUID string as a key# Return the time UUID as a string to the userON next page# Lookup the the ES cursor from Cassandra# Get the next page of results\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',218,'USERGRID-473','83','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-473\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 83, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Add Dead Letter Queue\", \"assignee\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',219,'USERGRID-460','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-460\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Geospatial/Geolocation query results are not sorted by distance\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Geospatial (\'within\') query results are not sorted by distance.  We should sort by distance ascending by default.  This is now MongoDB handles the $near queries.Please add a test to confirm sorting is done correctly.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',220,'USERGRID-485','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-485\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"2.1 - Rest Tests Must Pass\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Our tests take a long time and don\'t passwe should at least make them pass\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',221,'USERGRID-482','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-482\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Change dynamic mapping to static \", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Change dynamic mapping to static - we discussed that during the call having a lot of mappings changes may be demanding to Elasticsearch. The change from fully dynamic and changing very often to mostly static mapping would result in way less pressure on Elasticsearch data nodes in general\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',222,'USERGRID-70','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-70\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"summary\": \"Geo-location queries with more than two parameters return only the first page of data\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"\\\"User is doing a geolocation query using three parameters. When he does this the first page of data (10 records) is returned but subsequent pages are empty. For example this query returns 19 rows: \\\"\\\"location within 40075160 of 37.33517518 -122.03255055 and bucketId=\'LosAngels\'\\\"\\\" whereas this query which should only omit one record returns 10 records: \\\"\\\"location within 40075160 of 37.33517518 -122.03255055 and NOT email=\'test1@ss.com\' and bucketId=\'LosAngels\'\\\"\\\" The order doesn\'t seem to matter. I tried it with both bucketId before and after email. Also the field doesn\'t seem to matter because the following query also returns only 10 rows when it should return 18: \\\"\\\"location within 40075160 of 37.33517518 -122.03255055 and NOT name=\'Fyndher Vtwo\' and bucketId=\'LosAngels\'\\\"\\\" .\\\"\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',223,'USERGRID-448','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-448\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Remove redundant appinfos collections in ManagementServiceImpl\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"There is a flaw in the two-dot-o CpEntityManagerFactory.The factory stores a collection of \\\"appinfo\\\" type entities but the ManagementServiceImpl stores a redundant collection of \\\"application_info\\\" entities. The problem becomes evident when you try to delete an application. The application will only be deleted from the \\\"appinfos\\\" collection. When you call the management org/apps end-point you will still see the application because the end-point uses the \\\"application_infos\\\". To fix this:- Ensure that only one collection is stored- Add code to migrate the existing app information collections\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',224,'USERGRID-480','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-480\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Enable doc values in our index writes\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Aggregation with large data sets are causing memory pressure.  We need to enable doc values for faster aggregation especially when using SSD ES Nodshttp://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/guide/current/doc-values.html\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',225,'USERGRID-483','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-483\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Change index structure to single index for many apps\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Change the index architecture - Right now you are using an index per client which is good for small number of clients but doesn\'t scale well especially considering that Elasticsearch doesn\'t handle large number of shards well. I need to analyze a few things that I have left and I will come up with a proposition of index architecture.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',226,'USERGRID-371','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-371\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Ensure that all services that use amazon keys are using the same identifier for those amazon keys.\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Technical task\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently the way notifications looks for access and secret keys is different from the way that export and import services look for keys. This needs to be changed so that we all look for the same name of the keys.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',227,'USERGRID-484','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-484\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Introduce doc_values\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Introducing doc_values for numeric and not analyzed string fields. Since your queries are using fielddata cache changing this will also lower heap pressure.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',228,'USERGRID-476','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-476\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Durability of entity writes / Write problem - entities are not necessarily persisted.  Could this be on the unique entity fix?\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"...\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',229,'USERGRID-475','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-475\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Monitoring Metrics: Add Metrics to low levels of cass and es\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',230,'USERGRID-466','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-466\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Rejected ES Index jobs are dropped.  \", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When the index queue is full and ES rejects index requests Usergrid drops them.  The result could be that entities cannot be returned.We should handle this soon.  At a minimum we should put them in an SQS queue or something similar for future handling.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',231,'USERGRID-474','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-474\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Update cloudformation to use dedicated elasticsearch master nodes\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We should update our cloudformation scripts to use a dedicated master node for ES to more closely mirror suggestion production usage during stress testing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',232,'USERGRID-478','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-478\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Put entity cleanup and entity delete tasks back to delete by batch.\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',233,'USERGRID-396','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-396\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Create UniqueIndexCleanup tool that works with 2.0\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Current instance of tools don\'t work correctly with 2.0. This should have a RESTful endpoint that is trigged with a PUT.  We should have something like this endpoint.Check all unique values across the entire system => PUT /system/database/unqiuecheckCheck all unique values across a single applications => PUT /system/database/uniquecheck/[appid]Check all unique values in a single collection => PUT /system/database/uniquecheck/[appid]/[collectionname]Check a specific unique value for a collection.PUT=> system/database/uniquecheck/[appid]/[collectionname]/[unique value]The unique check will need to audit the unique index and ensure that the unique value exists for the entity specified. If the entity does not exist they should be removed.I think we should implement specific property cleanup first then implement the other operations as an input of Observables\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',234,'USERGRID-463','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-463\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Do not create index if a write alias exists\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Users can administer their indexes outside of UG.  When running a re-index an index will be created even if the write alias points to a valid index.  Instead of checking for an index by name at create time we should instead check for the existence of an alias.  If the write alias exists we should not allocate a new index.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',235,'USERGRID-472','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-472\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"fix array type index issue when types alternate\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',236,'USERGRID-479','97','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-479\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 97, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"summary\": \"CLONE - Could not retrieve unique value for field name unable to verify\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"2015-02-16 05:33:23590 [http-bio-8080-exec-313] ERROR org.apache.usergrid.rest.exceptions.AbstractExceptionMapper- java.lang.RuntimeException Server Error (500)java.lang.RuntimeException: Could not retrieve unique value for field name unable to verify        at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.write.WriteUniqueVerify.call(WriteUniqueVerify.java:167)        at org