blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Geospatial/Geolocation query results are not sorted by distance\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Geospatial (\'within\') query results are not sorted by distance.  We should sort by distance ascending by default.  This is now MongoDB handles the $near queries.Please add a test to confirm sorting is done correctly.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',238,'USERGRID-509','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-509\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Cardinality of the EntityCollectionManager is incorrect and may need refactored\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"An entity can only exist in a single scope. However this makes it impossible to batch fetch entities from multiple scopes in a single network request.  This interface needs changed.  Our EntityCollectionManagerFactory needs to change to return an EntityCollectionManager by ApplicationScope.  Further read/write requests would then need to take an encapsulating CollectionScope.  This would allow us to batch write and batch fetch multiple entities across different collections in a single request.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',239,'USERGRID-491','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-491\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 2, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Create app has stopped returning new apps\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 2, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 5, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"When creating a new app no error is returned.  However the app never appears in the portal.  Investigate and fix this issue.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 10, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',240,'USERGRID-448','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-448\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Remove redundant appinfos collections in ManagementServiceImpl\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"There is a flaw in the two-dot-o CpEntityManagerFactory.The factory stores a collection of \\\"appinfo\\\" type entities but the ManagementServiceImpl stores a redundant collection of \\\"application_info\\\" entities. The problem becomes evident when you try to delete an application. The application will only be deleted from the \\\"appinfos\\\" collection. When you call the management org/apps end-point you will still see the application because the end-point uses the \\\"application_infos\\\". To fix this:- Ensure that only one collection is stored- Add code to migrate the existing app information collections\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',241,'USERGRID-501','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-501\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Create migration strategy from multiple index to single indexes\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',242,'USERGRID-494','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-494\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"More than 10 apps will not be returned for organizations\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 3, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When we have more than 10 apps we cannot return them due to bugs in the PagingResults Iterator.  Refactor this to work correctly.  In the process we should also refactor the repair logic to work when reading connected entities as well as collections.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',243,'USERGRID-348','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-348\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Update ExportResourceIT to new REST test framework\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',244,'USERGRID-480','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-480\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Enable doc values in our index writes\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Aggregation with large data sets are causing memory pressure.  We need to enable doc values for faster aggregation especially when using SSD ES Nodshttp://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/guide/current/doc-values.html\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',245,'USERGRID-492','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-492\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"When a newer version of an entity appears before a previous version in candidate results it is not correctly removed\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The following use case causes lazy repair to fail.# Create entity with \\\"ordinal\\\":0# Update an entity with ordinal:1# Perform a \\\"select * order by ordinal desc\\\"The original version with ordinal 0 should be removed from the index.  It will not be in it\'s current implementation.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',246,'USERGRID-490','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-490\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Update index aliases to be created atomically\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently we move our index aliases in multiple steps.  This can lead to inconsistent alias state if fail during one of these operations.  Our alias operation should perform a single swap command.  We should perform the following during index allocation.# Create the target index successfully# Issue a single http call that will move the write alias and add the read alias to the new index per this HTTP command equivalent.http://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/indices-aliases.html#indices-aliases\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',247,'USERGRID-486','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-486\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Create a load testing framework for the query module\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need to create a simple stress testing framework for our query module to perform profiling of our indexing scheme.  We can do so easily with the following.Re-use our existing gattling cloud formation and usergrid cloud formationCreate integration tests that can have an overridden URL to elasticsearchRun these via maven and parallel ssh to get performance results.Use metrics to report throughput possibly to graphite so we can compare results.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',248,'USERGRID-493','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-493\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Refactor jersey resource calls in rest test framework to use generics.\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',249,'USERGRID-335','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-335\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Test Not Passing: CollectionsResourceIT\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',250,'USERGRID-341','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-341\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Fix BrowserCompatibilityTest\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',251,'USERGRID-414','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-414\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Set Build Version to Java 8\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 3, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We\'re significantly behind our in our RX java implementation.  Before work on the EM/RM refactor work starts we should upgrade to Java 8 to clean up our functional syntax as well as upgrade to the latest RxJava for performance improvements.We should evaluate missing functions we use in RX as Java 8 streams.  If we can re-create our operations as Java 8 streams we should evaluate the performance of RX Java vs Java 8 streams and pick the most performant solution.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',252,'USERGRID-345','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-345\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Fix RetrieveUsersTest\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',253,'USERGRID-338','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-338\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Fix OwnershipResourceIT\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Failing the contextualConnectionOwnership test everytime. The others pass.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',254,'USERGRID-347','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-347\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Fix AccessTokenIT\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',255,'USERGRID-483','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-483\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Change index structure to single index for many apps\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Change the index architecture - Right now you are using an index per client which is good for small number of clients but doesn\'t scale well especially considering that Elasticsearch doesn\'t handle large number of shards well. I need to analyze a few things that I have left and I will come up with a proposition of index architecture.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',256,'USERGRID-451','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-451\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade rx to latest version\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',257,'USERGRID-502','98','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-502\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 98, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Convert BasicIT over to new rest test framework\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Convert\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',258,'USERGRID-510','103','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-510\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 103, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Write/Review Test Framework Guide\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Task for writing up how the current REST test framework behaves and what expectations are for new tests.We should have 90 minutes web conf where we record how we go about doing the tests to review a \'good\' test a \'bad\' test and a test that is not on the current framework.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',259,'USERGRID-509','103','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-509\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 103, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Cardinality of the EntityCollectionManager is incorrect and may need refactored\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"An entity can only exist in a single scope. However this makes it impossible to batch fetch entities from multiple scopes in a single network request.  This interface needs changed.  Our EntityCollectionManagerFactory needs to change to return an EntityCollectionManager by ApplicationScope.  Further read/write requests would then need to take an encapsulating CollectionScope.  This would allow us to batch write and batch fetch multiple entities across different collections in a single request.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',260,'USERGRID-448','103','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-448\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 103, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Remove redundant appinfos collections in ManagementServiceImpl\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"There is a flaw in the two-dot-o CpEntityManagerFactory.The factory stores a collection of \\\"appinfo\\\" type entities but the ManagementServiceImpl stores a redundant collection of \\\"application_info\\\" entities. The problem becomes evident when you try to delete an application. The application will only be deleted from the \\\"appinfos\\\" collection. When you call the management org/apps end-point you will still see the application because the end-point uses the \\\"application_infos\\\". To fix this:- Ensure that only one collection is stored- Add code to migrate the existing app information collections\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',261,'USERGRID-511','103','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-511\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 103, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Refactor current collection and connection code to quickly fix our current read issues\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 3, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The refactor into our new functional framework is taking longer than anticipated.  We should quickly adapt our current 2.0 implementation to resolve this issue then fix it properly in the USERGRID-494 issue.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',262,'USERGRID-501','103','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-501\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 103, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Create migration strategy from multiple index to single indexes\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',263,'USERGRID-494','103','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-494\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 103, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"More than 10 apps will not be returned for organizations\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 3, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When we have more than 10 apps we cannot return them due to bugs in the PagingResults Iterator.  Refactor this to work correctly.  In the process we should also refactor the repair logic to work when reading connected entities as well as collections.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',264,'USERGRID-536','107','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-536\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 2, \"sprint\": 107, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Change our index structure for static mapping and cleanup api\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 2, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 3, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"Currently our dynamic mapping causes several issues with elastic search.  We should change our mapping to use a static structure and resolve this operational pain.We need to make the following changes.h2. Modify our IndexScopeThis should more closely resemble the elements of an edge since this represents an edge. It will simplify the use of our query module and make development clearer.  This scope should be refactored into the following objects.  * IndexEdge - Id name timestamp edgeType (source or target)* SearchEdge - Id name edgeTypeNote: edgeType is the type of the Id within the edge.  Does this Id represent a source Id or does it represent a targetId?  The entity to be indexed will implicitly be the opposite of the type specified.  I.E if it\'s a source edge the document is the target.  If it\'s a target edge the document is the source.These values should also be stored within our document so that we can index our documents.  Note that we perform bidirectional indexing in some cases such was users groups etc.  When we do this we need to ensure that mark the direction of the edge appropriately.h2. Change default sort orderingWhen sorting is unspecified we should order by timestamp descending from our index edge.  This ensures that we retain the correct edge time semantics and will properly order collections and connectionsh2. Remove the legacy query classWe don\'t need the Query class it has far too many functions to be a well encapsulated object.  Instead we should simply take the string QL the SearchEdge and the limit to return our candidates.  From there we should parse and visit the query internally to the query logic NOT externally.h2. Create a static mappingThe mapping should contains the following static fields.* entityId - The entity id* entityType - The entity type (from the id)* entityVersion - The entity version* edgeId - The edge Id* edgeName - The edge name* edgeTimestamp - The edge timestamp* edgeType - source | target* edgeSearch - edgeId + edgeName + edgeTypeIt will then contain an array of \\\"fields\\\"  Each of these fields will have the following formation.{code}{ \\\"name\\\":\\\"[entity field name as a path]\\\" \\\"[field type]\\\":[field value}{code}We will define a field type for each type of field.  Note that each field tuple will always contain a single field and a single value.  Possible field types are the following.* string - This will be mapped into 2 mapping with multi mappings.  It will be a string unanalyzed and an analyzed string.  The 2 fields will then be \\\"string_u\\\" and \\\"string_a\\\".  The Query visitor will need to update the field name appropriately* long - An unanalyzed long* double - An unanalyzed double* boolean - An unanalyzed boolean* location - A geolocation field* uuid - A UUID stored as an unanalyzed stringThe entity path will be a flattened path from the root json element to the max json element.  It can be though of as a path through the tree of json elements.  We will use a dot \'.\' to delimit the fields.  X.Y.Z for nested objects.  Primitive arrays will contain a field object for each element in the array.h2. Indexing  When indexing entities we will no longer modify or prefix field names.  They will be inserted into the value exactly as their path appears after lower case.h2. Querying  When querying the \\\"contains\\\" operation for a string will need to use the \\\"string_a\\\" data type.  When using = we will need to use the string_u data type.  Each criteria will need to use nested object querying to ensure the property name and property value are both part of the same field tuple.h3. ReferencesMulti Field Mapping: http://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/_multi_fields.htmlNested Objects: http://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/guide/current/nested-objects.htmlNested Object Search: http://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/guide/master/nested-sorting.html\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 10, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',265,'USERGRID-518','107','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-518\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 107, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Update copyright in footer of Portal to 2015\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',266,'USERGRID-342','107','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-342\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 107, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Fix AdminEmailEncodingIT\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',267,'USERGRID-336','107','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-336\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 107, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Fix ContentTypeResourceIT\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',268,'USERGRID-515','107','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-515\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 107, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"[SPIKE] Creating collections in the portal throws an error\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"The \'+\' button to create a collection in the UI does not work.  In Chrome dev tools it looks like it is doing a PUT to this URL: https://{host}/{org}/{app}/?access_token={token} with this request data: {\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"collections\\\":{\\\"foo\\\":{}}}}And the response looks like this:duration: 6er