 new Usergrid Central SSO so if it is to be deployed before Central SSO is enabled in prod then you will have to disable central SSO in the portal before deploying it.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',404,'USERGRID-610','126','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-610\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 126, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Core Tests...\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"write more stories\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',405,'USERGRID-677','126','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-677\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 126, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Create new parser for Scrolling api\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently we only do search results and parse those results under the assumption that we will only do one search. As we query elasticsearch we want to be able to use the scrolling api to batch pull all the results we can find from elasticsearch. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',406,'USERGRID-616','129','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-616\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 129, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Queries using greater/less than on float fields fail\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',407,'USERGRID-617','129','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-617\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 129, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Queries using order by on float fields result in incorrect ordering \", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',408,'USERGRID-652','129','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-652\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 129, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Index Routing/Location Strategy\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We should consider implementing a proxy which provides the index being used for an application.  This proxy should provide both the Index strategy and the entity type mapping strategy.The goal is to provide a point where we can implement a strategy function that could do one (or more) of the following strategies for indexes:- Single index per cluster (static index allocation)- Index per org/app (dynamic index allocation)- Index per org (dynamic index allocation)- Index per cluster (dynamic index allocation)- Index per customer (dynamic index allocation)- Hash/bucketing across a fixed range of indexes (static index allocation)- Per environment (TBD)- Static (for the management app should always match the Cassandra keyspace name as the index)In order to do this we need to update EntityIndexFactory.createApplicationEntityIndex.For Entity Type Mapping the goal is to enable bucketing of entity types (collections) in a manner that can be more optimal for the indexing strategy that is chosen.  For example a single index strategy might have a single entity type but for the index per org/app it might have a separate entity type.  Looking up the management index would have a strategy where the index name matches the cassandra keyspace name\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',409,'USERGRID-698','129','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-698\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 129, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Test Not Passing: ConnectionResourceTest.connectionsLoopbackTest:103 NullPointer\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',410,'USERGRID-618','129','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-618\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 129, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Additional testing of Usergrid SSO\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',411,'USERGRID-678','129','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-678\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 129, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"ElasticSearch Type Mapping has _all in wrong place\", \"assignee\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey