e:this.deleteApplicationMeter = metricsFactory.getMeter(EsApplicationEntityIndexImpl.class \\\"application.delete\\\");https://github.com/apache/incubator-usergrid/pull/269\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',462,'USERGRID-729','133','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-729\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 133, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"SNS Queue Manager uses ARN to read instead of URL\", \"assignee\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"There is a bug in org.apache.usergrid.persistence.queue.impl.SNSQueueManagerImpl which results in the ARN of the queue being used when the URL should be used.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',463,'USERGRID-473','133','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-473\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 133, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Add Dead Letter Queue\", \"assignee\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',464,'USERGRID-740','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-740\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Temp files from asset upload not removed causing the file system to use all inodes\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"After running Usergrid 2.0 for over 1 month on a tomcat we have saturated the inodes of the disk on the tomcat machine.  Our temporary files for uploads are not getting removed.  Files of this structure appear in {code} ls -lrt  /var/cache/tomcat7/temp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME377627531473294092.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME2634951521985073318.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME1066361445384372180.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME3554741621747313255.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME1805372544199883785.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME414525331725926400.tmp{code}We need to ensure that all temporary files are removed.  Note that all the files remaining are 0 bytes.  This seems to be caused by an edge case when a 0 byte file is uploaded or possibly the upload is failing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',465,'USERGRID-724','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-724\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"JMX Metrics/Counters for Cassandra\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Would be nice to add metrics and counters at the lower level for bytes in/out Cassandra and latency\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',466,'USERGRID-586','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-586\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Test app_info migration\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',467,'USERGRID-701','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-701\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Rewrite Registration tests to fully cover the registration flow.\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The current set of tests have very few comments and don\'t logically make sense in some cases. We need more tests to expose the registration flow and possible edge cases when certain properties aren\'t correctly set. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 2}'),('UserGrid',468,'USERGRID-750','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-750\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Brandon Shelley\", \"summary\": \"When setting accesstokenttl to 0 client credentials auth still returns 604800\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Brandon Shelley\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"If I send a PUT request to set the accesstokenttl to 0 for an app:{code}{    \\\"accesstokenttl\\\": 0}{code}And then make a subsequent client_credentials token request the token ttl in the response is still 604800:{code}{    \\\"client_id\\\": \\\"***\\\"    \\\"client_secret\\\": \\\"***\\\"    \\\"grant_type\\\": \\\"client_credentials\\\"    \\\"ttl\\\": 0}{code}Response: {code}{    \\\"access_token\\\": \\\"***\\\"    \\\"expires_in\\\": 604800    \\\"application\\\": \\\"***\\\"}{code}[~tnine] suggests this may be a response rendering problem and that it is actually setting the expiration correctly in the stack.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',469,'USERGRID-670','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-670\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"App Credentials do not work when accessing a collection within an app (2.0)\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"In order to access collections it seems the org credentials are required as app credentials do not work.  \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 7, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',470,'USERGRID-755','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-755\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"MVCC serialization error on reindex\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"2015-06-16 22:06:31223 [http-bio-8080-exec-15] ERROR org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.serialization.impl.MvccLogEntrySerializationStrategyImpl- DATA CORRUPTION DETECTED when de-serializing entity with Id SimpleId{uuid=2034290e-109c-11e5-a3f5-06b0ee5388b2 type=\'user\'}.  This means the write was truncated.org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.exception.DataCorruptionException: Unable to read entity dataat org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.serialization.impl.MvccEntitySerializationStrategyV3Impl$EntitySerializer.fromByteBuffer(MvccEntitySerializationStrategyV3Impl.java:457)at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.co