\"USERGRID-745\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Test Not Passing: AssetResourceIT\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',482,'USERGRID-719','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-719\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Pushy creates/leaves too many threads \", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Pushy client opens up hundreds of threads and has some failed connection alerts which need to be investigated.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',483,'USERGRID-751','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-751\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Change MvccEntitySerializationStrategyV3Impl to use native JSON when storing in the column value\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Currently we use SMILE binary serialization to serialize our column values.  During production debugging this makes it extremely difficult to debug.  I propose we remove the SMILE binary serialization and instead use json serialization with the following formation{code}{  \\\"version\\\": [serialization implementation version number as an int]  \\\"entity\\\": {... entity as a nested json object }}{code}If the entity is present then the entity has not been deleted.  If the entity field is not present then the entity should be read as a marked for deletion.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',484,'USERGRID-704','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-704\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Test Not Passing: DevicesresourceIT \", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"seems to be a graph compaction issue DevicesResourceIT.putWithUUIDShouldCreateAfterDelete\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',485,'USERGRID-757','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-757\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Exception on system/database/setup\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"throws duplicate unique key exception on managementserviceimpl\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',486,'USERGRID-604','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-604\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Spike: Core test suite should complete in Maven\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',487,'USERGRID-527','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-527\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Write external ES test to ensure we get even routing across the ES cluster\", \"assignee\": \"Senthil Kumar K\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"One of the problems we have faced is uneven distribution in the ES cluster.  We have made changes for document routing that seemed to help but we are still getting hot nodes in the cluster.  We need to have a test that hits ES directly with load as UG would do to test our cluster distribution.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 7, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',488,'USERGRID-739','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-739\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Implement Bucketing Algorithm for assignment of Application Index Aliases to Physical Indexes\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"When allocating an index alias to one of the physical indexes a bucketing strategy should be used with ranges based off the number of indexes in elasticsearch.For example if there are 10 physical indexes then there would be 10 buckets based on a hash of the Application ID which would result in the assignment of an app alias to a physical index based on the range in which it falls.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',489,'USERGRID-747','138','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-747\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 138, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Error with Push Queue on 2.1\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"2015-06-11 19:56:06334 [Notifications_Processor8a95f9c7-30e2-4ebe-9a87-62deb1f131c9] ERROR org.apache.usergrid.services.notifications.QueueListener- failed to start pushjava.util.NoSuchElementException: Sequence contains no elementsat rx.internal.operators.OperatorSingle$ParentSubscriber.onCompleted(OperatorSingle.java:116)at rx.internal.operators.NotificationLite.accept(NotificationLite.java:140)at rx.internal.operators.TakeLastQueueProducer.emit(TakeLastQueueProducer.java:100)at rx.internal.operators.TakeLastQueueProducer.startEmitting(TakeLastQueueProducer.java:45)at rx.internal.operators.OperatorTakeLast$1.onCompleted(OperatorTakeLast.java:59)at rx.internal.operators.OperatorDoOnEach$1.onCompleted(OperatorDoOnEach.java:53)at rx.internal.operators.OperatorBufferWithSize$1.onCompleted(OperatorBufferWithSize.java:125)at rx.internal.operators.OnSubscribeFromIterable$IterableProducer.request(OnSubscribeFromIterable.java:79)at rx.internal.operators.OperatorBufferWithSize$1$1.request(OperatorBufferWithSize.java:86)at rx.Subscriber.setProducer(Subscriber.java:177)at rx.Subscriber.setProducer(Subscriber.java:171)at rx.internal.operators.OperatorBufferWithSize$1.setProducer(OperatorBufferWithSize.java:74)at rx.internal.operators.OnSubscribeFromIterable.call(OnSubscribeFromIterable.java:47)at rx.internal.operators.OnSubscribeFromIterable.call(OnSubscribeFromIterable.java:33)at rx.Observable$1.call(Observable.java:144)at rx.Observable$1.call(Observable.java:136)at rx.Observable$1.call(Observable.