s\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We are seeing a large number of fetches/queries when we are doing PUT by name.  This creates load on ES and therefore makes indexing take longer.  We should make sure we\'re not hitting ES for PUT by name.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',491,'USERGRID-716','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-716\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"ryan bridges\", \"summary\": \"Use combo boxes instead of text areas for inputting multiple pieces of data\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"ryan bridges\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',492,'USERGRID-764','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-764\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Instance Validation Script\", \"assignee\": \"Brandon Shelley\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need a script which does testing of a Usergrid instance to confirm a set of functionality works.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',493,'USERGRID-586','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-586\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Test app_info migration\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',494,'USERGRID-681','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-681\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Support single-region delivery of messages in 2.1\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 0.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"With the introduction of SNS and the default configuration of multi-region push notifications will be sent once-per-region.  We need the queue interface to be updated to support single-region delivery.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',495,'USERGRID-752','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-752\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Update Usergrid 1.0 search to use concurrent search per shard\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently we merge all shards together with every page seek in usergrid 1.0. This means we select 20k columns and discard 19k with each page selection.  Instead I propose that we create an AST per shard and execute the iterator on these shards concurrently.  We then merge on the last step greatly reducing the amount of network I/O and discarded data on queries of large data sets.Proposed Changes:1 AST instance per shard evaluated concurrently via some worker pool.Change final gather of concurrent iterators.Change cursor generation to create the cursor from the merged trees.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',496,'USERGRID-732','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-732\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Implement SNS-based Queue Provider in 2.0\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',497,'USERGRID-750','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-750\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Brandon Shelley\", \"summary\": \"When setting accesstokenttl to 0 client credentials auth still returns 604800\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Brandon Shelley\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"If I send a PUT request to set the accesstokenttl to 0 for an app:{code}{    \\\"accesstokenttl\\\": 0}{code}And then make a subsequent client_credentials token request the token ttl in the response is still 604800:{code}{    \\\"client_id\\\": \\\"***\\\"    \\\"client_secret\\\": \\\"***\\\"    \\\"grant_type\\\": \\\"client_credentials\\\"    \\\"ttl\\\": 0}{code}Response: {code}{    \\\"access_token\\\": \\\"***\\\"    \\\"expires_in\\\": 604800    \\\"application\\\": \\\"***\\\"}{code}[~tnine] suggests this may be a response rendering problem and that it is actually setting the expiration correctly in the stack.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',498,'USERGRID-670','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-670\", \"votes\": 0, \"