0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"SNS Topic/Queue Implementation should use the Topics.subscribe helper methid\", \"assignee\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"There is a helper method which should be used to subscribe SQS queues to SNS topics.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',503,'USERGRID-758','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-758\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Introduce Semantic Versioning in Build Artifacts\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"We should include in the WAR manifests a version number to be able to identify a version of a build and which branch it belongs to.  For example right now we have 1.0 2.0 and 2.1 branches and nothing about the artifact filenames differentiates them.  This results to mistakes and builds of the wrong version getting deployed and mistaken.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',504,'USERGRID-708','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-708\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"ryan bridges\", \"summary\": \"cursor in username field on login jumps to the end with update\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"ryan bridges\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',505,'USERGRID-228','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-228\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"summary\": \"Portal should not give username/password error when error was due to some other problem\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Sometimes when Usergrid starts it errors gracefully if one of the ports is in use (7000) sometimes it gives a timeout (8080) and sometimes it works (8080) even though the port is used but then when you try the portal it tells you the username/password was not valid when in fact the error is a 501 on ΓÇÿOPTIONSΓÇÖ though it could be a different error depending on what is already using the port (screenshot below).  This same behavior happens if the port cannot be reached.  So the questions are:1) Can we configure all the different ports using the Launcher JAR?  Including Cassandra?2) Can we update the portal to display something other than invalid user/name when this happens?\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',506,'USERGRID-615','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-615\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Inaccurate (or lack of) error message when logging into BaaS\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"In some cases the following error is uncaught and the portal fails to load:Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property \'applications\' of undefinedUsergrid.Client.parseApplicationsArray @ usergrid-libs.min.js:14(anonymous function) @ usergrid-libs.min.js:14Usergrid.Client.request.xhr.onload @ usergrid-libs.min.js:13\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',507,'USERGRID-760','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-760\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Merge master to two-dot-o branches & rewrite tests to use new framework\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"There\'s one new test from master that needs to be rewritten using the new framework: ApplicationResourceIT.applicationCollectionWithAppToken()\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',508,'USERGRID-703','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-703\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Test Not Passing: ManagementResourceIT\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"testSuperuserOnlyWhenValidateExternalTokensEnabledand the other external test are broken.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 7, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',509,'USERGRID-667','140','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-667\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 140, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"1.0.2 Release Candidate 2\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0