b63a11d83adca56839d8b409cca.For example limit=2 gives you 1 sometimes limit=750 gives anywhere from 625 to 749.  For example this script:{code}#!/bin/bashfor count in `seq 1 10`do     curl -s \\\"https://example.com/appservices/testorg/sandbox/scmocks?limit=750\\\" > file${count}    grep uuid file${count} | wc    rm file${count}done{code}Produces these results:     685    2055   36305     750    2250   39750     749    2247   39697     742    2226   39326     750    2250   39750     749    2247   39697     747    2241   39591     744    2232   39432     750    2250   39750     749    2247   39697A different count every time.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',524,'USERGRID-752','146','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-752\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 146, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Update Usergrid 1.0 search to use concurrent search per shard\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently we merge all shards together with every page seek in usergrid 1.0. This means we select 20k columns and discard 19k with each page selection.  Instead I propose that we create an AST per shard and execute the iterator on these shards concurrently.  We then merge on the last step greatly reducing the amount of network I/O and discarded data on queries of large data sets.Proposed Changes:1 AST instance per shard evaluated concurrently via some worker pool.Change final gather of concurrent iterators.Change cursor generation to create the cursor from the merged trees.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',525,'USERGRID-732','146','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-732\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 146, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Implement SNS-based Queue Provider in 2.0\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',526,'USERGRID-706','146','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-706\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 146, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Test re-index system\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The first pass of the re-index with is complete.  Testing in a system to ensure that re-index works as expected still needs to be completed.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',527,'USERGRID-555','146','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-555\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 146, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Test Migration of Entity Versions\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Test migration from v2 to v3 for the upcoming release\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',528,'USERGRID-585','146','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-585\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 146, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Test migration from old index format to new\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Test migration from old index format to new\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',529,'USERGRID-765','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-765\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Validate JMX Meters / Timers are the ones we want to be in place for measuring/monitoring performance\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Validate JMS Meters / Timers are the ones we want to be in place for measuring/monitoring performance\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',530,'USERGRID-772','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-772\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Characterize the performance of 2.1\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need to characterize the performance of 2.1.  This will involve using:- Varying numbers of tomcats-- we can start with 20 and progressively add more into a load balancer to see the performance impact- Varying ES cluster size - starting with 6 and going up to 20-- we can start with 20 nodes and only have the indexes targeted to a subset- Varying ES bucket/shard counts - starting with 10- Varying Cassandra sizes - starting with 6 and going up to 12General approach should be:1) Start with 2 tomcats 6 ES and 6 C*2) Add +2 Tomcats iteratively until the performance starts to not increase (implying that either ES or C* is the limiting factor)3) Add +3 ES nodes and test again.  Document impact.4) Add +3 C* nodes remove -3 ES nodes and test again.  Document impact.5) Add +3 C* nodes and +3 ES nodes and test again.  Document impact.6) Add +2 Tomcats and see the slope of the TPS graph7) Add +3 C* - (now at 12) and test again8) Test iteratively with +2 Tomcats until performance plateaus up to 20 Tomcats\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',531,'USERGRID-716','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-716\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"ryan bridges\", \"summary\": \"Use combo boxes instead of text areas for inputting multiple pieces of data\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"ryan bridges\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',532,'USERGRID-869','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-869\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Asset creation when using S3BinaryStore doesn\'t function\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When creating an asset the following call works in 1.0 usergrid.curl -X POST -F name=\'example\' -F file=@example.jpg \'https://localhost:8080/temp/test?access_token=<token>\'properly uploading the asset. In 2.1 however the following gets returned. {\\\"error\\\":\\\"uncaught\\\"\\\"timestamp\\\":1437415007666\\\"duration\\\":0\\\"error_description\\\":\\\"Internal Server Error\\\"\\\"exception\\\":\\\"org.apache.usergrid.rest.exceptions.UncaughtException\\\"\\\"error_id\\\":\\\"b0c5930c-2f08-11e5-818e-060beb1b9051\\\"}%\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',533,'USERGRID-771','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-771\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Add a separate email address for approving new Org Admin users which can be different from approving new Orgs\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Currently the email address appears to be the same for approving new orgs and new admins.  We need a separate configurable email address for each.If this setting is blank the admin email can be used instead.This needs to be fixed in 2.0 as well as 2.1.  2.0 first please :)\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',534,'USERGRID-740','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-740\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Temp files from asset upload not removed causing the file system to use all inodes\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"After running Usergrid 2.0 for over 1 month on a tomcat we have saturated the inodes of the disk on the tomcat machine.  Our temporary files for uploads are not getting removed.  Files of this structure appear in {code} ls -lrt  /var/cache/tomcat7/temp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME377627531473294092.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME2634951521985073318.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME1066361445384372180.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME3554741621747313255.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME1805372544199883785.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME414525331725926400.tmp{code}We need to ensure that all temporary files are removed.  Note that all the files remaining are 0 bytes.  This seems to be caused by an edge case when a 0 byte file is uploaded or possibly the upload is failing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',535,'USERGRID-724','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-724\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"JMX Metrics/Counters for Cassandra\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Would be nice to add metrics and counters at the lower level for bytes in/out Cassandra and latency\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',536,'USERGRID-764','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-764\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Instance Validation Script\", \"assignee\": \"Brandon Shelley\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need a script which does testing of a Usergrid instance to confirm a set of functionality works.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',537,'USERGRID-778','152','{\"key\": \"