\"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',542,'USERGRID-534','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-534\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \" Load Test with 2.1\", \"assignee\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Test load with the frankenloader in e2e for the upcoming release\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',543,'USERGRID-860','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-860\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"QL for contains \'text*\' does not appear to work\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"select * where title contains \'ta*\' does not work (at all) as documented here:http://apigee.com/docs/app-services/content/working-queries\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',544,'USERGRID-840','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-840\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Complete Multi Region ES management implementation\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When indexes are created on setup as well as aliases assigned on application creation this is only performed in the local region.  We need to create indexes in all regions during an index administration operation as well as create aliases. We will also probably want to make our aliases and underlying indexes identical in order to allow for ease of administration regardless of region.We need to account for two cases:1) Secondary region does not already have ES indexes configured - need to create the indexes and aliases2) Secondary region already has ES installed and configured (indexes existing) - only need to create aliases\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',545,'USERGRID-788','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-788\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"New ExportApp tool\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Provide new tool that exports an app:1. Writes two types of files: entities and connections2. Each line of output files will be one complete JSON object3. Use RxJava for multithreading of reads and of writes\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',546,'USERGRID-851','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-851\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"ImportAdmins tool should merge organizations of duplicate users\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Some older Usergrid systems may have multiple accounts with the same username or email address something which is not allowed and problematic now. When such users are imported into a new system by the ImportAdmins program we can \\\"repair\\\" such users by merging the duplicates and ensure that the resulting single user account has the union of organization in the one or more duplicate users.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',547,'USERGRID-596','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-596\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Confirm PUT by Name Does not Fetch/Query ES\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We are seeing a large number of fetches/queries when we are doing PUT by name.  This creates load on ES and therefore makes indexing take longer.  We should make sure we\'re not hitting ES for PUT by name.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',548,'USERGRID-854','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-854\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"[SPIKE] Look at \'Fix X test\' and close if needed\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',549,'USERGRID-861','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-861\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Test and Profile performance of ExportApp tool\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"This tool is designed to export from 1.0 with the intent of using the resulting entities and collections in 2.x and higher.  However this data will be imported using the API so it is not import-to-2.x specific.\", \"fixVersions\": 2, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',550,'USERGRID-870','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-870\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Inconsistent results returned while adding another data center to the Cassandra cluster.\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"During the addition of a new data center to the Cassandra cluster being used by Usergrid 2.1 inconsistent results were returned:-no entities in response-unable to find application\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',551,'USERGRID-754','152','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-754\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 152, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"External Set of REST Tests that confirms Usergrid functionality in an execution environment\", \"assignee\": \"Brandon Shelley\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need a script which executes API calls to test an installation given a set of test cases to confirm that it \'works\' with a bare minimum of functionality.- CRUD on entity- Query entities - CRUD on connectionsAdd queries from here: http://apigee.com/docs/app-services/content/working-queries as test cases.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',552,'USERGRID-765','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-765\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Validate JMX Meters / Timers are the ones we want to be in place for measuring/monitoring performance\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Validate JMS Meters / Timers are the ones we want to be in place for measuring/monitoring performance\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',553,'USERGRID-772','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-772\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Characterize the performance of 2.1\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need to characterize the performance of 2.1.  This will involve using:- Varying numbers of tomcats-- we can start with 20 and progressively add more into a load balancer to see the performance impact- Varying ES cluster size - starting with 6 and going up to 20-- we can start with 20 nodes and only have the indexes targeted to a subset- Varying ES bucket/shard counts - starting with 10- Varying Cassandra sizes - starting with 6 and going up to 12General approach should be:1) Start with 2 tomcats 6 ES and 6 C*2) Add +2 Tomcats iteratively until the performance starts to not increase (implying that either ES or C* is the limiting factor)3) Add +3 ES nodes and test again.  Document impact.4) Add +3 C* nodes remove -3 ES nodes and test again.  Document impact.5) Add +3 C* nodes and +3 ES nodes and test again.  Document impact.6) Add +2 Tomcats and see the slope of the TPS graph7) Add +3 C* - (now at 12) and test again8) Test iteratively with +2 Tomcats until performance plateaus up to 20 Tomcats\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',554,'USERGRID-875','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-875\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Test and Validate Multi-Region Indexing\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"1) Ensure that the indexes (including buckets) can get created in region n+12) Ensure that read/write aliases get created in region n+13) Ensure that queries in both regions return the same data4) Attempt to quantify the latency of a PUT in region A making it to Region B and being indexed in region BComing out of this we need a guide for setting up region N+1\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',555,'USERGRID-882','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-882\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Release 2.0 with Admin email fixes\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',556,'USERGRID-831','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-831\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Confirm 2.1 LICENSE file has requisite versions and module names\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',557,'USERGRID-716','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-716\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"ryan bridges\", \"summary\": \"Use combo boxes instead of text areas for inputting multiple pieces of data\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"ryan bridges\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',558,'USERGRID-869','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-869\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Asset creation when using S3BinaryStore doesn\'t function\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When creating an asset the following call works in 1.0 usergrid.curl -X POST -F name=\'example\' -F file=@example.jpg \'https://localhost:8080/temp/test?access_token=<token>\'properly uploading the asset. In 2.1 however the following gets returned. {\\\"error\\\":\\\"uncaught\\\"\\\"timestamp\\\":1437415007666\\\"duration\\\":0\\\"error_description\\\":\\\"Internal Server Error\\\"\\\"exception\\\":\\\"org.apache.usergrid.rest.exceptions.UncaughtException\\\"\\\"error_id\\\":\\\"b0c5930c-2f08-11e5-818e-060beb1b9051\\\"}%\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',559,'USERGRID-771','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-771\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Add a separate email address for approving new Org Admin users which can be different from approving new Orgs\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Currently the email address appears to be the same for approving new orgs and new admins.  We need a separate configurable email address for each.If this setting is blank the admin email can be used instead.This needs to be fixed in 2.0 as well as 2.1.  2.0 first please :)\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',560,'USERGRID-740','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-740\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Temp files from asset upload not removed causing the file system to use all inodes\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"After running Usergrid 2.0 for over 1 month on a tomcat we have saturated the inodes of the disk on the tomcat machine.  Our temporary files for uploads are not getting removed.  Files of this structure appear in {code} ls -lrt  /var/cache/tomcat7/temp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME377627531473294092.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME2634951521985073318.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME1066361445384372180.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME3554741621747313255.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME1805372544199883785.tmp-rw-r--r-- 1 tomcat tomcat 0 Jun  9 23:23 MIME414525331725926400.tmp{code}We need to ensure that all temporary files are removed.  Note that all the files remaining are 0 bytes.  This seems to be caused by an edge case when a 0 byte file is uploaded or possibly the upload is failing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',561,'USERGRID-778','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-778\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Limit on Queries results in a highly variable number of results\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"This behavior is observed on a build from the two-dot-o branch with commit ID 2d1c8b8ac7b20b63a11d83adca56839d8b409cca.For example limit=2 gives you 1 sometimes limit=750 gives anywhere from 625 to 749.  For example this script:{code}#!/bin/bashfor count in `seq 1 10`do     curl -s \\\"https://example.com/appservices/testorg/sandbox/scmocks?limit=750\\\" > file${count}    grep uuid file${count} | wc    rm file${count}done{code}Produces these results:     685    2055   36305     750    2250   39750     749    2247   39697     742    2226   39326     750    2250   39750     749    2247   39697     747    2241   39591     744    2232   39432     750    2250   39750     749    2247   39697A different count every time.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',562,'USERGRID-752','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-752\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Update Usergrid 1.0 search to use concurrent search per shard\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently we merge all shards together with every page seek in usergrid 1.0. This means we select 20k columns and discard 19k with each page selection.  Instead I propose that we create an AST per shard and execute the iterator on these shards concurrently.  We then merge on the last step greatly reducing the amount of network I/O and discarded data on queries of large data sets.Proposed Changes:1 AST instance per shard evaluated concurrently via some worker pool.Change final gather of concurrent iterators.Change cursor generation to create the cursor from the merged trees.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',563,'USERGRID-682','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-682\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Soak Testing Scripts\", \"assignee\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Create scripts that will run for a period of time and generate data/load.  Start scripts and run for a week.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',564,'USERGRID-833','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-833\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Implement script for configuring Grafana dashboards based on new JMX counters\", \"assignee\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\