\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"SQS Queue Manager should be updated to use Observable and emit a stream of messages.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',570,'USERGRID-469','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-469\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"[FIXED?] Investigate using a new TimeUUID as our routing value\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We have been using our entityId as our routing value.  This gives us a much better distribution than our documentId format.  However when a node will be heavily connected it will introduce a hotspot in our ES cluster.  Instead we should either route based a new time UUID a new time uuid just for routing.  This way we can put each de-normalized document on it\'s own shard regardless of collection membership or connections.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',571,'USERGRID-874','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-874\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"[SPIKE] Review Usergrid Documentation\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need to make sure docs are updated for 2.1\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',572,'USERGRID-877','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-877\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Start Usergrid graduation process\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"1. update status page to include all users2. create DRAFT Top Level Project resolution3. start discussion on dev list\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',573,'USERGRID-598','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-598\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Merge two-dot-o-dev into two-dot-o\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 2, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',574,'USERGRID-878','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-878\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Investigate Serialization issue for Notifications\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',575,'USERGRID-880','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-880\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Refactor Serialization in Core and move it down to corepersistence\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"move all serialization down to low levels\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',576,'USERGRID-754','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-754\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"External Set of REST Tests that confirms Usergrid functionality in an execution environment\", \"assignee\": \"Brandon Shelley\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need a script which executes API calls to test an installation given a set of test cases to confirm that it \'works\' with a bare minimum of functionality.- CRUD on entity- Query entities - CRUD on connectionsAdd queries from here: http://apigee.com/docs/app-services/content/working-queries as test cases.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',577,'USERGRID-558','153','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-558\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 153, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"[FIXED?] Add resume to entity migration\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need to build resume into entity migration.  To do this we should make the AllEntitiesObservable allow for resume by default.  This way if the node performing the migration fails it can be restarted on another node.Note that we also need a way to clear state via REST so that we can restart our migration.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',578,'USERGRID-765','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-765\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Validate JMX Meters / Timers are the ones we want to be in place for measuring/monitoring performance\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Validate JMS Meters / Timers are the ones we want to be in place for measuring/monitoring performance\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',579,'USERGRID-772','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-772\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Characterize the performance of 2.1\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need to characterize the performance of 2.1.  This will involve using:- Varying numbers of tomcats-- we can start with 20 and progressively add more into a load balancer to see the performance impact- Varying ES cluster size - starting with 6 and going up to 20-- we can start with 20 nodes and only have the indexes targeted to a subset- Varying ES bucket/shard counts - starting with 10- Varying Cassandra sizes - starting with 6 and going up to 12General approach should be:1) Start with 2 tomcats 6 ES and 6 C*2) Add +2 Tomcats iteratively until the performance starts to not increase (implying that either ES or C* is the limiting factor)3) Add +3 ES nodes and test again.  Document impact.4) Add +3 C* nodes remove -3 ES nodes and test again.  Document impact.5) Add +3 C* nodes and +3 ES nodes and test again.  Document impact.6) Add +2 Tomcats and see the slope of the TPS graph7) Add +3 C* - (now at 12) and test again8) Test iteratively with +2 Tomcats until performance plateaus up to 20 Tomcats\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',580,'USERGRID-875','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-875\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Test and Validate Multi-Region Indexing\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"1) Ensure that the indexes (including buckets) can get created in region n+12) Ensure that read/write aliases get created in region n+13) Ensure that queries in both regions return the same data4) Attempt to quantify the latency of a PUT in region A making it to Region B and being indexed in region BComing out of this we need a guide for setting up region N+1\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',581,'USERGRID-882','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-882\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Release 2.0 with Admin email fixes\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',582,'USERGRID-831','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-831\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Confirm 2.1 LICENSE file has requisite versions and module names\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',583,'USERGRID-216','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-216\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Strong Liu\", \"summary\": \"GET an non-exists entity by ID or Name throws 401 if no authorisation is required\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Strong Liu\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"for exampleget /sandbox/users/non-exist-username throws 401 error codethis is because below code{code}@Providerpublic class ServiceResourceNotFoundExceptionMapper extends AbstractExceptionMapper<ServiceResourceNotFoundException> {    @Override    public Response toResponse( ServiceResourceNotFoundException e ) {        if ( SubjectUtils.getSubjectUserId() == null ) {            return toResponse( UNAUTHORIZED e );        }        else {            return toResponse( NOT_FOUND e );        }    }}{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',584,'USERGRID-411','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-411\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"[FIXED?] Fix default index routing rules\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"When allocating indexes we\'ve seen issues with unbalanced shard allocation within our cluster.  To get around this we need to set the following setting in each index.  http://www.elasticsearch.org/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/index-modules-allocation.html#_total_shards_per_nodeWe should allow this to be a configurable value via properties.  During new index allocation we\'ll also need to take this parameter in the payload of index allocation. We need to document this to be set asmax shards = # primaries + (# primaries * replicas) / number of nodes\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',585,'USERGRID-559','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-559\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"[FIXED?] Add re-index resume\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need the ability to resume re-indexing.  To do this we should make the AllEntitiesObservable allow for resume by default.  This way if the node performing the migration fails it can be restarted on another node.Note that we also need a way to clear state via REST so that we can restart our indexing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',586,'USERGRID-370','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-370\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"[FIXED?] Use ElasticSearch Filters instead of Term Query for exact matches\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"This is something recommended in the O\'Reilly ElasticSearch book.\\\"For exact value searches you probably want to use a filter instead of a query as a filter will be cached.\\\"Page 107 Chapter 7 \\\"Full Body Search\\\"\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',587,'USERGRID-457','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-457\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"summary\": \"Content length headers are not being sent on POSTS for ping identity\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 9, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',588,'USERGRID-560','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-560\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Ensure USERGRID-530 is addressed in two-dot-o(-dev)\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/USERGRID-530.  Make sure it gets in 2.0\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',589,'USERGRID-898','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-898\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Add proper error checking to Asset Code along with error checking tests.\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnB