 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Validate migrate_entity_data script produces consistent migrations.\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Validate that https://github.com/apache/incubator-usergrid/blob/two-dot-o-dev/stack/scripts/migrate_entity_data.py produces consistent entity data migrations. 1) put data into UG build from latest in two-dot-o2) stand up UG build from two-dot-o-dev pointing to same keyspace (different queue names) and run /system/database/setup3) from UG running two-dot-o-dev run migrate_entity_data.py4) read data from UG two-dot-4) once finished  read entities from UG two-dot-o and UG two-dot-o-dev and ensure there is an exact match\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',597,'USERGRID-900','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-900\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Re-index using AmazonAsyncEventService should support updated date\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"see implemented example for InMemoryAsyncEventServiceorg/apache/usergrid/corepersistence/asyncevents/EventBuilderImpl.java:166This filters out based on modified/updated date for the events to be indexed.  Need to ensure AmazonAsyncEventService consumers implement something similar OR look to have the producer filter out the events and not even drop on the AWS queues.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',598,'USERGRID-907','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-907\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Batch interval in seconds not honored\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The following property is present in the configuration of counter batch submits.{code}usergrid.counter.batch.interval=30{code}This is not honored.  This needs fixed in the 2.0 and 2.1 branch.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',599,'USERGRID-543','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-543\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Add Queue Length to /status page\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Add queue length (SQS akka etc.) to the data returned by /status\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',600,'USERGRID-558','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-558\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"[FIXED?] Add resume to entity migration\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need to build resume into entity migration.  To do this we should make the AllEntitiesObservable allow for resume by default.  This way if the node performing the migration fails it can be restarted on another node.Note that we also need a way to clear state via REST so that we can restart our migration.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',601,'USERGRID-908','157','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-908\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 157, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"run specific migration\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',602,'USERGRID-103','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-103\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Strong Liu\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade to latest Jersey 2.x release\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Strong Liu\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 8, \"description\": \"JAX-RS 2.0 brings lots of new features much better extensible and async support are ones I think most useful \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 17, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',603,'USERGRID-941','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-941\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Spike: Investigate using Java Annotations to generate Swagger\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',604,'USERGRID-909','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-909\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Evaluate removing cache from edge shard management\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently using caches with the proposal phase for new shards has caused large numbers of tombstones.  Review the algorithm and determine the cause of the additional shard proposals.Usergrid currently performs 5 shard lookups on write and most miss the cache.  We\'ll change the following*Shard allocation*Shard allocation will not perform a propose + check phase. The following algorithm will occur.  This must occur at EACH_QUORUM to ensure that we have consensus across regions.  Any node will propose a new shard pivot.  This pivot will have compacted set to false and will have a column timestamp of a new timeuuid in microsThe proposing node will then read back all compacted = false shard pivots.  The shard pivot with the minimum timestamp will be retained all others will be deleted as proposals.  This will function similarly to distributed read locks in Cassandra.  Lowest proposed value always wins. Allocation is complete*Shard compaction*After a successful proposal allocation the allocating node will copy all edges from the previously compacted shard into the new shard.  It will continue to copy until no new edges are returned on read.Once read has been completed all edges that were copied can be deleted from the previous shard.  This target shard will be marked as compacted*Consistency*When performing consistency we will need a higher consistency level.  To ensure that shards exist worldwide proposal + selection should occur at EACH_QUORUM.  Standard reads can occur as LOCAL_QUORUM\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',605,'USERGRID-944','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-944\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Prototype using Spark to perform functions on data in Cassandra\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"As we discussed we\'d like to see about using Spark for things such as:1) migrating orgs from one keyspace to another2) deleting all records for an app from Cassandra\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',606,'USERGRID-950','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-950\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Remove Cassandra Keyspace name from Index Naming Strategy\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',607,'USERGRID-918','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-918\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Add qparam to skip retrieving metadata and graph edges\", \"assignee\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"If the qparam is not there use current/default behavior.  If the qparam is there then skip pulling the extra data which will result in better performance.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',608,'USERGRID-929','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-929\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Test the creation of entities which have an OldUUID to migrate from 1.0 to 2.1\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',609,'USERGRID-816','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-816\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Implement the ability to track the storage used by an app\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Depends on counters getting fixed\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',610,'USERGRID-545','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-545\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Endpoint for checking storage consumed\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"As we move to separate keyspaces for each tenant we need to have an endpoint to monitor storage consumed for the keyspace.  This will be followed by the ability to show data consumed in the console and notifications when storage consumed is at X%.1. add size to entities2. add size to index.3. migrate field mapping in index4. add endpoint for getting storage by appapi is management/orgs/orgname/applications/appname/sizeor management/orgs/orgname/applications/appname/size/collectionName\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 5, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',611,'USERGRID-912','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-912\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade Shiro to be current version\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"In order to support NIO.  Current version is ancient.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',612,'USERGRID-937','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-937\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Nested Arrays in documents result in infinite loop / stack overflow\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Need to investigate and decide on an approach.  In addition do we support arrays with elements of varying types?at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.model.entity.MapToEntityConverter.processListForField(MapToEntityConverter.java:148)\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',613,'USERGRID-914','176','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-914\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 176, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Blog post for 10k TPS and horizontal scalability\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',614,'USERGRID-945','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-945\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Perform load testing of new shard management impl\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We\'ll want to load test this with our existing entity writes during heavy load.  We need to ensure shard allocation can keep up and that we have a consistent view of the shards.  We need to test the following scenarios# Write over 10 million entities in a single collection single region only# Write over 10 million entities concurrently in 2 regions# Write over 10 million entities concurrently in 2 regions and fail 1 of the regions.  The system should still function just not allocate new shards.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',615,'USERGRID-785','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-785\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Unable to run 2.0 to 2.1 data migration on large data set.\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Attempted to run entity data migration in (UG 2.0 to UG 2.1 ) with a instance having 1.1 million entities in a single collection within a single application.  Thi