dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',618,'USERGRID-941','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-941\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Spike: Investigate using Java Annotations to generate Swagger\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',619,'USERGRID-1018','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1018\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Create a job to remove duplicate connections and fix connection write logic\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"A bug in 2.0 has led to multiple edges on a connection.  We need a job that scans all connections and keeps the lowest timestamp on the connection.  Other edges should be deleted.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',620,'USERGRID-992','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-992\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Enable Org-level properties\", \"assignee\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',621,'USERGRID-1015','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1015\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Test Notification Migration \", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',622,'USERGRID-993','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-993\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Separate database system and system bootstrap\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"A call to /system/database/setup currently performs a database setup ES setup and then proceeds to migrate data.  This should be split into 2 separate events.  They should be the following. /system/database/setup creates all column families and ES indexes/system/database/bootstrap runs a datamigration manager then  creates all bootstrap data required for usergrid to function\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',623,'USERGRID-989','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-989\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Create a multi region lock ability for shard allocation\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"With the new shard proposal algorithm we need the ability to either 1)  Perform routing aware shard allocation across multi regions.  This ensures that we \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',624,'USERGRID-909','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-909\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Evaluate removing cache from edge shard management\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently using caches with the proposal phase for new shards has caused large numbers of tombstones.  Review the algorithm and determine the cause of the additional shard proposals.Usergrid currently performs 5 shard lookups on write and most miss the cache.  We\'ll change the following*Shard allocation*Shard allocation will not perform a propose + check phase. The following algorithm will occur.  This must occur at EACH_QUORUM to ensure that we have consensus across regions.  Any node will propose a new shard pivot.  This pivot will have compacted set to false and will have a column timestamp of a new timeuuid in microsThe proposing node will then read back all compacted = false shard pivots.  The shard pivot with the minimum timestamp will be retained all others will be deleted as proposals.  This will function similarly to distributed read locks in Cassandra.  Lowest proposed value always wins. Allocation is complete*Shard compaction*After a successful proposal allocation the allocating node will copy all edges from the previously compacted shard into the new shard.  It will continue to copy until no new edges are returned on read.Once read has been completed all edges that were copied can be deleted from the previous shard.  This target shard will be marked as compacted*Consistency*When performing consistency we will need a higher consistency level.  To ensure that shards exist worldwide proposal + selection should occur at EACH_QUORUM.  Standard reads can occur as LOCAL_QUORUM\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',625,'USERGRID-1016','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1016\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Remove UUID field encoding in our ES fields\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We shouldn\'t encode a UUID as a specific UUID field type since we\'re encoding it as a string.  To keep our index tuples simple and support both queries we should store it as a string type.  We should support the following formats.{code}select * where myUuid = \'aaa65d8a-16a6-11e5-86ea-7b4f7ff44431\'{code}As well as {code}select * where myUuid = aaa65d8a-16a6-11e5-86ea-7b4f7ff44431{code}Notice the addition of single quotes in the first query vs the parsing as a UUID type in the second query.  This will enable users to use both versions but does not affect performance.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',626,'USERGRID-1005','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1005\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Add Background processing for delete application\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',627,'USERGRID-991','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-991\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Fix tests after Jersey 2.0 upgrade\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',628,'USERGRID-857','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-857\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Portal page shows \\\"Thanks for signing up for a spot on our private beta\\\" when registering\", \"assignee\": \"ryan bridges\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"The portal has the following text when someone registers.  We need to change it to be more meaningful and remove \'beta\'.We\'re holding a seat for you! Thanks for signing up for a spot on our private beta. We will send you an email as soon as we\'re ready for you!In the mean time you can stay up to date with App Services on our GoogleGroup.Back to login\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',629,'USERGRID-54','177','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-54\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 177, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Remove old dead code and fully utilize guicy fig\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"In the CollecitonModule for Guice there appears to be old configuration code.  Can we remove and consolidate this t