\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need the ability to de-dupe connections per application.  This will enable migrating specific user applications when a shared keyspace is used.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',641,'USERGRID-1029','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1029\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"When PUTing by uuid or name add the entry into entity_id_sets column family\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When a PUT occurs in 1.0 then entry to Entity_Id_Sets is not re-inserted.  We need to ensure it is re-written.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',642,'USERGRID-1018','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1018\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Create a job to remove duplicate connections and fix connection write logic\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"A bug in 2.0 has led to multiple edges on a connection.  We need a job that scans all connections and keeps the lowest timestamp on the connection.  Other edges should be deleted.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',643,'USERGRID-992','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-992\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Enable Org-level properties\", \"assignee\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',644,'USERGRID-1015','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1015\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Test Notification Migration \", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',645,'USERGRID-1023','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1023\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Delete from collection does not use SQS or the event service\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',646,'USERGRID-1027','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1027\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Occational MIsses on Indexing into Elasticsearch\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Occasionally applications still aren\'t being indexed into elasticsearch. Need to investigate why these might be occuring. \", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',647,'USERGRID-1013','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1013\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"Automate upload of api baas 2.1 build to s3\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',648,'USERGRID-532','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-532\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Endpoint to get the size of the SQS index queue\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',649,'USERGRID-1022','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1022\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"remove batching in index processing\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',650,'USERGRID-1007','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1007\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Implement a cache for Shiro & permissions\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"How will a cache help improve performance?* Reduce load on Tomcat ES and C* caused by permissons calculation.          Do we need a distributed cache?* YES: Todd says we tried non-distributed cache (w/EhCache) and the caching was not effective (bad hit/mss ratio).Implementation ideas:* Use Cassandra column family implementation * Use Hazelcast cache* Use EhCache configured for distributed operationHow much should we expect performance to improve? How can we test this?* JUnit + metrics collection in our cache implementationSimplest approach seems to be Cassandra. Here\'s a design:h1. Add new Core Persistence Cache moduleThis is a new module that depends only on the Core Persistence Common module (and maybe Model?) and provides a generic cache interface that is \\\"segmented\\\" by a cache scope. When you put or get things you specify the cache scope and it is possible to invalidate all things within a cache scope with one call.{code}public interface SegmentedCache<KV> {   /** Put value into segment with ttl */   void put( CacheScope scope K key V value long ttl );   /** Get value from segment */   V get( CacheScope segment K key );   /** Delete all cache data of all types and of all scopes */   void invalidate();   /** Delete all cache data within specified segment */   void invalidate( CacheScope segment );}{code}Caches are stored in Cassandra *Usergrid_Cache* column family:* Row-key is applicationId* Column key is toString() of K key* Value is serialized V value objecth1. Plugin our Cache into Shiro at the REST module levelTo plugin to Shiro we provide implementations of the Shiro *CacheManager* and *Cache* interfaces that are backed by the Cache module. When permissions are updated we need need to ensure that the old cached permissions are invalidated. So we will modify the *EntityManager* revoke and grant methods to call invalidate for the application\'s cache scope.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 6, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',651,'USERGRID-1058','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1058\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Ability to generate a master Jacoco coverage report\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"In addition to separate Jacoco reports for each module we should also be able to generate a master Jacoco report.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',652,'USERGRID-1038','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1038\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"2.1-release: fix index batching from SQS reader\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',653,'USERGRID-1052','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1052\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"After large deletions graph seek time becomes slow\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 3, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"After a large number of deletions 100k + seek time on graph becomes very slow when searching collections.  Identify the issue and implement a fix based off of sha  a09485a3a5ac8b4217b294f4754ea8a70a7ec447\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',654,'USERGRID-1048','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1048\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"When reading messages from SQS an elevated consistency may be needed with latent replication\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Occasionally Cassandra multi-region replication lags during high load.  During this high load messages fail to process because it cannot read the entity from Cassandra.  Rather than fail we should retry with a high consistency level of quorum in all regions to ensure we replicate the data correctly.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',655,'USERGRID-1049','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1049\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"summary\": \"Add originating region to SQS queue message\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The region will be used to optimize handling of SQS messages that arrive faster than the corresponding C* changes.Name in the SQS message body \\\"sourceRegion\\\".\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',656,'USERGRID-1050','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1050\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Remove SQS implementation\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"SQS impl is no longer necessary with the current implementation.  We should always use the SNS implementation.  Remove it and configure the SNS implementation to work with a single region.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',657,'USERGRID-1021','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1021\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Improve Location Attribute Handling to not require Lat/Lon and also be indexable\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We should be able to store entities which have a \'location\' attribute which does not have both \'lat\' an \'lon\'.  These fields should also be queryable and therefore indexed.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',658,'USERGRID-1056','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1056\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"ES Documents not getting deleted when deleting entities\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"EntityDeleteEvents are not processing successfully causing no documents to get deleted when an entity is deleted.{code}2015-10-21 03:17:02177 [QueueConsumer_3] ERROR org.apache.usergrid.corepersistence.asyncevents.AmazonAsyncEventService- Received empty index sequence message:(d51bd93b-f26d-4bb1-a643-19ff097f4ba5) body:({\\\"entityDeleteEvent\\\":{\\\"creationTime\\\":1445396528637\\\"sourceRegion\\\":\\\"us-east-1\\\"\\\"entityIdScope\\\":{\\\"id\\\":{\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"3504d238-7467-11e5-b7a4-123f5d920dd1\\\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"testentity\\\"}\\\"applicationScope\\\":{\\\"application\\\":{\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"857fd592-7385-11e5-93f4-0af922a4f655\\\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"application\\\"}}}}}){code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',659,'USERGRID-1062','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1062\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Entity Edges are not getting deleted from graph when handling delete event\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',660,'USERGRID-1065','178','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1065\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 178, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Create a system endpoint for the superuser to GET all apps for an org\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',661,'USERGRID-1066','178','{\"key\": \"USERGR