", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Create a Repair tool that will address null pointer exceptions on entity returns and then properly handle them\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"500 null pointer exceptions return when data is present in an entity reference but not returned from cassandra while this may be a data consistency issue an investigation needs to be done. That said in the mean time a tool should be created that either can retrieve the data and restore it ( update ) or to delete the left over entity reference. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',665,'USERGRID-1073','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1073\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Test Windows phone\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',666,'USERGRID-926','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-926\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Include distances in geoquery responses\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"The best place for this would be in the metadata of the results in metadata.distance perhaps.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 6, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',667,'USERGRID-945','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-945\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Perform load testing of new shard management impl\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We\'ll want to load test this with our existing entity writes during heavy load.  We need to ensure shard allocation can keep up and that we have a consistent view of the shards.  We need to test the following scenarios# Write over 10 million entities in a single collection single region only# Write over 10 million entities concurrently in 2 regions# Write over 10 million entities concurrently in 2 regions and fail 1 of the regions.  The system should still function just not allocate new shards.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',668,'USERGRID-1085','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1085\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Create RPM Distributable for Usergrid 2.1\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',669,'USERGRID-785','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-785\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Unable to run 2.0 to 2.1 data migration on large data set.\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\