\"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"In Usergrid we don\'t support n+1 arrays for indexing however if you have objects nested within arrays we should index the nested object\'s key/value pairs.In the below document *\\\"nestedKey\\\": \\\"nestedValue\\\"* and *\\\"key\\\": \\\"value\\\"* should get indexed.  The value  *\\\"1\\\" in nestedLists* should still NOT be indexed.{code}{  \\\"name\\\": \\\"region3\\\"  \\\"nestedLists\\\": [    [      \\\"1\\\"    ]  ]  \\\"nestedObjects\\\": [    {      \\\"array\\\": [        {          \\\"nestedKey\\\": \\\"nestedValue\\\"        }      ]      \\\"key\\\": \\\"value\\\"    }  ]}{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',677,'USERGRID-1067','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1067\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Finish 2.1 release testing\", \"assignee\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need to test the following issues to verify they\'ve been fixed.Multi region writes and index syncingMulti region mass collection deletes: Delete the entire collection then ensure that seek times are fast with no query language.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',678,'USERGRID-1068','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1068\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Create a per app migration script\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Create a python script that will allow users to upgrade from 2.0 to 2.1 per application.  This will ultimately allow an incremental deployment across an existing 2.0 cluster without user impact.  Template for full system script that already exists: https://github.com/apache/usergrid/blob/2.1-release/stack/scripts/migrate_entity_data.pyIt should allow for the following migration process:tenant 11) setup new 2.1 tomcat2) run migration bootstrap3) migrate appinfo4) reindex mgmt app only5) run de-dup for whatever APP6) reindex whatever APP7) add 2.1 tomcats to customer ELB after 1-6 completed for all customer apps8) run delta re-index/migration for all customer appstenant 21) reset appinfo version2) migrate app info3) reindex mgmt app4) run de-dup for whatever APP5) reindex whatever app7) add 2.1 tomcats to customer ELB after 1-6 completed for all customer apps8) run delta re-index/migration for all customer appsafter all apps migration1) migrate entity data\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',679,'USERGRID-1071','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1071\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Test iOS push notifications\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',680,'USERGRID-1072','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1072\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Test Android push notifications\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',681,'USERGRID-1074','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1074\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"[SPIKE] Evaluate read repair of unique values in 1.0\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',682,'USERGRID-1069','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1069\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"summary\": \"implement build metrics in jenkins\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',683,'USERGRID-1079','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1079\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Add 2 endpoints for password hash migration\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"It is currently possible to migrate from a 1.0 installation to a 2.1 installation via a RESTful client.  However due to the inability to securely move password hashes application user\'s passwords are not retained.   Add the following.# In the 1.x branch add the ability to retrieve the password hash.   This should only be allowed by the superuser.# In 2.1-release add the ability to write the password hash to an application user.  This should only be allowed by the superuser.Note that the reason this is only allowed as a superuser is that we want to disable this functionality by default.  Any UG installation that is public facing should not have superuser enable.  This allows us to disable this functionality in environments that are publicly available environments.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',684,'USERGRID-1080','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1080\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"summary\": \"Change elasticsearch query for retrieving versions\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Currently using scroll and also does a select * followed by post query filters which may be hugely inefficient.New solution uses repeated requests where we query (not scroll) through the results by ordering by edge timestamp and then excluding previously found timestamp range in successive queries.Michael/Mike pairing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',685,'USERGRID-1091','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1091\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"AbstractReadGraphFilter produces and queues empty queue operations\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When read repair is triggered it is possible that there are now deIndexRequests to be queued.  Currently we\'re queueing empty operations and need to filter this properly.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',686,'USERGRID-462','186','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-462\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 186, \"status\": \"Resolved\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"[SPIKE] Investigate geo location re-index failure\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 1, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"When re-indexing entities that have a geo_location on it the geo_field is missing.  We need to investigate why this is happening.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',687,'USERGRID-933','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-933\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"[SPIKE] Understand what remains and break up tasks for migrating properties from files on Tomcat to Org-level in the management app\", \"assignee\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 13, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',688,'USERGRID-1187','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1187\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Ensure that PUT or POST does not create duplicate org association connections. \", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Doing PUT creates a duplicate edge on /management/orgs/org/users/emailfor existing users who were already on the org the POST command to /management/orgs/org/users/email creates a duplicate edge\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',689,'USERGRID-1076','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1076\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Create a Repair tool that will address null pointer exceptions on entity returns and then properly handle them\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"500 null pointer exceptions return when data is present in an entity reference but not returned from cassandra while this may be a data consistency issue an investigation needs to be done. That said in the mean time a tool should be created that either can retrieve the data and restore it ( update ) or to delete the left over entity reference. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',690,'USERGRID-1073','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1073\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Test Windows phone\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',691,'USERGRID-926','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-926\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Include distances in geoquery responses\", \"assignee\": \"Shawn Feldman\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"The best place for this would be in the metadata of the results in metadata.distance perhaps.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 6, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',692,'USERGRID-945','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-945\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Perform load testing of new shard management impl\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We\'ll want to load test this with our existing entity writes during heavy load.  We need to ensure shard allocation can keep up and that we have a consistent view of the shards.  We need to test the following scenarios# Write over 10 million entities in a single collection single region only# Write over 10 million entities concurrently in 2 regions# Write over 10 million entities concurrently in 2 regions and fail 1 of the regions.  The system should still function just not allocate new shards.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',693,'USERGRID-1085','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1085\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Create RPM Distributable for Usergrid 2.1\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcou