": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Order of operations error in Query Execution\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"I have a test that shows that queries of this form work:C = c and ( A > a or B = false )But the very same query formed like this will not work properly:( A > a or B = false ) and C = c\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',698,'USERGRID-872','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-872\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix and prune Usergrid tools in 2.1\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The Usergrid tools are broken in a variety of ways in the two-dot-o and two-dot-o-dev brands. The tools do not compile. Many rely on outdated 1.0 concepts. Many are obsolete.1. Delete any obsolete tools2. Make all tools compile\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',699,'USERGRID-1101','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1101\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Unique Value Cleanup in 2.1 - cleaning up old columns for old versions\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Ensure code makes it in to prevent wide rows in unique_values CF due to old versions not getting cleaned up\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',700,'USERGRID-1053','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1053\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"[SPIKE] Audit TODOs in the code\", \"assignee\": \"Todd Nine\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need to audit the TODO statements in the code.  For each we must:1) Check if there is an existing ticket- If there is no ticket create one2) Update the TODO statement with the link to the ticket3) Prioritize based on:- Will this generate a P1 case with a customer?- What is the usability impact of the product?Once we have audited these we will prioritize and schedule fixes\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',701,'USERGRID-1115','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1115\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix AdminUsersIT tests\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Six of the AdminUsersIT tests are ignored because they interfere with other tests and other reasons.  Figure out how to run those tests serially or some other way to test admin user features.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',702,'USERGRID-1112','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1112\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Test and Fix Shard Delete\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"There is a race condition between shard allocation and shard delete.  When a shard has been allocated it is getting removed AFTER edges are present.  This needs resolved.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',703,'USERGRID-1122','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1122\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"NullPointerException during read repair\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"In buildEntityDelete in EventBuilderImpl it can return null.  This is causing NPEs in AbstractReadGraphFilter.  We should return a result set with an empty observable instead of returning null.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',704,'USERGRID-1119','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1119\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix GroupResourceIT.postGroupActivity() test\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',705,'USERGRID-1106','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1106\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix test: clientCredentialsFlowWithHeaderAuthorization()\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Currently this test is ignored in Usergrid master branch:ApplicationResourceIT.clientCredentialsFlowWithHeaderAuthorization()If it is still relevant we should fix it and un-ignore it.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',706,'USERGRID-1126','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1126\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Documents not getting index when JSON contains latitude or longitude fields with empty string values\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Exception seen:{code}2015-11-21 21:40:37249 [Usergrid-SQS-Pool-88] ERROR org.apache.usergrid.corepersistence.asyncevents.AmazonAsyncEventService- Failed to index message: 7435e8a3-9f4c-4a08-a833-307698c45cbdjava.lang.RuntimeException: Error during processing of bulk index operations one of the responses failed.MapperParsingException[failed to parse]; nested: NumberFormatException[empty String];{code}Inside the entities there are latitude and longitude fields which contain empty strings.  These are mapped in Usergrid/Elasticsearch as geo_point types which are expected to be numbers or non-empty strings that can parse to coordiantes.  This is causing the document to get rejected upon indexing.  See the following for ensuring we are pre-validating so documents don\'t get rejected: https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/1.7/mapping-geo-point-type.htmlNeeds to be fixed here to not add the lat and lon properties if the values are null or empty strings  (non empty strings index without a problem).org/apache/usergrid/persistence/index/impl/EntityMappingParser.java:133A temporary workaround is just to assign a number value for these fields or just don\'t include them at all in the JSON request.Current:{code}\\\"geographicCoordinates\\\": {              \\\"latitude\\\": \\\"\\\"              \\\"longitude\\\": \\\"\\\"            }{code}Example workaround:{code}\\\"geographicCoordinates\\\": {              \\\"latitude\\\": 1              \\\"longitude\\\": 1            }{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',707,'USERGRID-1186','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1186\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Add DELETE for Admin Users\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"#NAME?\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',708,'USERGRID-1100','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1100\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"POST /users/{user}/devices/notifications does not work.\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',709,'USERGRID-1181','210','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1181\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 210, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summ