.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Currently many of the NotificationsServiceIT and NotifiersServiceIT test are either broken or incomplete because we were unable to create the mocks we need to test the code. We should revisit this and figure out how to get better test coverage for notifications in general.Search the code for USERGRID-1113 to find the tests that should be unignored fixed replace or deleted.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',724,'USERGRID-1182','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1182\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Support GCM 3.0 for Android Push Notifications\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 2, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 7, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',725,'USERGRID-35','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-35\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"summary\": \"Cannot delete an entity that has a connection to it\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 5, \"description\": \"\\\"To repro attempt to delete an entity that has a connection to it such as: curl -X DELETE \\\"\\\"https://api.com/fdsafdsa/testapp/dog/Dachsund\\\"\\\" Notice that you get error message: {\\\"\\\"error\\\"\\\":\\\"\\\"class_cast\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\"timestamp\\\"\\\":1386200483978\\\"\\\"duration\\\"\\\":0\\\"\\\"exception\\\"\\\":\\\"\\\"java.lang.ClassCastException\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\"error_description\\\"\\\":\\\"\\\"org.usergrid.persistence.cassandra.ConnectedEntityRefImpl cannot be cast to org.usergrid.persistence.cassandra.ConnectionRefImpl\\\"\\\"} It is expected that the entity is deleted and the connection is deleted as well.\\\"\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',726,'USERGRID-1083','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1083\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"getEntityByName 404 API response logs unnecessary Uncaught Exception ERROR\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"2015-10-29 00:50:19056 [http-bio-8080-exec-342] ERROR org.apache.usergrid.rest.exceptions.AbstractExceptionMapper- Uncaught Exceptionorg.apache.usergrid.persistence.exceptions.EntityNotFoundException: Cannot find entity with name: test2307924        at org.apache.usergrid.services.AbstractCollectionService.getItemByName(AbstractCollectionService.java:155)\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',727,'USERGRID-144','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-144\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"summary\": \"Assets: File meta not refreshed after PUT\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"In the new implementation of assets PUT operations update the asset data but do not update the file metadata.This means that if the content-type of the asset changes GET operations fail if I specify the expected content-type in the Accept header.For example if I attach an asset with content-type: image/jpeg I can PUT a new jpeg and retrieve the new image with the Accept: image/jpeg header.But...If I PUT a text file the file metadata remains content-type: image/jpeg so a GET with Accept: text/plain fails.But...A GET with Accept: image/jpeg succeeds and I get back the data for my text file.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',728,'USERGRID-1012','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1012\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Geolocation with limit of 610.000 returns a result with distance of 610.09\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"Testing with the following entities and locations shows that we are rounding when people might not be expecting it:    UsergridEntity e = new UsergridEntity(collectionName);    e.setLocation(37.334115 -121.894340);    e.setProperty(\\\"name\\\" \\\"Apigee Office\\\");    e.POST();    UsergridEntity amicis = new UsergridEntity(collectionName);    amicis.setLocation(37.335616 -121.894168);    amicis.setProperty(\\\"name\\\" \\\"Amicis\\\");    amicis.POST();    UsergridEntity sanPedroMarket = new UsergridEntity(collectionName);    sanPedroMarket.setLocation(37.336499 -121.894356);    sanPedroMarket.setProperty(\\\"name\\\" \\\"SanPedroMarket\\\");    sanPedroMarket.POST();    UsergridEntity saintJamesPark = new UsergridEntity(collectionName);    saintJamesPark.setLocation(37.339079 -121.891422);    saintJamesPark.setProperty(\\\"name\\\" \\\"saintJamesPark\\\");    saintJamesPark.POST();    UsergridEntity sanJoseNews = new UsergridEntity(collectionName);    sanJoseNews.setLocation(37.337812 -121.890784);    sanJoseNews.setProperty(\\\"name\\\" \\\"sanJoseNews\\\");    sanJoseNews.POST();    Usergri