onverter.java:148)\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',730,'USERGRID-767','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-767\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"WebApplicationException / Uncaught Exception embarassment\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 4, \"description\": \"The following exception is returned for many cases including a parse error and if an endpoint doesn\'t support the attempted HTTP method.  We need more descriptive messages in these cases.{\\\"error\\\":\\\"web_application\\\"\\\"timestamp\\\":1435156493000\\\"duration\\\":0\\\"exception\\\":\\\"javax.ws.rs.WebApplicationException\\\"}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',731,'USERGRID-1203','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1203\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Allow certs in notifiers to be updated and store their details in the entity.\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',732,'USERGRID-1200','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1200\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"summary\": \"Org config override for portal and API URLs\", \"assignee\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"1. Add usergrid.api.url.base property (defaults to http://localhost:8080/ROOT) that can be overridden for an org.2. The confirmation and activation properties are hardcoded paths and don\'t need org overrides. Example:usergrid.admin.activation.url is built by concatenating usergrid.api.url.base and \\\"/management/users/%s/activate\\\"3. swagger.basepath removed and replaced by usergrid.api.url.base.4. Refactor orgconfig to return system defaults if not configurable by org.usergrid.redirect_root changes will happen later -- org not known when setting is being used so no need to add an org config item.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',733,'USERGRID-1047','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1047\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"GET on missing Asset file in S3 generates 500 error not 404\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"When doing a GET on an asset file that doesn\'t exist it should return a 404 rather than a 500 error because the file is not there. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',734,'USERGRID-1209','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1209\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"GET on missing Asset file in S3 generates 500 error not 404\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',735,'USERGRID-1210','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1210\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"George Reyes\", \"summary\": \"Fix AwsAssetResourceIT\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"George Reyes\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Fix all the broken asset tests\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',736,'USERGRID-1211','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1211\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Migrate locks from Hector to Astyanax\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Implement locks and a lock manager using Astyanax driver.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',737,'USERGRID-1241','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1241\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"summary\": \"Org config settings for view redirects\", \"assignee\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The usergrid.view.* properties are currently used to redirect on activation or confirmation of organizations or users. These may need to be configured differently for different customers.The usergrid.view.* property names are made by concatenating package template and class names so instead of adding them as hardcoded org config items add a property (usergrid.org.config.property.regex) to specify the regex for additional properties that may be configured by org.Also add check for org overrides for the redirect properties.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 4, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',738,'USERGRID-1243','187','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1243\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 187, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"summary\": \"Replace logging string concatenation with formatting\", \"assignee\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Mike Dunker\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Concatenating strings when logging creates temporary strings that can have a negative effect on GC. Instead log4j\'s string formatting functionality should be used.Example:Replacelogger.info(\\\"Invalid property value. name = \\\" + name + \\\" value = \\\" + value);withlogger.info(\\\"Invalid property value. name = {} value = {}\\\" name value);Also:1) Standardize on slf4j version 1.7.2 which includes variable argument support.2) Remove extraneous object creation (for when variable argument support didn\'t exist).3) Change debug statements for element creation/deletion connections etc. to trace.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',739,'USERGRID-1120','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1120\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix CounterIT.testIncrementAndDecrement() test\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 2}'),('UserGrid',740,'USERGRID-1116','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1116\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix MessagesIT tests\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Four of the MessagesIT tests are ignored. Fix these tests and un-ignore them.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 2}'),('UserGrid',741,'USERGRID-1118','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1118\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix EventsResource and IT\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The EventsResource was broken during two-dot-o development and the tests in EventsResourceIT were marked ignore.Fix the EventsResource and re-enable the tests.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',742,'USERGRID-1256','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1256\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Introduce Datastax Java Driver in effort to migration away from Astyanax\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',743,'USERGRID-1093','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1093\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Load test in-memory queue with current consumer and queue implementation\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',744,'USERGRID-1253','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1253\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Investigate and Refactor WriteUniqueVerify\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Seeing a lot of exceptions like the following which indicate that the current workflow for writing and validating unique values (e.g. name/username/email properties):Caused by: java.lang.RuntimeException: Could not retrieve unique value for field email unable to verify        at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.write.WriteUniqueVerify$ConsistentReplayCommand.executeStrategy(WriteUniqueVerify.java:201)        at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.write.WriteUniqueVerify$ConsistentReplayCommand.run(WriteUniqueVerify.java:173)        at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.write.WriteUniqueVerify$ConsistentReplayCommand.run(WriteUniqueVerify.java:150)        at com.netflix.hystrix.HystrixCommand$1.call(HystrixCommand.java:294)        ... 21 moreCaused by: rx.exceptions.OnErrorThrowable$OnNextValue: OnError while emitting onNext value: org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.CollectionIoEvent.class        at rx.exceptions.OnErrorThrowable.addValueAsLastCause(OnErrorThrowable.java:104)        at rx.internal.operators.OperatorDoOnEach$1.onNext(OperatorDoOnEach.java:81)        at rx.internal.util.ScalarSynchronousObservable$ScalarSynchronousAction.call(ScalarSynchronousObservable.java:115)        at rx.internal.schedulers.ScheduledAction.run(ScheduledAction.java:55)        at rx.schedulers.ExecutorScheduler$ExecutorSchedulerWorker.run(ExecutorScheduler.java:98)We should see how to improve this so we can handle unique values at scale (likely introducing something like akka with consistent hash routing of the write operation).\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',745,'USERGRID-522','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-522\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Support for Partial Indexing of types\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This task is to create a design document and proposal for the approach which we would use for explicit/partial indexing.  With something like this we need to review the proposal with the community since it is a big change to how we handle indexing.Indexing everything all the time by default has gotten us into trouble and will continue to do so.  We should make index-everything configuratble and introduce a way of defining the fields to be indexed.Perhaps consider using JSON Schema to define the schema for a collection which can also define the fields for indexing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',746,'USERGRID-832','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-832\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"[SPIKE] Investigate and propose 2-3 approaches for indexing specific attributes of documents\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Please investigate and propose a few different options for explicit indexing.Things to consider:1) How other databases handle this2) Ability to index all occurrences of a given field name - for example index \'cat\' whether it is a root property pets.cat owners.cat etc.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',747,'USERGRID-990','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-990\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"REST API Endpoint for defining indexes\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',748,'USERGRID-1191','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1191\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Create 2.1 Release for Apache\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need to create a 2.1 release for Apache.  Would be nice to have a binary WAR distribution.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',749,'USERGRID-1124','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1124\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Internal \\\"size\\\" within entity metadata is not displayed when doing a GET by entity name \", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This request does not come back with size in metadata object. GET /org/app/collection/entityName{code}{  \\\"action\\\" : \\\"get\\\"  \\\"application\\\" : \\\"ec2df3b3-6e0e-11e5-9798-0223e9015bf9\\\"  \\\"params\\\" : { }  \\\"path\\\" : \\\"/regions\\\"  \\\"uri\\\" : \\\"https://testing\\\"  \\\"entities\\\" : [ {    \\\"uuid\\\" : \\\"2dcf254c-8ef5-11e5-87c2-069a7df27e87\\\"    \\\"type\\\" : \\\"region\\\"    \\\"name\\\" : \\\"region6\\\"    \\\"created\\\" : 1447961939135    \\\"modified\\\" : 1447961939135    \\\"metadata\\\" : {      \\\"path\\\" : \\\"/regions/2dcf254c-8ef5-11e5-87c2-069a7df27e87\\\"    }  } ]  \\\"timestamp\\\" : 1447976782774  \\\"duration\\\" : 77  \\\"organization\\\" : \\\"org\\\"  \\\"applicationName\\\" : \\\"app\\\"}{code}However get with the entity\'s UUID does return the metadata size.GET /org/app/collection/2dcf254c-8ef5-11e5-87c2-069a7df27e87{code}{  \\\"action\\\" : \\\"get\\\"  \\\"application\\\" : \\\"ec2df3b3-6e0e-11e5-9798-0223e9015bf9\\\"  \\\"params\\\" : { }  \\\"path\\\" : \\\"/regions\\\"  \\\"uri\\\" : \\\"https://testing\\\"  \\\"entities\\\" : [ {    \\\"uuid\\\" : \\\"2dcf254c-8ef5-11e5-87c2-069a7df27e87\\\"    \\\"type\\\" : \\\"region\\\"    \\\"name\\\" : \\\"region6\\\"    \\\"created\\\" : 1447961939135    \\\"modified\\\" : 1447961939135    \\\"metadata\\\" : {      \\\"path\\\" : \\\"/regions/2dcf254c-8ef5-11e5-87c2-069a7df27e87\\\"      \\\"size\\\" : 334    }  } ]  \\\"timestamp\\\" : 1447977010952  \\\"duration\\\" : 36  \\\"organization\\\" : \\\"org\\\"  \\\"applicationName\\\" : \\\"app\\\"}{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',750,'USERGRID-1252','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1252\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Default entity types do not show up on GET /<application> endpoint when there are 0 entities\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Default entity types do not show up on GET /<application> endpoint when there are 0 entities of that type (none in the collection)e.g. usersDue to this the portal may not show the default collections when there are 0 entities in the collection.  This is happening now that graph edges are cleaned up properly but we should discuss showing these since they are default reserved typed entities in Usergrid.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',751,'USERGRID-891','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-891\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Convert Usergrid docs & Update for 2.0: Push Notifications\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',752,'USERGRID-238','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-238\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Yegor Pomortsev\", \"summary\": \"Remove ARS Maquette font from Portal\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Yegor Pomortsev\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Wish\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 2.0, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": \"portal/css/arsmarquette/*dist/usergrid-portal/css/arsmarquette/*dist-cov/usergrid-portal/css/arsmarquette/*These fonts are Copyright (c) ARS Type┬«-Angus R. Shamal 1999-2010. All rights reserved. Do we have a license to redistribute them?\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',753,'USERGRID-119','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-119\", \"votes\": 1, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Automate create of Usergrid release bundles\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"There are two parts to this:1. The source code release bundleApache releases are source code so this is the \\\"primary\\\" release bundle. It should be a Tar and/or Gzipped Tar file that contains all of our source code.2. The binary release bundleThis is intended to be a convenience for people who want to get a copy of the Usergrid that is ready for deployment. It should contain the ROOT.war file the launcher Jar and the Portal Zip file plus a pointer to docs that explain how to deploy and run them.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',754,'USERGRID-1205','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1205\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Duplicate Admin Repair\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Develop a duplicate admin user repair tool that is testable with a dry-run feature.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',755,'USERGRID-286','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-286\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 1, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"In Progress\", \"creator\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"summary\": \"Build Application and Collection Delete Async Distributed Workflow\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Rod Simpson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 1, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Akka and the Usergrid ActorSystem module is now used in Usergrid from 2.1.1 onwards.  We need to develop an asynch distributed workflow leveraging this ActorSystem for things like data cleanup after app/collection deletion.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',756,'USERGRID-402','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-402\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Remove old dictionary calls with Hector and migrate to the map module\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',757,'USERGRID-403','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-403\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Migrate counters from Hector to Datastax Java Driver\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need to migrate our counters from Hector to a more reliable counter framework.  Use counter column and leverage Datastax Java Driver for time being assuming Cassandra 2.1 improvements are solid.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',758,'USERGRID-1250','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1250\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Create additional push notification tests for the node.js integration tests\", \"assignee\": \"Abhinav Sinha\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Need to test the following example endpoints:/users/michael/notifications/users/michael/devices/notifications/users/michael/devices/*/notifications/users;ql=select * where username=\'michael\'/notifications/devices/*/notifications/devices/device1/notifications/devices/af94a111-a927-11e5-8d9c-12c60bce005f/notifications/devices;ql=select * where uuid=\'a4b7dc0b-b4d3-11e5-80bb-12c60bce005f\'/notificationsAlso it\'s important to test creating groups of users and sending notifications to 1 or more groups. \", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',759,'USERGRID-1245','218','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1245\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 218, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Find alternative to com.clearspring.analytics\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"com.clearspring.analytics.hash.MurmurHash is found in the fasterutil dependency which is 16MB.  We want to pare down the size of the REST WAR file.  Let\'s see if there is an alternative.Here is the maven dependency:{code}    <dependency>      <groupId>com.clearspring.analytics</groupId>      <artifactId>stream</artifactId>      <version>2.7.0</version>    </dependency>{code}Look for the com.clearspring.analytics package.  Seems to be used in GCM Adapter:{code}   private Batch getBatch( Map<String Object> payload) {       synchronized (this) {           long hash = MurmurHash.hash64(payload);           Batch batch = batches.get(hash);           if (batch == null && payload != null) {               batch = new Batch(notifier payload);               batches.put(hash batch);           }           return batch;       }   }{code}Also the CountMinSketch is used from this dependency:org/apache/usergrid/services/notifications/impl/ApplicationQueueManagerImpl.java:111{code}final CountMinSketch sketch = new CountMinSketch(0.0001.997364181); //add probablistic counter to find dups{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',760,'USERGRID-1120','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1120\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix CounterIT.testIncrementAndDecrement() test\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 2}'),('UserGrid',761,'USERGRID-1116','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1116\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix MessagesIT tests\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Four of the MessagesIT tests are ignored. Fix these tests and un-ignore them.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 2}'),('UserGrid',762,'USERGRID-1118','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1118\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix EventsResource and IT\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The EventsResource was broken during two-dot-o development and the tests in EventsResourceIT were marked ignore.Fix the EventsResource and re-enable the tests.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',763,'USERGRID-1256','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1256\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Introduce Datastax Java Driver in effort to migration away from Astyanax\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',764,'USERGRID-1093','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1093\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Load test in-memory queue with current consumer and queue implementation\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',765,'USERGRID-1253','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1253\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Investigate and Refactor WriteUniqueVerify\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Seeing a lot of exceptions like the following which indicate that the current workflow for writing and validating unique values (e.g. name/username/email properties):Caused by: java.lang.RuntimeException: Could not retrieve unique value for field email unable to verify        at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.write.WriteUniqueVerify$ConsistentReplayCommand.executeStrategy(WriteUniqueVerify.java:201)        at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.write.WriteUniqueVerify$ConsistentReplayCommand.run(WriteUniqueVerify.java:173)        at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.write.WriteUniqueVerify$ConsistentReplayCommand.run(WriteUniqueVerify.java:150)        at com.netflix.hystrix.HystrixCommand$1.call(HystrixCommand.java:294)        ... 21 moreCaused by: rx.exceptions.OnErrorThrowable$OnNextValue: OnError while emitting onNext value: org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.CollectionIoEvent.class        at rx.exceptions.OnErrorThrowable.addValueAsLastCause(OnErrorThrowable.java:104)        at rx.internal.operators.OperatorDoOnEach$1.onNext(OperatorDoOnEach.java:81)        at rx.internal.util.ScalarSynchronousObservable$ScalarSynchronousAction.call(ScalarSynchronousObservable.java:115)        at rx.internal.schedulers.ScheduledAction.run(ScheduledAction.java:55)        at rx.schedulers.ExecutorScheduler$ExecutorSchedulerWorker.run(ExecutorScheduler.java:98)We should see how to improve this so we can handle unique values at scale (likely introducing something like akka with consistent hash routing of the write operation).\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',766,'USERGRID-522','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-522\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Support for Partial Indexing of types\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This task is to create a design document and proposal for the approach which we would use for explicit/partial indexing.  With something like this we need to review the proposal with the community since it is a big change to how we handle indexing.Indexing everything all the time by default has gotten us into trouble and will continue to do so.  We should make index-everything configuratble and introduce a way of defining the fields to be indexed.Perhaps consider using JSON Schema to define the schema for a collection which can also define the fields for indexing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',767,'USERGRID-832','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-832\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"[SPIKE] Investigate and propose 2-3 approaches for indexing specific attributes of documents\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Please investigate and propose a few different options for explicit indexing.Things to consider:1) How other databases handle this2) Ability to index all occurrences of a given field name - for example index \'cat\' whether it is a root property pets.cat owners.cat etc.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',768,'USERGRID-990','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-990\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"REST API Endpoint for defining indexes\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',769,'USERGRID-1268','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1268\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Proof of Concept: use Akka for Unique Value enforcement\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"By using an distributed Actor System we can ensure that only one thread accesses any one unique value at a time. I have a working proof of concept of this that writes to Cassandra (via Java Native Driver).Initial design is here:https://docs.google.com/document/d/1o9okFgNb_c1RY0eIcZMhijhxE9v7BxHYDiuI8BqkLgU/edit#Proof of Concept (POC) code is here:https://github.com/snoopdave/akka_poc1Presentation that explains the POC is here:https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/11ARSPZ6IAxOYSTo4jcmEdnzXvOgVGNGslznmVtLOZjY/edit?usp=sharing\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',770,'USERGRID-1191','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1191\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Create 2.1 Release for Apache\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"We need to create a 2.1 release for Apache.  Would be nice to have a binary WAR distribution.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',771,'USERGRID-1124','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1124\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Internal \\\"size\\\" within entity metadata is not displayed when doing a GET by entity name \", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This request does not come back with size in metadata object. GET /org/app/collection/entityName{code}{  \\\"action\\\" : \\\"get\\\"  \\\"application\\\" : \\\"ec2df3b3-6e0e-11e5-9798-0223e9015bf9\\\"  \\\"params\\\" : { }  \\\"path\\\" : \\\"/regions\\\"  \\\"uri\\\" : \\\"https://testing\\\"  \\\"entities\\\" : [ {    \\\"uuid\\\" : \\\"2dcf254c-8ef5-11e5-87c2-069a7df27e87\\\"    \\\"type\\\" : \\\"region\\\"    \\\"name\\\" : \\\"region6\\\"    \\\"created\\\" : 1447961939135    \\\"modified\\\" : 1447961939135    \\\"metadata\\\" : {      \\\"path\\\" : \\\"/regions/2dcf254c-8ef5-11e5-87c2-069a7df27e87\\\"    }  } ]  \\\"timestamp\\\" : 1447976782774  \\\"duration\\\" : 77  \\\"organization\\\" : \\\"org\\\"  \\\"applicationName\\\" : \\\"app\\\"}{code}However get with the entity\'s UUID does return the metadata size.GET /org/app/collection/2dcf254c-8ef5-11e5-87c2-069a7df27e87{code}{  \\\"action\\\" : \\\"get\\\"  \\\"application\\\" : \\\"ec2df3b3-6e0e-11e5-9798-0223e9015bf9\\\"  \\\"params\\\" : { }  \\\"path\\\" : \\\"/regions\\\"  \\\"uri\\\" : \\\"https://testing\\\"  \\\"entities\\\" : [ {    \\\"uuid\\\" : \\\"2dcf254c-8ef5-11e5-87c2-069a7df27e87\\\"    \\\"type\\\" : \\\"region\\\"    \\\"name\\\" : \\\"region6\\\"    \\\"created\\\" : 1447961939135    \\\"modified\\\" : 1447961939135    \\\"metadata\\\" : {      \\\"path\\\" : \\\"/regions/2dcf254c-8ef5-11e5-87c2-069a7df27e87\\\"      \\\"size\\\" : 334    }  } ]  \\\"timestamp\\\" : 1447977010952  \\\"duration\\\" : 36  \\\"organization\\\" : \\\"org\\\"  \\\"applicationName\\\" : \\\"app\\\"}{code}\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',772,'USERGRID-1252','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1252\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Default entity types do not show up on GET /<application> endpoint when there are 0 entities\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Default entity types do not show up on GET /<application> endpoint when there are 0 entities of that type (none in the collection)e.g. usersDue to this the portal may not show the default collections when there are 0 entities in the collection.  This is happening now that graph edges are cleaned up properly but we should discuss showing these since they are default reserved typed entities in Usergrid.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',773,'USERGRID-446','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-446\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Removed unused column families\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"There are a lot of remnant column families from 1.0 that are causing bloat in our system.  We need to audit each 1.0 column family.  If it is no longer used it should be removed.  If it is more complicated to remove these column families (such as queues) we\'ll need to open tickets for them and address them later.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',774,'USERGRID-402','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-402\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Remove old dictionary calls with Hector and migrate to the map module\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',775,'USERGRID-403','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-403\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"Open\", \"creator\": \"Todd Nine\", \"summary\": \"Migrate counters from Hector to Datastax Java Driver\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Todd Nine\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"We need to migrate our counters from Hector to a more reliable counter framework.  Use counter column and leverage Datastax Java Driver for time being assuming Cassandra 2.1 improvements are solid.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',776,'USERGRID-1262','221','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1262\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 221, \"status\": \"In Progress\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Always return JSON as application/json\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Bug\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"Sometimes Usergrid returns JSON data as text/html so that it may be displayed in a browser. This is a bad practice and should be discontinued.\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',777,'USERGRID-1120','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1120\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix CounterIT.testIncrementAndDecrement() test\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 2}'),('UserGrid',778,'USERGRID-1116','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1116\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix MessagesIT tests\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Four of the MessagesIT tests are ignored. Fix these tests and un-ignore them.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 2}'),('UserGrid',779,'USERGRID-1283','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1283\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Improve ServiceManager.init() start-up logic\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Improvement\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 1, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Changes related to management app / startup logic1) Lock Manager setup now happens in the EntityManagerFactory and is invoked as part of the normal /database/setup process.2) CpEntityManagerFactory now checks for the existence of the management app and will retry if it cannot be found unless Usergrid has not yet been bootstrapped. It will log the root cause exception and a track trace. Max retries and interval are configurable.3) CpEntityManagerFactory now keeps a \\\"cache\\\" of the latest fetched Management App object. EntityManager cache will update the cached Management App object whenever it is successfully fetched.4) CpEntityManagerFactory\'s cache of EntityManagers will not cache bad EntityManagers i.e. those that cannot fetch their own applications or the application\'s name is null.5) EntityManager cache size configurable via a new property \'\'entity.manager.cache.size\\\"6) Additional logging for when EntityManager EntityManagerFactory QueueManager or QueueManagerFactory is null.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 8, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',780,'USERGRID-1289','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1289\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Make /org/app/users/me permissions more robust.\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 3, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 3, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',781,'USERGRID-1118','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1118\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Fix EventsResource and IT\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"The EventsResource was broken during two-dot-o development and the tests in EventsResourceIT were marked ignore.Fix the EventsResource and re-enable the tests.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',782,'USERGRID-1256','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1256\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Introduce Datastax Java Driver in effort to migration away from Astyanax\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 1.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',783,'USERGRID-1093','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1093\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Load test in-memory queue with current consumer and queue implementation\", \"assignee\": \"Michael Russo\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 3.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',784,'USERGRID-1253','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1253\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Michael Russo\", \"summary\": \"Investigate and Refactor WriteUniqueVerify\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"Michael Russo\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Seeing a lot of exceptions like the following which indicate that the current workflow for writing and validating unique values (e.g. name/username/email properties):Caused by: java.lang.RuntimeException: Could not retrieve unique value for field email unable to verify        at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.write.WriteUniqueVerify$ConsistentReplayCommand.executeStrategy(WriteUniqueVerify.java:201)        at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.write.WriteUniqueVerify$ConsistentReplayCommand.run(WriteUniqueVerify.java:173)        at org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.write.WriteUniqueVerify$ConsistentReplayCommand.run(WriteUniqueVerify.java:150)        at com.netflix.hystrix.HystrixCommand$1.call(HystrixCommand.java:294)        ... 21 moreCaused by: rx.exceptions.OnErrorThrowable$OnNextValue: OnError while emitting onNext value: org.apache.usergrid.persistence.collection.mvcc.stage.CollectionIoEvent.class        at rx.exceptions.OnErrorThrowable.addValueAsLastCause(OnErrorThrowable.java:104)        at rx.internal.operators.OperatorDoOnEach$1.onNext(OperatorDoOnEach.java:81)        at rx.internal.util.ScalarSynchronousObservable$ScalarSynchronousAction.call(ScalarSynchronousObservable.java:115)        at rx.internal.schedulers.ScheduledAction.run(ScheduledAction.java:55)        at rx.schedulers.ExecutorScheduler$ExecutorSchedulerWorker.run(ExecutorScheduler.java:98)We should see how to improve this so we can handle unique values at scale (likely introducing something like akka with consistent hash routing of the write operation).\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',785,'USERGRID-522','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-522\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"Support for Partial Indexing of types\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"This task is to create a design document and proposal for the approach which we would use for explicit/partial indexing.  With something like this we need to review the proposal with the community since it is a big change to how we handle indexing.Indexing everything all the time by default has gotten us into trouble and will continue to do so.  We should make index-everything configuratble and introduce a way of defining the fields to be indexed.Perhaps consider using JSON Schema to define the schema for a collection which can also define the fields for indexing.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',786,'USERGRID-832','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-832\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"[SPIKE] Investigate and propose 2-3 approaches for indexing specific attributes of documents\", \"assignee\": \"George Reyes\", \"priority\": 2, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 5.0, \"watchcount\": 2, \"description\": \"Please investigate and propose a few different options for explicit indexing.Things to consider:1) How other databases handle this2) Ability to index all occurrences of a given field name - for example index \'cat\' whether it is a root property pets.cat owners.cat etc.\", \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 1, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',787,'USERGRID-990','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-990\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"summary\": \"REST API Endpoint for defining indexes\", \"assignee\": null, \"priority\": 4, \"reporter\": \"Jeffrey West\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": null, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": null, \"fixVersions\": 1, \"commentCount\": 0, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 1}'),('UserGrid',788,'USERGRID-1268','224','{\"key\": \"USERGRID-1268\", \"votes\": 0, \"blocks\": 0, \"sprint\": 224, \"status\": \"Closed\", \"creator\": \"David Johnson\", \"summary\": \"Proof of Concept: use Akka for Unique Value enforcement\", \"assignee\": \"David Johnson\", \"priority\": 3, \"reporter\": \"David Johnson\", \"subtasks\": 0, \"blockedBy\": 0, \"issueType\": \"Story\", \"dependedOn\": 0, \"issueLinks\": 0, \"storyPoint\": 8.0, \"watchcount\": 1, \"description\": \"By using an distributed Actor System we can ensure that only one thread accesses any one unique value at a time. I have a working proof of concept of this that writes to Cassandra (via Java Native Driver).Initial design is here:https://docs.google.com/document/d/1o9okFgNb_c1RY0eIcZMhijhxE9v7BxHYDiuI8BqkLgU/edit#Proof of Concept (POC) code is here:https://github.com/snoopdave/akka_poc1Presentation that explains the POC is here:https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/11ARSPZ6IAxOYSTo4jcmEdnzXvOgVGNGslznmVtLOZjY/edit?usp=sharing\", \"fixVersions\": 0, \"commentCount\": 2, \"dependedOnBy\": 0, \"affectedVersions\": 0}'),('UserGrid',789,'USERGRID-1266','224','{\"key\": \"US